many and Denmark of associations between quality of leadership and subsequent 5-year development of mental distress","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-804543","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"DNA methylation patterns have emerged as reliable markers for age estimation, offering potential applications in forensic investigations, namely, in cases where there is no information about a possible suspect, in the identification of victims of mass disasters, or in immigration cases when assessing the age of individuals seeking asylum. This study aimed to evaluate the 11-CpG panel proposed by Aliferi et al. (2022) for age estimation. During the implementation phase, the ELOVL2 amplicon from the original work was replaced with a shorter fragment, and the two PCR multiplexes were optimized by changing the amplicons and primer conditions of each multiplex. The technical performance of the optimised assay was assessed using artificially methylated DNA standards. Robust quantification of the methylation levels at the 11 CpG sites was observed. Sensitivity tests demonstrated that DNA inputs down to 10 ng could produce reliable methylation quantification. Using the optimised panel, 148 Danish blood samples (18 - 68 years of age) were typed for their methylation status at the 11 CpG sites. Results showed that the DNA methylation at the 11 CpG loci was significantly correlated with age (0.68 ≤ r ≤ 0.88) in the Danish sample set, confirming the potential of the 11 CpGs in age prediction. A Danish age prediction model was constructed using 108 of the Danish blood samples and a support vector machine with polynomial function (SVMp). The performances of the new model and the original model based on UK individuals were compared using the remaining 40 Danish blood samples. Comparing the published model to the one developed in this study gave similar results with mean absolute errors (MAE) of 3.28 and 3.35, respectively. However, the original model showed a bias in the age predictions, underestimating the age by an average of 1.53 years in the Danish samples. This bias towards underestimation was not observed in the newly developed age prediction model based on Danish individuals. In summary, this assay provides a reasonably accurate age estimation of a single-source donor, if the sample material is blood and more than 10 ng of nuclear DNA can be extracted from the sample.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Refn, Mie Rath","Kampmann, Marie-Louise","Vyöni, Agnes","Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","Sørensen, Erik","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Kongstad, Mette","Aliferi, Anastasia","Giangasparo, Federica","Morling, Niels","Ballard, David","Børsting, Claus","Pereira, Vania"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789801"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King's College London"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"independent evaluation of an 000000000011 cpg panel for age estimation in blood","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fsigen.2024.103214","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789801","identifier":[{"id":"39693839","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85212155546","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-011a3115-ccb4-4ccb-a140-305b51710973"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA7AA73F8F87EE9B031667060E6C75F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/416506596/1_s2.0_S1872497324002102_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fsigen.2024.103214","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Section of Forensic Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King's College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mie Rath","key":"refnpau","last":"Refn","locid":"052a2e3f-5114-4f3d-b444-7707de9aef7d","name":"Refn, Mie Rath","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie-Louise","key":"kampmannpau","last":"Kampmann","locid":"6407dfca-f642-42c6-a444-a2fae2093b04","name":"Kampmann, Marie-Louise","orcid":"0000-0001-5403-5960","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Agnes","key":"vyönipau","last":"Vyöni","name":"Vyöni, Agnes","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"tfelthansenpau","last":"Tfelt-Hansen","locid":"bdd29054-7062-428a-a97d-e32cb8d80d38","name":"Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0003-3895-9316","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"6d7c4886-3171-40db-be0a-9b06c12f0f8e","name":"Sørensen, Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sisse Rye","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"kongstadpau","last":"Kongstad","locid":"790c76e3-7fbb-4215-9cb5-ff2234261997","name":"Kongstad, Mette","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anastasia","key":"aliferipau","last":"Aliferi","name":"Aliferi, Anastasia","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Federica","key":"giangasparopau","last":"Giangasparo","name":"Giangasparo, Federica","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"morlingpau","last":"Morling","locid":"6a809f42-2644-434a-9bec-a1fbf5e26093","name":"Morling, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-9463-5087","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"David","key":"ballardpau","last":"Ballard","name":"Ballard, David","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus","key":"børstingpau","last":"Børsting","locid":"70c85e72-9aa9-429d-a4bb-9cabd7528618","name":"Børsting, Claus","orcid":"0000-0003-0421-7429","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vania","key":"pereirapau","last":"Pereira","locid":"d5a50a5b-d242-4baf-8b82-e0acaf8ae52f","name":"Pereira, Vania","orcid":"0000-0002-8789-5286","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39693839"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fsigen.2024.103214","issn":["18724973","18780326"],"issn_org":["18724973"],"journal":"Forensic Science International: Genetics","paperid":"103214","status":"p","title":"Forensic Science International: Genetics","title_org":"Forensic science international. Genetics","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212155546"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-011a3115-ccb4-4ccb-a140-305b51710973"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Independent evaluation of an 11-CpG panel for age estimation in blood","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789801","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Elevated arterial ammonia is associated with several complications of liver disease as it predicts mortality for in-patients and decompensation, hospitalization and death in out-patients with cirrhosis. In this review, our aim was to estimate how the individual organs contribute to arterial ammonia based on published data from human studies. The brain removes ammonia from arterial blood in a concentration-dependent fashion. Ammonia that is released from the gut to portal blood is mainly from metabolism of glutamine in the enterocytes using this as a source of energy. Ammonia produced by bacterial metabolism of urea and proteins only partially reach portal blood and is likely recycled into bacterial proteins. In general, the liver efficiently removes ammonia from arterial or portal blood in proportion to the delivered concentration. As a result,– and in some contrast to conventional wisdom–, the hepato-splanchnic region only contributes marginally to arterial ammonia; even during a simulated upper GI bleed. The only exception is acute liver failure where hepatocyte necrosis allows large quantities of portal ammonia to pass. The kidneys release ammonia from glutamine metabolism into systemic blood. The renal ammonia release increases during a simulated upper GI bleed or hypokalemia where it becomes a major source of elevated arterial ammonia. In the resting state, muscles remove ammonia in a concentration-dependent manner and muscles are the primary ammonia lowering organ in most situations with elevated arterial ammonia. During strenuous exercise, muscles produce large amounts of ammonia into systemic blood. Thus, the complete pattern of ammonia metabolism is very dynamic and illustrates the difficulties in designing ammonia lowering therapies.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ott, Peter","Eriksen, Peter Lykke","Kjærgaard, Kristoffer","Sørensen, Michael","Thomsen, Karen Louise","Vilstrup, Hendrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-795717"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ott, Peter"],"keyword":["Ammonia metabolism","Hepatic Encephalopathy","Liver Cirrhosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"down the road towards hepatic encephalopathy ii the elusive ammonia what determines the arterial concentration","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11011-024-01435-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-795717","identifier":[{"id":"85211214358","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39621139","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11611965","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-1b45b777-7c4b-4e05-b183-be03b644959e"],"keyword":["Ammonia concentration","Ammonia metabolism","Hepatic encephalopathy","Liver cirrhosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A133F744CCB6D88C35CC39B0E329ABA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11011-024-01435-3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hepatology and Gastroenterology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"ottpau","last":"Ott","locid":"60cc04a0-da79-417d-a8d9-c0b200b04caf","name":"Ott, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Lykke","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"02b5f3f7-8692-403b-9a17-1dc588d638e7","name":"Eriksen, Peter Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-1115-8308","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristoffer","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"35ec4dba-1425-425c-9860-460c3989eba7","name":"Kjærgaard, Kristoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-6440-2784","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"52635821-2c0d-418e-848d-e3e1f1175e12","name":"Sørensen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-8750-4329","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen Louise","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"32baa31f-0b93-4c6d-af7e-0da0519f574f","name":"Thomsen, Karen Louise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hendrik","key":"vilstruppau","last":"Vilstrup","locid":"9e1905f3-3094-4aea-bbde-7178733bf6cb","name":"Vilstrup, Hendrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39621139"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11011-024-01435-3","issn":["08857490","15737365"],"issn_org":["08857490"],"issue":"1","journal":"Metabolic Brain Disease","paperid":"48","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Metabolic Brain Disease","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211214358"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1b45b777-7c4b-4e05-b183-be03b644959e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Down the road towards hepatic encephalopathy II. The elusive ammonia– what determines the arterial concentration?","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-795717","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Pediatric obesity is associated with multi-organ inflammation and an increased risk of cardiometabolic disease. To identify novel biomarkers of early-onset obesity-related cardiometabolic risk, we performed targeted proteomics, analyzing 149 proteins related to inflammation and cardiovascular disease in a cross-sectional sample of 2,377 children and adolescents with overweight/obesity and 1,647 with normal weight. In addition, we analyzed 64 circulating inflammation-related proteins in 184 children and adolescents, who participated in a 1-year family-based obesity management program. We identified a three plasma protein panel (CDCP1, FGF21 and HAOX1) that improved prediction of hepatic steatosis, compared with the predictive value of liver enzymes alone. In the prospective trial, we found that the non-pharmacological intervention induced a decline in circulating inflammatory cytokine levels, some of which were linked to improvements in cardiometabolic phenotypes. Our results may suggest that circulating proteomic signatures may mediate the associations between pediatric obesity and cardiometabolic risk.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Stinson, Sara Elizabeth","Huang, Yun","Thielemann, Roman","Stankevic, Evelina","Lund, Morten Asp Vonsild","Holm, Louise Aas","Fonvig, Cilius Esmann","Juel, Helene Bæk","Borisevich, Dmitrii","Thiele, Maja","Krag, Aleksander","Ängquist, Lars","Sørensen, Thorkild I A","Pedersen, Oluf","Christiansen, Michael","Holm, Jens-Christian","Hansen, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-820530"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of modifiable plasma protein markers of cardiometabolic risk in children and adolescents with obesity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.02.25.25322850","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-820530","ids":["ku-fe65fa88-5e3f-4c54-8968-10197f4df0da"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-72EA9FBD67452B883667C5039BA9E036"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/452218117/Identification_of_modifiable_plasma.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.02.25.25322850","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Hansen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Holbæk"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capit