 Birth - Qualitative Interviews on Motivation and Attitudes","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-823268","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: No validated epilepsy-specific questionnaire exists to measure healthrelated quality of life (HRQOL) for children and adolescents with epilepsy in Denmark. This study aimed to translate and validate the Danish version of the Quality of Life in Childhood Epilepsy (QOLCE) questionnaire and explore associations between HRQOL domains, psychiatric comorbidities, and the number of antiseizure medications (ASMs). Material and methods: Data were collected from 104 children and adolescents with epilepsy from two Danish pediatric departments. Reliability was evaluated using using McDonald's omega coefficient Ω for internal consistency. Criterion validity was examined via Spearman's correlation coefficient (rho) between QOLCE and SDQ subscales. Test-retest reliability was assessed using the intraclass correlation coefficient (ICC). Univariable linear regression analyses explored associations between QOLCE scores, psychiatric comorbidities, and ASMs. Results: The QOLCE-D demonstrated sufficient reliability and validity, making it applicable in Denmark. Internal consistency reliability was high with McDonald's omega coefficient from 0.79 to 0.94, with the highest coeffiecients in the emotional and cognition domains. QOLCE subscales showed moderate to strong correlations (rho = 0.5–0.7) in cognitive and emotional domains, while correlations in other domains were moderate or weaker. Criterion validity was supported by correlations of rho < -0.35 between SDQ and QOLCE-D subscales. Test-retest reliability was sufficient, with ICC values ranging from 0.71 to 0.91. Psychiatric comorbidities significantly affected all QOLCE domains, whereas the number of ASMs showed no significant impact. Conclusion: The Danish version of the QOLCE-76 is a reliable and valid tool for assessing HRQOL in children and adolescents with epilepsy in Denmark.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Brix, Ninna","Chaaban, Nadia","Østergaard, Michelle","Skals, Regitze Gyldenholm","Evald, Jane","Torp Sørensen, Louise Maria","Vium, Emil Stiil","Busch, Andreas","Hansen, Jonas Kjeldbjerg","Boxill, Martin Faber","Handrup, Mette Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-826535"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Brix, Ninna"],"keyword":["Childhood epilepsy","Quality of Life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"verification of the reliability and validity of a danish version of the quality of life in childhood epilepsy questionnaire qolce d","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.yebeh.2025.110564","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-826535","identifier":[{"id":"40694978","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105011197053","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d858e964-7673-455a-aecc-fdbdd5255b81"],"keyword":["Childhood epilepsy","Quality of life","Quality of life in childhood epilepsy questionnaire"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7B719F387B6E3281E8A438533931DBC7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.yebeh.2025.110564","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ninna","key":"brixpau","last":"Brix","name":"Brix, Ninna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia","key":"chaabanpau","last":"Chaaban","name":"Chaaban, Nadia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","name":"Østergaard, Michelle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Regitze Gyldenholm","key":"skalspau","last":"Skals","name":"Skals, Regitze Gyldenholm","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"evaldpau","last":"Evald","name":"Evald, Jane","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Maria","key":"torpsørensenpau","last":"Torp Sørensen","name":"Torp Sørensen, Louise Maria","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Stiil","key":"viumpau","last":"Vium","name":"Vium, Emil Stiil","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"buschpau","last":"Busch","name":"Busch, Andreas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Kjeldbjerg","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Jonas Kjeldbjerg","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"boxillpau","last":"Boxill","locid":"48bc2e68-75f2-4893-8d33-76a5c1feb620","name":"Boxill, Martin Faber","name_org":"Boxill, Martin","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Møller","key":"handruppau","last":"Handrup","locid":"f91b79f9-5ae7-4cff-b02b-02b2e6657c1c","name":"Handrup, Mette Møller","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40694978"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.yebeh.2025.110564","issn":["15255050","15255069"],"issn_org":["15255050"],"journal":"Epilepsy & Behavior","paperid":"110564","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Epilepsy & Behavior","title_org":"Epilepsy and Behavior","volume":"171"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105011197053"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d858e964-7673-455a-aecc-fdbdd5255b81"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Verification of the reliability and validity of a Danish version of the quality of life in childhood epilepsy questionnaire (QOLCE-D)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-826535","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"A concern with ethics and commitments to ethical conduct and standards has increasingly been raised within archaeology, recently also concerning aDNA data. We suggest that codes, whether for working with ancient DNA or other archaeological practices, need to be multi-faceted, or layered, to reflect the different situational contexts of research. We further argue for a more reflexive text addressing \"issues of attention\"or \"concerns.\"We address a number of concerns that should be considered and balanced against each other in the research process. They include respect, rights, appropriation, access, and collaboration.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sørensen, Marie Louise Stig","Hofmann, Daniela","Kristiansen, Kristian","Demeter, Fabrice","Nielsen, Rasmus","Willerslev, Eske"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-829783"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["France","Norway","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Paris-Cité University","University of Bergen","University of California at Berkeley","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Ethical concerns","aDNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a framework for archaeological involvement with human genetic data for european prehistory","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/opar-2025-0053","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-829783","identifier":[{"id":"105012130544","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-becbfdf6-5d09-49fa-b424-3f086bbef32e"],"keyword":["aDNA","ethical concerns","multi-faceted","research contexts"],"lang":"English","lev