cid":"d7f313ee-f9ca-4dbc-9628-fa4339ef9c01","name":"Petersen, Jens Jakob Herrche","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Jette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christina Louise","key":"lindhardtpedh","last":"Lindhardt","name":"Lindhardt, Christina Louise","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"holgersenpedh","last":"Holgersen","name":"Holgersen, Mie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788702436785"],"isbn":["9788702411393"],"pages":"83-100","place":"København","publisher":"Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Sygepleje til børn og unger"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9440b880-9824-488e-87d6-082cc928f349"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sygepleje til unge","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-831285","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients with hard-to-treat or rare cancers and those not responding to standard-of-care (SoC) treatment have unmet needs. Limited access to novel drugs is an increasing additional challenge. In 2003, the Danish government adopted a Health Act to ensure that treatment of patients with life-threatening disease could be reevaluated by independent experts. The Danish Health Authority (DHA) set up an Expert Advisory Panel to provide advice on possibilities for further treatment of patients, including treatment not approved nationally. A few years later, clinical units were established that could offer unestablished treatment to patients by referral from the Panel. The treatment was first reimbursed by the Government and later by regional authorities. Materials and methods: We present the structure, workflow, and impact of the Health Act for 21 years for patients with cancer. Annual reports from the DHA were the primary data source. Results: 11 034 cases from 9603 cancer patients were evaluated by the Panel from 2003 to 2023, representing a median of 372 unique cases yearly. In 53%, the Panel advised on further treatment in Denmark, and of these, 56% were recommended nationally nonapproved treatment, 21% SoC treatment or workup, and 19% clinical trial participation. In 4.5% of cases, advice was given on treatment abroad. A significant decline in admissions to the Panel from a peak of 1167 patients in 2008 to 3-400 yearly from 2012 to 2017 followed the conversion of nonapproved treatments to SoC practice. A shift in drug reimbursement, independent of Panel advise, reduced the clinical impact and explained the further decline observed in admissions lately to only 51 patients in 2023. Conclusions: This unique national scheme provided early access to treatment for patients with no further SoC options and facilitated the introduction of new cancer treatments, initiation of clinical trials, and establishment of trial units in the country. The scheme may be adapted to other countries with a public healthcare system. Results of the current report indicate that impact is dependent on delivering clinical units and reimbursement associated with the recommended treatment.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ladekarl, Morten","Mørk, Mette Louise","Albertsen, Emma Skotte","Nielsen, Dorte","Lassen, Ulrik","Mau-Sørensen, Morten","Nielsen, Claus Malta","Jakobsen, Anders","Von Der Maase, Hans"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-813485"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Ladekarl, Morten"],"keyword":["Drug reimbursement","clinical trial units","equal drug access","experimental treatment","regulatory drug approval","second opinion of treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Danish Health Authority"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"twenty one year report from the danish health authority expert advisory panel for review of treatment of 000000000010 000000000000 cancer patients","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/oncolo/oyaf059","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-813485","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12060716","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40338216","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105004781429","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e447fb83-f751-4d9a-b718-61e3b6401b32","ku-94a50243-946a-41d3-8b44-73624abcc923","sdu-f0b48ac6-737e-4c2c-b7eb-fc63f6272551"],"keyword":["clinical trial units","drug reimbursement","equal drug access","experimental treatment","regulatory drug approval","second opinion of treatment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6D1B80245805A7F8C6534EA6A247B4BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/290533136/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/oncolo/oyaf059","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/450655909/oyaf059.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/787080950/Ladekarl_et_al._2025_Twenty-one-year_report_from_the_Danish_Health_Authority.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Clinical Cancer Research Center","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Oncology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Health Authority"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Oncology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"ladekarlmortenpau","last":"Ladekarl","locid":"20d748a1-54df-4c32-88df-754b7f581a98","name":"Ladekarl, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-0182-1228","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Louise","key":"mørkmettelouisepau","last":"Mørk","name":"Mørk, Mette Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma Skotte","key":"albertsenemmaskottepau","last":"Albertsen","name":"Albertsen, Emma Skotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Dorte","key":"nielsendortelisbetpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8bd14092-b1da-4f24-b4db-d31d38f5f1b7","name":"Nielsen, Dorte Lisbet","name_org":"Nielsen, Dorte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Ulrik","key":"lassenulrikpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"b50a79bb-8e67-4ef3-bf2e-fa3f1d614672","name":"Lassen, Ulrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"mausørensenmortenpau","last":"Mau-Sørensen","name":"Mau-Sørensen, Morten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Malta","key":"nielsenclausmaltapau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Claus Malta","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"jakobsenanderspau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"6c772581-e8fe-48bc-a932-1d1c5122c25a","name":"Jakobsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-2110-2615","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","first":"Hans","key":"vondermaasehanspau","last":"von der Maase","name":"von der Maase, Hans","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40338216"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/oncolo/oyaf059","issn":["10837159","1549490X"],"issn_org":["10837159"],"issue":"5","journal":"Oncologist","paperid":"oyaf059","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Oncologist","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004781429"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e447fb83-f751-4d9a-b718-61e3b6401b32","ku-94a50243-946a-41d3-8b44-73624abcc923","sdu-f0b48ac6-737e-4c2c-b7eb-fc63f6272551"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Twenty-one-year report from the Danish Health Authority Expert Advisory Panel for review of treatment of 10 000 cancer patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-813485","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"There is a limited understanding of risk factors and comorbidities in trigeminal neuralgia, a disease characterized by paroxysms of severe unilateral facial pain and a higher incidence in women. We aim to identify temporally associated comorbidities involving trigeminal neuralgia by analyzing nationwide disease trajectories. Using data from 7.2 million unique individuals in the Danish National Patient Register between 1994 and 2018, each individual diagnosed with trigeminal neuralgia was compared with 10,000 matched controls to identify co-occurring diseases. The sequential disease associations were identified in sex-stratified disease trajectories. A Cox-regression analysis investigated whether treatment with carbamazepine or oxcarbazepine, as compared with gabapentin, pregabalin, or lamotrigine, was associated with stroke risk. Finally, we investigated the stroke polygenic risk score and its association with stroke incidence in a subset of genotyped individuals with trigeminal neuralgia. We included 7141 individuals with trigeminal neuralgia (64.2% female, mean age at diagnosis 58.7 years) and identified 18 diseases associated with subsequent trigeminal neuralgia. After diagnosis, trigeminal neuralgia was associated with 9 diseases, including ischemic stroke (relative risk 1.55). Carbamazepine or oxcarbazepine treatment increased the ischemic stroke risk (hazard ratio 1.78; 95% confidence interval 1.47-2.17); however, the polygenic risk of stroke showed no association. In the Danish population, a trigeminal neuralgia diagnosis is temporally associated with 27 diseases revealed in systematic disease trajectories. Trigeminal neuralgia itself and its first-line treatment, but not a stroke polygenic risk score, was associated with an increased risk of ischemic stroke indicating that vascular risk factors should be routinely assessed in individuals with trigeminal neuralgia.","author_count":60,"contributors":["Worm, Jacob","Jørgensen, Isabella Friis","Davídsson, Ólafur Birgir","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Röder, Timo","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Erikstrup, Christian","Bruun, Mie Topholm","Jensen, Bitten Aagaard","Sørensen, Erik","Ullum, Henrik","Björnsdóttir, Gyða","Thorgeirsson, Thorgeir","Stefánsson, Hreinn","Sveinsson, Ólafur Árni","Stefansson, Kari","Schytz, Henrik Winther","Bendtsen, Lars","Brunak, Søren","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Maarbjerg, Stine","Banasik, Karina","Bay, Jacob","Boldsen, Jens Kjærgaard","Brodersen, Thorsten","Brunak, Søren","Burgdorf, Kristoffer","Chalmer, Mona Ameri","Didriksen, Maria","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Dowsett, Joseph","Erikstrup, Christian","Fenstraa, Bjarke","Geller, Frank","Gudbjartsson, Daniel","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Hindhede, Lotte","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Jacobsen, Rikke Louise","Jemec, Gregor","Jensen, Bitten Aagaard","Kaspersen, Kathrine Agergård","Kjerulff, Bertram","Kogelman, Lisette","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Louloudis, Ioannis","Lundgard, Agnete","Mikkelsen, Susan","Mikkelsen, Christina","Nissen, Ioanna","Nyegaard, Mette","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Henriksen, Alexander Pil","Rohde, Palle Duun","Rostgaard, Klaus","Schwinn, Michael","Stefansson, Kari","Stefánsson, Hreinn","Sørensen, Erik","Porsteinsdóttir, Unnur","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Brun, Mie Topholm","Ullum, Henrik","Werge, Thomas","Westergaard, David"],"cuid":["S04-089.87-803658"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["DBDS Genomic Consortium","Danish Blood Donor Study Genomic Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Maarbjerg, Stine"],"country":["Iceland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Landspitali University Hospital","The National University Hospital of Iceland","University of Iceland","deCODE Genetics"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Antiseizure medication","Carbamazepine therapeutic use","Cardiovascular disease","Cohort study","Comorbidity","Denmark epidemiology","Epidemiology","Facial Pain","Female","Humans","Incidence","Ischemic stroke","Male","Middle Aged","Neuropathic pain","Oxcarbazepine therapeutic use","Registries","Risk Factors","Risk factor","Stroke epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trigeminal neuralgia and its comorbidities a nationwide disease trajectory study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85206841828","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["J. Worm received research support from Trigeminus Foreningen. I.F. J\\u00F8rgensen reported receiving an institutional grant (NNF14CC0001) for this study from Novo Nordisk Foundation. G. Bj\\u00F6rnsdottir, T. Thorgeirsson, H. Stefansson, and K. Stefansson are also employees of Amgen Inc. S. Brunak reported receiving an institutional grant (NNF14CC0001) for this study from Novo Nordisk Foundation. The remaining authors have no conflicts of interest to declare. Acknowledgements The authors thank the Danish blood donors for their valuable participation in DBDS and deCODE Genetics, Iceland for genotyping the DBDS and CHB cohorts. This study was supported in part by grant agreement NNF14CC0001 from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (Dr J\\u00F8rgensen, Prof. Brunak). The authors also thank the patient society Trigeminus Foreningen for their financial support (Worm)."],"id":"S04-089.87-803658","identifier":[{"id":"39365662","type