{"abstract":"This essay juxtaposes the particularity of archaeological traces against the grand narratives manufactured under the banner of the so-called Third Science Revolution. As the latter has come to dominate large parts of archaeological discourse in recent decades, I offer a reading of Walter Benjamin’s trope of the ‘ragpicker’ as a critique of the perceived need in current archaeology for a return of the grand narrative after its problematization during postmodernity. I suggest that the general empirical condition of archaeology, with textile research as an exemplary point of reference, provides an impetus for questioning the current gravitation towards generalizations and the narrative normativity of the macro-perspective. Brushing the grand narrative against the grain is not merely achieved by replacing outdated unilinear master narratives with updated and empirically expanded or scientifically ‘corrected’ interpretations along the same narrative discourse. Rather, writing against the dominant narrative only becomes possible by recognizing archaeology as a perspective from which to attend more carefully — and sensibly — to the epistemology and aesthetics nested in heterogeneous, messy, and erratic fragments, or, in Benjamin’s terms, by doing justice to ‘the rags, the refuse’.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Tim Flohr"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765029"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Faculty of Humanities","Textile Archaeology"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ragpickers critiquing the third science revolution with walter benjamin","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1484/M.NAA-EB.5.141751","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-765029","ids":["ku-6515b746-bdf0-4083-a8d9-d91392639ad4"],"keyword":["Aesthetics","Faculty of Humanities","Grand narrative","Rags and refuse","Textile archaeology","Third Science Revolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0C1C465969B43FC375F9F81765970EFC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1484/M.NAA-EB.5.141751","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/407598344/S_rensen_2024_Ragpickers.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tim Flohr","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"89cb27fb-ea96-4323-a9fd-e3e07ddae445","name":"Sørensen, Tim Flohr","orcid":"0000-0003-2473-6963","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulla","key":"manneringpedh","last":"Mannering","name":"Mannering, Ulla","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marie-Louise","key":"noschpedh","last":"Nosch","name":"Nosch, Marie-Louise","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"drewsenpedh","last":"Drewsen","name":"Drewsen, Anne","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1484/m.naa-eb.5.141751","eisbn":["9782503612782"],"isbn":["9782503612775"],"pages":"11-23","publisher":"Brepols Publishers","series":"New Approaches in Archaeology","status":"p","subtitle":"Collected Essays in Honour of Eva Andersson Strand","title":"The Common Thread"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6515b746-bdf0-4083-a8d9-d91392639ad4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ragpickers : Critiquing the Third Science Revolution with Walter Benjamin","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765029","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Prostate cancer (PCa) is the most commonly diagnosed cancer in males. Early PCa usually shows no clinical symptoms and its primary diagnosis is currently guided by liquid-biopsy testing of serum prostate-specific antigen (PSA). This testing suffers from high false-positive and false-negative rates. Identifying new biomarkers for precise liquid-biopsy detection of PCa is, thus, an acute clinical request. Here, by using an advanced dual-functional aptamer assay, we quantified the extent of glycosylation of PSA circulating in cancer patients’ serum, linked it to cancer-related breakage of PSA complexes with serum-circulating proteins, and proved its facility for stratification of primary and metastatic PCa. PSA’s “Glycan Score” 100% accurately informed about PCa status in a 30-patient cohort, while serum PSA’s concentration correctly classified only 53% of PCa patients and did not inform about their PCa status. The Glycan Score liquid-biopsy test thus has a huge potential for accurate diagnosis and staging of PCa, enabling mass-screening program progress and advanced PCa treatment monitoring.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Díaz-Fernández, Ana","Jochumsen, Mads Ryø","Christensen, Nana Louise","Sørensen, Karina Dalsgaard","Bouchelouche, Kirsten","Borre, Michael","Holm Vendelbo, Mikkel","Ferapontova, Elena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-773247"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ferapontova, Elena"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liquid biopsy glycan score biomarker accurately indicates and stratifies primary and metastatic prostate cancers","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85209234537","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-773247","identifier":[{"id":"39535906","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85209234537","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a4a85cf0-f59e-43c3-8a4c-ae7af79f0945"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A3D3DC8982911C0B796EC1B66C7E84B5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana","key":"díazfernándezpau","last":"Díaz-Fernández","locid":"3b67bcc8-7139-4e7e-9537-dbafbc1bc87b","name":"Díaz-Fernández, Ana","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"ryøjochumsenpau","last":"Ryø Jochumsen","locid":"a37a78df-6321-4fa5-b7c6-bffff0aa5a00","name":"Jochumsen, Mads Ryø","name_org":"Ryø Jochumsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-7676-2322","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nana Louise","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"796a6fa5-29d9-40b3-b549-0610eb49705c","name":"Christensen, Nana Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-9936-1636","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karina","key":"dalsgaardsørensenpau","last":"Dalsgaard Sørensen","locid":"41846f4d-63e9-4498-ac72-0a788c36e789","name":"Sørensen, Karina Dalsgaard","name_org":"Dalsgaard Sørensen, Karina","orcid":"0000-0002-4902-5490","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirsten","key":"bouchelouchepau","last":"Bouchelouche","locid":"f253980f-a953-448a-bdfb-2a0fcfe82101","name":"Bouchelouche, Kirsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"borrepau","last":"Borre","locid":"f0a95cf0-1ff2-4308-991f-749123c14ba5","name":"Borre, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"holmvendelbopau","last":"Holm Vendelbo","name":"Holm Vendelbo, Mikkel","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elena E.","key":"ferapontovapau","last":"Ferapontova","locid":"fb776e85-d3fe-451d-ba01-40d092a0e54c","name":"Ferapontova, Elena","name_org":"Ferapontova, Elena E.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39535906"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.analchem.4c04316","issn":["00032700","15204782"],"issn_org":["00032700"],"issue":"47","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","pages":"18815-18823","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Analytical Chemistry","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209234537"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a4a85cf0-f59e-43c3-8a4c-ae7af79f0945"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Liquid-Biopsy Glycan Score Biomarker Accurately Indicates and Stratifies Primary and Metastatic Prostate Cancers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-773247","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: Despite advances in the medical treatment of Crohn's disease (CD), many patients will still need bowel resections and face the subsequent risk of recurrence and re-resection. We describe contemporary re-resection rates and identify disease-modifying factors and risk factors for re-resection. METHODS: We conducted a retrospective, population-based, individual patient data cohort study covering 47.4% of the Danish population, including all CD patients who underwent a primary resection between 2010 and 2020. RESULTS: Among 631 primary resected patients, 24.5% underwent a second resection, and 5.3% a third. Re-resection rates after one, five, and 10 years were 12.6%, 22.4%, and 32.2%, respectively. Reasons for additional resections were mainly disease activity (57%) and stoma reversal (40%). Disease activity-driven re-resection rates after one, five, and 10 years were 3.6%, 10.1%, and 14.1%, respectively. Most stoma reversals occurred within one year (80%). The median time to recurrence was 11.0 months. Biologics started within one year of the first resection revealed protective effect against re-resection for stenotic and penetrating phenotypes. Prophylactic biologic therapy at primary ileocecal resection reduced disease recurrence and re-resection risk (HR 0.58, 95% CI (0.34-0.99), p=0.047). Risk factors for re-resection were location of resected bowel segments at the primary resection, disease location, disease behavior, smoking, and perianal disease. CONCLUSION: Re-resection rates, categorized by disease activity, are lower than those reported in other studies and are closely associated with disease phenotype and localization. Biological therapy may be disease-modifying for certain subgroups when initiated within one year of resection.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Poulsen, Anja","Rasmussen, Julie","Wewer, Mads Damsgaard","Hansen, Esben Holm","Nordestgaard, Rie Louise Møller","Jespersen, Hans Søe Riis","Christiansen, Dagmar","Surnacheva, Elena","Lin, Viviane Annabelle","Aydemir, Nurcan","Verlo, Kari Anne","Pachler, Frederik Rønne","Ovesen, Pernille Dige","Fuglsang, Kristian Asp","Brandt, Christopher Filtenborg","Sørensen, Lars Tue","Krarup, Peter-Martin","Gögenur, Ismail","Burisch, Johan","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777045"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"re resection rates and disease recurrence in crohn s disease a population based study using individual level patient data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-777045","identifier":[{"id":"85206597804","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38727089","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-168b400f-f5ea-4a8e-aae9-0231c0c6bcc7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3CEAF5AE281128F1AA3DF0EEAAA57981"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg","Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U",