rd, Cecilie","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"sandmarkpau","last":"Sandmark","name":"Sandmark, Marie","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jana","key":"reinhartpau","last":"Reinhart","name":"Reinhart, Jana","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7 8 9 10 11 12","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph U.","key":"correllpau","last":"Correll","name":"Correll, Christoph U.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39547246"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s2215-0366(24)00314-6","issn":["22150366","22150374"],"issn_org":["22150366"],"issue":"12","journal":"The Lancet Psychiatry","pages":"975-989","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Psychiatry","title_org":"The lancet. Psychiatry","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209236767"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-af5d3c4e-c379-4665-b734-565543ff8932","sdu-8e9ad8ec-fc71-4a9b-b667-84bf69884dcf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prevalence, correlates, tolerability-related outcomes, and efficacy-related outcomes of antipsychotic polypharmacy : a systematic review and meta-analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.08-767774","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Weight loss is reported with oral roflumilast, which is approved for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Recently, the drug has shown efficacy in psoriasis, a disease strongly linked to overweight/obesity. Objective: To describe the effects of oral roflumilast on body weight and cardio-metabolic parameters in patients with psoriasis. Methods: Posthoc analyses from the PSORRO study, where patients with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis were randomized 1:1 to oral roflumilast 500 μg once-daily or placebo for 12 weeks, followed by active, open-label treatment through week 24 in both groups. Changes in body weight, blood pressure, gastrointestinal symptoms, and laboratory tests were registered. No lifestyle or dietary interventions were applied. Results: Forty-six patients were randomized. Baseline characteristics across groups were comparable; mean weight was 103.6 kg. In patients receiving roflumilast, median weight change was −2.6% and −4% at week 12 and 24, respectively. Corresponding numbers were 0.0% and 1.3% in patients initially allocated to placebo. Reduced appetite was more frequent with active therapy. No changes in blood pressure or laboratory tests were observed. Limitations: Posthoc analyses and low numbers. Conclusion: Oral roflumilast induced weight loss and reduced appetite, which support the growing evidence of roflumilast as an attractive treatment alternative for patients with psoriasis.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gyldenløve, Mette","Sørensen, Jennifer Astrup","Fage, Simon","Meteran, Howraman","Skov, Lone","Zachariae, Claus","Knop, Filip Krag","Nielsen, Mia Louise","Egeberg, Alexander"],"cuid":["S02-099.50-741663"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gyldenløve, Mette"],"keyword":["Appetite","COPD","Cardiometabolic","Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease","Metabolism","PDE4 inhibitor","PSORRO","Phosphodiesterase 4","Psoriasis","RCT","Randomized Controlled Trial","Roflumilast","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of oral roflumilast therapy on body weight and cardiometabolic parameters in patients with psoriasis results from a randomized controlled trial psorro","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaad.2024.02.036","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.50-741663","identifier":[{"id":"38431099","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85189094417","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-083a95a7-6570-4d0d-84da-588e1fab32a6","ku-d388e226-9e88-4e3f-971f-f5c594e7bcb2"],"keyword":["COPD","PDE4-inhibitor","PSORRO","RCT","appetite","cardiometabolic","chronic obstructive pulmonary disease","metabolism","phosphodiesterase-4","psoriasis","randomized controlled trial","roflumilast","weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3E983BAC1EA2067CD61969F66D8A6B01"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaad.2024.02.036","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/395382715/1_s2.0_S0190962224004262_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty 