{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Childhood-onset obesity poses significant health risks, including early-onset type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and reduced quality of life. Hospital-based non-pharmacological obesity care can reduce childhood obesity, but 25% of children do not respond. Therefore, this study investigates the effect of the glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist, semaglutide, as an add-on to hospital-based obesity care in youth who still have obesity following hospital-based obesity care as children. Furthermore, biomedical and psychosocial factors linked to treatment response will be investigated, alongside an exercise-based strategy to prevent weight regain and maintain a healthy body composition after semaglutide treatment. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: This is an investigator-initiated, randomised, placebo-controlled, double-blind trial. We will enrol expectedly 180-270 young adults aged 18-28 years based on their previous response to a paediatric obesity management programme and their current body mass index (BMI). Participants are categorised into four groups: low treatment response (BMI SD score (SDS) reduction <0.10; BMI ≥30 kg/m2); medium treatment response (BMI SDS reduction >0.25; BMI ≥30 kg/m2); high treatment response (BMI SDS reduction >0.50; BMI <30 kg/m2) and a population-based reference group with normal weight development in childhood. Participants with BMI ≥30 kg/m2 are randomised 2:1 to subcutaneous injections of semaglutide 2.4 mg/week or placebo as an add-on to hospital-based obesity care for 68 weeks. The primary outcome is the change in BMI from randomisation to the end of treatment with semaglutide compared with placebo. Secondary endpoints are changes in weight and body composition. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The trial has been approved by the Danish Medicines Agency and the Ethical Committee of the Capital Region of Denmark (H-20039422). The trial will be conducted in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki and follow the guidelines for Good Clinical Practice. Results will be presented at international scientific conferences and published in peer-reviewed scientific journals. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: EudraCT 2019-002274-31.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Byberg, Sarah","Holt, Joachim","Sandsdal, Rasmus Michael","Holm, Louise Aas","Madsen, Lærke Bruun","Christensen, Bodil Just","Jensen, Simon Birk Kjær","Hansen, Torben","Holm, Jens-Christian","Torekov, Signe Sørensen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-779634"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Body Mass Index","Obesity","Randomized Controlled Trial"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protocol for a randomised double blinded controlled trial of youth with childhood onset obesity treated with semaglutide 000000000002 000000000004 mg week the resettle trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-082446","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-779634","identifier":[{"id":"39551589","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11574404","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85209955425","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ff1f9865-6da0-473d-869b-e37bd2c90cdb"],"keyword":["Body Mass Index","Obesity","Randomized Controlled Trial"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DA2CCBA1B9A160758D3FA223A98A6B73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/413555403/Protocol_for_a_randomised.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-082446","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Torekov Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Holbæk"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"bybergsarahpau","last":"Byberg","locid":"f06174c4-506c-46c7-8805-97a0900e20da","name":"Byberg, Sarah","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joachim","key":"holtjoachimpau","last":"Holt","locid":"ae8bb934-cd85-4557-a342-dd5ca6922444","name":"Holt, Joachim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus Michael","key":"sandsdalrasmusmichaelpau","last":"Sandsdal","locid":"e1a6c85c-8801-466b-971b-65a2303b0527","name":"Sandsdal, Rasmus Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-0590-6285","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Louise Aas","key":"holmlouiseaaspau","last":"Holm","locid":"3c8db4dd-1b63-4f0c-8b8b-606ecb645ef9","name":"Holm, Louise Aas","orcid":"0000-0002-5439-5429","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lærke Bruun","key":"madsenlærkebruunpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"bee51c87-f784-4e8a-a154-a8fcda8229c4","name":"Madsen, Lærke Bruun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bodil Just","key":"christensenbodiljustpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"610aa898-48ea-4ebe-86ff-4664cf197551","name":"Christensen, Bodil Just","orcid":"0000-0003-4529-8253","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Simon Birk Kjær","key":"jensensimonbirkkjærpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"9edd5734-2279-4744-b174-f70c08e9ad82","name":"Jensen, Simon Birk Kjær","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Torben","key":"hansentorbenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jens Christian","key":"holmjenschristianpau","last":"Holm","locid":"d61af840-e87e-4a2e-8be2-b481959ef6c9","name":"Holm, Jens-Christian","name_org":"Holm, Jens Christian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe","key":"torekovsignesørensenpau","last":"Torekov","locid":"c1d71a61-ee09-4c29-ae48-7520707a73be","name":"Torekov, Signe Sørensen","name_org":"Torekov, Signe","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-0252","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39551589"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2023-082446","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"11","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e082446","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209955425"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ff1f9865-6da0-473d-869b-e37bd2c90cdb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Protocol for a randomised, double-blinded, controlled trial of youth with childhood-onset obesity treated with semaglutide 2.4 mg/week : the RESETTLE trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779634","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Daylight provides us with an understanding of time and space, specifying where we are in the world, every day. We delight in experiencing the changeability of daylight – from morning to evening perceiving how light and darkness affect the spaces surrounding us. This paper highlights daylight as one of the central elements in architecture, by emphasising its qualitative potentials: creating healthy, aesthetic, and poetic spaces. The setting for this study is a 1:1 pavilion, Poetic Daylight, built for the UIA Conference in Copenhagen. Presenting studies of scale models 1:10 and studies of the built 1:1 pavilion, this study lays out the possibilities and potentials in the use of scale models when designing spaces, with a focus on the qualitative appearances of daylight. Bearing the distinction laid out by Vitruvius in mind, i.e. firmitas, utilitas and venustas, the pavilion focuses on venustas (beauty or delight) in order to form spaces where the atmosphere and the beauty of daylight can be perceived and experienced. The Vitruvian concept of beauty, together with J. J. Gibson's definition of the perception of an environment, constitutes the theoretical framework. The analysis and the description of the three different spaces in the pavilion relates to the theory on defining light as presented by Anders Liljefors in his compendium: \"Seende och Ljusstrålning\" where he describes seven variables of light and Sophus Frandsen's definition of the four different kinds of shadows. The methodology involves the development of models, observations, and representations. This study shows that using 1:10 scale models in the design process to include qualitative aspects of daylight is practicable and effective, producing tangible and transferable knowledge that will influence the experience and perception of daylight in the built 1:1 pavilion, Poetic Daylight.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Grønlund, Louise","Mathiasen, Nanet","Sørensen, Pernille","Frandsen, Anne Kathrine"],"cuid":["S02-092.43-755920"],"event":{"end":"2023-12-06","place":"Stockholm, se","start":"2023-12-04","title":"9th Light Symposium 2023: Architecture Lighting Environments - Space With(Out) Light, LS 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Daylight","Daylight Model","Daylight and architecture","Phenomenology"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"poetic daylight a pavilion for the perception of daylight","src":["aau","arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1755-1315/1320/1/012006","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.43-755920","identifier":[{"id":"85190441674","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e32fe733-8dd0-4d34-8a20-53f594f46adb","arkc-0ea0e2fa-278e-4c85-8215-1ec87df3323c"],"keyword":["Daylight","Daylight Model","Daylight and architecture","No","Phenomenology","Poetic Daylight"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78E084518BE88EC8AF6EBFD9540FC9EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/741767431/Gr_nlund_2024_IOP_Conf._Ser._Earth_Environ._Sci._1320_012006.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1755-1315/1320/1/012006","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/83811070/Gr_nlund_2024_IOP_Conf._Ser._Earth_Environ._Sci._1320_012006.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Center for Interior Studies","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Light in Architecture and Design","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Design"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Town, Housing and Property","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Universal Design Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"grønlundpau","last":"Grønlund","locid":"b5bd2523-ca04-4275-9a2f-e81f54f9f017","name":"Grønlund, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"N.","key":"mathiasenpau","last":"Mathiasen","locid":"d4fda523-2337-4b09-869f-b89851643b67","name":"Mathiasen, Nanet","name_org":"Mathiasen, N.","orcid":"0000-0003-3488-306X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Pernille","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A. K.","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","locid":"762e65be-7e39-4f6c-b004-d0672416f25a","name":"Frandsen, Anne Kathrine","name_org":"Frandsen, A. K.","orcid":"0000-0001-5296-6622","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1755-1315/1320/1/012006","issn":["17551307","17551315"],"issn_org":["17551307"],"issue":"1","journal":"IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science","paperid":"012006","publisher":"Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science","volume":"1320"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e32fe733-8dd0-4d34-8a20-53f594f46adb","arkc-0ea0e2fa-278e-4c85-8215-1ec87df3323c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Poetic Daylight : A pavilion for the perception of daylight","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.43-755920","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation (ECPR) for selected refractory out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) is increasingly used. Detailed knowledge of health-related quality of life (HRQoL) and long-term cognitive function is limited. HRQoL and cognitive function were assessed in ECPR-survivors and OHCA-survivors with prehospital return of spontaneous circulation after standard advanced cardiac life support (sACLS). Methods: Fifteen ECPR-survivors and 22 age-matched sACLS-survivors agreed to participate in this follow-up study. Participants were examined with echocardiography, 6-minute walk test, and neuropsychological testing, and answered HRQoL (EQ-5D-5L and Short Form 36 (SF-36)), and mental health questionnaires. Results: Most patients were male (73 % and 82 %) and median age at follow-up was similar between groups (55 years and 60 years). Low flow time was significantly longer for ECPR-survivors (86 min vs. 15 min) and lactate levels were significantly higher (14.1 mmol/l vs. 3.9 mmol/l). No between-group difference was found in physical function nor in cognitive function with scores corresponding to the 23rd worst percentile of the general population. SACLS-survivors had HRQoL on level with the Danish general population while ECPR-survivors scored lower in both EQ-5D-5L (index score 0.73 vs. 0.86, p = 0.03, visual analog scale: 70 vs. 84, p = 0.04) and in multiple SF-36 health domains (role physical, bodily pain, general health, and mental health). Conclusions: Despite substantially longer low flow times with thrice as high lactate levels, ECPR-survivors were similar in cognitive and physical function compared to sACLS-survivors. Nonetheless, ECPR-survivors reported lower HRQoL overall and related to mental health, pain management, and the perception of limitations in physical role.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Gregers, Emilie","Linde, Louise","Kunkel, Joakim Bo","Wiberg, Sebastian","Møller-Sørensen, Peter Hasse","Smerup, Morten","Borregaard, Britt","Schmidt, Henrik","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Hassager, Christian","Søholm, Helle","Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-725196"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gregers, Emilie"],"keyword":["Cognitive function","Extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Health related quality of life","Out of hospital cardiac arrest"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"health related quality of life and cognitive function after out of hospital cardiac arrest a comparison of prehospital return of spontaneous circulation and refractory arrest managed with extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2024.110151","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project was supported by the common foundation of Rigshospitalet and Odense University Hospital (grant number 83-A3759), The Danish Heart Foundation (grant number 2020-9587) and by the Beckett Foundation (grant number 23-2-10125). JK has a research grant from Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF22OC0079649) outside the submitted work. HS has a research grant from Novo Nordisk Foundation outside the submitted work. CH has a research grant from Novo Nordisk Foundation, Lundbeck Foundation and The Danish Heart Foundation outside the submitted work. JEM has a research grant from Novo Nordisk Foundation, Abiomed and The Danish Heart Foundation outside the submitted work. None of the other authors have anything to declare."],"id":"S02-100.00-725196","identifier":[{"id":"38401709","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85186623820","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-71a5af23-a0d6-47d9-b3fa-d422758c2642","sdu-a8d9276a-4e51-48fb-a82e-eadb04776bd8"],"keyword":["Cognitive function","Extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Health-related quality of life","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0F85C62E4BE5B9226D1BA528C7F5DAA4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2024.110151","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/256877555/PIIS0300957224000443.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385695257/1_s2.0_S0300957224000443_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University