roup","status":"p","title":"EBioMedicine","volume":"105"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198025462"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2a5854ac-045c-4f39-8ed2-127af3594028","sdu-1d1040fc-e990-4d29-be1a-de91d2666e51"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The interplay between birth weight and obesity in determining childhood and adolescent cardiometabolic risk","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.70-756228","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The evolution of land flora was an epochal event in the history of planet Earth. The success of plants, and especially flowering plants, in colonizing all but the most hostile environments required multiple mechanisms of adaptation. The mainly polysaccharide-based cell walls of flowering plants, which are indispensable for water transport and structural support, are one of the most important adaptations to life on land. Thus, development of vasculature is regarded as a seminal event in cell wall evolution, but the impact of further refinements and diversification of cell wall compositions and architectures on radiation of flowering plant families is less well understood. We approached this from a glyco-profiling perspective and, using carbohydrate microarrays and monoclonal antibodies, studied the cell walls of 287 plant species selected to represent important evolutionary dichotomies and adaptation to a variety of habitats. The results support the conclusion that radiation of flowering plant families was indeed accompanied by changes in cell wall fine structure and that these changes can obscure earlier evolutionary events. Convergent cell wall adaptations identified by our analyses do not appear to be associated with plants with similar lifestyles but that are taxonomically distantly related. We conclude that cell wall structure is linked to phylogeny more strongly than to habitat or lifestyle and propose that there are many approaches of adaptation to any given ecological niche.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Fangel, Jonatan U.","Sørensen, Klavs Martin","Jacobsen, Niels","Mravec, Jozef","Ahl, Louise Isager","Bakshani, Cassie","Mikkelsen, Maria Dalgaard","Engelsen, Søren Balling","Willats, William","Ulvskov, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-725068"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ulvskov, Peter","Willats, William"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Newcastle University","University of Newcastle"],"keyword":["Adaptation","Adaption","CoMPP","Glyco arrays","Plant cell wall fine structure","Plant cell wall polysaccharides","Plant cell wall types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the legacy of terrestrial plant evolution on cell wall fine structure","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/pce.14785","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-725068","identifier":[{"id":"38173082","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181242296","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a943dae1-6e21-4120-aa8b-e8be3a40de1d","ku-fd9f537e-00c0-4d22-889d-9f7e8e7d1a91"],"keyword":["Adaption","CoMPP","Glyco-arrays","Plant cell wall fine structure","Plant cell wall polysaccharides","Plant cell wall types","adaptation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C848FFEA50CA9B68EE7F181221FCDB4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/384571181/Plant_Cell_Environment_2024_Fangel_The_legacy_of_terrestrial_plant_evolution_on_cell_wall_fine_structure.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/pce.14785","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/354650187/Plant_Cell_Environment_-_2024_-_Fangel_-_The_legacy_of_terrestrial_plant_evolution_on_cell_wall_fine_structure.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Unive