{"abstract":"Midbrain dopaminergic neurons (DANs) are subject to extensive metabotropic regulation, but the repertoire of G protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs) present in these neurons has not been mapped. Here, we isolate DANs from Dat-eGFP mice to generate a GPCR atlas by unbiased qPCR array expression analysis of 377 GPCRs. Combined with data mining of scRNA-seq databases, we identify multiple receptors in DAN subpopulations with 38 of these receptors representing the majority of transcripts. We identify 41 receptors expressed in midbrain DANs but not in non-DAN midbrain cells, including the free fatty acid receptor 4 (FFAR4). Functional expression of FFAR4 is validated by ex vivo Ca2+ imaging, and in vivo experiments support that FFAR4 negatively regulates food and water intake and bodyweight. In addition to providing a critical framework for understanding metabotropic DAN regulation, our data suggest fatty acid sensing by FFAR4 as a mechanism linking high-energy intake to the dopamine-reward pathway.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Christiansen, M.","Burm, Hayley","Schmidt, Jan Hendrik","Skov, Louise J","Andersen, Rita Chan","Bowin, Carl Fredrik","Støier, Jonatan Fullerton","Jensen, Kathrine Louise","Posselt, Leonie P.","Dmytriyeva, Oksana","Sørensen, Andreas Toft","Egerod, Kristoffer Lihme","Holst, Birgitte","Rickhag, Mattias","Schwartz, Thue W.","Gether, Ulrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754584"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet"],"keyword":["CP Metabolism","CP Neuroscience","Dopamine","FFAR4","Fatty acids","Fluorescence activated cell sorting","G protein coupled receptors","GPR120","Heterogeneity","Metabolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an atlas of gpcrs in dopamine neurons identification of the free fatty acid receptor 000000000004 as a regulator of food and water intake","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2024.114509","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754584","identifier":[{"id":"85198346797","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39003735","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7a5b8b0c-1623-4607-a185-ceb6122b7a6d"],"keyword":["CP: Metabolism","CP: Neuroscience","Dat-eGFP mice","FFAR4","G protein-coupled receptors","array analysis","dopamine","fatty acids","fluorescence-activated cell sorting","gpr120","heterogeneity","metabolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D2EB8CD093A55870295A20D7E3C3E532"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/399065222/1_s2.0_S2211124724008386_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2024.114509","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Neuropharm and Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"M.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"da67432e-c0c5-4dd1-933f-89321fa8f41e","name":"Christiansen, M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hayley B.","key":"burmpau","last":"Burm","locid":"133ac173-a703-4270-9462-01a0cf26b069","name":"Burm, Hayley","name_org":"Burm, Hayley B.","orcid":"0000-0001-7892-3663","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan H.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"8cfb18c6-950d-43d2-8fd1-4b9c999ca9a7","name":"Schmidt, Jan Hendrik","name_org":"Schmidt, Jan H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise J.","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"b1d76de4-cd32-4d36-85f5-12d31d701fb1","name":"Skov, Louise J","name_org":"Skov, Louise J.","orcid":"0000-0003-2977-9970","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rita C.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"4141e2a0-0d66-432f-ac68-edeb55a3ea78","name":"Andersen, Rita Chan","name_org":"Andersen, Rita C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Carl Fredrik","key":"bowinpau","last":"Bowin","locid":"bd399457-bbae-448a-aa4f-0576642fa665","name":"Bowin, Carl Fredrik","orcid":"0000-0001-9090-9493","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonatan F.","key":"støierpau","last":"Støier","locid":"8d6dc76f-03c9-46d0-b5b1-4639067d06e9","name":"Støier, Jonatan Fullerton","name_org":"Støier, Jonatan F.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kathrine L.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d16cc237-89d6-490c-9519-6265b3ddb48b","name":"Jensen, Kathrine Louise","name_org":"Jensen, Kathrine L.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Leonie P.","key":"posseltpau","last":"Posselt","locid":"a2acb443-51f9-4761-a2c7-b097c92dda8a","name":"Posselt, Leonie P.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Oksana","key":"dmytriyevapau","last":"Dmytriyeva","name":"Dmytriyeva, Oksana","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas T.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ac0f6a72-7014-4f0c-8c02-6c9a7721ccbd","name":"Sørensen, Andreas Toft","name_org":"Sørensen, Andreas T.","orcid":"0000-0001-5887-9247","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristoffer L.","key":"egerodpau","last":"Egerod","locid":"9339170e-b668-47c5-84dd-50cb68db17bb","name":"Egerod, Kristoffer Lihme","name_org":"Egerod, Kristoffer L.","orcid":"0000-0003-2781-1594","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birgitte","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"be07b398-88db-4db5-9851-89125f68edf4","name":"Holst, Birgitte","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Mattias","key":"rickhagpau","last":"Rickhag","name":"Rickhag, Mattias","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thue W.","key":"schwartzpau","last":"Schwartz","locid":"c5b7c219-e499-427a-99fa-35fa233e432b","name":"Schwartz, Thue W.","orcid":"0000-0002-0261-6904","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulrik","key":"getherpau","last":"Gether","locid":"9b3eed37-e0b0-412a-b790-48069d4d1e5e","name":"Gether, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0020-3807","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39003735"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.celrep.2024.114509","issn":["22111247"],"issue":"7","journal":"Cell Reports","paperid":"114509","status":"p","title":"Cell Reports","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198346797"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7a5b8b0c-1623-4607-a185-ceb6122b7a6d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An atlas of GPCRs in dopamine neurons : Identification of the free fatty acid receptor 4 as a regulator of food and water intake","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754584","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Shared decision making (SDM) is a fundamental right for patients, however implementation is lacking. Healthcare professionals’ (HCPs) perception of own abilities to adopt SDM are crucial for the implementation of SDM. IcanSDM 1 2 is developed to measure HCPs’ perception of their abilities to adopt SDM. To our knowledge no other measurements in Danish exist covering this area, why the aim of this study was to adapt the IcanSDM measure for Danish-speaking HCPs and evaluate its psychometric properties. Methods Cultural adaptation and translation based on Beaton et al’s approach was applied. A forward translation by ten people and a backward translation by two people were performed. To assess comprehensibility, cognitive interviews were conducted with 24 HCPs. Eighty HCPs who were trained in SDM for either one hour (n=65) or one day (n=15) participated in the psychometric evaluation. The evaluation concerned acceptance, item characteristics, skewness, item difficulties, corrected item-total, inter-item correlations, factorial structure, internal consistency, and responsiveness. Results The forward and backward translation revealed few discrepancies, and participants understood the items well. The psychometric evaluation showed a high completion rate and acceptable item difficulties and discrimination values. Both the factor analysis and the internal consistency showed a 2-factor structure. It obtained a Cronbach’s alpha coefficient of 0.74. The responsiveness showed improvement, but was not statistically significant. Discussion The IcanSDM_Danish is capable of providing reliable and valid measurement when evaluating constructed knowledge about SDM, and supporting the implementation of SDM training and evaluation of its impact. Conclusion The IcanSDM_Danish is a reliable cross-culturally valid measure with good internal consistency and a 2-factor structure. The IcanSDM_Danish represents a meaningful measure for identifying SDM barriers, monitoring the effect of SDM training, and supporting SDM implementation in clinical practice.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Finderup, Jeanette","Bekker, Hilary L","Albèr, Nadia T","Boel, Susanne","Buur, Louise E","Von Essen, Helle Sørensen","Kristensen, Anne W","Lyng, Kristian Damgaard","Vedelø, Tina W","Rasmussen, Gitte S","Skovlund, Pernille C","Søndergaard, Stine R","Giguère, Anik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762162"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-10","place":"Lausanne, ch","start":"2024-07-07","title":"12th International Shared Decision Making Conference 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Finderup, Jeanette"],"country":["Canada","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Leeds","Université Laval"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measuring healthcare professionals perceptions of their ability to adopt shared decision making translation and psychometric evaluation of the danish version of the icansdm questionnaire","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-762162","ids":["aau-2c1c7701-150f-4c77-87da-dffec99837f9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-BB2AC94FF4B8EF21051452446AEC2B93"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus 