rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Lars","key":"sandbergpau","last":"Sandberg","name":"Sandberg, Lars","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Morten","key":"frödinpau","last":"Frödin","locid":"46e46c92-5048-4269-a7aa-ffa0af4c0e8f","name":"Frödin, Morten","orcid":"0000-0003-3691-9820","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Etienne","key":"moussaypau","last":"Moussay","name":"Moussay, Etienne","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ana","key":"slipicevicpau","last":"Slipicevic","name":"Slipicevic, Ana","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Elisabeth","key":"letellierpau","last":"Letellier","name":"Letellier, Elisabeth","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jérôme","key":"paggettipau","last":"Paggetti","name":"Paggetti, Jérôme","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Claus Storgaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"fecf3302-04f9-4c43-871e-b3e4bc7392ab","name":"Sørensen, Claus Storgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6022-9710","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"helledaypau","last":"Helleday","name":"Helleday, Thomas","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Martin","key":"henrikssonpau","last":"Henriksson","name":"Henriksson, Martin","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Johannes","key":"meiserpau","last":"Meiser","name":"Meiser, Johannes","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37012496"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s42255-023-00771-5","issn":["25225812"],"issue":"4","journal":"Nature Metabolism","pages":"642-659","status":"p","title":"Nature Metabolism","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151482683"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ddac976c-06a7-48e6-b7d2-3ec7da3f5a36"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formate overflow drives toxic folate trapping in MTHFD1 inhibited cancer cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671071","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Insulin resistance is a critical cause of metabolic dysfunctions. Metabolic dysfunction is common in patients with cancer and is associated with higher cancer recurrence rates and reduced overall survival. Yet, insulin resistance is rarely considered in the clinic and thus it is uncertain how frequently this condition occurs in patients with cancer. Methods: To address this knowledge gap, we performed a systematic review and a meta-analysis guided by the Preferred Items for Systematic Review and Meta-Analyses (PRISMA) statement. We included studies assessing insulin resistance in patients with various cancer diagnoses, using the gold-standard hyperinsulinemic-euglycemic clamp method. Studies eligible for inclusion were as follows: (1) included cancer patients older than 18 years of age; (2) included an age-matched control group consisting of individuals without cancer or other types of neoplasms; (3) measured insulin sensitivity using the hyperinsulinemic-euglycemic clamp method. We searched the databases MEDLINE, Embase, and Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials for articles published from database inception through March 2023 with no language restriction, supplemented by backward and forward citation searching. Bias was assessed using funnel plot. Findings: Fifteen studies satisfied the criteria. The mean insulin-stimulated rate of glucose disposal (Rd) was 7.5 mg/kg/min in control subjects (n = 154), and 4.7 mg/kg/min in patients with a cancer diagnosis (n = 187). Thus, the Rd mean difference was -2.61 mg/kg/min [95% confidence interval, -3.04; -2.19], p<.01). Heterogeneity among the included studies was insignificant (p=.24). Interpretation: These findings suggest that patients with a cancer diagnosis are markedly insulin resistant. As metabolic dysfunction in patients with cancer associates with increased recurrence and reduced overall survival, future studies should address if ameliorating insulin resistance in this population can improve these outcomes thereby improving patient care.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Màrmol, Joan M.","Carlsson, Michala","Raun, Steffen Henning","Grand, Mia K","Sorensen, Jonas","Lang Lehrskov, Louise","Richter, Erik A.","Norgaard, Ole","Sylow, Lykke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677895"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cancer","Faculty of Science","Hyperinsulinemic euglycemic clamp","Insulin Resistance","Meta analysis","Metabolic dysfunction","Systematic review"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"insulin resistance in patients with cancer a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/0284186X.2023.2197124","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677895","identifier":[{"id":"85152370982","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37042166","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-33b4cde7-1c3c-478b-b8b0-5b33677c82b2"],"keyword":["Cancer","Faculty of Science","Hyperinsulinemic-euglycemic clamp","Insulin resistance","Meta-analysis","Metabolic dysfunction","Systematic review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C6C1B7AA9B474B134FD753B50489330B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/406128287/Insulin_resistance_in_patients_with_cancer_a_systematic_review_and_meta_analysis.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/0284186X.2023.2197124","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Joan M.","key":"màrmolpau","last":"Màrmol","name":"Màrmol, Joan M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michala","key":"carlssonpau","last":"Carlsson","locid":"d6939479-3649-444c-8618-0869d865170b","name":"Carlsson, Michala","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steffen Henning","key":"raunpau","last":"Raun","locid":"c3f5e98f-b81f-4cde-b7dd-93c2d92dd26d","name":"Raun, Steffen Henning","orcid":"0000-0003-2050-505X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mia K","key":"grandpau","last":"Grand","name":"Grand, Mia K","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Jonas","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"a7f098bb-752d-4fcb-8342-e6410423f33c","name":"Sorensen, Jonas","name_org":"Sørensen, Jonas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Louise","key":"langlehrskovpau","last":"Lang Lehrskov","name":"Lang Lehrskov, Louise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik A.","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","locid":"c9ba60ad-a6b9-439f-bbd2-e6fd31a4e009","name":"Richter, Erik A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6850-3056","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Ole","key":"norgaardpau","last":"Norgaard","name":"Norgaard, Ole","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lykke","key":"sylowpau","last":"Sylow","locid":"f86d592e-fb11-4ec7-a7b4-d63eb53f94c8","name":"Sylow, Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-0905-5932","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37042166"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2023.2197124","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["11001704"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"364-371","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152370982"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-33b4cde7-1c3c-478b-b8b0-5b33677c82b2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Insulin resistance in patients with cancer: a systematic review and meta-analysis","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677895","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Kidney transplant recipients (KTRs) have increased risk of human papillomavirus (HPV)-related cancers, including cervical and anal cancer. In this cross-sectional clinical study, we investigated the prevalence of cervical high-risk HPV (hrHPV) and low-risk (lrHPV), risk factors for cervical hrHPV infection, and the prevalence of cervical and anal hrHPV co-infection in KTRs and immunocompetent controls. Methods: During 2016–2017, we recruited 125 female KTRs and 125 female immunocompetent controls from one dermatology department (KTRs and controls) and five nephrology departments (KTRs) in Denmark. Liquid-based cervical and anal cytology samples were tested for HPV DNA using the INNO-LiPA test and participants answered a questionnaire on lifestyle. Odds ratios (ORs) were estimated using logistic regression, adjusting for age, lifetime sexual partners, smoking, and (in models concerning anal HPV) receptive anal sex. Results: KTRs had higher prevalence of cervical hrHPV than controls (35.5% vs. 18.2; ORadjusted = 2.9, 95% CI, 1.5–5.5). In contrast, the prevalence of lrHPV was similar in KTRs and controls (25.6% vs. 23.1; ORadjusted = 1.2, 95% CI, 0.7‒2.3). KTRs were more likely than controls to have cervical and anal hrHPV co-infection (27.3% vs. 6.6%, ORadjusted = 6.3, 95% CI, 2.7–15.0). Conclusions: Female KTRs had high prevalence of cervical hrHPV, and co-infection with anal and cervical hrHPV was common. Our results underline that KTRs are an important target group for preventive efforts against HPV-related diseases. (Figure presented.).","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ring, Linea Landgrebe","Thomsen, Louise T.","Haedersdal, Merete","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Bonde, Jesper Hansen","Lok, Trine Thorborg","Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-678548"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anus","Cervix","Co infection","Human papillomavirus","Kidney Transplantation","Prevalence"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence of cervical human papillomavirus and the risk of anal co infection in kidney transplant recipients results from a danish clinical study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/tid.14019","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-678548","identifier":[{"id":"36695181","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85147499643","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-835fc5cd-9b05-420d-a8c7-21f82eb277c8"],"keyword":["anus","cervix","co-infection","human papillomavirus","kidney transplantation","prevalence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-18BBE8A4BE81E62BBACD863FE42995FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/tid.14019","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359318868/Transplant_Infectious_Dis_2023_Ring_Prevalence_of_cervical_human_papillomavirus_and_the_risk_of_anal_co_infection_in.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Linea Landgrebe","key":"ringpau","last":"Ring","name":"Ring, Linea Landgrebe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise T.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Louise T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Merete","key":"hædersdalpau","last":"Hædersdal","locid":"fef92f7f-7d21-4a42-903e-24071d35047b","name":"Haedersdal, Merete","name_org":"Hædersdal, Merete","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Søren Schwartz","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper Hansen","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","name":"Bonde, Jesper Hansen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Trine Thorborg","key":"lokpau","last":"Lok","name":"Lok, Trine Thorborg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Helle K.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cff32a53-c07d-466a-9bf3-cc621c1e2cb6","name":"Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","name_org":"Larsen, Helle K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjær, Susanne K.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36695181"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/tid.14019","issn":["13982273","13993062"],"issn_org":["13982273"],"issue":"2","journal":"Transplant Infectious Disease","paperid":"e14019","status":"p","title":"Transplant Infectious Disease","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147499643"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-835fc5cd-9b05-420d-a8c7-21f82eb277c8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevalence of cervical human papillomavirus and the risk of anal co-infection in kidney transplant recipients : Results from a Danish clinical study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-678548","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Metabolic acidosis and the uremic toxins, indoxyl sulphate (IS) and p-cresyl sulphate (PCS), are associated with increased risks of kidney disease progression, muscle catabolism, cardiovascular disease, and mortality in patients with chronic kidney disease (CKD). The New Nordic Renal Diet (NNRD) is a plant focused meal pattern, with reduced phosphorus and protein content compared to an average Danish diet. Due to a higher amount of plant-based products, we hypothesized that NNRD would reduce renal excretion of acids and uremic toxins. Thus, we evaluated the effects of NNRD on metabolic acidosis and uremic toxins in patients with moderate CKD, stages 3-4. Design and methods: This post hoc analysis is based on a randomized controlled crossover trial comparing 1-week of the NNRD to a control period of an average Danish diet with a 1-week period, in patients with CKD stages 3 and 4. Urine pH and urine excretion of bicarbonate, ammonium, titratable acids, IS and PCS alongside plasma total CO2 (tCO2) were measured at days 1, 4, and 7 in 18 patients. Results: After 7 days on NNRD 24-h urine net acid excretion (NAE) was decreased by 80% (P<.001), 24-h urine excretion of ammonium and bicarbonate decreased by 34% (P<.001) and increased by 678% (P<.001), respectively, compared with the control period. Plasma tCO2 was increased by 8% (P=.005). Moreover, 24-hour urine excretion of PCS and IS were reduced by 31% (P=.018) and 29% (P<.001), respectively. Conclusion: One week of NNRD in patients suffering from moderate CKD effectively improved metabolic acidosis with a marked reduction in urine NAE that included a large increase in urine bicarbonate excretion. In addition, NNRD reduced urinary excretion of the uremic toxins PCS and IS. These results encourage further investigations of the long-term effects of NNRD on renal protection in patients with CKD.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hansen, Nikita Misella","Berg, Peder","Rix, Marianne","Pareek, Manan","Leipziger, Jens","Kamper, Anne-Lise","Astrup, Arne","Sørensen, Mads Vaarby","Salomo, Louise"],"cuid":["S02-095.27-685818"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yale University"],"keyword":["Chronic kidney disease CKD","Faculty of Science","New Nordic Renal Diet NNRD"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the new nordic renal diet induces a pronounced reduction of urine acid excretion and uremic toxins in chronic kidney disease patients stage 000000000003 and 000000000004","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85143894355","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.27-685818","identifier":[{"id":"85143894355","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36195272","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-02034c0d-96eb-45c1-a991-093bc77459d8","ku-b17fee70-f5cb-4e25-a879-26097ada9708"],"keyword":["Chronic kidney disease (CKD)","Faculty of Science","New Nordic Renal Diet (NNRD)","Renal protection","Urenic toxins","Urine acid excretion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C2D18D9E549CCA946411E302DF07119B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"yale university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Yale University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Nikita Misella","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"318efa0a-440b-4901-8853-b20d0acbc5ab","name":"Hansen, Nikita Misella","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peder","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"e78b0bcb-ed5f-4b7d-ae94-1793d5d65e21","name":"Berg, Peder","orcid":"0000-0002-5216-2891","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marianne","key":"rixpau","last":"Rix","name":"Rix, Marianne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Manan","key":"pareekpau","last":"Pareek","name":"Pareek, Manan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"leipzigerpau","last":"Leipziger","locid":"89f75d86-f3d8-4ed3-8754-24c9bcf0080c","name":"Leipziger, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6719-7034","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne-Lise","key":"kamperpau","last":"Kamper","name":"Kamper, Anne-Lise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"5d943631-c9fc-4b63-8aaa-263ba4248735","name":"Astrup, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-8968-8996","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Vaarby","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f42195c2-31a1-460d-aecc-316e6dfe8baf","name":"Sørensen, Mads Vaarby","orcid":"0000-0001-6398-1035","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Louise","key":"salomopau","last":"Salomo","name":"Salomo, Louise","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36195272"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1053/j.jrn.2022.09.010","issn":["10512276","15328503"],"issn_org":["10512276"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Renal Nutrition","pages":"412-419","publisher":"WB  Saunders","publisher_org":"W.B. Saunders","status":"p","title":"Journal of Renal Nutrition","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143894355"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-02034c0d-96eb-45c1-a991-093bc77459d8","ku-b17fee70-f5cb-4e25-a879-26097ada9708"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The New Nordic Renal Diet induces a pronounced reduction of urine acid excretion and uremic toxins in chronic kidney disease patients (stage 3 and 4)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.27-685818","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Low cardiorespiratory fitness (ie, peak oxygen consumption [V.O2peak]) is associated with cardiovascular disease and all-cause mortality and is recognized as an important clinical tool in the assessment of patients. Cardiopulmonary exercise test (CPET) is the gold standard procedure for determination of V.O2peak but has methodological challenges as it is time-consuming and requires specialized equipment and trained professionals. Seismofit is a chest-mounted medical device for estimating V.O2peak at rest using seismocardiography. Objective: The purpose of this study was to investigate the validity and reliability of Seismofit V.O2peak estimation in a healthy population. Methods: On 3 separate days, 20 participants (10 women) underwent estimations of V.O2peak with Seismofit (×2) and Polar Fitness Test (PFT) in randomized order and performed a graded CPET on a cycle ergometer with continuous pulmonary gas exchange measurements. Results: Seismofit V.O2peak showed a significant bias of –3.1 ± 2.4 mL·min–1·kg–1 (mean ± 95% confidence interval) and 95% limits of agreement (LoA) of ±10.8 mL·min–1·kg–1 compared to CPET. The mean absolute percentage error (MAPE) was 12.0%. Seismofit V.O2peak had a coefficient of variation of 4.5% ± 1.3% and an intraclass correlation coefficient of 0.95 between test days and a bias of 0.0 ± 0.4 mL·min–1·kg–1 with 95% LoA of ±1.6 mL·min–1·kg–1 in test–retest. In addition, Seismofit showed a 2.4 mL·min–1·kg–1 smaller difference in 95% LoA than PFT compared to CPET. Conclusion: The Seismofit is highly reliable in its estimation of V.O2peak. However, based on the measurement error and MAPE >10%, the Seismofit V.O2peak estimation model needs further improvement to be considered for use in clinical settings.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Mikkel Thunestvedt","Rømer, Tue","Højgaard, Amalie","Husted, Karina Louise Skov","Sørensen, Kasper","Schmidt, Samuel E.","Dela, Flemming","Helge, Jørn Wulff"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-697732"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Mikkel T"],"keyword":["Cardiorespiratory fitness test","Method agreement","Nonexercise VOpeak equation","Seismocardiography","VOmax estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["VentriJect"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validity and reliability of seismocardiography for the estimation of cardiorespiratory fitness","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cvdhj.2023.08.020","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["All participants are thanked for their commitment and participation in the study. VentriJect Aps are thanked for providing the equipment for performing the V.O2peak estimation. This work was financially supported by VentriJect Aps. VentriJect Aps support two-thirds of Dr Mikkel Hansen's scholarship. Dr Samuel Emil Schmidt and Dr Kasper Sørensen hold shares in VentriJect Aps. Dr Schmidt works part-time as Chief Scientific Officer and Dr Sørensen full-time as Head of Software at VentriJect Aps. There was no restriction on publication. Declaration of Generative AI and AI-assisted Technologies in the writing process: No generative AI or AI-assisted technologies have been used in the preparation of this work. All authors attest they meet the current ICMJE criteria for authorship. All patients provided written consent. The study conforms to the Helsinki Declaration and was approved by the Science Ethical Committee of the Greater Region of Copenhagen, Denmark (H-19081375). All data that were used in the current study are available upon reasonable request. The estimated and measured V.O2peak values on the 3 test days from all the participants are given in Supplemental Table 3. This work was financially supported by VentriJect Aps ."],"id":"S02-100.00-697732","identifier":[{"id":"85173021779","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10577491","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37850043","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-764658bd-2d9c-4861-86a5-5c0ed882e958","ku-9c54a70a-d2ad-4290-b37d-f09b97febf93"],"keyword":["Cardiorespiratory fitness test","Method agreement","Nonexercise VOpeak equation","Seismocardiography","VOmax estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6402D999397193B6464CDD0DE04FBD72"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/558200292/1-s2.0-S2666693623000695-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cvdhj.2023.08.020","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/369867947/Validity_and_reliability_o.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Exercise and Muscle"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, CardioTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["VentriJect"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel T.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58070c3b-ed1e-4859-9467-29b512cdea42","name":"Hansen, Mikkel Thunestvedt","name_org":"Hansen, Mikkel T.","orcid":"0000-0002-3879-2192","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tue","key":"rømerpau","last":"Rømer","locid":"32b26587-2ba1-4451-b564-da70a76f4712","name":"Rømer, Tue","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Amalie","key":"højgaardpau","last":"Højgaard","name":"Højgaard, Amalie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karina","key":"hustedpau","last":"Husted","locid":"6d16a70a-d967-4c50-8c2c-7625021b4586","name":"Husted, Karina Louise Skov","name_org":"Husted, Karina","orcid":"0000-0002-9280-1694","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"81eaf062-83d5-4963-9de6-f713214ff461","name":"Sørensen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-0358-9354","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel E","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"bb4b7dd4-cb80-4ac8-971e-160921ec26a2","name":"Schmidt, Samuel","name_org":"Schmidt, Samuel E","orcid":"0000-0002-0917-634X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Flemming","key":"delapau","last":"Dela","locid":"5d84458e-34c1-4874-a128-7fc3cb13f7f2","name":"Dela, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-9970-9535","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørn W.","key":"helgepau","last":"Helge","locid":"a5560afa-4f31-4278-8ae9-0c49fb0027c1","name":"Helge, Jørn Wulff","name_org":"Helge, Jørn W.","orcid":"0000-0001-9724-5423","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37850043"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cvdhj.2023.08.020","issn":["26666936"],"issue":"5","journal":"Cardiovascular Digital Health Journal","pages":"155-163","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Cardiovascular Digital Health Journal","title_org":"Cardiovascular digital health journal","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173021779"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","ventriject aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-764658bd-2d9c-4861-86a5-5c0ed882e958","ku-9c54a70a-d2ad-4290-b37d-f09b97febf93"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Validity and reliability of seismocardiography for the estimation of cardiorespiratory fitness","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-697732","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES: Two years after implementing a new national donor vigilance system, the Danish Haemovigilance Committee conducted a nationwide survey to evaluate the implementation among different staff groups. We present the results here. MATERIALS AND METHODS: The study was designed as an anonymous online survey to evaluate the satisfaction with the new registration, understanding of the parameters used and the user-friendliness. The REDCap platform was used. The questionnaire consisted of 22 questions. Ordinal variables were answered using five-point Likert scale (1 = strongly disagree to 5 = strongly agree). The data were analysed using descriptive statistics. Successful implementation was defined as mean overall satisfaction ≥4 and mean understanding of the individual components (adverse reaction category, severity and imputability) in the registration ≥4. RESULTS: In all, 104 staff members (77.9% donation staff) participated. The mean (SD) overall satisfaction among all participants was 3.96 (0.94), highest among medical doctors (4.43 (0.78)) and lowest for administrative or other personnel (2.78 (1.09)). The mean scores for understanding the adverse reaction categories, severity and imputability were 3.92 (0.94), 3.92 (0.94) and 3.88 (1.00), respectively. Experience with a previous donor vigilance system was associated with lower scores. The most successful implementation programme included a medical doctor for introduction and a contact person. CONCLUSION: The goal for successful implementation was not met. However, the overall attitude towards the new registration was positive and indicates that the system is suitable for different staff groups. Our results suggest that implementation could benefit from special attention to administrative staff and those accustomed to another donor vigilance system.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Christina","Paarup, Helene Martina","Bruun, Mie Topholm","Pedersen, Louise Ørnskov","Hasslund, Sys","Larsen, Rune","Aagaard, Bitten","Sørensen, Betina Samuelsen"],"cuid":["S03-093.88-011547"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Mikkelsen, Christina"],"keyword":["Attitude","Denmark","Donor health","Donors","Humans","Personal Satisfaction","Surveys and Questionnaires","Tissue Donors","haemovigilance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Danish Medicines Agency"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a danish national multicentre evaluation of the new donor vigilance system among different staff groups","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/vox.13392","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["H.M.P., B.S.S. and C.M.I. drafted the questionnaire, performed focus group interview and organized the survey. C.M.I. compiled and analysed the data. M.T.B., L.Ø.P., S.H., R.L. and B.A. all reviewed and edited the manuscript."],"id":"S03-093.88-011547","identifier":[{"id":"36520050","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000899240800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85144095187","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f1a62529-66d8-411d-a8dd-f5b07ea65675","ku-1ad83bd5-8c6f-4470-9774-8b327a920647","sdu-9de61b57-429f-4aa3-84ac-522e36f318b7"],"keyword":["Attitude","Denmark","Humans","Personal Satisfaction","Surveys and Questionnaires","Tissue Donors","donor health","donors","haemovigilance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["G