:"sveinssonolafurapau","last":"Sveinsson","name":"Sveinsson, Olafur A","rank":56,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sisse R","key":"ostrowskisisserpau","last":"Ostrowski","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse R","rank":57,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hilma","key":"holmhilmapau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Hilma","rank":58,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel F.","key":"gudbjartssondanielfpau","last":"Gudbjartsson","name":"Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","rank":59,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gudmar","key":"thorleifssongudmarpau","last":"Thorleifsson","name":"Thorleifsson, Gudmar","rank":60,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"sulempatrickpau","last":"Sulem","name":"Sulem, Patrick","rank":61,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hreinn","key":"stefanssonhreinnpau","last":"Stefansson","name":"Stefansson, Hreinn","rank":62,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorgeir E","key":"thorgeirssonthorgeirepau","last":"Thorgeirsson","name":"Thorgeirsson, Thorgeir E","rank":63,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas F","key":"hansenthomasfpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Thomas F","rank":64,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kari","key":"stefanssonkaripau","last":"Stefansson","name":"Stefansson, Kari","rank":65,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"24","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"nyegaardmetteoth","last":"Nyegaard","locid":"c048a688-cd64-40ca-a277-53f16360f7a1","name":"Nyegaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-4973-8543","rank":66,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"24","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Palle Duun","key":"rohdepalleduunoth","last":"Rohde","locid":"fb6ff2cf-6e9c-4d3f-a461-8a834cc0b141","name":"Rohde, Palle Duun","orcid":"0000-0003-4347-8656","rank":67,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["37884687"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41588-023-01538-0","issn":["10614036","15461718"],"issn_org":["10614036"],"issue":"11","journal":"Nature Genetics","pages":"1843-1853","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Genetics","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174915851"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3dde059d-6010-49c8-851f-2dcba23c2bf6","au-da5cf8e1-d180-42d9-a439-9252daeb6322","ku-2951c4b0-8c4a-44fb-8d66-15c4fba70b29","sdu-92efa4eb-7bca-42cd-ab04-976273bcfee0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Rare variants with large effects provide functional insights into the pathology of migraine subtypes, with and without aura","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-096.28-715639","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Syncope is a common and clinically challenging condition. In this study, the genetics of syncope were investigated to seek knowledge about its pathophysiology and prognostic implications. METHODS AND RESULTS: This genome-wide association meta-analysis included 56 071 syncope cases and 890 790 controls from deCODE genetics (Iceland), UK Biobank (United Kingdom), and Copenhagen Hospital Biobank Cardiovascular Study/Danish Blood Donor Study (Denmark), with a follow-up assessment of variants in 22 412 cases and 286 003 controls from Intermountain (Utah, USA) and FinnGen (Finland). The study yielded 18 independent syncope variants, 17 of which were novel. One of the variants, p.Ser140Thr in PTPRN2, affected syncope only when maternally inherited. Another variant associated with a vasovagal reaction during blood donation and five others with heart rate and/or blood pressure regulation, with variable directions of effects. None of the 18 associations could be attributed to cardiovascular or other disorders. Annotation with regard to regulatory elements indicated that the syncope variants were preferentially located in neural-specific regulatory regions. Mendelian randomization analysis supported a causal effect of coronary artery disease on syncope. A polygenic score (PGS) for syncope captured genetic correlation with cardiovascular disorders, diabetes, depression, and shortened lifespan. However, a score based solely on the 18 syncope variants performed similarly to the PGS in detecting syncope risk but did not associate with other disorders. CONCLUSION: The results demonstrate that syncope has a distinct genetic architecture that implicates neural regulatory processes and a complex relationship with heart rate and blood pressure regulation. A shared genetic background with poor cardiovascular health was observed, supporting the importance of a thorough assessment of individuals presenting with syncope.","author_count":65,"contributors":["Aegisdottir, Hildur M.","Thorolfsdottir, Rosa B.","Sveinbjornsson, Gardar","Stefansson, Olafur A.","Gunnarsson, Bjarni","Tragante, Vinicius","Thorleifsson, Gudmar","Stefansdottir, Lilja","Thorgeirsson, Thorgeir E.","Ferkingstad, Egil","Sulem, Patrick","Norddahl, Gudmundur","Rutsdottir, Gudrun","Banasik, Karina","Christensen, Alex Hoerby","Mikkelsen, Christina","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Brunak, Søren","Bruun, Mie Topholm","Erikstrup, Christian","Jacobsen, Rikke Louise","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Sørensen, Erik","Frigge, Michael L.","Hjorleifsson, Kristjan E.","Ivarsdottir, Erna V.","Helgadottir, Anna","Gretarsdottir, Solveig","Steinthorsdottir, Valgerdur","Oddsson, Asmundur","Eggertsson, Hannes P.","Halldorsson, Gisli H.","Jones, David A.","Andersson, Jeffrey L.","Knowlton, Kirk U.","Nadauld, Lincoln D.","Haraldsson, Magnus","Thorgeirsson, Gudmundur","Bundgaard, Henning","Arnar, David O.","Thorsteinsdottir, Unnur","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Holm, Hilma","Stefansson, Kari","Andersen, Steffen","Burgdorf, Kristoffer Sølvsten","Didriksen, Maria","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Folkmann Hansen, Thomas","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Jemec, Gregor Borut Ernst","Jennum, Poul","Johansson, Pär Ingemar","Hørup Larsen, Margit Anita","Mikkelsen, Susan","Nyegaard, Mette","Stefánsson, Hreinn","Sækmose, Susanne","Ullum, Henrik","Werge, Thomas"],"cuid":["S05-098.38-681230"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["DBDS Genomic Consortium","Danish Blood Donor Study Genomic Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Holm, Hilma","Stefansson, Kari"],"country":["Iceland","United States"],"glorg":["Agricultural University of Iceland","All Global Affiliations","Amgen Incorporated","Intermountain Healthcare","Intermountain Heart Institute","Intermountain Medical Center","Landspitali University Hospital","Natl Univ Hosp Iceland, Dept Med, Landspitali","Natl Univ Hosp Iceland, Dept Psychiat, Landspitali","Primary Children's Medical Center","Stanford University","The National University Hospital of Iceland","The University of Utah","University of Iceland","University of Utah","deCODE Genetics","deCODE genetics, Inc"],"keyword":["Architecture","Family history","GWAS","Genome wide association","Identification","Imprinting","Mendelian randomization","Meta analysis","PTPRN2","Prevalence","Quality of Life","Resting heart rate","Syncope","Vasovagal reaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Mental Health Centre Sct. Hans, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic variants associated with syncope implicate neural and autonomic processes","src":["aau","au","cbs","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85150751952","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was partly supported by NordForsk through the funding to PM Heart (project number 90580). This work was partly funded by the Innovation Fund Denmark (IFD) under File No. 8114-00033B and also by the Technology Development Fund, Iceland (project number 90580). Karina Banasik and Søren Brunak acknowledge the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grants NNF17OC0027594 and NNF14CC0001). We wish to express special gratitude to the individual participants in the deCODE genetics, UK Biobank, Copenhagen Hospital Biobank, Danish Blood Donor Study, FinnGen, and Intermountain cohorts. We also thank those who worked on generating these resources through data and sample collection, genotyping, and analysis. This work was partly supported by NordForsk through the funding to PM Heart (project number 90580). This work was partly funded by the Innovation Fund Denmark (IFD) under File No. 8114-00033B and also by the Technology Development Fund, Iceland (project number 90580)."],"id":"S05-098.38-681230","identifier":[{"id":"85150751952","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000926382600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"36747475","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-45c15d73-cc3c-41db-9edf-922b39228dc7","au-d9545292-6653-4a2b-a948-f19b9cd76422","cbs-cd076913-ce7d-4945-80cc-bded068504c0","ku-d84ab774-dbea-4ff1-a0cc-b1926e949979","sdu-57a00972-17c6-49d6-b200-b474b38321e0"],"keyword":["ARCHITECTURE","FAMILY-HISTORY","GENOME-WIDE ASSOCIATION","GWAS","IDENTIFICATION","Imprinting","MENDELIAN RANDOMIZATION","Meta-analysis","PREVALENCE","PTPRN2","QUALITY-OF-LIFE","RESTING HEART-RATE","Syncope","UP TILT","VASOVAGAL SYNCOPE","Vasovagal reaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-8-D9498A6756253008C6594C638DBF0395"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"is","key":"decode genetics","loc":["Iceland","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"deCODE Genetics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"is","key":"university of iceland","loc":["Iceland","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Iceland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"amgen incorporated","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Amgen Incorporated","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"is","key":"decode genetics inc","loc":["Iceland","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"deCODE genetics, Inc","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU Univers