:"Ullum, Henrik","rank":60,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"29","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"wergethomaspau","last":"Werge","name":"Werge, Thomas","rank":61,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36747475"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurheartj/ehad016","issn":["0195668X","15229645"],"issn_org":["0195668X"],"issue":"12","journal":"European Heart Journal","pages":"1070-1080","paperid":"ehad016","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150751952"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-45c15d73-cc3c-41db-9edf-922b39228dc7","au-d9545292-6653-4a2b-a948-f19b9cd76422","cbs-cd076913-ce7d-4945-80cc-bded068504c0","ku-d84ab774-dbea-4ff1-a0cc-b1926e949979","sdu-57a00972-17c6-49d6-b200-b474b38321e0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","CBS Copenhagen Business School","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Genetic Variants Associated with Syncope Implicate Neural and Autonomic Processes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-098.38-681230","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Biofouling is a ubiquitous problem in many industrial systems including reverse osmosis (RO) desalination units where the biofilm impedes the water flow. It is essential to develop novel cleaning methods that are non-damaging and environmentally friendly. The most promising cleaning agents are enzymes, which can selectively cleave the components that stabilize the biofilm. However, biofilm-degrading enzymes are often difficult to identify due to the unknown matrix composition and lack of effective screening methods. To overcome this, a flexible screening platform was developed to evaluate enzyme treatment on fouling removal directly on RO membranes. The developed platform was used to identify enzymes that could degrade biofilms on fouled RO membranes. The membrane biofilms were destabilized by a range of enzyme groups, most effectively by proteases, lipases, DNase, cellulolytic enzymes, and pectin-degrading enzymes. The most effective enzyme formulations could clean the membranes more effectively than conventional chemical cleaning agents, removing 45 % of the biofilm compared with 0 %–19 % for the chemicals (p ≤ 0.001), indicating that enzymes have the potential to replace or complement chemical cleaning. The screening platform thus proved a potent tool for systematically studying biofilms and could be applied to combat biofilms in many other applications.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Møllebjerg, Andreas","Zarebska, Agata","Nielsen, Henrik Bangsø","Hansen, Lea Benedicte Skov","Sørensen, Sebastian R.","Seredynska-Sobecka, Bozena","Villacorte, Loreen O.","Gori, Klaus","Palmén, Lorena Gonzales","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-151249"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Møllebjerg, Andreas"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Reverse osmosis","Screening","optical coherence tomography OCT"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GFS","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-GFS","DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel high throughput screening platform identifies enzymes to tackle biofouling on reverse osmosis membranes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.desal.2023.116485","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-151249","identifier":[{"id":"85148771574","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-26230021-488e-45a3-9f57-5b1ca6953c99"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Biological Fouling","Enzyme Cleaning","Reverse Osmosis","Screening","optical coherence tomography (OCT)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-241149A25A9187CC159D3D42EE69980C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/418459054/1-s2.0-S0011916423001170-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.desal.2023.116485","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology - WATEC Aarhus University Centre for Water Technology, Ny Munkegade"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"grundfos","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GFS","l3nl":"Grundfos","l3nn":"Grundfos","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Grundfos","namevar":["Grundfos A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GFS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"møllebjergpau","last":"Møllebjerg","locid":"4176d27b-9e84-42e2-9357-cd93796c3046","name":"Møllebjerg, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Agata","key":"zarebskapau","last":"Zarebska","name":"Zarebska, Agata","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bangsø","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henrik Bangsø","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lea Benedicte Skov","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lea Benedicte Skov","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian R.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Sebastian R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bozena","key":"seredynskasobeckapau","last":"Seredynska-Sobecka","name":"Seredynska-Sobecka, Bozena","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Loreen O.","key":"villacortepau","last":"Villacorte","name":"Villacorte, Loreen O.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"goripau","last":"Gori","name":"Gori, Klaus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorena Gonzales","key":"palménpau","last":"Palmén","name":"Palmén, Lorena Gonzales","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.desal.2023.116485","issn":["00119164","18734464"],"issn_org":["00119164"],"journal":"Desalination","paperid":"116485","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Desalination","volume":"554"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148771574"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Grundfos","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-26230021-488e-45a3-9f57-5b1ca6953c99"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Novel high-throughput screening platform identifies enzymes to tackle biofouling on reverse osmosis membranes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-151249","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND & AIMS: The term post-colonoscopy colorectal cancer (PCCRC) refers to colorectal cancer (CRC) diagnosed after a negative colonoscopy. Using the root-cause algorithm proposed by the World Endoscopy Organization, we aimed to investigate plausible explanations for PCCRCs and potential changes in plausible explanations for PCCRCs over time in a Danish Region. METHODS: During 1995 to 2021, we used national health registries and electronic medical records in the Central Denmark Region to identify PCCRC cases, defined as CRCs recorded within 6 to 48 months after a colonoscopy. We then applied the World Endoscopy Organization algorithm to categorize explanations for PCCRC as follows: (A) possible missed lesion, prior examination adequate; (B) possible missed lesion, prior examination inadequate; (C) detected lesion, not resected; or (D) likely incomplete resection of previously identified lesion. PCCRCs were identified before (1995-2013) and after (2014-2021) implementation of nationwide fecal immunochemical test-based CRC screening and quality indicators for colonoscopy. RESULTS: We identified 762 PCCRCs, 53.5% among males and 57% among individuals ≥70 years. Forty-five percent were located in the proximal colon. We identified 616 (80.8%; 95% confidence interval [CI], 74.6%-87.5%) category A PCCRCs; 36 (4.7%; 95% CI, 3.3%-6.5%) category B PCCRCs; 26 (3.4%; 95% CI, 2.2%-4.9%) category C PCCRCs; and 84 (11%; 95% CI, 8.8%-13.6%) category D PCCRCs. Similar patterns were observed during the early (1995-2013) and late (2014-2021) study periods. CONCLUSIONS: Most PCCRCs originate from possible missed lesions and incompletely resected lesions during the complete study period. These findings indicate the importance of quality assurance of colonoscopy procedures and polypectomy techniques.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Troelsen, Frederikke Schønfeldt","Sørensen, Henrik Toft","Pedersen, Lars","Brix, Lone Dragnes","Grode, Louise Bang","Dekker, Evelien","Erichsen, Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-195669"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC"],"keyword":["Colonoscopy","Colonoscopy adverse effects","Colorectal Neoplasms diagnosis","Colorectal cancer","Denmark epidemiology","Early Detection of Cancer","Humans","Male","Population based","Risk Factors","Time Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"root cause analysis of 000000000762 danish post colonoscopy colorectal cancer patients","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cgh.2023.03.034","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-195669","identifier":[{"id":"85159867757","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37031719","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-7439fed0-2fd7-456b-bf8f-98212d20d287"],"keyword":["Colonoscopy","Colonoscopy/adverse effects","Colorectal Cancer","Colorectal Neoplasms/diagnosis","Denmark/epidemiology","Early Detection of Cancer","Humans","Male","Population-based","Post-colonoscopy Colorectal Cancer","Risk Factors","Root-causes Analysis","Time Factors","World Endoscopy Organization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A1AE66931003DF05E638C2FD964A815"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/384477732/1-s2.0-S1542356523002422-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cgh.2023.03.034","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aar