{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Lichen sclerosus (LS) is a chronic, autoimmune skin disease predominantly located in the anogenital region in women. In recent years, the role of the human microbiota in the pathogenesis of autoimmune diseases, including LS, has received interest. OBJECTIVES: The study aimed to evaluate and compare the composition of the urinary, vaginal and gut microbiota in women with LS versus non-affected controls. STUDY DESIGN: Women diagnosed with LS (n = 16) and matched controls (n = 14) were enrolled in the study. From each participant, midstream urine, upper and lower vaginal swabs, as well as faecal samples, were collected. The microbiota composition was assessed using 16S ribosomal RNA (rRNA) gene sequencing of the V4 hypervariable region. RESULTS: We observed no LS-specific clustering in either of the four anatomic niches, using either hierarchical cluster analysis or weighted beta diversity metrics. However, for unweighted UniFrac, significant differences in the urinary and lower vaginal microbiota were observed when comparing women with LS to controls. These findings indicate that while the two groups have microbiota dominated by the same bacteria, variations do occur amongst less abundant bacteria. The LEfSe analysis revealed a higher relative abundance of the genus Streptococcus in the urinary and lower vaginal microbiota in women with LS compared to controls. Additionally, a higher relative abundance of phylum Euryarchaeota was observed in the gut microbiota in women with LS compared to controls. CONCLUSION: In this study, we demonstrated several differences amongst less abundant bacteria in the urinary, lower vaginal and faecal microbiota when comparing women with LS to controls. However, further research is required to assess whether these microbiota differences are causative or merely a result of the underlying LS disease.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nygaard, Sofie","Gerlif, Katrine","Bundgaard-Nielsen, Caspar","Saleh Media, Jean","Leutscher, Peter Derek Christian","Sørensen, Suzette","Villadsen, Annemarie Brusen","Arenholt, Louise Thomsen Schmidt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-686826"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Arenholt, Louise Thomsen Schmidt"],"keyword":["Autoimmune Diseases","Autoimmunity","Case Control Studies","Female","Gastrointestinal Microbiome","Humans","Lichen Sclerosus et Atrophicus","Lichen sclerosus","Microbiota","RNA Ribosomal 16S genetics","Vagina microbiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the urinary vaginal and gut microbiota in women with genital lichen sclerosus a case control study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejogrb.2023.08.004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-686826","identifier":[{"id":"37591024","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85172424013","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-80ba08c3-fe29-4149-833b-a21c51718bf1"],"keyword":["Autoimmune Diseases","Autoimmunity","Case-Control Studies","Female","Gastrointestinal Microbiome","Humans","Lichen Sclerosus et Atrophicus","Lichen sclerosus","Microbiota","RNA, Ribosomal, 16S/genetics","Vagina/microbiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EDD2199C82BC7F58FDA484823CE9441C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/551303498/1-s2.0-S0301211523003093-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejogrb.2023.08.004","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for Clinical Research","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, North Denmark Regional Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"e0e1cc81-8cc3-459b-817a-799e94ead0a5","name":"Nygaard, Sofie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine","key":"gerlifpau","last":"Gerlif","locid":"d5961638-eacf-42ea-b812-ad7be5e20bdc","name":"Gerlif, Katrine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Caspar","key":"bundgaardnielsenpau","last":"Bundgaard-Nielsen","locid":"621f32eb-b0ed-4146-bed9-a4b793ee401d","name":"Bundgaard-Nielsen, Caspar","orcid":"0000-0002-2700-2378","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jean","key":"salehmediapau","last":"Saleh Media","locid":"8a810824-ca82-451d-b5b9-6518e3dd2175","name":"Saleh Media, Jean","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"leutscherpau","last":"Leutscher","locid":"56e8c48e-c3f9-4a4d-8b9b-0719c74da258","name":"Leutscher, Peter Derek Christian","name_org":"Leutscher, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-1168-4041","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Suzette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c96d8309-747c-403d-a858-2efad1aea498","name":"Sørensen, Suzette","orcid":"0000-0002-4201-1168","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annemarie","key":"brusenvilladsenpau","last":"Brusen Villadsen","locid":"71f9e538-f8b1-48d5-a0e3-3bb05794c38c","name":"Villadsen, Annemarie Brusen","name_org":"Brusen Villadsen, Annemarie","orcid":"0000-0002-4064-2900","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"thomsenschmidtarenholtpau","last":"Thomsen Schmidt Arenholt","locid":"9fe53819-b8b7-4220-8f9f-125eb33881e8","name":"Arenholt, Louise Thomsen Schmidt","name_org":"Thomsen Schmidt Arenholt, Louise","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37591024"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejogrb.2023.08.004","issn":["03012115","09218750"],"issn_org":["03012115"],"journal":"European Journal of Obstetrics & Gynecology and Reproductive Biology","pages":"1-8","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Obstetrics & Gynecology and Reproductive Biology","volume":"289"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172424013"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-80ba08c3-fe29-4149-833b-a21c51718bf1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The urinary, vaginal and gut microbiota in women with genital lichen sclerosus - A case-control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-686826","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The loss of mass from the Greenland ice sheet causes an increasing influx of freshwater to the Greenlandic fjords and the oceans. Freshwater fluxes from marine-terminating glaciers are important to understand fjord circulation and ecosystem dynamics. Here, we present a data set constructed by reformulating existing products into a shared temporal and spatial framework. We combine three publicly available data sets of solid-ice discharge (iceberg), liquid-surface runoff (runoff) and basal melt to present a cohesive overview of the flow of freshwater from marine-terminating glaciers to the Greenlandic fjords. We also calculate glacier drainage basins and compare our findings to previous studies showing that drainage-basin sizes may vary considerably depending on how they were reconstructed. The data set will be a valuable asset to oceanographic, glaciological and marine biological research activities.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Karlsson, Nanna B.","Mankoff, Kenneth D.","Solgaard, Anne M.","Larsen, Signe H.","How, Penelope R.","Fausto, Robert S.","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689173"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Karlsson, Nanna B."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NASA Goddard Institute for Space Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a data set of monthly freshwater fluxes from the greenland ice sheet s marine terminating glaciers on a glacier basin scale 000000002010 000000002020","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://