","name":"Severinsen, Marianne Tang","orcid":"0000-0003-0996-1812","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"bøgstedpau","last":"Bøgsted","locid":"a51116b7-e9b7-4f83-a74b-2d76bb8b1475","name":"Bøgsted, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-9192-1814","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 8 9","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Stidsholt","key":"rougpau","last":"Roug","locid":"6815294f-af82-4b80-927c-b641f2f717a1","name":"Roug, Anne Stidsholt","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37489268"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ejh.14046","issn":["09024441","09024506"],"issn_org":["09024441"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Journal of Haematology","pages":"573-582","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Haematology","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85165614316"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1096ac34-fcce-494b-babe-9d83dab3a500","au-de9e8052-9952-4d3e-8ddc-abc17637de6d","sdu-42090f30-24d2-4fb7-8b90-64c5d01001e1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Venetoclax-based therapy for relapsed or refractory acute myeloid leukaemia following intensive induction chemotherapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-092.86-691687","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Therapy with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) is effective in patients with metastatic mismatch-repair deficient (dMMR) colorectal cancer (CRC); however, data on treatment with neoadjuvant ICI in patients with locally advanced CRC are limited. From March 2019 to June 2020, five Danish oncological centers treated 10 patients with a treatment-naïve dMMR CRC with preoperative pembrolizumab, 9 with a nonmetastatic, unresectable colon cancer and 1 with a locally advanced rectum cancer. All 10 patients were evaluated regularly at a multidisciplinary team (MDT) meeting, and they all had a radical resection after a median of 8 cycles (range 2-13) of pembrolizumab. A microscopic evaluation of the resected tumors revealed no remaining tumor cells in five patients, while five still had tumor cells present. The patients were given no additional therapy. No recurrences were reported after a median follow-up of 26 months (range 23-38.5 months). Biopsies from Danish patients with CRC are routinely screened for dMMR proteins. In 2017, data from the Danish Colorectal Cancer Group showed that 19% (565/3000) of the patients with colon cancer and 1.5% (19/1279) of those with rectum cancer had an dMMR tumor. Among the patients with MMR determination, 26% (99/384) patients had a T4 dMMR colon cancer; thus, the 10 patients treated with neoadjuvant pembrolizumab comprised about 9% of the patients with a T4 dMMR colon cancer (9/99) and 5% of patients with dMMR rectal cancer (1/19). Therapy with pembrolizumab was feasible and effective. Larger prospective trials are needed to confirm our findings.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Eefsen, Rikke Løvendahl","Larsen, Jim S.","Klarskov, Louise L.","Altaf, Rahim","Høgdall, Estrid","Ingeholm, Peter","Lykke, Jakob","Nielsen, Dorte L.","Pfeiffer, Per","Poulsen, Laurids Østergaard","Qvortrup, Camilla","Schou, Jakob V.","Mau-Sørensen, Morten","Østerlind, Kell","Jensen, Benny V."],"cuid":["S03-093.75-672393"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Eefsen, Rikke Løvendahl"],"keyword":["Checkpoint inhibition","Colonic Neoplasms","Colorectal Neoplasms pathology","Colorectal cancer","DNA Mismatch Repair","Humans","Microsatellite Instability","Pembrolizumab","Prospective Studies","Rectal Neoplasms","mismatch repair deficient","unresectable"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"therapy with pembrolizumab in treatment naïve patients with nonmetastatic mismatch repair deficient colorectal cancer","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/532569047/Therapy_with_pembrolizumab_in_treatment_na_ve_patients_with_non_metastatic_mismatch_repair_deficient_colorectal_cancer.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-093.75-672393","identifier":[{"id":"36594580","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146921738","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-94e1599c-0c5a-4bc6-b16a-682b899567b5","ku-fb87b331-6a8d-46d1-b8c3-f1b77fbc5008","sdu-d4db290c-595f-4778-b027-9c9ed6ff215c"],"keyword":["Colonic Neoplasms","Colorectal Neoplasms/pathology","DNA Mismatch Repair","Humans","Microsatellite Instability","Prospective Studies","Rectal Neoplasms","checkpoint inhibition","colorectal cancer","mismatch repair deficient","pembrolizumab","unresectable"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-EA6F94D397D388C599D43EFA63EA8780"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/532569047/