{"abstract":"DNA methylation, a pivotal epigenetic modification, plays a crucial role in regulating gene expression and is known to undergo dynamic changes with age. The present study investigated epigenome-wide methylation profiles in 64 individuals over two time points, 15 years apart, using the Illumina EPIC850k arrays. A mixed-effects model identified 2821 age-associated differentially methylated CpG positions (aDMPs) with a median rate of change of 0.18% per year, consistent with a 10–15% change during a human lifespan. Significant variation in the baseline DNA methylation levels between individuals of similar ages as well as inconsistent direction of change with time across individuals were observed for all the aDMPs. Twenty-three of the 2821 aDMPs were previously incorporated into forensic age prediction models. These markers displayed larger changes in DNA methylation with age compared to all the aDMPs and less variation among individuals. Nevertheless, the forensic aDMPs also showed inter-individual variations in the direction of DNA methylation changes. Only cg16867657 in ELOVL2 exhibited a uniform direction of the age-related change among the investigated individuals, which supports the current knowledge that CpG sites in ELOVL2 are the best markers for age prediction.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Refn, Mie Rath","Andersen, Mikkel Meyer","Kampmann, Marie-Louise","Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","Sørensen, Erik","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Morling, Niels","Børsting, Claus","Alves E Silva Pereira, Vania"],"cuid":["S02-096.85-715624"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Refn, Mie Rath"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"longitudinal changes and variation in human dna methylation analysed with the illumina methylationepic beadchip assay and their implications on forensic age prediction","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-49064-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.85-715624","identifier":[{"id":"85178886205","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38066081","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10709620","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-31f3e21c-a411-4b8b-a52e-c9aaa86ea2cc","ku-09eac3b8-18a8-4547-a5a6-e92677d5d791"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4091CB84BBE34FBBEE362580EFFFD414"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-49064-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375961812/s41598_023_49064_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/676586608/s41598-023-49064-7.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Section of Forensic Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mie Rath","key":"refnpau","last":"Refn","locid":"052a2e3f-5114-4f3d-b444-7707de9aef7d","name":"Refn, Mie Rath","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Meyer","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f522a535-60f0-41f7-b9e5-a34f77a3005c","name":"Andersen, Mikkel Meyer","orcid":"0000-0002-0234-0266","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie-Louise","key":"kampmannpau","last":"Kampmann","locid":"6407dfca-f642-42c6-a444-a2fae2093b04","name":"Kampmann, Marie-Louise","orcid":"0000-0001-5403-5960","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"tfelthansenpau","last":"Tfelt-Hansen","locid":"bdd29054-7062-428a-a97d-e32cb8d80d38","name":"Tfelt-Hansen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0003-3895-9316","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Margit Anita Hørup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"morlingpau","last":"Morling","locid":"6a809f42-2644-434a-9bec-a1fbf5e26093","name":"Morling, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-9463-5087","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus","key":"børstingpau","last":"Børsting","locid":"70c85e72-9aa9-429d-a4bb-9cabd7528618","name":"Børsting, Claus","orcid":"0000-0003-0421-7429","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vania","key":"pereirapau","last":"Pereira","locid":"d5a50a5b-d242-4baf-8b82-e0acaf8ae52f","name":"Pereira, Vania","orcid":"0000-0002-8789-5286","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38066081"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-023-49064-7","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"21658","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178886205"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-31f3e21c-a411-4b8b-a52e-c9aaa86ea2cc","ku-09eac3b8-18a8-4547-a5a6-e92677d5d791"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Longitudinal changes and variation in human DNA methylation analysed with the Illumina MethylationEPIC BeadChip assay and their implications on forensic age prediction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.85-715624","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Women with polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS) often change their metabolic profile over time to decrease levels of androgens while often gaining a propensity for the development of the metabolic syndrome. Recent discoveries indicate that microRNAs (miRNAs) play a role in the development of PCOS and constitute potential biomarkers for PCOS. We aimed to identify miRNAs associated with the development of an impaired metabolic profile in women with PCOS, in a follow-up study, compared with women without PCOS. Methods and materials: Clinical measurements of PCOS status and metabolic disease were obtained twice 6 years apart in a cohort of 46 women with PCOS and nine controls. All participants were evaluated for degree of metabolic disease (hypertension, dyslipidemia, central obesity, and impaired glucose tolerance). MiRNA levels were measured using Taqman® Array cards of 96 pre-selected miRNAs associated with PCOS and/or metabolic disease. Results: Women with PCOS decreased their levels of androgens during follow-up. Twenty-six of the miRNAs were significantly changed in circulation in women with PCOS during the follow-up, and twenty-four of them had decreased, while levels did not change in the control group. Four miRNAs were significantly different at baseline between healthy controls and women with PCOS; miR-103-3p, miR-139-5p, miR-28-3p, and miR-376a-3p, which were decreased in PCOS. After follow-up, miR-28-3p, miR-139-5p, and miR-376a-3p increased in PCOS women to the levels observed in healthy controls. Of these, miR-139-5p correlated with total testosterone levels (rho = 0.50, padj = 0.013), while miR-376-3p correlated significantly with the waist-hip ratio at follow-up (rho = 0.43, padj = 0.01). Predicted targets of miR-103-3p, miR-139-5p, miR-28-3p, and miR-376a-3p were enriched in pathways associated with Insulin/IGF signaling, interleukin signaling, the GNRH receptor pathways, and other signaling pathways. MiRNAs altered during follow-up in PCOS patients were enriched in pathways related to immune regulation, gonadotropin-releasing hormone signaling, tyrosine kinase signaling, and WNT signaling. Conclusions: These studies indicate that miRNAs associated with PCOS and androgen metabolism overall decrease during a 6-year follow-up, reflecting the phenotypic change in PCOS individuals towards a less hyperandrogenic profile.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Udesen, Pernille B.","Sørensen, Anja E.","Svendsen, Rikke","Frisk, Nanna L.S.","Hess, Anne Lundby","Aziz, Mubeena","Wissing, Marie Louise M.","Englund, Anne Lis M.","Dalgaard, Louise T."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-698218"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biomarker","Circulation","Clinical trial","Metabolic syndrome","Non coding RNA","Ovary","PCOS","Polycystic Ovary Syndrome","microRNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Unknown external organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating mirnas in women with polycystic ovary syndrome a longitudinal cohort study","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells12070983","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-698218","identifier":[{"id":"85152353821","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10093401","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37048055","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4d6b5177-9537-4d86-ae0a-572c6efc7529","ruc-9f23f5a4-5817-409a-ae1e-856b27394946"],"keyword":["PCOS","biomarker","circulation","clinical trial","metabolic syndrome","microRNA","non-coding RNA","ovary","polycystic ovary syndrome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FEFA62F9FFF956450873449FAB690BFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/370797281/cells_12_00983.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/100126820/cells-12-00983.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells12070983","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unknown external organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille B.","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","name":"Udesen, Pernille B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Anja E.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7e5d1e2c-5d4b-4436-bb66-acdca4058c08","name":"Sørensen, Anja Elaine","name_org":"Sørensen, Anja E.","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-5376","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"64c98108-e41d-4368-a5ef-8b49c0ecde50","name":"Svendsen, Rikke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Nanna L.S.","key":"friskpau","last":"Frisk","locid":"25f309b3-6a87-40f7-8fe6-7475e7ecce58","name":"Frisk, Nanna Lond Skov","name_org":"Frisk, Nanna L.S.","orcid":"0000-0001-6150-2408","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anne L.","key":"hesspau","last":"Hess","locid":"4cb53830-64c2-49c6-b870-86a781431a98","name":"Hess, Anne Lundby","name_org":"Hess, Anne L.","orcid":"0000-0001-7144-0925","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mubeena","key":"azizpau","last":"Aziz","name":"Aziz, Mubeena","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Marie Louise M.","key":"wissingpau","last":"Wissing","name":"Wissing, Marie Louise M.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Lis M.","key":"englundpau","last":"Englund","name":"Englund, Anne Lis M.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Louise T.","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"a219fdaf-f994-4a7a-beb8-1f353846ed5a","name":"Dalgaard, Louise Torp","name_org":"Dalgaard, Louise T.","orcid":"0000-0002-3598-2775","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37048055"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cells12070983","issn":["20734409"],"issue":"7","journal":"Cells","paperid":"983","status":"p","title":"Cells","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152353821"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4d6b5177-9537-4d86-ae0a-572c6efc7529","ruc-9f23f5a4-5817-409a-ae1e-856b27394946"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Circulating miRNAs in Women with Polycystic Ovary Syndrome : A Longitudinal Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-698218","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Organoid technologies are rapidly advancing and hold great potential and hope for disease modeling and clinical translational research. Still, they raise a number of complex, ethical questions regarding their current and future use. Patient and public involvement is important in building public trust and helping to secure responsible conduct and valued innovations; nevertheless, research into patient and public perspectives on organoid technologies remains scarce. We report on a first public dialogue on organoid technologies through three cross-country deliberative workshops with a diverse group of stakeholders to identify their perceptions and concerns. Participants generally support organoid technologies on the condition that responsible governance, ethical oversight, and sound informed consent procedures are in place. Yet, a broad set of potential concerns are identified, primarily concerning commercialization, healthcare access, and cerebral organoids. Participants’ insights and recommendations can help inform researchers and ethics and policy bodies toward supporting responsible and ethical organoid approaches.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ravn, Tine","Sørensen, Mads P.","Capulli, Emma","Kavouras, Panagiotis","Pegoraro, Renzo","Picozzi, Mario","Saugstrup, Louise Isgaard","Spyrakou, Eleni","Stavridi, Vana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-164757"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ravn, Tine"],"country":["Greece","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Technical University of Athens","University of Insubria"],"keyword":["Ethics","Humans","Informed consent","Motivation","Organoids","Public Deliberation","Public opinion","Translational Research Biomedical"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"public perceptions and expectations disentangling the hope and hype of organoid research","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.stemcr.2023.03.003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-164757","identifier":[{"id":"85151496730","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10147824","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37001517","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-3e34483e-2f2a-4149-817d-21f51a36eade"],"keyword":["Humans","Informed Consent","Motivation","Organoid technologies","Organoids","Public Opinion","Translational Research, Biomedical","ethics","public and patient perspectives","public deliberation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-29E0262A3616C2D1B210CD9410024CE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/314865864/Stem_cell_reports.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.stemcr.2023.03.003","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science - Danish Centre for Studies in Research and Research Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of insubria","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Insubria","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gr","key":"national technical university of athens","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Technical University of Athens","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tine","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"5d9fc737-4fb5-4383-b789-448caeab3f0b","name":"Ravn, Tine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads P.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"fa411f34-079c-444b-afc9-a1ad05e462e3","name":"Sørensen, Mads P.","orcid":"0000-0003-2455-2515","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma","key":"capullipau","last":"Capulli","name":"Capulli, Emma","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Panagiotis","key":"kavouraspau","last":"Kavouras","name":"Kavouras, Panagiotis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Renzo","key":"pegoraropau","last":"Pegoraro","name":"Pegoraro, Renzo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario","key":"picozzipau","last":"Picozzi","name":"Picozzi, Mario","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise Isgaard","key":"saugstruppau","last":"Saugstrup","locid":"7b78b3b3-f514-4873-bca5-d34cff566038","name":"Saugstrup, Louise Isgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eleni","key":"spyrakoupau","last":"Spyrakou","name":"Spyrakou, Eleni","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vana","key":"stavridipau","last":"Stavridi","name":"Stavridi, Vana","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37001517"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.stemcr.2023.03.003","issn":["22136711"],"issue":"4","journal":"Stem Cell Reports","pages":"841-852","publisher":"Cell Press","status":"p","title":"Stem Cell Reports","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151496730"],"se