Chi Ho","rank":28,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Astrid Marie","key":"kolteastridmarieoth","last":"Kolte","name":"Kolte, Astrid Marie","rank":29,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"westergaarddavidoth","last":"Westergaard","name":"Westergaard, David","rank":30,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Unnur","key":"þorsteinsdóttirunnuroth","last":"þorsteinsdóttir","name":"þorsteinsdóttir, Unnur","rank":31,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Kári","key":"stefánssonkárioth","last":"Stefánsson","name":"Stefánsson, Kári","rank":32,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Hákon","key":"jónssonhákonoth","last":"Jónsson","name":"Jónsson, Hákon","rank":33,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Ólafur","key":"magnússonólafuroth","last":"Magnússon","name":"Magnússon, Ólafur","rank":34,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Valgerdur","key":"steinthorsdottirvalgerduroth","last":"Steinthorsdottir","name":"Steinthorsdottir, Valgerdur","rank":35,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Lone","key":"schmidtloneoth","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Lone","rank":36,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Karsten","key":"kristiansenkarstenoth","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Karsten","rank":37,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia Rørbæk","key":"kamstruppiarørbækoth","last":"Kamstrup","name":"Kamstrup, Pia Rørbæk","rank":38,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria Christine","key":"krogmariachristineoth","last":"Krog","name":"Krog, Maria Christine","rank":40,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ellen Christine Leth","key":"løkkegaardellenoth","last":"Løkkegaard","locid":"e07484e2-8c0a-4f40-ad5d-0359a1341ad4","name":"Løkkegaard, Ellen","name_org":"Løkkegaard, Ellen Christine Leth","rank":41,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle Ejdrup","key":"bredkjærhelleejdrupoth","last":"Bredkjær","name":"Bredkjær, Helle Ejdrup","rank":42,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"wilkenjensencharlotteoth","last":"Wilken-Jensen","name":"Wilken-Jensen, Charlotte","rank":43,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["36739882"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s0140-6736(22)02610-1","issn":["00995355","01406736"],"issn_org":["01406736"],"issue":"10378","journal":"The Lancet","pages":"762-771","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"The Lancet","title_org":"Lancet","volume":"401"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149715335"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-71680817-4e75-4218-8aa5-eb2b74c614d2","ku-008c6cad-106e-4668-a3c3-5ba33b9373b4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cell-free fetal DNA for genetic evaluation in Copenhagen Pregnancy Loss Study (COPL) : a prospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.13-005502","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Chronic kidney disease (CKD) leads to an accumulation of waste products and causes adverse cardiometabolic effects. Objectives: We investigated the health effects of the New Nordic Renal Diet (NNRD), a novel meal pattern reduced in phosphorus, protein, and sodium. Methods: A 26-wk randomized trial compared the NNRD with a habitual diet. The NNRD group received weekly home deliveries of food and recipes. Monthly study visits included fasting blood samples, 24-h urine samples, blood pressure, and anthropometric measurements. Intention-to-treat analysis used linear mixed-effects models. Results: Sixty patients, mean estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) 34 mL/min/1.73 m 2 and body mass index of 25–27 kg/m 2, were included and 58 completed. Metabolic syndrome was present in 53% (NNRD group) and 57% (control group). The NNRD group (n = 30) reduced their 24-h urine phosphorus excretion by 19% (−153 mg; 95% confidence interval [CI]: −210, −95), control group (n = 30) (no change), between-group difference −171 mg (95% CI: −233, −109; P < 0.001). Proteinuria was reduced by 39% in the NNRD group (−0.33 g/d; 95% CI: −0.47, −0.18), control group (no change), between-group difference −0.34 g/d (95% CI: −0.52, −0.17; P < 0.001). Plasma urea was reduced by −1.5 mmol/L in the NNRD group (95% CI: −2.1, −0.9), control group (no change), between-group difference −1.4 mmol/L (95% CI: −2.0, −0.7; P < 0.001). Systolic blood pressure fell by −5.2 mmHg in the NNRD group (95% CI: −8.4, −2.1), control group (no change), between-group difference −3.9 mmHg (95% CI; −7.6, −0.2; P = 0.04). The NNRD group lost −1.7 kg (95% CI: −2.6, −0.8), control group (no change), between-group difference −2.0 kg (95% CI: −3.0, −1.0; P < 0.001). There were no effects on eGFR during the 26-wk intervention. Conclusion: NNRD in moderate CKD reduces phosphorus excretion, proteinuria, systolic blood pressure, and weight, mainly by reducing abdominal fat. This trial was registered at clinicaltrials.gov as NCT04579315.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Misella Hansen, Nikita","Kamper, Anne-Lise","Rix, Marianne","Feldt-Rasmussen, Bo","Leipziger, Jens","Sørensen, Mads Vaarby","Berg, Peder","Astrup, Arne","Salomo, Louise"],"cuid":["S02-098.68-715979"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["24h urine phosphorus","Acid base","Blood Pressure","Chronic kidney disease","Dietary intervention","Metabolic syndrome","New Nordic Renal Diet","Proteinuria","Weight loss","low dietary protein","low dietary sodium"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"health effects of the new nordic renal diet in patients with stage 000000000003 and 000000000004 chronic kidney disease compared with habitual diet a randomized trial","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajcnut.2023.08.008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.68-715979","identifier":[{"id":"37598748","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85171384471","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5e2f1854-fcd6-4f89-9e51-50c6803abd49","ku-958a5616-7c45-4a7a-a25d-f2cc7352841a"],"keyword":["24h urine phosphorus","New Nordic Renal Diet","acid base","blood pressure","chronic kidney disease","dietary intervention","low dietary protein","low dietary sodium","metabolic syndrome","proteinuria","weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6BD4F543A63A1DA799DD34DE9030C64D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajcnut.2023.08.008","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/408410543/1-s2.0-S0002916523660782-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375051257/1_s2.0_S0002916523660782_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Skou-bygningen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Nikita","key":"misellahansenpau","last":"Misella Hansen","locid":"318efa0a-440b-4901-8853-b20d0acbc5ab","name":"Hansen, Nikita Misella","name_org":"Misella Hansen, Nikita","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Lise","key":"kamperpau","last":"Kamper","name":"Kamper, Anne-Lise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"rixpau","last":"Rix","name":"Rix, Marianne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Bo","key":"feldtrasmussenpau","last":"Feldt-Rasmussen","locid":"cdd06e7b-83c5-4118-8808-eb4591586aac","name":"Feldt-Rasmussen, Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"leipzigerpau","last":"Leipziger","locid":"89f75d86-f3d8-4ed3-8754-24c9bcf0080c","name":"Leipziger, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6719-7034","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Vaarby","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f42195c2-31a1-460d-aecc-316e6dfe8baf","name":"Sørensen, Mads Vaarby","orcid":"0000-0001-6398-1035","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peder","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"e78b0bcb-ed5f-4b7d-ae94-1793d5d65e21","name":"Berg, Peder","orcid":"0000-0002-5216-2891","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","name":"Astrup, Arne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"salomopau","last":"Salomo","name":"Salomo, Louise","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37598748"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ajcnut.2023.08.008","issn":["00029165","19383207"],"issn_org":["00029165"],"issue":"5","journal":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","pages":"1042-1054","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","volume":"118"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171384471"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5e2f1854-fcd6-4f89-9e51-50c6803abd49","ku-958a5616-7c45-4a7a-a25d-f2cc7352841a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Health effects of the New Nordic Renal Diet in patients with stage 3 and 4 chronic kidney disease, compared with habitual diet : A randomized trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.68-715979","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this study, we conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis to summarize and evaluate the global research potential of different circulating miRNAs as an early diagnostic biomarker for OC. A systematic literature search for relevant studies was conducted in June 2020 and followed up in November 2021. The search was conducted in English databases (PubMed, ScienceDirect). The primary search resulted in a total of 1887 articles, which were screened according to the prior established inclusion and exclusion criteria. We identified 44 relevant studies, of which 22 were eligible for the quantitative meta-analysis. Statistical analysis was performed using the Meta-package in Rstudio. Standardized mean differences (SMD) of relative levels between control subjects and OC patients were used to evaluate the differential expression. All studies were quality evaluated using a Newcastle-Ottawa Scale. Based on the meta-analysis, nine miRNAs were identified as dysregulated in OC patients compared to controls. Nine were upregulated in OC patients compared to controls (miR-21, -125, -141, -145, -205, -328, -200a, -200b, -200c). Furthermore, miR-26, -93, -106 and -200a were analyzed, but did not present an overall significant difference between OC patients and controls. These observations should be considered when performing future studies of circulating miRNAs in relation to OC: sufficient size of clinical cohorts, development of consensus guidelines for circulating miRNA measurements, and coverage of previously reported miRNAs.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Frisk, Nanna Lond Skov","Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Pedersen, Ole Birger Vesterager","Dalgaard, Louise Torp"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716492"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biomarker","Diagnostics","Meta analysis","Ovarian cancer","Systematic review","miR 106","miR 141","miR 200b","miR 200c","miR 205","miR 21","miR 26","miR 328","miR 429","microRNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating micrornas for early diagnosis of ovarian cancer a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biom13050871","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-716492","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10216356","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85160373525","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37238740","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b32fded6-1b87-47cb-8b13-e022148a9738","ruc-40e7ccb3-9947-4c82-a880-4521628d12a7"],"keyword":["biomarker","diagnostics","meta-analysis","miR-106","miR-141","miR-200b","miR-200c","miR-205","miR-21","miR-26","miR-328","miR-429","microRNA","ovarian cancer","systematic review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D8D18F69D9724F115A91E9FE4147F16A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/95109076/biomolecules_13_00871.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biom13050871","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/374051054/biomolecules_13_00871.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical immunology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Nanna Lond Skov","key":"friskpau","last":"Frisk","locid":"25f309b3-6a87-40f7-8fe6-7475e7ecce58","name":"Frisk, Nanna Lond Skov","orcid":"0000-0001-6150-2408","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Anja Elaine","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7e5d1e2c-5d4b-4436-bb66-acdca4058c08","name":"Sørensen, Anja Elaine","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-5376","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ole Birger Vesterager","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0d43956a-6e43-42d7-8b29-4505d03ea5c8","name":"Pedersen, Ole Birger","name_org":"Pedersen, Ole Birger Vesterager","orcid":"0000-0003-2312-5976","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Louise Torp","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"a219fdaf-f994-4a7a-beb8-1f353846ed5a","name":"Dalgaard, Louise Torp","orcid":"0000-0002-3598-2775","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37238740"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/biom13050871","issn":["2218273X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Biomolecules","paperid":"871","status":"p","title":"Biomolecules","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160373525"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b32fded6-1b87-47cb-8b13-e022148a9738","ruc-40e7ccb3-9947-4c82-a880-4521628d12a7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Circulating microRNAs for Early Diagnosis of Ovarian Cancer : A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-716492","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Postmenopausal women are at risk of developing an overactive bladder (OAB). Conventional vaginal estrogen has shown promise for symptom relief. Isoflavones have proven effective as an alternative to estrogen treatment against menopause-related symptoms. However, its effect on OAB symptoms has not been studied. This study investigates if fermented red clover isoflavones reduce OAB symptoms in postmenopausal women. In this randomized, double-blinded, placebo-controlled trial, women were administered red clover extract (RCE) or a placebo twice daily for three months. Women filled out the International Consultation on Incontinence Questionnaire Overactive Bladder (ICIQ-OAB) and Urinary Incontinence Short Form (ICIQ-UI-SF), together with a fluid intake and voiding diary. A total of 33 women (16 in the RCE group and 17 in the placebo group) were included in the analysis. Baseline demographics and OAB characteristics were comparable across groups. Intake of RCE did not lead to significant relief in most urinary bladder symptom measures, although a significant reduction in the bother of urinary urgency (p = 0.033) and a tendency towards a decreased ICIQ-OAB score were observed (p = 0.056). In contrast, the placebo exhibited a significant decrease in the ICIQ-OAB score (p = 0.021) and in some diary outcomes. We found that an intake of isoflavones did not relieve OAB symptoms in postmenopausal women.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Villadsen, Annemarie Brusen","Holm-Jacobsen, Julie Niemann","Prabhala, Bala K.","Bundgaard-Nielsen, Caspar","Huntjens, Pam","Kornum, Jette Brommann","Glavind, Karin","Leutscher, Peter Derek Christian","Christensen, Lars P.","Jeppesen, Per B.","Sørensen, Suzette","Arenholt, Louise Thomsen Schmidt"],"cuid":["S03-098.29-715713"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Arenholt, Louise Thomsen Schmidt"],"keyword":["Estrogens therapeutic use","Female","Humans","Isoflavones","Overactive bladder","Postmenopause","Quality of Life","Red clover","Surveys and Questionnaires","Treatment Outcome","Trifolium","Urinary Bladder","Urinary Bladder Overactive drug therapy","Urinary incontinence"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of fermented red clover isoflavones in the treatment of overactive bladder in postmenopausal women a randomized double blinded placebo controlled trial","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu15194165","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was funded by “Ulla og Mogens Folmer Andersen’s Legat”, “Marie Pedersen og Jensine Heiberg’s Legat”, “Niels Jensens Forskningslegat”, “Region Nordjyllands Sundhedsvidenskabelige Forskningsfond”, “Torben og Alice Frimodt’s Legat”, “Aase og Ejnar Danielsen’s Legat”, and “Lilly og Herbert Hansen’s Legat”. The funding organizations were not involved in protocol formulation or data analysis, the decision to publish, or the preparation of the manuscript."],"id":"S03-098.29-715713","identifier":[{"id":"85173823809","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10574253","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37836449","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-8bd2ffbd-8461-4917-8435-a4688c47bfc1","au-0c4ddeab-d870-4f9c-9de9-0fd8a6a50d90","sdu-08006969-c299-4ddb-896c-73f2d01dabaa"],"keyword":["Estrogens/therapeutic use","Female","Humans","Postmenopause","Quality of Life","Surveys and Questionnaires","Treatment Outcome","Trifolium","Urinary Bladder","Urinary Bladder, Overactive/drug therapy","Urinary Incontinence","isoflavones","overa