","key":"bonfilspau","last":"Bonfils","locid":"54d2dc84-1696-4dea-96ca-ca070e660ca8","name":"Bonfils, Inge Storgaard","name_org":"Bonfils, Inge Birthe Storgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7219-9061","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Møldrup","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Louise Møldrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"maribopedh","last":"Maribo","name":"Maribo, Thomas","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Claus","key":"vinternielsenpedh","last":"Vinter Nielsen","name":"Vinter Nielsen, Claus","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte","key":"møllerstamppedh","last":"Møller Stamp","name":"Møller Stamp, Birgitte","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe","key":"sørensenpedh","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Dorthe","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"3.","isbn":["9788712065500"],"pages":"87-98","place":"København","publisher":"Gad","status":"p","title":"Rehabilitering - en grundbog"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-5fdd602c-50f7-4510-aa07-395ee6329de2"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Konteksten","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677371","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Aims: The increasing prevalence of childhood obesity escalates the risk for related complications. Circulating microRNAs (miRNAs) have been suggested as good predictive markers of insulin resistance in those with obesity. The aim was to identify a circulating miRNA profile that reflects insulin resistance in prepubertal children with obesity. Material and methods: Plasma miRNAs were measured in prepubertal children (n = 63, 5–9 years) using TaqMan Advanced miRNA Human Serum/Plasma plates and then were validated by RT-qPCR. Subjects were divided into normal weight (n = 20, NW) and overweight or obese (n = 43, OW/OB) groups according to their BMI z-scores. The OW/OB group was further subdivided into insulin sensitive or metabolically healthy obese (n = 26, MHO) and insulin resistant or metabolically unhealthy obese (n = 17, MUO) according to HOMA-IR. Key findings: While no differences were observed in the fasting plasma glucose levels, serum insulin levels were significantly elevated in the OW/OB compared to the NW group. Of 188 screened miRNAs, eleven were differentially expressed between the NW and OW/OB groups. Validation confirmed increased circulating levels of miR-146a-5p and miR-18a-5p in the OW/OB group, which correlated with BMI z-score. Interestingly, miR-146a-5p was also correlated with HOMA-IR index. While only miR-18a-5p was upregulated in the OW/OB children, independently of their degree of insulin sensitivity, miR-146-5p, miR-423-3p and miR-152-3p were associated with insulin resistance. Significance: The present study provides evidence of molecular alterations that occur early in life in prepubertal obesity. These alterations may potentially be crucial for targeted prevention or prompt precision therapeutic development and subsequent interventions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Santos, Diana","Porter-Gill, Patricia","Goode, Grace","Delhey, Leanna","Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Rose, Shannon","Børsheim, Elisabet","Dalgaard, Louise Torp","Carvalho, Eugenia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-684928"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal","United States"],"glorg":["APDP – Portuguese Diabetes Association","All Global Affiliations","Arkansas Children's Research Institute","University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences","University of Coimbra"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Early molecular alterations","Insulin Resistance","MicroRNAs","Prepubertal obesity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating microrna levels differ in the early stages of insulin resistance in prepubertal children with obesity","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/87958550/Manuscript_LFS_D_22_03037_R1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-684928","identifier":[{"id":"85143372349","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36455651","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ruc-ea3923a0-bcb3-4a85-8cbc-6a2cb96802cc"],"keyword":["Biomarker","Early molecular alterations","Insulin resistance","Prepubertal obesity","microRNAs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-483E515798FC6B0D7B2519AD073351D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/87958550/Manuscript_LFS_D_22_03037_R1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"university of coimbra","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Coimbra","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"arkansas children s research institute","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Arkansas Children's Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of arkansas for medical sciences","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"pt","key":"apdp portuguese diabetes association","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"APDP – Portuguese Diabetes Association","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Diana","key":"santospau","last":"Santos","name":"Santos, Diana","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Patricia","key":"portergillpau","last":"Porter-Gill","name":"Porter-Gill, Patricia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Grace","key":"goodepau","last":"Goode","name":"Goode, Grace","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Leanna","key":"delheypau","last":"Delhey","name":"Delhey, Leanna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Anja Elaine","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7e5d1e2c-5d4b-4436-bb66-acdca4058c08","name":"Sørensen, Anja Elaine","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-5376","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Shannon","key":"rosepau","last":"Rose","name":"Rose, Shannon","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Elisabet","key":"børsheimpau","last":"Børsheim","name":"Børsheim, Elisabet","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Louise Torp","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"a219fdaf-f994-4a7a-beb8-1f353846ed5a","name":"Dalgaard, Louise Torp","orcid":"0000-0002-3598-2775","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 4 5","first":"Eugenia","key":"carvalhopau","last":"Carvalho","name":"Carvalho, Eugenia","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36455651"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lfs.2022.121246","issn":["00243205","18790631"],"issn_org":["00243205"],"journal":"Life Sciences","paperid":"121246","status":"p","title":"Life Sciences","volume":"312"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143372349"],"sdg":["1. No Poverty","10. Reduced Inequalities","3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-ea3923a0-bcb3-4a85-8cbc-6a2cb96802cc"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Circulating microRNA levels differ in the early stages of insulin resistance in prepubertal children with obesity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-684928","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: A predominant side effect of radiotherapy for head and neck cancer is salivary gland hypofunction and xerostomia leading to debilitating oral disorders and impaired quality of life (QoL). Intraglandular mesenchymal stem cell therapy has shown promising results as a treatment for xerostomia. Methods: This is a randomised, double-blinded, placebo-controlled, parallel-group, prospective, single-centre trial investigating the safety, tolerability, and effectiveness of allogeneic stem cells as a treatment for radiation-induced hyposalivation and xerostomia for previous head and neck cancer patients. We will include a total of 120 patients who previously have been treated with radiotherapy for a head and neck cancer in Denmark. Participants will be randomly assigned using block randomisation to one of two parallel groups in a 1:1 ratio to receive ultrasound-guided injection of allogeneic adipose-derived mesenchymal stem cell (ASC) (n = 60) or placebo (n = 60) into the submandibular glands. Placebo will consist of CryoStor10 (BiolifeSolutions), the freeze media for ASCs containing 10% dimethyl sulfoxide (DMSO). The primary endpoint is change in unstimulated whole saliva flow rate. The secondary endpoints are change in stimulated whole saliva flow rate, QoL, and composition of saliva. Further secondary endpoints are safety and immune response (human leukocyte antigen (HLA) response) to the stem cells will be assessed. Patients are evaluated at baseline (before treatment), after 4 months, and after 12 months. All study personnel, except study personnel thawing and preparing the treatment for injection, and participants will be blinded to group assignment. Unblinded study personnel will not participate in the outcome assessment. Discussion: The trials will investigate the efficacy and safety of ASC injection to the submandibular gland as a potential new treatment for post-radiation xerostomia. We hope the results will pave the way for a clinically relevant treatment to ameliorate patients with xerostomia, a severely hampering condition. Trial registration: The study is approved by the Danish Data Protection Agency (protocol number P-2020-1164), the National Ethics Committee protocol number: (Protocol number: 1802872), and the Danish Medical Agency (2018-000348-24). The protocol was registered at the ClinicalTrials.gov database (NCT04776538).","author_count":15,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Kathrine Kronberg","Carlander, Amanda Louise Fenger","Grønhøj, Christian","Todsen, Tobias","Melchiors, Jacob","Paaske, Natasja","Madsen, Anne Kathrine Østergaard","Kastrup, Jens","Ekblond, Annette","Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","Farhadi, Mohammad","Maare, Christian","Friborg, Jeppe","Lynggard, Charlotte Duch","von Buchwald, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749212"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Hyposalivation","MSC","Mesenchymal stem cells","Mesenchymal stromal cells","Xerostomia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effectiveness and safety of mesenchymal stem stromal cell for radiation induced hyposalivation and xerostomia in previous head and neck cancer patients mesrix iii a study protocol for a single centre double blinded randomised placebo controlled phase ii study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-023-07594-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-749212","identifier":[{"id":"85169527650","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10474624","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37658468","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d312a3f7-1628-4fdf-85a0-98129d6fd3d6"],"keyword":["Hyposalivation","MSC","Mesenchymal stem cells","Mesenchymal stromal cells","Xerostomia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67CF24C247CCFCBE568C68F2B25E296D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/397384831/s13063_023_07594_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-023-07594-5","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Otorhinolaryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kathrine Kronberg","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, Kathrine Kronberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Amanda Louise Fenger","key":"carlanderpau","last":"Carlander","name":"Carlander, Amanda Louise Fenger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pa