{"abstract":"River water surface slopes (WSS) can improve the performance of rating curves for discharge estimates and provides information about river hydraulic processes and phenomena. Utilising the beam pattern of ICESat-2, the WSS can be estimated by the slope of a linear regression of the water surface elevation and the distance along the river. This paper presents a robust processing scheme for calculating WSS along rivers in the SWOT River Database. We demonstrate the processing scheme for the Amur River basin using four years of data. This yields 7306 WSS estimates across 1693 reaches approximately 10 km in length. The slopes were estimated between 0.60 cm/km and 651.04 cm/km with a median standard error of 0.47 cm/km. The method works for slopes larger than 0.5 cm/km and river widths larger than 50 m. The software presented in this paper is available as the R package ICE2WSS on Github (https://github.com/lindchr/ICE2WSS).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Linda","Bauer-Gottwein, Peter","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Nielsen, Karina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-694907"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Christoffersen, Linda"],"keyword":["Hydrology","ICESat 2","Laser altimetry","R package"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ice000000000002wss an r package for estimating river water surface slopes from icesat 000000000002","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envsoft.2023.105789","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-694907","identifier":[{"id":"85168535254","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-57a0d86c-281a-4628-94a6-560e82984fd3"],"keyword":["Hydrology","ICESat-2","Laser altimetry","R package","River water surface slope","SWOT river database"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DACDBEB99C434C2904C215F3C2FC9118"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envsoft.2023.105789","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/336755075/1-s2.0-S1364815223001755-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Geodesy and Earth Observation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Linda","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"ada5479c-ca29-42af-b586-1a642ad85ed9","name":"Christoffersen, Linda","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"bauergottweinpau","last":"Bauer-Gottwein","locid":"3ec7650b-0b07-4092-8a01-1ee18a996436","name":"Bauer-Gottwein, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9861-4240","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karina","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"35a43dde-d05b-4527-b0e7-1094f9e66c04","name":"Nielsen, Karina","orcid":"0000-0002-0035-1869","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envsoft.2023.105789","issn":["13648152","18736726"],"issn_org":["13648152"],"journal":"Environmental Modelling & Software","paperid":"105789","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Environmental Modelling & Software","title_org":"Environmental Modelling and Software","volume":"168"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168535254"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-57a0d86c-281a-4628-94a6-560e82984fd3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"ICE2WSS; An R package for estimating river water surface slopes from ICESat-2","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-694907","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Grønlund, Louise","Sørensen, Pernille","Bennetzen, Amalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-706381"],"event":{"end":"2023-07-06","place":"København, dk","start":"2023-07-02","title":"UIA World Congress of Architects 2023 Copenhagen","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Daylight","Daylight Model"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"poetic daylight a scale model","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-706381","ids":["arkc-65385a88-00bf-4084-a78d-e5de958b5e31"],"keyword":["Daylight","Daylight Model","Nej","Scale model 1:20"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-591C948C1AD88F1FFD16A8C604E6B998"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Center for Interior Studies","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Light in Architecture and Design","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Design"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"grønlundoth","last":"Grønlund","locid":"b5bd2523-ca04-4275-9a2f-e81f54f9f017","name":"Grønlund, Louise","rank":1,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"sørensenppu","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Pernille","rank":2,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalie","key":"bennetzenppu","last":"Bennetzen","name":"Bennetzen, Amalie","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-65385a88-00bf-4084-a78d-e5de958b5e31"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Poetic Daylight - a scale model","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-706381","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Cardiorespiratory fitness measured as ?VO 2max is considered an important variable in the risk prediction of cardiovascular disease and all-cause mortality. Non-exercise ?VO 2max prediction models are applicable, but lack accuracy. Here a model for the prediction of ?VO 2max using seismocardiography (SCG) was investigated. 97 healthy participants (18-65 yrs., 51 females) underwent measurement of SCG at rest in the supine position combined with demographic data to predict ?VO 2max before performing a graded exercise test (GET) on a cycle ergometer for determination of ?VO 2max using pulmonary gas exchange measurements for comparison. Accuracy assessment revealed no significant difference between SCG and GET ?VO 2max (mean±95% CI; 38.3±1.6 and 39.3±1.6 ml·min -1·kg -1, respectively. P=0.075). Further, a Pearson correlation of r=0.73, a standard error of estimate (SEE) of 5.9 ml·min -1·kg -1, and a coefficient of variation (CV) of 8±1% were found. The SCG ?VO 2max showed higher accuracy, than the non-exercise model based on the FRIENDS study, when this was applied to the present population (bias=-3.7±1.3 ml·min -1·kg -1, p<0.0001. r=0.70. SEE=7.4 ml·min -1·kg -1, and CV=12±2%). The SCG ?VO 2max prediction model is an accurate method for the determination of ?VO 2max in a healthy adult population. However, further investigation on the validity and reliability of the SCG ?VO 2max prediction model in different populations is needed for consideration of clinical applicability.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Mikkel Thunestvedt","Husted, Karina Louise Skov","Fogelstrøm, Mathilde","Rømer, Tue","Schmidt, Samuel","Sørensen, Kasper","Helge, Jørn"],"cuid":["S02-083.68-681328"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Exercise Test","Female","Heart Function Tests","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Oxygen Consumption","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["VentriJect"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accuracy of a clinical applicable method for prediction of vo sub 000000000002 sub max using seismocardiography","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/429745907/Accuracy_of_a_Clinical_Applicable_Method_for_Prediction.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-083.68-681328","identifier":[{"id":"36577438","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146638490","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fae1e7d7-f03e-44b9-a78f-145c160c437a","ku-3e6454ce-454e-461d-a57d-40189c9d9ad1"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Exercise Test","Female","Heart Function Tests","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Oxygen Consumption","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-49A3D543871BF7F8A82520EC45919AD4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/429745907/Accuracy_of_a_Clinical_Applicable_Method_for_Prediction.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Exercise and Muscle"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, CardioTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["VentriJect"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Thunestvedt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58070c3b-ed1e-4859-9467-29b512cdea42","name":"Hansen, Mikkel Thunestvedt","orcid":"0000-0002-3879-2192","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karina Louise Skov","key":"hustedpau","last":"Husted","locid":"6d16a70a-d967-4c50-8c2c-7625021b4586","name":"Husted, Karina Louise Skov","orcid":"0000-0002-9280-1694","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Mathilde","key":"fogelstrømpau","last":"Fogelstrøm","locid":"2a9fe837-0ae5-4c77-aab7-2d1ba510c60e","name":"Fogelstrom, Mathilde","name_org":"Fogelstrøm, Mathilde","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tue","key":"rømerpau","last":"Rømer","locid":"32b26587-2ba1-4451-b564-da70a76f4712","name":"Rømer, Tue","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Samuel Emil","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"bb4b7dd4-cb80-4ac8-971e-160921ec26a2","name":"Schmidt, Samuel","name_org":"Schmidt, Samuel Emil","orcid":"0000-0002-0917-634X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"81eaf062-83d5-4963-9de6-f713214ff461","name":"Sørensen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-0358-9354","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørn","key":"helgepau","last":"Helge","locid":"a5560afa-4f31-4278-8ae9-0c49fb0027c1","name":"Helge, Jørn Wulff","name_org":"Helge, Jørn","orcid":"0000-0001-9724-5423","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36577438"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1055/a-2004-4669","issn":["01724622","0943917X"],"issn_org":["01724622"],"issue":"9","journal":"International Journal of Sports Medicine","pages":"650-656","publisher":"Georg Thieme Verlag","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sports Medicine","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146638490"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fae1e7d7-f03e-44b9-a78f-145c160c437a","ku-3e6454ce-454e-461d-a57d-40189c9d9ad1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Accuracy of a Clinical Applicable Method for Prediction of VO2max Using Seismocardiography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.68-681328","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To describe characteristics of patients admitted with refractory cardiac arrest for possible extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation (ECPR) and gain insight into the reasons for refraining from treatment in some. Methods: Nationwide retrospective cohort study involving all tertiary centres providing ECPR in Denmark. Consecutive patients admitted with ongoing chest compression for evaluation for ECPR treatment were enrolled. Presenting characteristics, duration of no-flow and low-flow time, end-tidal carbon dioxide (ETCO2), lactate and pH, and recording of reasons for refraining from ECPR documented by the treating team were recorded. Outcomes were survival to intensive care unit admission and survival to hospital discharge. Results: Of 579 patients admitted with refractory cardiac arrest for possible ECPR, 221 patients (38%) proceeded to ECPR and 358 patients (62%) were not considered candidates. Median prehospital low-flow time was 70 min (IQR 56 to 85) in ECPR patients and 62 min (48 to 81) in no-ECPR patients, p<0.001. Intra-arrest transport was more than 50 km in 92 (42%) ECPR patients and 135 in no-ECPR patients (38%), p=0.25. The leading causes for not initiating ECPR stated by the treating team were duration of low-flow time in 39%, severe metabolic derangement in 35%, and in 31% low ETCO2. The prevailing combination of contributing factors were non-shockable rhythm, low ETCO2, and metabolic derangement or prehospital low-flow time combined with low ETCO2. Survival to discharge was only achieved in six patients (1.7%) in the no-ECPR group. Conclusions: In this large nationwide study of patients admitted for possible ECPR, two-thirds of patients were not treated with ECPR. The most frequent reasons to abstain from ECPR were long duration of prehospital low-flow time, metabolic derangement and low ETCO2.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Linde, Louise","Mørk, Sivagowry Rasalingam","Gregers, Emilie","Andreasen, Jo Bønding","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Schmidt, Henrik","Riber, Lars Peter","Thomassen, Sisse Anette","Laugesen, Helle","Eiskjær, Hans","Terkelsen, Christian Juhl","Christensen, Steffen","Tang, Mariann","Moeller-Soerensen, Hasse","Holmvang, Lene","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Hassager, Christian","Moller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S04-084.94-007871"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Moller, Jacob Eifer","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation adverse effects","Emergency medicine","Ethics Medical","Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation","Heart Assist Devices","Humans","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Patient Selection","Retrospective Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"selection of patients for mechanical circulatory support for refractory out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/heartjnl-2022-321405","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-084.94-007871","identifier":[{"id":"85138641183","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9872231","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36371665","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a2c562f3-c1b8-4f7d-a632-38929d2a2145","au-4e560555-0b88-4682-9da5-4a72980fd970","ku-bcb37826-a45d-4d74-bab8-655a6c3ea4f4","sdu-48d66005-80a7-43ee-800d-525ea2cdfd65"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation/adverse effects","EMERGENCY MEDICINE","Ethics, Medical","Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenatio