,"key":"hyltoftpau","last":"Hyltoft","locid":"b6acdd80-bb49-4fc2-bd81-2dfc2b03745e","name":"Hyltoft, Emilie M.","name_org":"Hyltoft, Emilie Marie Engelbrecht","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"dausørensenpau","last":"Dau Sørensen","locid":"694179e5-e3d4-42ef-aefe-e99906c0f78e","name":"Dau Sørensen, Elisabeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Astrid Ditte","key":"højgaardpau","last":"Højgaard","locid":"b29eeeec-d1b1-4971-afd7-a63fdadaa241","name":"Højgaard, Astrid Ditte","orcid":"0000-0002-8866-8181","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik Schiøler","key":"kesmodelpau","last":"Kesmodel","locid":"874905db-9134-43c7-83be-94f4fc6d8b62","name":"Kesmodel, Ulrik Schiøler","orcid":"0000-0003-3868-106X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte Schantz","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"1945772f-2516-4a29-9196-e026bf54ae1c","name":"Laursen, Birgitte Schantz","orcid":"0000-0003-4300-4645","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0ca10c67-cb36-4bf1-a0ba-e9cd8bbcd8b0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Offering cryopreservation of semen to transgender persons assigned male at birth - qualitative interviews on motivation and attitudes","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053736","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Manufacturing companies are increasingly engaging in digital transformation initiatives with the intent to improve the performance of their production operations. Nevertheless, a common challenge lies in understanding where to focus to obtain a significant production improvement, as well as in quantifying such potential. This research, structured according to the Design Science Research framework, proposes and demonstrates a novel tool – the Digital Factory Mapping – to address these issues. This analytic tool has been built on top of previous research efforts that shared the same intention, linking the continuous improvement philosophy with the digital maturity concept. The tool has been applied to four small- and medium-sized Danish manufacturers, validating its capability in facilitating the identification of company-specific production improvement opportunities, the formulation of digital innovation initiatives to capture them and the quantification of their potential. This paper contributes to the operations management body of knowledge by answering the need for frameworks to tangibly support the digital transformation process. From a managerial perspective, the feedback obtained by the four test cases highlighted how the tool generates an internal awareness concerning production improvement needs and digital innovation opportunities, catalyzing the execution of the suggested digital innovation initiatives by providing a quantification of their potential impact.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Colli, Michele","Wagner, Morten","Sørensen, Søren Bronnée","Wæhrens, Brian Vejrum"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113332"],"event":{"end":"2021-11-02","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2021-11-01","title":"8th Changeable, Agile, Reconfigurable and Virtual Production Conference, CARV 2021 and 10th World Mass Customization and Personalization Conference, MCPC 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Colli, Michele"],"keyword":["Continuous improvement","Digital innovation","Industry 4 0","Operations management","Production"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-FORC"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-FORC","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identifying production improvement opportunities enabled by digital innovation the digital factory mapping approach","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85119405789&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-113332","identifier":[{"id":"85119405789","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d9c6add5-0397-41d0-8060-3ac1dfacd4c7"],"keyword":["Continuous improvement","Digital innovation","Industry 4.0","Operations management","Production"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B20D1A49D932C1BA5242773F56CFA18C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"force technology","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-FORC","l3nn":"FORCE Technology","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"FORCE Technology","namevar":["FORCE Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-FORC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Operations and Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"collimichelepau","last":"Colli","name":"Colli, Michele","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"wagnermortenpau","last":"Wagner","name":"Wagner, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Bronnée","key":"sørensensørenbronnéepau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Søren Bronnée","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Brian Vejrum","key":"wæhrensbrianvejrumpau","last":"Wæhrens","locid":"b4ed4be4-3e26-4121-904a-bacd1ef30da1","name":"Wæhrens, Brian Vejrum","orcid":"0000-0001-6140-5587","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ann-Louise","key":"andersenannlouisepedh","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Ann-Louise","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus","key":"andersenrasmuspedh","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Rasmus","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas Ditlev","key":"brunoethomasditlevpedh","last":"Brunoe","name":"Brunoe, Thomas Ditlev","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria Stoettrup Schioenning","key":"larsenmariastoettrupschioenningpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Maria Stoettrup Schioenning","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kjeld","key":"nielsenkjeldpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Kjeld","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alessia","key":"napoleonealessiapedh","last":"Napoleone","name":"Napoleone, Alessia","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefan","key":"kjeldgaardstefanpedh","last":"Kjeldgaard","name":"Kjeldgaard, Stefan","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-90700-6_83","eisbn":["9783030907006"],"isbn":["9783030906993","9783030907020"],"issn":["21954356"],"pages":"730-737","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Mechanical Engineering","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 8th Changeable, Agile, Reconﬁgurable and Virtual Production Conference (CARV2021) and the 10th World Mass Customization &amp; Personalization Conference (MCPC2021), Aalborg, Denmark, October/November 2021","title":"Towards Sustainable Customization: Bridging Smart Products and Manufacturing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119405789"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d9c6add5-0397-41d0-8060-3ac1dfacd4c7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Identifying Production Improvement Opportunities Enabled by Digital Innovation : The Digital Factory Mapping Approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-113332","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: SARS-CoV-2 has resulted in a global pandemic since its outbreak in Wuhan, 2019. Virus transmission primarily occurs through close contact, respiratory droplets, and aerosol particles. However, since SARS-CoV-2 has been detected in fecal and rectal samples from infected individuals, the fecal-oral route has been suggested as another potential route of transmission. This study aimed to investigate the prevalence and clinical implications of rectal SARS-CoV-2 shedding in Danish COVID-19 patients.Methods: Hospitalized and non-hospitalized adults and children who were recently tested with a pharyngeal COVID-19 test, were included in the study. A rectal swab was collected from all participants. Hospitalized adults and COVID-19 positive children were followed with both pharyngeal and rectal swabs until two consecutive negative results were obtained. RT-qPCR targeting the envelope gene was used to detect SARS-CoV-2 in the samples. Demographic, medical, and biochemical information was obtained through questionnaires and medical records.Results: Twenty-eight of 52 (53.8%) COVID-19 positive adults and children were positive for SARS-CoV-2 in rectal swabs. Seven of the rectal positive participants were followed for more than 6 days. Two of these (28.6%) continued to test positive in their rectal swabs for up to 29 days after the pharyngeal swabs had turned negative. Hospitalized rectal positive and rectal negative adults were comparable regarding demographic, medical, and biochemical information. Furthermore, no difference was observed in the severity of the disease among the two groups.Conclusions: We provided evidence of rectal SARS-CoV-2 shedding in Danish COVID-19 patients. The clinical importance of rectal SARS-CoV-2 shedding appears to be minimal.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Holm-Jacobsen, Julie Niemann","Bundgaard-Nielsen, Caspar","Rold, Louise Søndergaard","Jensen, Ann-Maria","Shakar, Shakil Ahmad","Ludwig, Marc","Kirk, Karina Frahm","Donneborg, Mette Line","Vonasek, Julia Helena","Pedersen, Benjamin","Arenholt, Louise Thomsen Schmidt","Hagstrøm, Søren","Leutscher, Peter Derek Christian","Sørensen, Suzette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-123797"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Suzette"],"keyword":["Covid 19","Feces","Rectal shedding","SARS CoV 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the prevalence and clinical implications of rectal sars cov 000000000002 shedding in danish covid 000000000019 patients and the general population","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2021.804804","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-123797","identifier":[{"id":"85123779880","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35096894","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-fe089e2d-9177-47f4-a1ef-6f3d061691f0"],"keyword":["COVID-19","SARS-CoV-2","feces","rectal shedding","viral shedding"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-46104DA5ACD6FAFB8F00AB31EB620CE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2021.804804","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/459970671/Holm_Jacobsen_et_al._2022_The_Prevalence_and_Clinical_Implications_of_Rectal_SARS_CoV_2_Shedding_in_Danish_COVID_19_Patients_and_the_General_Population.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l