{"abstract":"Despite the accelerating number of uncultivated virus sequences discovered in metagenomics and their apparent importance for health and disease, the human gut virome and its interactions with bacteria in the gastrointestinal tract are not well understood. This is partly due to a paucity of whole-virome datasets and limitations in current approaches for identifying viral sequences in metagenomics data. Here, combining a deep-learning based metagenomics binning algorithm with paired metagenome and metavirome datasets, we develop Phages from Metagenomics Binning (PHAMB), an approach that allows the binning of thousands of viral genomes directly from bulk metagenomics data, while simultaneously enabling clustering of viral genomes into accurate taxonomic viral populations. When applied on the Human Microbiome Project 2 (HMP2) dataset, PHAMB recovered 6,077 high-quality genomes from 1,024 viral populations, and identified viral-microbial host interactions. PHAMB can be advantageously applied to existing and future metagenomes to illuminate viral ecological dynamics with other microbiome constituents.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Johansen, Joachim","Plichta, Damian R.","Nissen, Jakob Nybo","Jespersen, Marie Louise","Shah, Shiraz A.","Deng, Ling","Stokholm, Jakob","Bisgaard, Hans","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","Sørensen, Søren J.","Rasmussen, Simon"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-033903"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Simon"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Broad Institute of Harvard University and Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Harvard University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome binning of viral entities from bulk metagenomics data","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-28581-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-033903","identifier":[{"id":"35181661","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8857322","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85124932686","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000780120200011","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-3abc3f17-79ae-441d-94ef-587928511330","ku-152f5736-d036-4501-a392-22bcd3b18827"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BFED8641127C30DB2EEF95F86433C495"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/298733410/s41467_022_28581_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/270418533/s41467_022_28581_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-28581-5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Rasmussen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"broad in