"Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-7be9bd27-cd64-453b-8cde-91044ec398cb"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Towards Flexible PCB Assembly Using Simulation-Based Optimization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-608670","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Kidney transplant recipients (KTRs) have increased risk of human papillomavirus (HPV)-related anogenital (pre)cancers, including anal high-grade intraepithelial lesions and cancer. Previous studies on anal high-risk HPV (hrHPV) among KTRs are sparse. Methods: In a cross-sectional study, we included 247 KTRs and 248 controls from a dermatology department and 5 nephrology departments in Denmark during 2016-2017. All participants provided an anal cytobrush sample that was tested for HPV DNA. Participants completed a questionnaire on lifestyle and sexual habits. We used logistic regression to estimate odds ratios (ORs) of anal hrHPV in KTRs compared with controls and risk factors for anal hrHPV in KTRs. Results: The anal hrHPV prevalence was higher in female KTRs (45.5%) than in controls (27.2%). Female KTRs had almost 3-fold higher adjusted odds of anal hrHPV than controls (adjusted OR, 2.87 [95% confidence interval, 1.57-5.22]). In contrast, among men we did not observe increased prevalence or odds of anal hrHPV in KTRs compared with controls (prevalence, 19.4% vs 23.6%; adjusted OR, 0.85 [95% 95% confidence interval,. 44-1.64]). Among hrHPV-positive KTRs, 63% and 52% of men and women, respectively, were infected with hrHPV types covered by the nonavalent HPV vaccine (type 16, 18, 31, 33, 45, 52, or 58). Current smoking, >10 lifetime sexual partners, history of genital warts, and among men having had receptive anal sex were risk factors for anal hrHPV in KTRs. Conclusions: Female KTRs had an increased risk of anal hrHPV compared with immunocompetent controls. Our findings indicate that pretransplant HPV vaccination should be considered to prevent anal high-grade intraepithelial lesions and cancer caused by anal hrHPV infection in KTRs. Clinical Trials Registration: NCT03018327.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Haedersdal, Merete","Kjaer, Alexander K.","Bonde, Jesper Hansen","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Thomsen, Louise T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-670274"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anal","Human papillomavirus","Immunosuppression","Kidney transplant recipients"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anal human papillomavirus infection in kidney transplant recipients compared with immunocompetent controls","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-670274","identifier":[{"id":"35438132","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85144031618","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-62bbe617-b33f-4889-9751-017c8cf513d7"],"keyword":["anal","human papillomavirus","immunosuppression","kidney transplant recipients"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-033844E2F9F26D92EDD0891A9BBAF98E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Helle Kiellberg","key":"larsenhellekiellbergpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cff32a53-c07d-466a-9bf3-cc621c1e2cb6","name":"Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaersusannekpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merete","key":"haedersdalmeretepau","last":"Haedersdal","locid":"fef92f7f-7d21-4a42-903e-24071d35047b","name":"Haedersdal, Merete","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Alexander K.","key":"kjaeralexanderkpau","last":"Kjaer","name":"Kjaer, Alexander K.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper Hansen","key":"bondejesperhansenpau","last":"Bonde","name":"Bonde, Jesper Hansen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Schwartz","key":"sørensensørenschwartzpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Louise T.","key":"thomsenlouisetpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Louise T.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35438132"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/cid/ciac285","issn":["10584838","15376591"],"issn_org":["10584838"],"issue":"11","journal":"Clinical Infectious Diseases","pages":"1993-1999","status":"p","title":"Clinical Infectious Diseases","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144031618"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-62bbe617-b33f-4889-9751-017c8cf513d7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Anal Human Papillomavirus Infection in Kidney Transplant Recipients Compared with Immunocompetent Controls","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-670274","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background Children with congenital heart defects (CHD) have an increased risk of developmental delay. It remains sparsely investigated if these patients also have a delayed pubertal development. In this nationwide cohort study, we evaluated if CHD was associated with timing of puberty using longitudinally collected data on pubertal milestones. Methods and Results We used data from the Danish nationwide Puberty Cohort. Information on CHD was obtained from the Danish National Patient Register. Information on pubertal development was obtained from 15 780 children through questionnaires answered half-yearly from 11 years until 18 years or full maturity. Using a multivariable regression model for censored time-to-event data, mean difference in age at attaining each pubertal milestone was estimated, including a combined pubertal marker. Compared with children without CHD, analyses were performed for both CHD overall and subdivided into simple and complex CHD. In a subanalysis, analyses were repeated in children born at term. In total, 137 children (62 boys and 75 girls) had a CHD diagnosis. Overall, no difference in age at pubertal timing was observed for children with CHD compared with unaffected children. The average differences were small for both boys (1.6 [95% CI, -2.6 to 5.7] months) and girls (1.0 [95% CI, -2.5 to 4.4] months). The same differences were observed when subdividing into simple or complex CHD and when restricting to children born at term. Conclusions We found no association between CHD and pubertal timing. For the group of children with complex CHD, we were unable to exclude a later pubertal timing.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Udholm, Louise F","Gaml-Sørensen, Anne","Arendt, Linn Håkonsen","Brix, Nis","Lunddorf, Lea Lykke Harrits","Ernst, Andreas","Knudsen, Ulla Breth","Hjortdal, Vibeke E","Ramlau-Hansen, Cecilia Høst"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-028783"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Udholm, Louise F"],"keyword":["Congenital heart defects","Menarche","Puberty","Sexual Maturation","Sexual development"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"timing of pubertal development in boys and girls with congenital heart defects a nationwide cohort study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.121.023135","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.94-028783","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9075439","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35347999","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85128245547","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-de46c6d6-306e-407a-9859-6d5580659aba","ku-c4887eea-663c-4aef-a1df-e7b739ed69a7"],"keyword":["congenital heart defects","menarche","puberty","sexual development","sexual maturation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-95FDDED7B224BB9E6F8710F5ED9956EA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.121.023135","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/307756076/JAHA.121.023135.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise F","key":"udholmpau","last":"Udholm","name":"Udholm, Louise F","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"gamlsørensenpau","last":"Gaml-Sørensen","locid":"e0cfac79-955f-462b-9d78-ea3d0bbcb8db","name":"Gaml-Sørensen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-5242-939X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Linn H","key":"arendtpau","last":"Arendt","locid":"52f75e1e-f59e-487b-8094-ffe55c160ec3","name":"Arendt, Linn Håkonsen","name_org":"Arendt, Linn H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nis","key":"brixpau","last":"Brix","locid":"b7b20a3f-5e8e-405d-b27a-afbc74981902","name":"Brix, Nis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lea L H","key":"lunddorfpau","last":"Lunddorf","locid":"5f098e4a-40f0-4c63-87b8-93220e63a409","name":"Lunddorf, Lea Lykke Harrits","name_org":"Lunddorf, Lea L H","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"ernstpau","last":"Ernst","locid":"caa7bb72-d6c6-40ab-8ac4-e95c86d01a7b","name":"Ernst, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-5533-8891","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulla B","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"819b29d7-2cff-463c-821a-c79663795b76","name":"Knudsen, Ulla Breth","name_org":"Knudsen, Ulla B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Vibeke E.","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"69607db8-0b14-4d01-95f0-c114bbc826ef","name":"Hjortdal, Vibeke Elisabeth","name_org":"Hjortdal, Vibeke E.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cecilia H","key":"ramlauhansenpau","last":"Ramlau-Hansen","locid":"76e02a27-dc4a-4c88-968c-d82d47f9961f","name":"Ramlau-Hansen, Cecilia Høst","name_org":"Ramlau-Hansen, Cecilia H","orcid":"0000-0003-3296-0121","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35347999"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.121.023135","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e023135","publisher":"American Heart Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85128245547"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-de46c6d6-306e-407a-9859-6d5580659aba","ku-c4887eea-663c-4aef-a1df-e7b739ed69a7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Timing of Pubertal Development in Boys and Girls With Congenital Heart Defects : A Nationwide Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.94-028783","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: In refractory out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) with prolonged whole-body ischaemia, global tissue injury proceeds even after establishment of circulation with extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation (ECPR). We aimed to investigate the role of biomarkers reflecting hypoperfusion, inflammation, and organ injury in prognostication of patients with refractory OHCA managed with ECPR. METHODS AND RESULTS: This nationwide retrospective study included 226 adults with refractory OHCA managed with ECPR in Denmark (2011-2020). Biomarkers the first days after ECPR-initiation were assessed. Odds ratio of favourable neurological status (Cerebral Performance Category 1-2) at hospital discharge was estimated by logistic regression analyses. Cut-off values were calculated using the Youden's index. Fifty-six patients (25%) survived to hospital discharge, 51 (91%) with a favourable neurological status. Factors independently associated with favourable neurological status were low flow time <81 min, admission leukocytes ≥12.8 × 109/L, admission lactate <13.2 mmol/L, alkaline phosphatase (ALP) < 56 (day1) or <55 U/L (day2), and day 1 creatine kinase MB (CK-MB) < 500 ng/mL. Selected biomarkers (leukocytes, C-reactive protein, and lactate) were significantly better predictors of favourable neurological status than classic OHCA-variables (sex, age, low-flow time, witnessed arrest, shockable rhythm) alone (P = 0.001) after hospital admission. CONCLUSION: Biomarkers of hypoperfusion (lactate), inflammation (leucocytes), and organ injury (ALP and CK-MB) were independently associated with neurological status at hospital discharge. Biomarkers of hypoperfusion and inflammation (at hospital admission) and organ injury (days 1 and 2 after ECPR) may aid in the clinical decision of when to prolong or terminate ECPR in cases of refractory OHCA.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Gregers, Emilie","Mørk, Sivagowry Rasalingam","Linde, Louise","Andreasen, Jo Bønding","Smerup, Morten","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Møller-Sørensen, Peter Hasse","Holmvang, Lene","Christensen, Steffen","Terkelsen, Christian Juhl","Tang, Mariann","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Schmidt, Henrik","Riber, Lars Peter","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Thomassen, Sisse Anette","Laugesen, Helle","Hassager, Christian","Søholm, Helle"],"cuid":["S04-097.65-665735"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Gregers, Emilie"],"keyword":["Adult","Biomarkers","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation methods","Consensus statement","Coronary intervention","Elevation","Extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation","HOSPITAL CARDIAC ARREST","Humans","Hypoperfusion","Inflammation","Lactates","Neurological outcome","Organ injury","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest therapy","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Retrospective Studies","SCORE"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-HJER","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation a national study on the association between favourable neurological status and biomarkers of hypoperfusion inflammation and organ injury","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85162232273","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-097.65-665735","identifier":[{"id":"36229928","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000879846200001","type":"wos"