{"abstract":"MoLux is a shape-changing lamp designed to address some of the grand challenges in shape-changing interfaces (SCI). This includes the challenges of understanding the user experience, integrating interaction into the artefact, and conducting in-situ comparative studies with SCI. MoLux uses bi-directional and direct interaction, deploys shape-change for input and output, and enables manipulation of two independent shape-changing parameters. Through an in-situ study, we investigated how users experienced living with MoLux over four days. The study compared three different interaction paradigms; direct, indirect, and negotiated control. Our findings reveal that most users preferred negotiated interaction as well as enjoyed living with the shape-changing lamp. Our results further contribute some methodological lessons and implications for designing SCI for the home.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K","Bertelsen, Andreas Becker","Nordmark Hoffmann, Ninna","Petersen, Marianne Graves","Hoggan, Eve"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-162723"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-12","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2022-10-08","title":"12th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction: Participative Computing for Sustainable Futures, NordiCHI 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Interaction design","Research through Design","Shape changing interfaces"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"molux negotiating control with a shape changing lamp at home","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85140883598","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-162723","identifier":[{"id":"85140883598","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3a8fa657-b3d6-4d5a-8579-928547194e56"],"keyword":["actuated interface","in-situ study","interaction design","research through design","shape-changing interfaces"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-74601B82D014A6A869B81AAE81AF8107"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise Stisen Kjerstein","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"82f99f7d-c66a-4a81-bc6c-72792eee3017","name":"Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K","name_org":"Sørensen, Marie Louise Stisen Kjerstein","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Becker","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","locid":"162839d2-d245-4564-93e8-11d66f9c8f7c","name":"Bertelsen, Andreas Becker","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ninna","key":"nordmarkhoffmannpau","last":"Nordmark Hoffmann","locid":"3790d7d5-79df-434c-9435-bf37ca4c3506","name":"Nordmark Hoffmann, Ninna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Graves","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"da3161f7-ece7-471a-af07-f05e91059d3a","name":"Petersen, Marianne Graves","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eve","key":"hogganpau","last":"Hoggan","locid":"2eb4e432-9116-4a75-8144-3766c07762bc","name":"Hoggan, Eve","orcid":"0000-0002-2563-4320","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3546155.3547271","eisbn":["9781450396998"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Adjunct Proceedings of the 12th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction (NordiCHI'22)","title":"Participative Computing for Sustainable Futures"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140883598"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3a8fa657-b3d6-4d5a-8579-928547194e56"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"MoLux : Negotiating Control with a Shape-Changing Lamp at Home","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-162723","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Increasing incidence of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) calls for improved understanding of how the disease affects metabolic liver function. AIMS: To investigate in vivo effects of different NAFLD stages on metabolic liver function, quantified as regional and total capacity for galactose metabolism in a NAFLD model. METHODS: Male Sprague Dawley rats were fed a high-fat, high-cholesterol diet for 1 or 12 weeks, modelling early or late NAFLD, respectively. Each NAFLD group (n = 8 each) had a control group on standard chow (n = 8 each). Metabolic liver function was assessed by 2-[18F]fluoro-2-deoxy-D-galactose positron emission tomography; regional galactose metabolism was assessed as standardised uptake value (SUV). Liver tissue was harvested for histology and fat quantification. RESULTS: Early NAFLD had median 18% fat by liver volume. Late NAFLD had median 32% fat and varying features of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH). Median SUV reflecting regional galactose metabolism was reduced in early NAFLD (9.8) and more so in late NAFLD (7.4; p = 0.02), both significantly lower than in controls (12.5). In early NAFLD, lower SUV was quantitatively explained by fat infiltration. In late NAFLD, the SUV decrease was beyond that attributable to fat; probably related to structural NASH features. Total capacity for galactose elimination was intact in both groups, which in late NAFLD was attained by increased fat-free liver mass to 21 g, versus 15 g in early NAFLD and controls (both p ≤ 0.002). CONCLUSION: Regional metabolic liver function was compromised in NAFLD by fat infiltration and structural changes. Still, whole liver metabolic function was preserved in late NAFLD by a marked increase in the fat-free liver mass.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Eriksen, Peter Lykke","Thomsen, Karen Louise","Hamilton-Dutoit, Stephen Jacques","Vilstrup, Hendrik","Sørensen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-177106"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Diet High Fat adverse effects","Experimental animal model","Galactose metabolism","Liver pathology","Male","Metabolic liver function","Non alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease pathology","Non alcoholic fatty liver disease","Positron Emission Tomography","Rats","Rats Sprague Dawley"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental non alcoholic fatty liver disease causes regional liver functional deficits as measured by the capacity for galactose metabolism while whole liver function is preserved","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12876-022-02574-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-177106","identifier":[{"id":"36575375","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9793673","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85144786530","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-53c49d8d-9c3c-4f56-b917-3bc8ce7c79e2"],"keyword":["Animals","Diet, High-Fat/adverse effects","Experimental animal model","Galactose/metabolism","Liver/pathology","Male","Metabolic liver function","Non alcoholic fatty liver disease","Non-alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease/pathology","Positron emission tomography","Rats","Rats, Sprague-Dawley"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-61D8CE79AC3D7088B9B4E64B4AB92E4E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12876-022-02574-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hepatology and Gastroenterology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medicinsk afdeling, Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Lykke","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"02b5f3f7-8692-403b-9a17-1dc588d638e7","name":"Eriksen, Peter Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-1115-8308","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen Louise","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"32baa31f-0b93-4c6d-af7e-0da0519f574f","name":"Thomsen, Karen Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stephen","key":"hamiltondutoitpau","last":"Hamilton-Dutoit","locid":"9b291bda-53d8-40c3-a0f6-564aefbe8300","name":"Hamilton-Dutoit, Stephen Jacques","name_org":"Hamilton-Dutoit, Stephen","orcid":"0000-0003-2158-3885","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hendrik","key":"vilstruppau","last":"Vilstrup","locid":"9e1905f3-3094-4aea-bbde-7178733bf6cb","name":"Vilstrup, Hendrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"52635821-2c0d-418e-848d-e3e1f1175e12","name":"Sørensen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-8750-4329","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36575375"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12876-022-02574-6","issn":["1471230X"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Gastroenterology","paperid":"541","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Gastroenterology","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144786530"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-53c49d8d-9c3c-4f56-b917-3bc8ce7c79e2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Experimental non-alcoholic fatty liver disease causes regional liver functional deficits as measured by the capacity for galactose metabolism while whole liver function is preserved","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-177106","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Providing opportunities for students to collaborate while developing their computational thinking (CT) is a challenge, particularly for remote collaboration. To address this issue, an interdisciplinary team derived a set of design rationales (integration of learning activities, scaffolding progression, cross-device interaction and supporting collaboration in all activities) and developed CoTinker: a collaborative, cross-device tool designed to foster equity in the form of equal participation amongst students. Through a pilot study, we investigated high-school students (n=15), working with CT activities supported by CoTinker, in the form of a computer model of a biological phenomenon. We found that CoTinker was able to support students’ remote collaborative work and participation equity. Furthermore, students were able to take advantage of cross-device interaction using their laptop and mobile phones in concert. We conclude that the design rationales and CoTinker design can serve as useful starting points for enabling equitable collaboration amongst students working with CT.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Musaeus, Line Have","Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K","Palfi, Blanka Sara","Iversen, Ole Sejer","Klokmose, Clemens Nylandsted","Petersen, Marianne Graves"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-185727"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-12","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2022-10-08","title":"12th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction: Participative Computing for Sustainable Futures, NordiCHI 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Musaeus, Line Have"],"keyword":["CCTD","Computational thinking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cotinker designing a cross device collaboration tool to support computational thinking in remote group work in high school biology","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85140901398","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-185727","identifier":[{"id":"85140901398","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-62c98d25-9b9a-4b6d-9555-315c5c0334fd"],"keyword":["#CCTD","Computational Thinking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B2F8AD77A93CB0D3CDD695FF90755BC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Have","key":"musaeuspau","last":"Musaeus","locid":"cb00689c-3254-4d35-bc92-d0696cba7146","name":"Musaeus, Line Have","orcid":"0000-0002-2915-2767","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie-Louise Stisen K","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"82f99f7d-c66a-4a81-bc6c-72792eee3017","name":"Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Blanka Sara","key":"palfipau","last":"Palfi","locid":"3bee61bf-a9be-4313-a370-05560abfa9a0","name":"Palfi, Blanka Sara","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Sejer","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"445bdf88-e5a3-470b-ad4d-12a172f7c8a8","name":"Iversen, Ole Sejer","orcid":"0000-0002-8055-6716","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Clemens Nylandsted","key":"klokmosepau","last":"Klokmose","locid":"fad1a899-ad22-40bc-8b24-251b517a9c72","name":"Klokmose, Clemens Nylandsted","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Graves","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"da3161f7-ece7-471a-af07-f05e91059d3a","name":"Petersen, Marianne Graves","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3546155.3546709","eisbn":["9781450396998"],"place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 12th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction (NordiCHI’22)","title":"Participative Computing for Sustainable Futures"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140901398"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-62c98d25-9b9a-4b6d-9555-315c5c0334fd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"CoTinker: Designing a Cross-device Collaboration Tool to Support Computational Thinking in Remote Group Work in High School Biology","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-185727","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, computational thinking (CT) has focused on how children and citizens develop basic computing skills which empower them to participate in a digitised society and broaden participation and engagement with CT. We present the exploration of a craftsmanship-driven approach to engage people in CT. To explore this approach a team of knitters, a computer scientist and a computing education expert iteratively designed the KnitxCode workshop. KnitxCode utilises knitting in combination with CT concepts as the foundation for the activities. The workshop was evaluated by 12 participants with no programming experience and with knitting experience ranging from 2-25 years (M = 6). From the evaluation we found that the craftsmanship-driven approach seemed to provide the participants with confidence to learning CT, as shared concepts and practices between knitting and computing supported transitioning from knitting craftsmanship to computing and in this way served to demystify computing.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K","Fog, Bjarke Vognstrup","Musaeus, Line Have","Petersen, Marianne Graves"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-193763"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-12","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2022-10-08","title":"12th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction: Participative Computing for Sustainable Futures, NordiCHI 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K"],"keyword":["Applied computing","CCTD","HCI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"knit x code exploring a craftsmanship driven approach to computational thinking","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3547522.3547680","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-193763","identifier":[{"id":"85139819091","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-70d97c34-5209-44c6-8e4f-b3791af6294c"],"keyword":["#CCTD","HCI","applied computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2A2B8427CC54AD39F6748C5EC8AA2114"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3547522.3547680","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie-Louise Stisen K","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"82f99f7d-c66a-4a81-bc6c-72792eee3017","name":"Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarke Vognstrup","key":"fogpau","last":"Fog","locid":"f364aced-7950-4fd4-908e-de043633d1fd","name":"Fog, Bjarke Vognstrup","orcid":"0000-0001-7155-3735","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Have","key":"musaeuspau","last":"Musaeus","locid":"cb00689c-3254-4d35-bc92-d0696cba7146","name":"Musaeus, Line Have","orcid":"0000-0002-2915-2767","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Graves","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"da3161f7-ece7-471a-af07-f05e91059d3a","name":"Petersen, Marianne Graves","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3547522.3547680","eisbn":["9781450394482"],"place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Adjunct Proceedings of the 12th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction (NordiCHI'22)","title":"Participative Computing for Sustainable Futures"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139819091"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-70d97c34-5209-44c6-8e4f-b3791af6294c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Knit x Code : Exploring a Craftsmanship-driven Approach to Computational Thinking","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-193763","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"There is a growing focus on computational thinking (CT) in terms of supporting children's understanding of everyday technologies. But unlike other technologies, Augmented Reality (AR) has received limited attention. In this paper, we present ExposAR - a collaborative cross-device AR system enabling children to create, use, and reflect on AR technologies through the co-creation of a simple AR application. With ExposAR, we explore three core design principles: 1) reify computational concepts, 2) support collaborative cross-device authoring, and 3) incorporate the user's own world. These principles were developed through a co-design process with teachers and evaluated with 46 primary school students. We found that the collaborative authoring process with ExposAR supported students in understanding AR concepts and challenged their perspectives on AR. With these results, we bring AR to the CT agenda and contribute novel design principles for exposing the underlying mechanisms and implications of AR.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lunding, Mille Skovhus","Grønbæk, Jens Emil","Bilstrup, Karl-Emil Kjær","Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K","Petersen, Marianne Graves"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-206157"],"event":{"end":"2022-05-05","place":"Virtual, Online, us","start":"2022-04-30","title":"2022 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems, CHI 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Augmented reality","Computational thinking","Education","Interactive Learning System"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exposar bringing augmented reality to the computational thinking agenda through a collaborative authoring tool","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85130585085","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-206157","identifier":[{"id":"85130585085","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8692a910-f35a-438d-b3db-350986e00d77"],"keyword":["Augmented reality","computational thinking","education","interactive learning system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8B7E7888D569C868030CEA91A840341D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mille Skovhus","key":"lundingpau","last":"Lunding","locid":"806b2f20-b7ae-4ebc-a32f-98ee39a53380","name":"Lunding, Mille Skovhus","orcid":"0000-0002-5829-2208","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Emil Sloth","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"cb34ed1e-a18d-4b6d-8f80-1cace0ea64c2","name":"Grønbæk, Jens Emil","name_org":"Grønbæk, Jens Emil Sloth","orcid":"0000-0002-9566-7195","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karl Emil Kjær","key":"bilstruppau","last":"Bilstrup","locid":"3075671d-6078-4cd1-b0f1-ae0a4e575296","name":"Bilstrup, Karl-Emil Kjær","name_org":"Bilstrup, Karl Emil Kjær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise Stisen Kjerstein","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"82f99f7d-c66a-4a81-bc6c-72792eee3017","name":"Sørensen, Marie-Louise Stisen K","name_org":"Sørensen, Marie Louise Stisen Kjerstein","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Graves","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"da3161f7-ece7-471a-af07-f05e91059d3a","name":"Petersen, Marianne Graves","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3491102.3517636","eisbn":["9781450391573"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CHI 2022 - Proceedings of the 2022 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130585085"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8692a910-f35a-438d-b3db-350986e00d77"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"ExposAR : Bringing Augmented Reality to the Computational Thinking Agenda through a Collaborative Authoring Tool","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-206157","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Selection of optimal tracer activity for 82Rb PET is based on a trade-off between necessary count-statistics in the late static phase and detector saturation in the early blood-pool phase. Administered tracer activity recommended in prescribing information differs substantially from recommendations in current literature. The present study examines the effect on both absolute myocardial blood flow (MBF), myocardial flow reserve (MFR) and relative myocardial perfusion imaging (MPI) of reducing dose.Methods: Forty patients were scanned twice on a PMT-based PET/CT (GE D690): At recommended activity (1110 MBq) and at either 740 or 370 MBq. MBF, MFR, total perfusion deficit (TPD) and ejection fractions (EF) were quantified. Results were compared using linear regression and Bland–Altman plots.Results: Linear correlation between MBF at 1110 MBq at either reduced activity had an R2 > 0.98. A small bias (± 5%-9%) was observed with opposite signs for 1110/740 and 1110/370. Limits of agreement for MBF were larger for 1110/370. MFR had a lower linear correlation (R2 = 0.96), but wide limits of agreement especially for 1110/370. TPD and EF correlated well at 1110/740 (R2 = 0.96 and 0.99, respectively), but large scatter was observed for 1110/370.Conclusion: Reduction of the tracer activity to 740 MBq, significantly reduced dead-time correction factors, while still producing reliable static and gated images. However, despite large dead-time at 1110 MBq, no systematic bias on absolute MBF was observed compared to reduced activities.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hoff, Camilla Molich","Sørensen, Jens","Christensen, Nana Louise","Bouchelouche, Kirsten","Tolbod, Lars Poulsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-236331"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Accuracy","Coronary Artery Disease diagnostic imaging","Coronary Circulation physiology","Humans","Image analysis","Instrumentation","MPI","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging methods","Myocardial blood flow","PET","Perfusion","Positron Emission Tomography Computed Tomography","Positron Emission Tomography methods","Quantification","Rb 82 PET","Rubidium Radioisotopes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"activity regimes for 000000000082rb cardiac pet effects on absolute mbf and mpi","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85088019835","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-236331","identifier":[{"id":"32676911","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000549247200008","type":"wos"},{"id":"85088019835","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bb621811-796e-4192-b3a7-251fb7ca8174"],"keyword":["ACCURACY","Coronary Artery Disease/diagnostic imaging","Coronary Circulation/physiology","Humans","MPI","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging/methods","PERFUSION","PET","Positron Emission Tomography Computed Tomography","Positron-Emission Tomography/methods","QUANTIFICATION","RB-82 PET","Rubidium Radioisotopes","image analysis","instrumentation","myocardial blood flow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-12B374E7C0DB8550CB0C520CD4321CC3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Nuclear Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla Molich","key":"hoffpau","last":"Hoff","locid":"d6575e2b-ad37-43f4-9803-3528b63b0061","name":"Hoff, Camilla Molich","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"cab278f0-6db5-48a8-8764-b7da319d7818","name":"Sørensen, Jens","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nana Louise","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"796a6fa5-29d9-40b3-b549-0610eb49705c","name":"Christensen, Nana Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-9936-1636","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirsten","key":"bouchelouchepau","last":"Bouchelouche","locid":"f253980f-a953-448a-bdfb-2a0fcfe82101","name":"Bouchelouche, Kirsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Poulsen","key":"tolbodpau","last":"Tolbod","locid":"a1e56507-eb80-4f94-9470-df90dcecbc62","name":"Tolbod, Lars Poulsen","orcid":"0000-0002-8105-7046","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32676911"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12350-020-02266-2","issn":["10713581","15326551"],"issn_org":["10713581"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Nuclear Cardiology","pages":"449-460","publisher":"American Society of Nuclear Cardiology","status":"p","title":"Journal of Nuclear Cardiology","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088019835"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bb621811-796e-4192-b3a7-251fb7ca8174"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Activity regimes for 82Rb cardiac PET : Effects on absolute MBF and MPI.","type":"Journal Article"