{"abstract":"We have established and describe two measurement procedures to diagnose possible zinc (Zn) deficiency; albumin-corrected Zn concentration and available free Zn-binding capacity. Reference intervals for both biomarkers were established in healthy adults from the Danish population. The clinical usefulness of the measurement procedures was investigated in patients with cirrhosis and in patients given parenteral nutrition due to short bowel syndrome. The results of both methods indicate that there is a risk of overdiagnosing Zn deficiency based on low plasma Zn concentrations. Needless Zn supplementation may thus be avoided by using the albumin-corrected Zn concentration or available free Zn-binding capacity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Louise Helskov","Sørensen, Mia Dahl","Lauridsen, Mette Munk","Rasmussen, Lars Melholt","Alfiler, Rose M.","Iversen, Vilde N.","Schaffalitzky de Muckadell, Ove B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-597335"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Schaffalitzky de Muckadell, Ove B."],"keyword":["Adult","Albumin","Albumins","Biomarkers","Humans","Reference interval","Zinc"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"albumin corrected zn and available free zn binding capacity as indicators of zn status potential for clinical implementation","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85133188043","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-597335","identifier":[{"id":"35758940","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85133188043","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-541301c8-78ac-42ef-8e21-907236794b81"],"keyword":["Adult","Albumins","Biomarkers","Humans","Zinc","albumin","reference interval","zinc status"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-17F9EF78293C478B11D6AEF293332347"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Biochemistry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise H.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"9377a3d2-d14c-46cd-9deb-66359f638eea","name":"Jørgensen, Louise Helskov","name_org":"Jørgensen, Louise H.","orcid":"0000-0001-9982-1236","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mia D.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"3524a591-0bd0-4849-b735-4b916b84defb","name":"Sørensen, Mia Dahl","name_org":"Sørensen, Mia D.","orcid":"0000-0002-0105-2940","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette M.","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"47ea3fdf-66e2-4eb3-ade8-aaf22d015ee9","name":"Lauridsen, Mette Munk","name_org":"Lauridsen, Mette M.","orcid":"0000-0003-0586-8549","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L. M.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"bf5d4e3b-cb51-4e61-a6d1-e22445213324","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Melholt","name_org":"Rasmussen, L. M.","orcid":"0000-0001-5795-4794","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rose M.","key":"alfilerpau","last":"Alfiler","name":"Alfiler, Rose M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vilde N.","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Vilde N.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ove B.","key":"schaffalitzkydemuckadellpau","last":"Schaffalitzky de Muckadell","locid":"3bc4ff3b-1f9d-4045-85de-b1d6d16f57f3","name":"Schaffalitzky de Muckadell, Ove B.","orcid":"0000-0003-1969-2329","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35758940"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00365513.2022.2064764","issn":["00365513","0085591X"],"issn_org":["00365513"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","pages":"261-266","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","title_org":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical and Laboratory Investigation","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133188043"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-541301c8-78ac-42ef-8e21-907236794b81"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Albumin-corrected Zn and available free Zn-binding capacity as indicators of Zn status : potential for clinical implementation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-597335","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Context: In adults, hyperglucagonemia is associated with type 2 diabetes, impaired glucose tolerance, and obesity. The role of glucagon in pediatric overweight/obesity remains unclear. Objective: We examined whether fasting concentrations of glucagon are elevated in youth with overweight/obesity and whether this associates with cardiometabolic risk profiles. Methods: Analyses were based on the cross-sectional HOLBAEK study, including children and adolescents 6 to 19 years of age, with overweight/obesity from an obesity clinic group (n = 2154) and with normal weight from a population-based group (n = 1858). Fasting concentrations of plasma glucagon and cardiometabolic risk outcomes were assessed, and multiple linear and logistic regressions models were performed. Results: The obesity clinic group had higher glucagon concentrations than the population-based group (P < 0.001). Glucagon positively associated with body mass index (BMI) standard deviation score (SDS), waist, body fat %, liver fat %, alanine transaminase (ALT), high-sensitivity C-reactive protein, homeostasis model assessment of insulin resistance, insulin, C-peptide, LDL-C, triglycerides, SDS of diastolic and systolic blood pressure, and was inversely associated with fasting glucose. The inverse relationship between glucagon and glucose was attenuated in individuals with high BMI SDS and high fasting insulin. Glucagon was associated with a higher prevalence of insulin resistance, increased ALT, dyslipidemia, and hypertension, but not with hyperglycemia. Glucagon was positively associated with fasting total glucagon-like peptide-1. Conclusion: Compared with normal weight peers, children and adolescents with overweight/obesity had elevated concentrations of fasting glucagon, which corresponded to worsened cardiometabolic risk outcomes, except for hyperglycemia. This suggests hyperglucagonemia in youth may precede impairments in glucose regulation.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Stinson, Sara Elizabeth","Jonsson, Anna","Alzola, Ierai Fernández de Retana","Lund, Morten Asp Vonsild","Frithioff-Bøjsøe, Christine","Holm, Louise Aas","Fonvig, Cilius Esmann","Pedersen, Oluf","Ängquist, Lars","Sørensen, Thorkild I A","Holst, Jens Juul","Christiansen, Michael","Holm, Jens-Christian","Hartmann, Bolette","Hansen, Torben"],"cuid":["S02-097.28-045721"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Torben"],"keyword":["Adiposity physiology","Adolescent","Blood Glucose metabolism","Body Mass Index","Cardiometabolic risk","Cardiometabolic risk factors","Cardiovascular Diseases epidemiology","Child","Cross Sectional Studies","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Glucagon","Glucose","Humans","Hyperglycemia","Hyperglycemia complications","Insulin Resistance","Insulin metabolism","Obesity","Overweight complications","Pediatric Obesity complications","Risk Factors","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperglucagonemia in pediatric adiposity associates with cardiometabolic risk factors but not hyperglycemia","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1210/clinem/dgac108","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was supported by The Innovation Fund Denmark (grant number: 0603-00484B), The Novo Nordisk Foundation, (grant number: NNF15OC0016544), and The MicrobLiver Challenge (grant number: NNF15OC0016692). Sara E. Stinson is funded by the Copenhagen Bioscience PhD Programme (grant number: NNF18CC0033668). Morten A. V. Lund is funded by the Danish Heart Foundation (grant number: 18-R125-A8447). Cilius E. Fonvig is supported by the BRIDGE - Translational Excellence Programme (grant number: NNF18SA0034956)."],"id":"S02-097.28-045721","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9113783","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85130766964","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35213713","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000768441300001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-bb764125-51be-4173-9a31-aa6b81c6fc65","sdu-5ec78c2a-9cd9-44a2-b786-230e5e0cbd60"],"keyword":["Adiposity/physiology","Blood Glucose/metabolism","Body Mass Index","Cardiometabolic Risk Factors","Cardiovascular Diseases/epidemiology","Cross-Sectional Studies","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","Glucose","Humans","Hyperglycemia/complications","Insulin Resistance","Insulin/metabolism","Overweight/complications","Pediatric Obesity/complications","Risk Factors","Young Adult","adolescent","cardiometabolic risk","child","glucagon","hyperglycemia","obesity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A3FC83C81F09235EB8EECA53DA63363F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1210/clinem/dgac108","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/205927985/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/310844623/Hyperglucagonemia_in_Pediatric_Adiposity_Associates.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københav