k":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Bitten","key":"aagaardpau","last":"Aagaard","locid":"c9664360-51bb-439a-a8f0-ca5fc271587a","name":"Aagaard, Bitten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Betina Samuelsen","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"a3bd034a-cdf5-448c-9493-0aca200bc125","name":"Sørensen, Betina Samuelsen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34523137"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/vox.13202","issn":["00429007","02580330"],"issn_org":["00429007"],"issue":"3","journal":"Vox Sanguinis","pages":"321-327","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Vox Sanguinis","volume":"117"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114901375"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-72e053af-bd76-4472-8cbd-dbd5e859e7e4","ku-38979e12-33d9-4d89-94ae-f528bab869fd","sdu-ebc05d0f-260b-456e-bc29-bdd4f12a29ab"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The new donor vigilance system in Denmark reveals regional differences in adverse reactions supposedly caused by variation in the registration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-093.88-005573","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: The causal contribution of apolipoprotein B (apoB) particles to coronary artery disease (CAD) is established. We examined whether this atherogenic contribution is better reflected by non-high density lipoprotein cholesterol (non-HDL-C) or apoB particle concentration. METHOD AND RESULTS: We performed Mendelian randomization (MR) analysis using 235 variants as genetic instruments; testing the relationship between their effects on the exposures, non-HDL-C and apoB, and on the outcome CAD using weighted regression. Variant effect estimates on the exposures came from the UK Biobank (N = 376,336) and on the outcome from a meta-analysis of five CAD data-sets (187,451 cases and 793,315 controls). Subsequently, we carried out sensitivity and replication analyses.In univariate MR analysis both exposures associated with CAD (βnon-HDL-C = 0.40, P = 2.8 × 10-48 and βapoB = 0.38, P = 1.3 × 10-44). Adding effects on non-HDL-C into a model that already included those on apoB significantly improved the genetically predicted CAD effects (P = 3.9 × 10-5), while adding apoB into the model including non-HDL-C did not (P = 0.69). Thirty-five percent (82/235) of the variants used as genetic instruments had discordant effects on the exposures, associating with non-HDL-C/apoB ratio at P < 2.1 × 10-4 (0.05/235). Fifty-one variants associated at genome-wide significance. CONCLUSION: Many sequence variants have discordant effects on non-HDL-C and apoB. These variants allowed us to show that the causal mechanism underlying the relationship between apolipoprotein B particles and CAD is more associated with non-HDL-C than apoB particle concentration.","author_count":56,"contributors":["Helgadottir, Anna","Thorleifsson, Gudmar","Snaebjarnarson, Audunn","Stefansdottir, Lilja","Sveinbjornsson, Gardar","Tragante, Vinicius","Björnsson, Eyþór","Steinthorsdottir, Valgerdur","Gretarsdottir, Solveig","Helgason, Hannes","Saemundsdottir, Jona","Olafsson, Isleifur","Thune, Jens Jakob","Raja, Anna Axelsson","Ghouse, Jonas","Salling Olesen, Morten","Christensen, Alex","Jacobsen, Rikke Louise","Dowsett, Joseph","Bruun, Mie Topholm","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Knowlton, Kirk","Nadauld, Lincoln","Benediktsson, Rafn","Erikstrup, Christian","Pedersen, Ole Birger","Banasik, Karina","Brunak, Søren","Bundgaard, Henning","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Sulem, Patrick","Arnar, David O.","Thorgeirsson, Gudmundur","Thorsteinsdottir, Unnur","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","Stefansson, Kari","Holm, Hilma","Andersen, Steffen","Banasik, Karina","Burgdorf, Kristoffer Sølvsten","Didriksen, Maria","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Folkmann Hansen, Thomas","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Jemec, Gregor Borut Ernst","Jennum, Poul","Johansson, Pär Ingemar","Hørup Larsen, Margit Anita","Mikkelsen, Susan","Nyegaard, Mette","Stefánsson, Hreinn","Sækmose, Susanne","Sørensen, Erik","Ullum, Henrik","Werge, Thomas"],"cuid":["S05-097.04-011944"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["DBDS Genomic Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Helgadottir, Anna"],"country":["Iceland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Intermountain Healthcare","Intermountain Medical Center","Landspitali University Hospital","The National University Hospital of Iceland","University of Iceland","deCODE Genetics","deCODE genetics, Inc"],"keyword":["Apolipoprotein","Apolipoprotein B 100 genetics","Apolipoproteins B genetics","Atherosclerosis","Cholesterol","Cholesterol HDL","Cholesterol LDL","Coronary Artery Disease genetics","Coronary artery disease","Humans","Lipoproteins","Mendelian Randomization Analysis","Mendelian randomization","Non HDL cholesterol","Risk Factors","apolipoprotein B"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-A