":"Jin, Chunyu","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sara L","key":"jepsenpau","last":"Jepsen","locid":"01376a1a-125b-4cc7-8ad3-3497de4df56d","name":"Jepsen, Sara L","orcid":"0000-0003-1911-1563","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Louis M.E.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Louis M.E.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael P.","key":"achiampau","last":"Achiam","locid":"dfd48120-815f-4309-a218-ca71a476dfda","name":"Achiam, Michael Patrick","name_org":"Achiam, Michael P.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Rune B.","key":"strandbypau","last":"Strandby","name":"Strandby, Rune B.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"bachpau","last":"Bach","locid":"44d88cbf-9cb6-41c6-84a4-5ddda26517d8","name":"Bach, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4305-9910","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas M.","key":"frimurerpau","last":"Frimurer","locid":"4592246e-6be7-4da6-bbc4-fa9f5061d96b","name":"Frimurer, Thomas M.","orcid":"0000-0002-9682-8245","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Siv A.","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"55a4d23b-7003-4fc0-9d95-544bbb48f635","name":"Hjorth, Siv A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6470-650X","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Michel","key":"bouvierpau","last":"Bouvier","name":"Bouvier, Michel","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Helen","key":"coxpau","last":"Cox","name":"Cox, Helen","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Birgitte","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"be07b398-88db-4db5-9851-89125f68edf4","name":"Holst, Birgitte","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33711555"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.molmet.2021.101207","issn":["22128778"],"journal":"Molecular Metabolism","paperid":"101207","status":"p","title":"Molecular Metabolism","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103395528"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-18f27c6e-fa51-4a0d-b70d-c83acf970d95"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Selective release of gastrointestinal hormones induced by an orally active GPR39 agonist","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-408357","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Standardised assessment is key to structured surgical training. Currently, there is no consensus on which surgical assessment tool to use in live gynaecologic surgery. The purpose of this review is to identify assessment tools measuring technical skills in gynaecologic surgery and evaluate the measurement characteristics of each tool. METHOD: We utilized the scoping review methodology and searched PubMed, Medline, Embase and Cochrane. Inclusion criteria were studies that analysed assessment tools in live gynaecologic surgery. Kane's validity argument was applied to evaluate the assessment tools in the included studies. RESULTS: Eight studies out of the 544 identified fulfilled the inclusion criteria. The assessment tools were categorised as global rating scales, global and procedure rating scales combined, procedure-specific rating scales or as a non-procedure-specific error assessment tool. CONCLUSION: This scoping review presents the current different tools for observational assessment of technical skills in intraoperative, gynaecologic surgery. This scoping review can serve as a guide for surgical educators who want to apply a scale or a specific tool in surgical assessment.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hennings, Louise Inkeri","Sørensen, Jette Led","Hybscmann, Jane","Strandbygaard, Jeanett"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-494516"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clinical Competence","Female","Gynecologic Surgical Procedures","Humans"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tools for measuring technical skills during gynaecologic surgery a scoping review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12909-021-02790-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-494516","identifier":[{"id":"85111302954","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34311735","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8314568","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a93a7080-c216-4436-925e-8e079eb608b4"],"keyword":["Clinical Competence","Female","Gynecologic Surgical Procedures","Humans"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-41DAFE6056F3CC5CAE53C6ABDFC24D9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/275831008/s12909_021_02790_w.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12909-021-02790-w","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Louise Inkeri","key":"henningspau","last":"Hennings","name":"Hennings, Louise Inkeri","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jette Led","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"84ce4092-8277-45c1-89d5-afedea9c65f0","name":"Sørensen, Jette Led","orcid":"0000-0002-7320-2784","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jane","key":"hybscmannpau","last":"Hybscmann","name":"Hybscmann, Jane","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jeanett","key":"strandbygaardpau","last":"Strandbygaard","locid":"93787b63-9902-40c2-a799-c92b515e7afc","name":"Strandbygaard, Jeanett","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34311735"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12909-021-02790-w","issn":["14726920"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Medical Education","paperid":"402","status":"p","title":"BMC Medical Education","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111302954"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a93a7080-c216-4436-925e-8e079eb608b4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tools for measuring technical skills during gynaecologic surgery : a scoping review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-494516","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Renal transplant recipients have increased risk of human papilloma virus-related anogenital (pre)cancers. Less is known about their risk of anogenital warts. The aim of this study was to estimate the prevalence and odds of anogenital warts in renal transplant recipients compared with immunocompetent controls, and to assess risk factors for intra-and perianal warts in renal transplant recipients. The study examined 248 renal transplant recipients and 250 controls for cutaneous and mucosal anogenital warts. Participants completed a questionnaire on lifestyle and sexual habits. For external anogenital warts (including penile, vulvar and perianal warts), renal transplant recipients had higher prevalence and odds than controls, both in men (8.1% vs 1.6%, adjusted odds ratio (ORad-justed)=5.09, 95% confidence interval (95% CI), 1.03– 25.04) and women (11.3% vs 1.6%, ORadjusted =8.09, 95% CI 1.69–38.82). For intra-anal warts, there was no clear pattern of higher odds in renal transplant recipients than controls. Current smoking and having had receptive anal sex increased the risk of intra-/perianal warts in renal transplant recipients. In conclusion, renal transplant recipients in this study had higher odds of external anogenital warts than controls.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","Thomsen, Louise T.","Haedersdal, Merete","Lok, Trine Thorborg","Hansen, Jesper Melchior","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-515593"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anogenital warts","Cross sectional study","Human papillomavirus","Renal transplant recipients"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of anogenital warts in renal transplant recipients compared with immunocompetent controls a cross sectional clinical study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/00015555-3858","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-515593","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9413648","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85111679409","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34184064","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-cc8bf668-fde4-4ecb-9ac4-b0fba8834d27"],"keyword":["Anogenital warts","Cross-sectional study","Human papillomavirus","Renal transplant recipients"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A4ED396917446E62DE1732CF0E75D98"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/301036824/7002.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/00015555-3858","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Helle K.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cff32a53-c07d-466a-9bf3-cc621c1e2cb6","name":"Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","name_org":"Larsen, Helle K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Louise T.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Louise T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merete","key":"hædersdalpau","last":"Hædersdal","locid":"fef92f7f-7d21-4a42-903e-24071d35047b","name":"Haedersdal, Merete","name_org":"Hædersdal, Merete","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Trine Thorborg","key":"lokpau","last":"Lok","name":"Lok, Trine Thorborg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Melchior","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3926a380-bc2a-42ca-b393-f1b9b464d1bc","name":"Hansen, Jesper Melchior","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Schwartz","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34184064"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/00015555-3858","issn":["00015555","16512057"],"issn_org":["00015555"],"issue":"7","journal":"Acta Dermato-Venereologica","paperid":"adv00497","status":"p","title":"Acta Dermato-Venereologica","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111679409"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cc8bf668-fde4-4ecb-9ac4-b0fba8834d27"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of anogenital warts in renal transplant recipients compared with immunocompetent controls : A cross-sectional clinical study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-515593","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Dysfunctional dopaminergic neurotransmission is central to movement disorders and mental diseases. The dopamine transporter (DAT) regulates extracellular dopamine levels, but the genetic and mechanistic link between DAT function and dopamine-related pathologies is not clear. Particularly, the pathophysiological significance of monoallelic missense mutations in DAT is unknown. Here, we use clinical information, neuroimaging, and large-scale exome-sequencing data to uncover the occurrence and phenotypic spectrum of a DAT coding variant, DAT-K619N, which localizes to the critical C-terminal PSD-95/Discs-large/ZO-1 homology-binding motif of human DAT (hDAT). We identified the rare but recurrent hDAT-K619N variant in exome-sequenced samples of patients with neuropsychiatric diseases and a patient with early-onset neurodegenerative parkinsonism and comorbid neuropsychiatric disease. In cell cultures, hDAT-K619N displayed reduced uptake capacity, decreased surface expression, and accelerated turnover. Unilateral expression in mouse nigrostriatal neurons revealed differential effects of hDAT-K619N and hDATWT on dopamine-directed behaviors, and hDAT-K619N expression in Drosophila led to impairments in dopamine transmission with accompanying hyperlocomotion and age-dependent disturbances of the negative geotactic response. Moreover, cellular studies and viral expression of hDAT-K619N in mice demonstrated a dominant-negative effect of the hDAT-K619N mutant. Summarized, our results suggest that hDAT-K619N can effectuate dopamine dysfunction of pathological relevance in a dominant-negative manner.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Herborg, Freja","Jensen, Kathrine Louise","Tolstoy, Sasha","Arends, Natascha","Posselt, Leonie P.","Shekar, Aparna","Aguilar, Jenny","Lund, Viktor Karlovich","Erreger, Kevin","Rickhag, Mattias","Lycas, Matthew D.","Lonsdale, Markus N.","Rahbek-Clemmensen, Troels","Sørensen, Andreas Toft","Newman, Amy H.","Løkkegaard, Annemette","Kjaerulff, Ole","Werge, Thomas","Moller, Lisbeth B.","Matthies, Heinrich J. G.","Galli, Aurelio","Hjermind, Lena Elisabeth","Gether, Ulrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518451"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corpau":["IPSYCH Researchers"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Institutes of Health","University of Alabama","Vanderbilt University"],"keyword":["Amphetamine","Architectures","GENE","Hyperactivity","Mice","Mutations","Neurotransmission","Oligomerization","SEQUENCE VARIATION","Trafficking"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identifying dominant negative actions of a dopamine transporter variant in patients with parkinsonism and neuropsychiatric disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/jci.insight.151496","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-518451","identifier":[{"id":"000701785700002","type":"wos"},{"id":"34375312","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85116159480","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8492322","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-d13ac011-8cf0-479d-8f70-740a36be84e8"],"keyword":["AMPHETAMINE","ARCHITECTURES","GENE","HYPERACTIVITY","MICE","MUTATIONS","NEUROTRANSMISSION","OLIGOMERIZATION","SEQUENCE VARIATION","TRAFFICKING"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D33BD9F450D94726584C7026F5BB6D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/jci.insight.151496","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/281594866/Identifyi