","name":"Owens, Trevor","orcid":"0000-0001-9315-6036","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"7a591b19-47c2-4620-8224-5ce392ca7441","name":"Meyer, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-9571-1336","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33482100"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.stemcr.2020.12.011","issn":["22136711"],"issue":"2","journal":"Stem Cell Reports","pages":"281-294","publisher":"Cell Press","status":"p","title":"Stem Cell Reports","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100405813"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7b115f47-3e9d-4a8d-97e1-40459a047b7a","sdu-bf952a87-b3a9-4e03-ae68-179eb26e26db"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Microglia-Secreted Factors Enhance Dopaminergic Differentiation of Tissue- and iPSC-Derived Human Neural Stem Cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.78-043708","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Headache and facial pain are among the most common, disabling and costly diseases in Europe, which demands for high quality health care on all levels within the health system. The role of the Danish Headache Society is to educate and advocate for the needs of patients with headache and facial pain. Therefore, the Danish Headache Society has launched a third version of the guideline for the diagnosis, organization and treatment of the most common types of headaches and facial pain in Denmark. The second edition was published in Danish in 2010 and has been a great success, but as new knowledge and treatments have emerged it was timely to revise the guideline. The recommendations for the primary headaches and facial pain are largely in accordance with the European guidelines produced by the European Academy of Neurology. The guideline should be used a practical tool for use in daily clinical practice for primary care physicians, neurologists with a common interest in headache, as well as other health-care professionals treating headache patients. The guideline first describes how to examine and diagnose the headache patient and how headache treatment is organized in Denmark. This description is followed by sections on the characteristics, diagnosis and treatment of each of the most common primary and secondary headache disorders and trigeminal neuralgia. The guideline includes many tables to facilitate a quick overview. Finally, the particular challenges regarding migraine and female hormones as well as headache in children are addressed.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Schytz, Henrik Winther","Amin, Faisal Mohammad","Jensen, Rigmor Højland","Carlsen, Louise","Maarbjerg, Stine","Lund, Nunu","Aegidius, Karen","Thomsen, Lise L.","Bach, Flemming W.","Beier, Dagmar","Johansen, Hanne","Hansen, Jakob M.","Kasch, Helge","Munksgaard, Signe B.","Poulsen, Lars","Sørensen, Per Schmidt","Schmidt-Hansen, Peter T.","Cvetkovic, Vlasta V.","Ashina, Messoud","Bendtsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S03-099.41-014247"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Schytz, Henrik W"],"keyword":["Child","Denmark","Europe","Facial Pain diagnosis","Female","Headache Disorders diagnosis","Headache diagnosis","Hovedpine","Humans"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reference programme diagnosis and treatment of headache disorders and facial pain danish headache society 000000000003rd edition 000000002020","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s10194-021-01228-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.41-014247","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8034101","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33832438","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85104078623","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000638134000001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-1719f7de-c3c6-44dc-968c-519fe10e7ef4","ku-f0dab747-d830-4ad4-b001-ce1c55939e42","sdu-2371f7a9-73f5-406b-9317-33a8daed08fb"],"keyword":["Child","Denmark","Europe","Facial Pain/diagnosis","Female","Headache Disorders/diagnosis","Headache/diagnosis","Hovedpine","Humans","ansigtssmerte"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-68406630084AD419D2328824D843790F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/181756347/s10194_021_01228_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s10194-021-01228-4","