{"abstract":"Synapses in the cerebral cortex constantly change and this dynamic property regulated by the action of neuromodulators such as dopamine (DA), is essential for reward learning and memory. DA modulates spike-timing-dependent plasticity (STDP), a cellular model of learning and memory, in juvenile rodent cortical neurons. However, it is unknown whether this neuromodulation also occurs at excitatory synapses of cortical neurons in mature adult mice or in humans. Cortical layer V pyramidal neurons were recorded with whole cell patch clamp electrophysiology and an extracellular stimulating electrode was used to induce STDP. DA was either bath-applied or optogenetically released in slices from mice. Classical STDP induction protocols triggered non-hebbian excitatory synaptic depression in the mouse or no plasticity at human cortical synapses. DA reverted long term synaptic depression to baseline in mouse via dopamine 2 type receptors or elicited long term synaptic potentiation in human cortical synapses. Furthermore, when DA was applied during an STDP protocol it depressed presynaptic inhibition in the mouse but not in the human cortex. Thus, DA modulates excitatory synaptic plasticity differently in human vs. mouse cortex. The data strengthens the importance of DA in gating cognition in humans, and may inform on therapeutic interventions to recover brain function from diseases.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Louth, Emma Louise","Jørgensen, Rasmus Langelund","Korshoej, Anders Rosendal","Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann","Capogna, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-229206"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dopamine","spike timing dependent plasticity","synaptic inhibition"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dopaminergic neuromodulation of spike timing dependent plasticity in mature adult rodent and human cortical neurons","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fncel.2021.668980","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-229206","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8102156","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85105404852","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33967700","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-af181ba6-3d8d-420d-98fb-5edcd0b52efb"],"keyword":["dopamine","human cortical slices","layer 5 pyramidal neurons","spike timing dependent plasticity","synaptic inhibition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E609ECF5AD6825878E3A8946314E833"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fncel.2021.668980","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Syd","Aarhus University, Interfaculty Centre, DANDRITE"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma Louise","key":"louthpau","last":"Louth","locid":"a84f69a1-1198-4cc9-bd94-afa014d83440","name":"Louth, Emma Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Langelund","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"1996f56c-481e-40b9-9df0-55c91fd4aaab","name":"Jørgensen, Rasmus Langelund","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Rosendal","key":"korshoejpau","last":"Korshoej","locid":"09d94078-676a-42ee-91c2-eb8ba8df356b","name":"Korshoej, Anders Rosendal","orcid":"0000-0003-4285-8171","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Christian Hedemann","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f442e934-3b4d-4fc2-91dc-93621be94d60","name":"Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann","orcid":"0000-0001-5139-7405","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"capognapau","last":"Capogna","locid":"736c59b0-60b3-4107-ae1a-58a2b2879c07","name":"Capogna, Marco","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33967700"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fncel.2021.668980","issn":["16625102"],"journal":"Frontiers in Cellular Neuroscience","paperid":"668980","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Cellular Neuroscience","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105404852"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-af181ba6-3d8d-420d-98fb-5edcd0b52efb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Dopaminergic Neuromodulation of Spike Timing Dependent Plasticity in Mature Adult Rodent and Human Cortical Neurons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-229206","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We present the first 1992‐2020 record of Greenland Ice Sheet (GrIS) mass balance derived from multi‐satellite Ku‐band altimetry. We employ an empirical approach as an alternative detailed to radar‐propagation modeling, and instead convert elevation changes observed by radar altimetry into mass changes using spatiotemporal calibration fields. This calibration field is derived from a machine learning approach that optimizes the prediction of a previously published mass balance field as a function of ice sheet variables. Our mass balance record shows a GrIS contribution of 12.1±2.3 mm sea‐level equivalent since 1992, with more than 80% of this contribution occurring after 2003. Our record also suggests that the 2017 hydrological year is the first year in the 21st century which, within uncertainties, the GrIS was in balance. Overall, the 28‐year radar‐derived mass balance record we present highlights the potential of the method to provide operational mass balance estimates derived from multi‐satellite Ku‐band altimetry.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Barletta, Valentina Roberta","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Colgan, William"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greenland ice sheet mass balance 000000001992 000000002020 from calibrated radar altimetry","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2020GL091216","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316159","identifier":[{"id":"85101187262","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2702be42-d4fd-4a85-a1a1-63d0b0d06b3b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD084D21BA854DE5F1D6A1FE0C18537E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/239868868/2020GL091216_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2020GL091216","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodesy and Earth Observation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian B.","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","name_org":"Simonsen, Sebastian B.","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina Roberta","key":"barlettapau","last":"Barletta","locid":"9662b7b8-5901-45b2-bba3-dd8e3879f864","name":"Barletta, Valentina Roberta","orcid":"0000-0003-4427-0830","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"William","key":"colganpau","last":"Colgan","name":"Colgan, William","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1029/2020gl091216","issn":["00948276","19448007"],"issn_org":["00948276"],"issue":"3","journal":"Geophysical Research Letters","paperid":"e2020GL091216","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Geophysical Research Letters","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101187262"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2702be42-d4fd-4a85-a1a1-63d0b0d06b3b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Greenland Ice Sheet mass balance (1992‐2020) from calibrated radar altimetry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316159","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Actuator disc and actuator line techniques are widely used for modelling wind turbines operating in wind farms. These techniques essentially replace the blade geometry with applied body forces, which reduce the resolved length scales significantly and hence the required grid resolution. This work is a verification of the coupling between the flow solver EllipSys3D and the aeroelastic tool Flex5, through a quantitative comparison of coupled actuator line, coupled actuator disc, and standalone Flex5. Steady state performance predictions, instantaneous reaction to turbulence and damage equivalent load analyses all show a very good agreement between the three methods. Differences can be explained primarily by the higher fidelity modelling of the coupled simulations; this is particularly in regard to the influence of blade flexibility, as the actuators deflect and interact with the modelled flow. Additionally, some overpredictions of loading at the blade tip and root below rated velocity for the actuator methods can be attributed to the Gaussian smearing used to apply the body forces.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hodgson, Emily Louise","Andersen, Søren Juhl","Troldborg, Niels","Meyer Forsting, Alexander Raul","Mikkelsen, Robert Flemming","Sørensen, Jens Nørkær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-322153"],"event":{"end":"2021-06-17","place":"Visby, se","start":"2021-06-15","title":"Wake Conference 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hodgson, Emily Louise"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a quantitative comparison of aeroelastic computations using flex000000000005 and actuator methods in les","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1742-6596/1934/1/012014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-322153","identifier":[{"id":"85108715916","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3b22fc65-982e-413c-bda8-e0bd40813310"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50CA9C70837EBF353C79F92561F1DCF9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1742-6596/1934/1/012014","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/247517259/Hodgson_2021_J._Phys._Conf._Ser._1934_012014.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy, Wind Turbine Design Division, Aero- and Fluid Dynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E L","key":"hodgsonpau","last":"Hodgson","locid":"e882e4e1-d244-45c7-8ac3-e707284bcfdf","name":"Hodgson, Emily Louise","name_org":"Hodgson, E L","orcid":"0000-0001-6443-2628","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S J","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"1a705d17-7389-40d5-99a2-820feefe7b9f","name":"Andersen, Søren Juhl","name_org":"Andersen, S J","orcid":"0000-0002-5935-751X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"N","key":"troldborgpau","last":"Troldborg","locid":"542863f7-1c93-46a6-ba00-178f1593d257","name":"Troldborg, Niels","name_org":"Troldborg, N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A Meyer","key":"forstingpau","last":"Forsting","locid":"64699c0c-51f0-4011-8ca2-6cc81150dc3e","name":"Meyer Forsting, Alexander Raul","name_org":"Forsting, A Meyer","orcid":"0000-0002-3133-1860","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R F","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"e9076e36-5567-4f6f-9779-10fc3e9e12ec","name":"Mikkelsen, Robert Flemming","name_org":"Mikkelsen, R F","orcid":"0000-0002-4095-1228","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J N","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"cb5cdeac-3157-4130-a990-29da0ed7be90","name":"Sørensen, Jens Nørkær","name_org":"Sørensen, J N","orcid":"0000-0002-1974-2675","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1742-6596/1934/1/012014","issn":["17426596"],"journal":"Journal of Physics: Conference Series","paperid":"012014","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physics: Conference Series","title_org":"Journal of Physics - Conference Series","volume":"1934"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108715916"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3b22fc65-982e-413c-bda8-e0bd40813310"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A Quantitative Comparison of Aeroelastic Computations using Flex5 and Actuator Methods in LES","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-322153","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Transfusion therapy is a critical part of supportive care early after allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation (allo-HCT). Platelet and RBC transfusions elicit immunomodulatory effects in the recipient, but if this impacts the risk of acute graft-versus-host disease (aGVHD) has only been scarcely investigated. We investigated if platelet and RBC transfusions were associated with the development of aGVHD following myeloablative allo-HCT in a cohort of 664 patients who underwent transplantation between 2000 and 2019. Data were further analyzed for the impact of blood donor age and sex and blood product storage time. Exploratory analyses were conducted to assess correlations between transfusion burden and plasma biomarkers of inflammation and endothelial activation and damage. Between day 0 and day +13, each patient received a median of 7 (IQR, 5 to 10) platelet transfusions and 3 (IQR, 2 to 6) RBC transfusions (Spearman's ρ = 0.49). The cumulative sums of platelet and RBC transfusions, respectively, received from day 0 to day +13 were associated with subsequent grade II-IV aGVHD in multivariable landmark Cox models (platelets: adjusted hazard ratio [HR], 1.27; 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.06 to 1.51; RBCs: adjusted HR, 1.41; 95% CI, 1.09 to 1.82; both per 5 units; 184 events). For both platelet and RBC transfusions, we did not find support for a difference in the risk of aGVHD according to age or sex of the blood donor. Transfusion of RBCs with a storage time longer than the median of 8 days was inversely associated with aGVHD (HR per 5 units, 0.54; 95% CI, 0.30 to 0.96); however, when using an RBC storage time of ≥14 days as a cutoff, there was no longer evidence for an association with aGVHD (HR, 1.03 per 5 units; 95% CI, 0.53 to 2.00). For platelets, there was no clear association between storage time and the risk of aGVHD. The transfusion burdens of platelets and RBCs were positively correlated with plasma levels of TNF-α, IL-6, and soluble thrombomodulin at day +14. In conclusion, platelet and RBC transfusions in the first 2 weeks after myeloablative allo-HCT were associated with subsequent development of grade II-IV aGVHD. We did not find evidence of an impact of blood donor age or sex or blood product storage time on the risk of aGVHD. Our findings support restrictive transfusion strategies in allo-HCT recipients.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Gjærde, Lars Klingen","Sørensen, Anne Louise Tølbøll","von Stemann, Jakob Hjorth","Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","Hansen, Morten Bagge","Sengeløv, Henrik","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-418100"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acute graft versus host disease","Allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation","Biomarkers","Blood Transfusion","Inflammation","Platelet Transfusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"platelet and red blood cell transfusions and risk of acute graft versus host disease after myeloablative allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtct.2021.07.001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-418100","identifier":[{"id":"85112530356","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34252580","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-294c5855-6b2c-40cf-8302-0d33a480d0dc"],"keyword":["Acute graft-versus-host disease","Allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation","Biomarkers","Blood transfusion","Inflammation","Platelet transfusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B2E9F39653677055809C75F366F3592"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/291019949/1_s2.0_S2666636721010368_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtct.2021.07.001","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Klingen","key":"gjærdepau","last":"Gjærde","locid":"59673200-3062-476a-bc8a-f46e634a54e6","name":"Gjærde, Lars Klingen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Louise Tølbøll","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Anne Louise Tølbøll","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Hjorth","key":"vonstemannpau","last":"von Stemann","locid":"6402e083-c5be-4ada-a57a-a30456d8cc67","name":"von Stemann, Jakob Hjorth","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"fischernielsenpau","last":"Fischer-Nielsen","locid":"af37e8db-0c68-4da1-9b25-5625d241b9ca","name":"Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Bagge","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"31f07839-f4e2-44f2-8668-3bd6d1a24b2f","name":"Hansen, Morten Bagge","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"sengeløvpau","last":"Sengeløv","locid":"ff0cb82b-deb8-4d4e-b871-8f70d359af15","name":"Sengeløv, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sisse Rye","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34252580"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jtct.2021.07.001","issn":["26666367"],"issue":"10","journal":"Transplantation and Cellular Therapy","status":"p","title":"Transplantation and Cellular Therapy","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112530356"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-294c5855-6b2c-40cf-8302-0d33a480d0dc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Platelet and Red Blood Cell Transfusions and Risk of Acute Graft-versus-Host Disease after Myeloablative Allogeneic Hematopoietic Cell Transplantation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-418100","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Play is a non-invasive, safe and inexpensive intervention that can help paediatric patients and their families manage difficult aspects of being ill or hospitalised. Although play has existed in hospitals for decades, research on hospital play interventions is scarce. This review aimed to categorise and synthesise the last 20 years of research on hospital play interventions. DESIGN: Scoping review. DATA SOURCES: PubMed, CINAHL, CENTRAL, ERIC and PsycINFO (1 January 2000- 9 September 2020). STUDY SELECTION AND DATA EXTRACTION: We systematically searched for original peer-reviewed articles, written in English, on hospital play interventions in paediatric patients (0-18 years) in non-psychiatric settings. Two reviewers independently screened titles and abstracts, reviewed full text of relevant articles and extracted data. We thematically synthesised the data from the included studies, and a descriptive analysis, based on a developed framework, is presented. RESULTS: Of the 297 included articles, 78% came from high-income countries and 56% were published within the last 5 years. Play interventions were carried out across all ages by various healthcare professionals. Play interventions served different roles within four clinical contexts: A) procedures and diagnostic tests, B) patient education, C) treatment and recovery and D) adaptation. Across these contexts, play interventions were generally facilitated and purpose-oriented and had positive reported effects on pain, stress, and anxiety. CONCLUSIONS: Play in hospitals is an emerging interdisciplinary research area with a significant potential benefit for child and family health. Future research should further describe principles for play in hospitals. High-quality studies investigating short-term and long-term effects are needed to guide when and how to best integrate play in hospitals.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Gjærde, Line Klingen","Hybschmann, Jane","Dybdal, Daniel","Topperzer, Martha Krogh","Schrøder, Morten Arnborg","Gibson, Jenny Louise","Ramchandani, Paul","Ginsberg, Elisabeth Ida","Ottesen, Bent","Frandsen, Thomas Leth","Sørensen, Jette Led"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-432765"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anxiety therapy","Child","Family Health","Health Personnel","Hospitals","Humans"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"play interventions for paediatric patients in hospital a scoping review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2021-051957","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-432765","identifier":[{"id":"34312210","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85111416783","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8314749","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-41cb10f3-4598-4551-96af-9b8502883043"],"keyword":["Anxiety/therapy","Child","Family Health","Health Personnel","Hospitals","Humans"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D80834890EF1174561797E61EBA8F351"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2021-051957","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/275884328/e051957.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Line Klingen","key":"gjærdepau","last":"Gjærde","name":"Gjærde, Line Klingen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jane","key":"hybschmannpau","last":"Hybschmann","name":"Hybschmann, Jane","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"dybdalpau","last":"Dybdal","name":"Dybdal, Daniel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martha Krogh","key":"topperzerpau","last":"Topperzer","name":"Topperzer, Martha Krogh","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten Arnborg","key":"schrøderpau","last":"Schrøder","name":"Schrøder, Morten Arnborg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jenny Louise","key":"gibsonpau","last":"Gibson","name":"Gibson, Jenny Louise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"ramchandanipau","last":"Ramchandani","name":"Ramchandani, Paul","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elisabeth Ida","key":"ginsbergpau","last":"Ginsberg","name":"Ginsberg, Elisabeth Ida","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bent","key":"ottesenpau","last":"Ottesen","locid":"5cc91f75-7bf4-4789-a5de-71cbf232e8d5","name":"Ottesen, Bent","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas Leth","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","name":"Frandsen, Thomas Leth","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jette Led","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"84ce4092-8277-45c1-89d5-afedea9c65f0","name":"Sørensen, Jette Led","orcid":"0000-0002-7320-2784","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34312210"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2021-051957","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"7","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e051957","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111416783"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-41cb10f3-4598-4551-96af-9b8502883043"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Play interventions for paediatric patients in hospital : a scoping review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-432765","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background Renal transplant recipients (RTRs) have increased risk of human papillomavirus (HPV)–related cancers, including anal cancer. We investigated the prevalence of anal high-grade intraepithelial lesions (HSILs) in RTRs compared with immunocompetent controls and risk factors for anal HSIL in RTRs. Methods We included 247 RTRs and 248 controls in this cross-sectional study. We obtained anal samples for HPV testing with INNO-LiPA and performed high-resolution anoscopy on all participants. The participants completed a questionnaire on lifestyle and sexual habits. We used logistic regression to estimate odds ratios (ORs) of histologically confirmed anal HSIL in RTRs vs controls and risk factors for anal HSIL in RTRs, stratified by sex and anal high-risk (hr) HPV status, adjusting for age, smoking, lifetime sexual partners, and receptive anal sex. Results RTRs had higher anal HSIL prevalence than controls, both among men (6.5% vs 0.8%; adjusted OR [aOR], 11.21 [95% confidence interval {CI}, 1.46–291.17]) and women (15.4% vs 4.0%; aOR, 6.41 [95% CI, 2.14–24.10]). Among those with anal hrHPV, RTRs had higher anal HSIL prevalence than controls (33.8% vs 9.5%; aOR, 6.06 [95% CI, 2.16–20.27]). Having had receptive anal sex (aOR, 6.23 [95% CI, 2.23–19.08]) or genital warts (aOR, 4.21 [95% CI, 1.53–11.48]) were risk factors for anal HSIL in RTRs. All HSIL cases occurred in individuals with anal hrHPV. Conclusions RTRs had increased risk of anal HSIL compared with immunocompetent controls, with particularly high prevalence in female RTRs. Receptive anal sex, previous genital warts, and anal hrHPV infection were risk factors for anal HSIL in RTRs. Screening for anal HSIL in RTRs should be considered.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","Haedersdal, Merete","Thomsen, Louise T","Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","Lok, Trine Thorborg","Bonde, Jesper","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Hansen, Jesper Melchior","Palefsky, Joel M","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-531294"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of anal high grade squamous intraepithelial lesions among renal transplant recipients compared with immunocompetent controls","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-531294","identifier":[{"id":"32544223","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85111693808","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e6d7283d-4f01-4caf-9ce5-e4ccbd5d1503"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-30581E68AA27BC7545D5471D17FED149"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Helle K","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cff32a53-c07d-466a-9bf3-cc621c1e2cb6","name":"Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","name_org":"Larsen, Helle K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merete","key":"hædersdalpau","last":"Hædersdal","locid":"fef92f7f-7d21-4a42-903e-24071d35047b","name":"Haedersdal, Merete","name_org":"Hædersdal, Merete","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise T","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Louise T","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hertzumlarsenpau","last":"Hertzum-larsen","locid":"2fcdde5d-5f87-4367-9ddb-d6c3ca8eaf90","name":"Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","name_org":"Hertzum-larsen, Rasmus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Trine Thorborg","key":"lokpau","last":"Lok","name":"Lok, Trine Thorborg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","name":"Bonde, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren S","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","name_org":"Sørensen, Søren S","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Melchior","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3926a380-bc2a-42ca-b393-f1b9b464d1bc","name":"Hansen, Jesper Melchior","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Joel M","key":"palefskypau","last":"Palefsky","name":"Palefsky, Joel M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne K","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjær, Susanne K","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32544223"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/cid/ciaa781","issn":["10584838","15376591"],"issn_org":["10584838"],"issue":"1","journal":"Clinical Infectious Diseases","pages":"21-29","status":"p","title":"Clinical Infectious Diseases","volume":"73"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111693808"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e6d7283d-4f01-4caf-9ce5-e4ccbd5d1503"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of Anal High-grade Squamous Intraepithelial Lesions Among Renal Transplant Recipients Compared With Immunocompetent Controls","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-531294","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: A multiphased mixed-methods study was performed to develop and validate a comprehensive patient-reported outcome measure (PROM) for arm lymphedema in women with breast cancer (i.e., the LYMPH-Q Upper Extremity Module). Methods: Qualitative interviews (January 2017 and June 2018) were performed with 15 women to elicit concepts specific to arm lymphedema after breast cancer treatment. Data were audio-recorded, transcribed, and coded. Scales were refined through cognitive interviews (October and Decemeber 2018) with 16 patients and input from 12 clinical experts. The scales were field-tested (October 2019 and January 2020) with an international sample of 3222 women in the United States and Denmark. Rasch measurement theory (RMT) analysis was used to examine reliability and validity. Results: The qualitative phase resulted in six independently functioning scales that measure arm symptoms, function, appearance, psychological function, and satisfaction with information and with arm sleeves. In the RMT analysis, all items in each scale had ordered thresholds and nonsignificant chi-square p values. For all the scales, the reliability statistics with and without extremes for the Person Separation Index were 0.80 or higher, Cronbach’s alpha was 0.89 or higher, and the Intraclass Correlation Coefficients were 0.92 or higher. Lower (worse) scores on the LYMPH-Q Upper Extremity scales were associated with reporting of more severe arm swelling, an arm problem caused by cancer and/or its treatment, and wearing of an arm sleeve in the past 12 months. Conclusions: The LYMPH-Q Upper Extremity Module can be used to measure outcomes that matter to women with upper extremity lymphedema. This new PROM was designed using a modern psychometric approach and, as such, can be used in research and in clinical care.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Klassen, Anne F.","Tsangaris, Elena","Kaur, Manraj N.","Poulsen, Lotte","Beelen, Louise M.","Jacobsen, Amalie Lind","Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf","Sørensen, Jens Ahm","Vasilic, Dalibor","Dayan, Joseph","Mehrara, Babak","Pusic, Andrea L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-600001"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Klassen, Anne F."],"country":["Canada","Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Harvard Medical School","McMaster University","Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center"],"keyword":["Arm","Female","Humans","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Patient Satisfaction","Psychometrics","Quality of Life","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires","Upper Extremity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development and psychometric validation of a patient reported outcome measure for arm lymphedema the lymph q upper extremity module","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1245/s10434-021-09887-y","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Phase 1 of this study was supported by the Canadian Breast Cancer Foundation Project Grant (now integrated into Canadian Cancer Society) (Grant No. 319371. Phase 2 of this study was supported by the Canadian Cancer Society (Grant No. 706256). Manraj Kaur was supported by the Canadian Institute of Health Research Canada’s Best Graduate Scholarship Doctoral Award (2015–2019). Louise Marie Beelen was partially supported by ZonMw (Network Grant). Contributions from Memorial Sloan-Kettering were funded in part through the NIH/NCI Cancer Center Support Grant P30CA008748."],"id":"S01-000.00-600001","identifier":[{"id":"85103858628","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34224044","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8349351","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-5da28e50-9be9-4ee5-a2e6-295b1baff6df"],"keyword":["Arm","Female","Humans","Lymphedema/diagnosis","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Patient Satisfaction","Psychometrics","Quality of Life","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires","Upper Extremity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8BAC59C6E3F9323E4EF5A377FEC7D9C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/184340145/Klassen2021_Article_DevelopmentAndPsychometricVali_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1245/s10434-021-09887-y","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"mcmaster university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McMaster University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"harvard medical school","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard Medical School","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Plastic Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"erasmus university medical center rotterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"memorial sloan kettering cancer 