"Louise","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","name":"Dalsgaard, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daniel Oxholm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Daniel Oxholm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jannie Møller","key":"hartleypedh","last":"Hartley","name":"Hartley, Jannie Møller","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"rimestadpedh","last":"Rimestad","name":"Rimestad, Lene","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793453715"],"pages":"243-264","publisher":"Ajour","status":"p","title":"Den undersøgende journalistiks metoder"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-bd9bf87f-5fa3-4767-ad07-1349d42b17e4"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Research, faktatjek og visualisering med Open Source Investigation (OSINT)","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-568700","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: In order to explore the pathophysiology underlying type 2 diabetes we examined the impact of gene variants associated with type 2 diabetes on circulating levels of glucagon during an oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT). Furthermore, we performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) aiming to identify novel genomic loci affecting plasma glucagon levels. Methods: Plasma levels of glucagon were examined in samples obtained at three time points during an OGTT; 0, 30 and 120 min, in two separate cohorts with a total of up to 1899 individuals. Cross-sectional analyses were performed separately in the two cohorts and the results were combined in a meta-analysis. Results: A known type 2 diabetes variant in EYA2 was significantly associated with higher plasma glucagon level at 30 min during the OGTT (Beta 0.145, SE 0.038, P = 1.2 × 10–4) corresponding to a 7.4% increase in plasma glucagon level per effect allele. In the GWAS, we identified a marker in the MARCH1 locus, which was genome-wide significantly associated with reduced suppression of glucagon during the first 30 min of the OGTT (Beta − 0.210, SE 0.037, P = 1.9 × 10–8), equivalent to 8.2% less suppression per effect allele. Nine additional independent markers, not previously associated with type 2 diabetes, showed suggestive associations with reduced glucagon suppression during the first 30 min of the OGTT (P < 1.0 × 10–5). Conclusions: A type 2 diabetes risk variant in the EYA2 locus was associated with higher plasma glucagon levels at 30 min. Ten additional variants were suggestively associated with reduced glucagon suppression without conferring increased type 2 diabetes risk.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Jonsson, Anna","Stinson, Sara E.","Torekov, Signe S.","Clausen, Tine D.","Færch, Kristine","Kelstrup, Louise","Grarup, Niels","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","Damm, Peter","Witte, Daniel R","Jørgensen, Marit E.","Pedersen, Oluf","Holst, Jens Juul","Hansen, Torben"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-023292"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Jonsson, Anna"],"keyword":["Adult","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","GWAS","Genome Wide Association Study","Glucagon","Glucose Tolerance Test","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide association study of circulating levels of glucagon during an oral glucose tolerance test","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12920-020-00841-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The ADDITION-Denmark study was supported by the National Health Services in the counties of Copenhagen, Aarhus, Ringkøbing, Ribe, and Southern Jutland in Denmark; the Danish Council for Strategic Research; the Danish Research Foundation for General Practice; Novo Nordisk Foundation; the Danish Centre for Evaluation and Health Technology Assessment; the Diabetes Fund of the National Board of Health; the Danish Medical Research Council; and the Aarhus University Research Foundation. The ADDITION-PRO study was funded by an unrestricted grant from the European Foundation for the Study of Diabetes/Pfizer for Research into Cardiovascular Disease Risk Reduction in Patients with Diabetes (74550801), by the Danish Council for Strategic Research and by internal research and equipment funds from Steno Diabetes Center. The RigCoh-study was supported by The Lundbeck Foundation, Civilingeniør H. C. Bechgaard's Foundation, The Danish Diabetes Association, The Danish Medical Research Council, the Gangsted Foundation, A. P. Moeller og Hustru Chastine Mc-Kinney Moeller's Foundation, Aase og Ejner Danielsen's Foundation, The Augustinus Foundation, and The Research Foundation of Rigshospitalet. This work was supported by an unrestricted grant from the European Foundation for the Study of Diabetes/Pfizer for Research into Cardiovascular Disease Risk Reduction in Patients with Diabetes (74550801), the Danish Council for Strategic Research, the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and Innovation programme (Grant Agreement No 667191) and internal research and equipment funds from Steno Diabetes Center. AJ is supported by the Danish Council for Independent Research, European Union, FP7, Marie Curie Actions, IEF, Lundbeck Foundation, Novo Nordisk Foundation and Danish Diabetes Academy (NNF17SA0031406). The Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research is an independent Research Center at the University of Copenhagen partially funded by an unrestricted donation from the Novo Nordisk Foundation. The funders had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript."],"id":"S03-099.97-023292","identifier":[{"id":"000610102400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7788944","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33407418","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85098762248","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-918d9c28-66e0-4a62-a157-dbc8ec398cc7","ku-06442fbc-f9fb-42b5-80d3-c680dcb7a97f","sdu-9806613c-904e-4e22-8b32-608143ebac1c"],"keyword":["Adult","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","GWAS","Genome-Wide Association Study","Glucagon","Glucose Tolerance Test","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-FA46988E58D5DB1822CB37DA62B3BC0B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC0","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178256030/s12920_020_00841_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284700681/Genome_wide_association_study_of_circulating_levels_of_glucagon_during_an_oral_glucose_tolerance_test_publisher_version_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12920-020-00841-7","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Hansen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - SDCA-Steno Diabetes Center Aarhus","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Department of Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Center for Public health in Greenland","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna","key":"jonssonpau","last":"Jonsson","locid":"63e3d75a-e34d-442b-80f1-b0ea09706850","name":"Jonsson, Anna","orcid":"0000-0003-1252-8673","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sara E.","key":"stinsonpau","last":"Stinson","locid":"75924fce-d276-4bc3-a247-362923bccbb5","name":"Stinson, Sara Elizabeth","name_org":"Stinson, Sara E.","orcid":"0000-0002-1491-9179","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe S.","key":"torekovpau","last":"Torekov","locid":"c1d71a61-ee09-4c29-ae48-7520707a73be","name":"Torekov, Signe Sørensen","name_org":"Torekov, Signe S.","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-0252","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tine D.","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"047e6356-0a01-48a6-9a2e-fa550c06183e","name":"Clausen, Tine Dalsgaard","name_org":"Clausen, Tine D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Kristine","key":"færchpau","last":"Færch","locid":"21e08d16-438a-4801-9fbd-94ab9cee9426","name":"Færch, Kristine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Louise","key":"kelstruppau","last":"Kelstrup","locid":"d503c725-38b5-4d24-864d-baac41449501","name":"Kelstrup, Louise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"graruppau","last":"Grarup","locid":"824a7159-a059-4de1-bf3f-e116ef59e0de","name":"Grarup, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5526-1070","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elisabeth R.","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"3acd58f4-6d64-4a89-a406-d2f43b310500","name":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel R.","key":"wittepau","last":"Witte","locid":"22db1993-176e-491b-833f-69a3d2d02b47","name":"Witte, Daniel R","name_org":"Witte, Daniel R.","orcid":"0000-0002-0769-2922","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Marit E.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"5a2309e5-48cd-4773-9887-7b0255811460","name":"Jørgensen, Marit Eika","name_org":"Jørgensen, Marit E.","orcid":"0000-0001-8356-5565","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Oluf","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0a2a7ad3-1719-43c6-bdf3-c3491a43a8af","name":"Pedersen, Oluf","orcid":"0000-0002-3321-3972","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Torben","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33407418"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12920-020-00841-7","issn":["17558794"],"journal":"BMC Medical Genomics","paperid":"3","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","publisher_org":"BioMed Central Ltd","status":"p","title":"BMC Medical Genomics","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098762248"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Novo Nordisk","Other Hospitals","Private Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","danish diabetes academy"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-918d9c28-66e0-4a62-a157-dbc8ec398cc7","ku-06442fbc-f9fb-42b5-80d3-c680dcb7a97f","sdu-9806613c-904e-4e22-8b32-608143ebac1c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Genome-wide association study of circulating levels of glucagon during an oral glucose tolerance test","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.97-023292","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"From 1985 to 2016, the prevalence of underweight decreased, and that of obesity and severe obesity increased, in most regions, with significant variation in the magnitude of these changes across regions. We investigated how much change in mean body mass index (BMI) explains changes in the prevalence of underweight, obesity, and severe obesity in different regions using data from 2896 population-based studies with 187 million participants. Changes in the prevalence of underweight and total obesity, and to a lesser extent severe obesity, are largely driven by shifts in the distribution of BMI, with smaller contributions from changes in the shape of the distribution. In East and Southeast Asia and sub-Saharan Africa, the underweight tail of the BMI distribution was left behind as the distribution shifted. There is a need for policies that address all forms of malnutrition by making healthy foods accessible and affordable, while restricting unhealthy foods through fiscal and regulatory restrictions.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Maja Bæksgaard","Bjerregaard, Peter","Christensen, Kaare","Eriksen, Louise","Grøntved, Anders","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Møller, Niels Christian","Rasmussen, Mette","Schramm, Stine","Sodemann, Morten","Tolstrup, Janne Schurmann","Wedderkopp, Niels","Ezzati, Majid"],"cuid":["S04-099.07-019929"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["NCD Risk Factor Collaboration (NCD-RisC)"],"corresponding_author":["Ezzati, Majid"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"keyword":["BMI","Epidemiology","Global Health","None","Obesity","Underweight"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-A