null,"first":"Magnus","key":"simrénpau","last":"Simrén","name":"Simrén, Magnus","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"öhmanpau","last":"Öhman","name":"Öhman, Lena","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/nu13113836","issn":["20726643"],"issue":"11","journal":"Nutrients","paperid":"3836","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Nutrients","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117906482"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Other Companies","Private Research","University Colleges","clinical microbiomics","dsm nutritional products ltd","ms-omics"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-87cf2ef9-2cda-4c73-bca3-8c9a1f673d54"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of human milk oligosaccharides on gut microbiota, metabolite profiles and host mucosal response in patients with irritable bowel syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-389489","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Metabolic syndrome (MetS) is a growing concern in survivors of pediatric hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (HSCT), but little is known about the underlying mechanisms. This study aimed to determine the prevalence and clinical presentation of MetS in male long-term survivors of pediatric HSCT and to investigate predisposing factors, including low-grade inflammation, altered fat distribution, and low testosterone levels. We included 98 survivors age 19 to 47 years at a median follow-up of 18 years (range, 8 to 35 years) after pediatric HSCT. MetS was defined according to the National Cholesterol Education Program Adult Treatment Panel III criteria. The prevalence and clinical manifestations of MetS were compared between our cohort and a control group of males from the background population (n = 4767). Fat distribution was assessed by android/gynoid ratio from a whole-body dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry scan. Systemic inflammation was evaluated by IL-6 and high-sensitivity C-reactive protein (hsCRP). Serum testosterone levels were measured in morning samples. The prevalence of MetS was 30%, corresponding to the prevalence in the 50- to 80-year-old males from the background population. In individuals with MetS, hyperglycemia was more frequent in the HSCT survivors compared with age-matched controls with MetS (76% versus 20%; P < .001), whereas hypertension was more dominant in the control group with MetS (69% versus 93%; P = .01). In addition, normal or low body mass index was more commonly observed among HSCT survivors with MetS compared with age-matched controls with MetS (41% versus 11%; P = .002). MetS was more often associated with total body irradiation (TBI) compared with chemotherapy regimens (odds ratio [OR], 4.3; 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.2 to 24.4; P = .02), lower testosterone levels (OR, 5.4; 95% CI, 1.3 to 23.6; P = .02), higher IL-6 levels (OR, 1.8; 95% CI, 1.2 to 2.8; P = .004), and higher hsCRP levels (OR, 1.8; 95% CI, 1.3 to 2.6; P < .001) (estimates per 2-fold increase). In addition, an increased android/gynoid (AG) fat ratio was strongly associated with MetS (OR, 2.1; 95% CI, 1.5 to 2.9; P < .001), even though only 7% of patients met the criteria for increased abdominal circumference. Our results indicate an increased risk of MetS in early adulthood after pediatric HSCT. The clinical manifestations differed from those seen in age-matched controls with MetS, indicating different pathophysiology driven by hyperglycemia, altered fat distribution (despite no clinical abdominal obesity), and low-grade inflammation. Risk factors included TBI-based conditioning and low testosterone levels. These results underline the importance of continuous clinical assessment of the cardiometabolic risk profile and stress the presence of important dissimilarities in the pathophysiology of MetS in HSCT survivors compared with the background population.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Muhic, Ena","Mathiesen, Sidsel","Nielsen, Malene Mejdahl","Suominen, Anu","Sørensen, Kaspar","Ifversen, Marianne","Nolsöe, Rúna Louise","Pedersen, Kasper M.","Lähteenmäki, Päivi","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Juul, Anders","Jahnukainen, Kirsi","Müller, Klaus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-408756"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet","University of Helsinki","University of Turku"],"keyword":["Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantation","Late effects","Long term survivors","Metabolic syndrome","Pediatrics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metabolic syndrome in male survivors of pediatric allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation impact of total body irradiation low grade inflammation and hypogonadism","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-408756","identifier":[{"id":"85110528766","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34091072","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-199e7972-cc8d-4566-bcbb-ac9386bf46fa"],"keyword":["Hematopoietic stem cell transplantation","Late effects","Long-term survivors","Metabolic syndrome","Pediatrics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2CC4779F25DF2BA9623FE6899C5C1DCE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fi","key":"university of turku","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Turku","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ena","key":"muhicpau","last":"Muhic","name":"Muhic, Ena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sidsel","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","name":"Mathiesen, Sidsel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malene Mejdahl","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Malene Mejdahl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anu","key":"suominenpau","last":"Suominen","name":"Suominen, Anu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kaspar","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Kaspar","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne","key":"ifversenpau","last":"Ifversen","name":"Ifversen, Marianne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rúna Louise","key":"nolsöepau","last":"Nolsöe","name":"Nolsöe, Rúna Louise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kasper Mønsted","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"4b91ba94-dffa-47a3-ae05-fbda7967701c","name":"Pedersen, Kasper M.","name_org":"Pedersen, Kasper Mønsted","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Päivi","key":"lähteenmäkipau","last":"Lähteenmäki","name":"Lähteenmäki, Päivi","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Børge Grønne","key":"nordestgaardpau","last":"Nordestgaard","locid":"733103b5-ddc2-416f-a686-48e694154a82","name":"Nordestgaard, Børge G","name_org":"Nordestgaard, Børge Grønne","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","first":"Kirsi","key":"jahnukainenpau","last":"Jahnukainen","name":"Jahnukainen, Kirsi","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Klaus","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","locid":"b909f13e-79e3-4363-aaff-e5a5ecbdf7ce","name":"Müller, Klaus","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34091072"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jtct.2021.05.025","issn":["26666367"],"issue":"9","journal":"Transplantation and Cellular Therapy","status":"p","title":"Transplantation and Cellular Therapy","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85110528766"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-199e7972-cc8d-4566-bcbb-ac9386bf46fa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Metabolic Syndrome in Male Survivors of Pediatric Allogeneic Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantation : Impact of Total Body Irradiation, Low-Grade Inflammation, and Hypogonadism","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-408756","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a feasibility study assessing the acceptability, demand, implementation, and practicality of postgraduate interprofessional case-based learning in childhood cancer at Copenhagen University Hospital—Rigshospitalet. Healthcare professionals included nurses, doctors, social workers, physiotherapists, occupational therapists, pharmacists, pharmacologists, dieticians, nursing assistants, and professionals with a supportive function (teachers, secretaries, priests, and daycare workers). All participated in a postgraduate interprofessional case-based learning session. Feasibility was assessed using Bowen’s focus areas of acceptability, demand, implementation, and practicality. Before and after the intervention session, three measurement tools were used 2–3 weeks before participation and 3–4 weeks after participation to collect data: Assessment of Interprofessional Team Collaboration Scale, Readiness for Interprofessional Learning Scale, and Safety Attitudes Questionnaire. Representing 13 occupational groups, 49 participants completed the case-based learning sessions, indicating acceptability and practicality. The pre-and post-intervention questionnaires were completed by 79% of the participants, 88% of whom rated the professional content as good or very good. A change over time was detected on all three scales measuring mean difference post-intervention scores. The outcome measures can be used to assess the effect of the intervention. Postgraduate interprofessional case-based learning in childhood cancer is feasible in terms of acceptability, demand, implementation, and practicality. Implementation requires leadership commitment at all levels.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Topperzer, Martha Krogh","Hoffmann, Marianne","Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","Rosthøj, Susanne","Fridh, Martin Kaj","Roug, Louise Ingerslev","Andres-Jensen, Liv","Pontoppidan, Peter Erik Lokto","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Sørensen, Jette Led"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-429575"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case based learning","Childhood cancer","Interprofessional","Postgraduate"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"postgraduate interprofessional case based learning in childhood cancer a feasibility study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers13174314","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-429575","identifier":[{"id":"34503122","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8430868","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85113514322","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3c77bc3f-8b5a-4465-ad39-50b05a005933"],"keyword":["Case-based learning","Childhood cancer","Interprofessional","Postgraduate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BB27EB806BD0A5F49F92DE323B9B5407"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/279273714/cancers_13_04314_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers13174314","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, No speciality"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martha Krogh","key":"topperzerpau","last":"Topperzer","name":"Topperzer, Martha Krogh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne","key":"hoffmannpau","last":"Hoffmann","name":"Hoffmann, Marianne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne Bækgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"88b48e37-454f-41e8-a110-a385dce66a6e","name":"Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Susanne","key":"rosthøjpau","last":"Rosthøj","locid":"56c290d5-658a-41a6-8540-26ae4ba1b42d","name":"Rosthøj, Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-3619-413X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin Kaj","key":"fridhpau","last":"Fridh","name":"Fridh, Martin Kaj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Louise Ingerslev","key":"rougpau","last":"Roug","locid":"267efa77-cd58-4287-9e1f-e1014c318205","name":"Roug, Louise Ingerslev","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Liv","key":"andresjensenpau","last":"Andres-Jensen","locid":"23762606-854b-4a40-831a-9da6952f0b67","name":"Andres-Jensen, Liv","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Erik Lokto","key":"pontoppidanpau","last":"Pontoppidan","name":"Pontoppidan, Peter Erik Lokto","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kjeld","key":"schmiegelowpau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"6ce2f948-244d-4f19-82aa-f08a71289674","name":"Schmiegelow, Kjeld","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jette Led","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"84ce4092-8277-45c1-89d5-afedea9c65f0","name":"Sørensen, Jette Led","orcid":"0000-0002-7320-2784","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34503122"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cancers13174314","issn":["20726694"],"issue":"17","journal":"Cancers","paperid":"4314","status":"p","title":"Cancers","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85113514322"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3c77bc3f-8b5a-4465-ad39-50b05a005933"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Postgraduate interprofessional case-based learning in childhood cancer : A feasibility study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-429575","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Dicer knockout mouse models demonstrated a key role for microRNAs in pancreatic β-cell function. Studies to identify specific microRNA(s) associated with human (pro-)endocrine gene expression are needed. We profiled microRNAs and key pancreatic genes in 353 human tissue samples. Machine learning workflows identified microRNAs associated with (pro-)insulin transcripts in a discovery set of islets (n = 30) and insulin-negative tissues (n = 62). This microRNA signature was validated in remaining 261 tissues that include nine islet samples from individuals with type 2 diabetes. Top eight microRNAs (miR-183-5p, -375-3p, 216b-5p, 183-3p, -7-5p, -217-5p, -7-2-3p, and -429-3p) were confirmed to be associated with and predictive of (pro-)insulin transcript levels. Use of doxycycline-inducible microRNA-overexpressing human pancreatic duct cell lines confirmed the regulatory roles of these microRNAs in (pro-)endocrine gene expression. Knockdown of these microRNAs in human islet cells reduced (pro-)insulin transcript abundance. Our data provide specific microRNAs to further study microRNA-mRNA interactions in regulating insulin transcription.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Wong, Wilson W.K.","Joglekar, Mugdha","Saini, Vijit","Jiang, Guozhi","Dong, Charlotte","Chaitarvornki, Alissa","Maciag, Grzegorz","Gerace, Dario","Farr, Ryan","Satoor, Sarang","Sahu, Subhshri","Sharangdhar, Tejaswini","Ahmed, Asma S","Chew, Yi Vee","Liuwantara, David","Heng, Benjamin","Lim, Chai K.","Hunter, Julie","Januszewski, Andrzej","Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Akil, Ammira","Gamble, Jennifer","Loudovaris, Thomas","Kay, Thomas W","Thomas, Helen","O'Connell, Philip","Guillemin, Gilles","Martin, David","Simpson, Ann","Hawthorne, Wayne","Dalgaard, Louise Torp","Ma, Ronald C","Hardikar, Anandwardhan A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-557172"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Hong Kong","Qatar"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Macquarie University","Sidra Medicine","Strathfield Private Hospital","The Chinese University of Hong Kong","The University of Melbourne","University of Sydney","University of Technology Sydney","Western Sydney University","Westmead Institute for Medical Research"],"keyword":["Pathophysiology","Transcriptomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["University of Sydney Medical School"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"machine learning workflows identify a microrna signature of insulin transcription in human tissues","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2021.102379","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-557172","identifier":[{"id":"85104302184","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-11b78252-7e4f-4724-98e9-b38c70b52b54"],"keyword":["Computational Bioinformatics","Pathophysiology","Transcriptomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7BEB96E977B137160E7AAE9F31A1D225"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/77428364/PIIS2589004221003473.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2021.102379","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"western sydney university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Western Sydney University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"the chinese university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The Chinese University of Hong Kong","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"