{"abstract":"Introduction Low cardiorespiratory fitness expressed as a low maximal oxygen consumption (V̇O2max) is associated with cardiovascular disease and all-cause mortality (1). Thus, V̇O2max is recognised as an important clinical tool in the assessment of patients (1,2). However, assessment of V̇O2max by exercise testing is both physically demanding and methodologically challenging and hence the clinical applicability is limited. Purpose Therefore, the aim of this study was to investigate the accuracy and precision of a clinical non-exercise method for assessment of V̇O2max. Methods On three separate days 20 healthy men (n=10) and women (n=10) with varying age (22–72 years) and fitness levels performed two tests for determination of V̇O2max; (a) a non-exercise test using seismocardiography (SCG V̇O2max) and (b) a graded exercise test to voluntary exhaustion on a cycle ergometer based on indirect calorimetry (IC V̇O2max). These tests were performed in order to examine the day-to-day reliability and the validity of SCG V̇O2max, respectively. Furthermore, SCG V̇O2max was assessed twice on each test day to investigate test-retest reliability. The SCG V̇O2max was performed in prone position following a short resting period by placing the SCG recording device on the xiphisternal joint with double adhesive tape. V̇O2max was assessed during a 5-minute recording of the sternal movement using SCG in combination with demographic data of the participants (3). In addition, body composition was measured and a resting blood sample collected each test day. Results On average SCG V̇O2max was 3.3±2.4 ml/min/kg (mean ± 95% CI) lower than IC V̇O2max (p=0.013, SCG V̇O2max: 36.6±3.3 ml/min/kg, IC V̇O2max: 39.9±3.0 ml/min/kg). A significant positive correlation was found between SCG V̇O2max and IC V̇O2max (Pearson, r=0.72, p<0.001). Both SCG V̇O2max and IC V̇O2max was similar between test days (p=0.972) and the intra-individual coefficient of variation was 4.5±2.9% and 4.0±2.5%, respectively. Within each test day SCG V̇O2max was highly correlated (r=0.99, p<0.0001) and no difference was observed between tests (p=0.993). Conclusions The accuracy of the current non-exercise assessment of cardiorespiratory fitness based on seismocardiography is not optimal as SCG V̇O2max was systematically lower than the gold standard assessment applying indirect calorimetry during a graded exercise test. Despite the abovementioned difference, SCG V̇O2max and IC V̇O2max were highly correlated. Furthermore, the precision of SCG V̇O2max is very high as both day-to-day and test-retest reliability were high.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hansen, Mikkel Thunestvedt","Rømer, Tue","Hoejgaard, A.","Husted, Karina Louise Skov","Soerensen, K.","Schmidt, S.","Dela, Flemming","Helge, Jørn Wulff"],"cuid":["S02-082.81-005026"],"event":{"end":"2021-08-30","place":"Virtual","start":"2021-08-27","title":"ESC Congress 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validity and reliability of a clinical non exercise method for assessment of cardiorespiratory fitness using seismocardiography","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-082.81-005026","identifier":[{"id":"000720456903473","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-67b9298e-524c-4209-8643-758b9629237c","ku-15552d75-5622-4539-a0cd-68bea5100cc5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4DFF1390A2277E490269E8A82AC06158"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Exercise and Muscle"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, CardioTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"M. Thunestvedt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58070c3b-ed1e-4859-9467-29b512cdea42","name":"Hansen, Mikkel Thunestvedt","name_org":"Hansen, M. Thunestvedt","orcid":"0000-0002-3879-2192","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"T.","key":"roemerpau","last":"Roemer","locid":"32b26587-2ba1-4451-b564-da70a76f4712","name":"Rømer, Tue","name_org":"Roemer, T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"A.","key":"hoejgaardpau","last":"Hoejgaard","locid":"aa3b35b9-6905-48cc-be99-6e94e364bf7a","name":"Hoejgaard, A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"81eaf062-83d5-4963-9de6-f713214ff461","name":"Sørensen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-0358-9354","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"K.","key":"hustedpau","last":"Husted","locid":"6d16a70a-d967-4c50-8c2c-7625021b4586","name":"Husted, Karina Louise Skov","name_org":"Husted, K.","orcid":"0000-0002-9280-1694","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. E.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"bb4b7dd4-cb80-4ac8-971e-160921ec26a2","name":"Schmidt, Samuel","name_org":"Schmidt, S. E.","orcid":"0000-0002-0917-634X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"K.","key":"soerensenpau","last":"Soerensen","name":"Soerensen, K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"F.","key":"delapau","last":"Dela","locid":"5d84458e-34c1-4874-a128-7fc3cb13f7f2","name":"Dela, Flemming","name_org":"Dela, F.","orcid":"0000-0001-9970-9535","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J. Wulff","key":"helgepau","last":"Helge","locid":"a5560afa-4f31-4278-8ae9-0c49fb0027c1","name":"Helge, Jørn Wulff","name_org":"Helge, J. Wulff","orcid":"0000-0001-9724-5423","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurheartj/ehab724.3044","issn":["0195668X","15229645"],"issn_org":["0195668X"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"European Heart Journal","paperid":"ehab724.3172","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-67b9298e-524c-4209-8643-758b9629237c","ku-15552d75-5622-4539-a0cd-68bea5100cc5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Validity and reliability of a clinical non-exercise method for assessment of cardiorespiratory fitness using seismocardiography","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.81-005026","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Most patients with symptoms suggestive of chronic coronary syndrome (CCS) have no obstructive coronary artery disease (CAD) and better selection of patients to be referred for diagnostic tests is needed. The CAD-score is a non-invasive acoustic measure that, when added to pretest probability of CAD, has shown good rule-out capabilities. We aimed to test whether implementation of CAD-score in clinical practice reduces the use of diagnostic tests without increasing major adverse cardiac events (MACE) rates in patients with suspected CCS. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: FILTER-SCAD is a randomised, controlled, multicenter trial aiming to include 2000 subjects aged ≥30 years without known CAD referred for outpatient assessment for symptoms suggestive of CCS. Subjects are randomised 1:1 to either the control group: standard diagnostic examination (SDE) according to the current guidelines, or the intervention group: SDE plus a CAD-score. The subjects are followed for 12 months for the primary endpoint of cumulative number of diagnostic tests and a safety endpoint (MACE). Angina symptoms, quality of life and risk factor modification will be assessed with questionnaires at baseline, 3 months and 12 months after randomisation. The study is powered to detect superiority in terms of a reduction of ≥15% in the primary endpoint between the two groups with a power of 80%, and non-inferiority on the secondary endpoint with a power of 90%. The significance level is 0.05. The non-inferiority margin is set to 1.5%. Randomisation began on October 2019. Follow-up is planned to be completed by December 2022. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: This study has been approved by the Danish Medical Agency (2019024326), Danish National Committee on Health Research Ethics (H-19012579) and Swedish Ethical Review Authority (Dnr 2019-04252). All patients participating in the study will sign an informed consent. All study results will be attempted to be published as soon as possible. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: NCT04121949; Pre-results.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Bjerking, Louise Hougesen","Hansen, Kim Wadt","Biering-Sørensen, Tor","Brønnum-Schou, Jens","Engblom, Henrik","Erlinge, David","Haahr-Pedersen, Sune Ammentorp","Heitmann, Merete","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Jensen, Magnus Thorsten","Kruse, Marie","Räder, Sune","Strange, Søren","Galatius, Søren","Prescott, Eva"],"cuid":["S02-095.79-040265"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bjerking, Louise Hougesen"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Skåne University Hospital"],"keyword":["Acoustics","Cardiology","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease diagnosis","Coronary heart disease","Cost Benefit Analysis","Humans","Ischaemic heart disease","Prospective Studies","Quality of Life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["The Danish Association of Practicing Medical Specialists"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cost effectiveness of adding a non invasive acoustic rule out test in the evaluation of patients with symptoms suggestive of coronary artery disease rationale and design of the prospective randomised controlled parallel group multicenter filter scad trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2021-049380","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Contributors EIBP, SG and KWH designed and initiated the study. LHB, KWH, EIBP and SG obtained funding. LHB wrote the manuscript. LHB, KWH, TB-S, JB-S, HE, DE, SAH-P, MH, JDH, MTJ, MK, SR, SS, SG and EIBP revised and approved the final version of the article. Funding Unrestricted grants for the study was provided by Acarix A/S, Kai Hansens Fond, Kai Houmann Nielsen Fond, and Fonden for Faglig Udvikling i Speciallægepraksis (A3068). Helsefonden (21-B-0348) has provided a grant for the study. Competing interests LHB, KWH, JB-S, HE, SAH-P, MH, JDH, MK, MTJ, SR, SS, SG and EP: None. TB-S: Steering Committee member of the Amgen financed GALACTIC-HF trial; Advisory Board: Sanofi Pasteur; Advisory Board: Amgen; Speaker Honorarium: Novartis; Speaker Honorarium: Sanofi Pasteur; Research grant: GE Healthcare; Research grant: Sanofi Pasteur. DE: Advisory board for Acarix A/S. Unrestricted grants for the study was provided by Acarix A/S, Kai Hansens Fond, Kai Houmann Nielsen Fond, and Fonden for Faglig Udvikling i Speciall?gepraksis (A3068). Helsefonden (21-B-0348) has provided a grant for the study."],"id":"S02-095.79-040265","identifier":[{"id":"85113508763","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34426466","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8383880","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-11288d20-d07c-49fa-80b6-c6b1983a9b17","sdu-8fed8ca9-8b01-41b4-aff6-42c279faea77"],"keyword":["Acoustics","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease/diagnosis","Cost-Benefit Analysis","Humans","Prospective Studies","Quality of Life","cardiology","coronary heart disease","ischaemic heart disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7428EC1723D86304A20C9881C8146793"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191412370/e049380.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/280733024/e049380.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2021-049380","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","m