","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bae0fea4-6951-4beb-875f-f41d468c2696","sdu-fed257da-5218-40f0-89da-1dcbdc23b6d0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Postoperative complications and waiting time for surgical intervention after radiologically guided drainage of intra-abdominal abscess in patients with Crohn's disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-009019","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Early identification of gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) aims to reduce the risk of adverse maternal and perinatal outcomes. Currently, no circulating biomarker has proven clinically useful for accurate prediction of GDM. In this study, we tested if a panel of small non-coding circulating RNAs could improve early prediction of GDM. We performed a nested case-control study of participants from the European multicenter ‘Vitamin D and lifestyle intervention for GDM prevention (DALI)’ trial using serum samples from obese pregnant women (BMI ≥ 29 kg/m2 ) entailing 82 GDM cases (early-and late-GDM), and 41 age-and BMI-matched women with normal glucose tolerance (NGT) throughout pregnancy (controls). Anthropometric, clinical and biochemical characteristics were obtained at baseline (<20 weeks of gestation) and throughout gestation. Baseline serum microRNAs (miRNAs) were measured using quantitative real time PCR (qPCR). Elevated miR-16-5p,-29a-3p, and-134-5p levels were observed in women, who were NGT at baseline and later developed GDM, compared with controls who remained NGT. A combination of the three miRNAs could distinguish later GDM from NGT cases (AUC 0.717, p = 0.001, compared with fasting plasma glucose (AUC 0.687, p = 0.004)) as evaluated by area under the curves (AUCs) using Receiver Operator Characteristics (ROC) analysis. Elevated levels of individual miRNAs or a combination hereof were associated with higher odds ratios of GDM. Conclusively, circulating miRNAs early in pregnancy could serve as valuable predictive biomarkers of GDM.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sørensen, Anja Elaine","van Poppel, Mireille N.M.","Desoye, Gernot","Damm, Peter","Simmons, David","Jensen, Dorte Møller","Dalgaard, Louise Torp"],"cuid":["S03-099.93-044826"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["DALI Core Investigator Group","The DALI Core Investigator Group"],"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Anja Elaine"],"country":["Australia","Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Medical University of Graz","University Hospital Graz","University of Graz","Western Sydney University"],"keyword":["Circulating microRNA","Gestational diabetes mellitus","MiR 122 5p","MiR 134 5p","MiR 16 5p","MiR 29a 3p","MicroRNAs","Obesity","Predictive biomarker","Pregnancy","Randomized control trial","Serum"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Institute of Metabolic Science, Addenbrookes Hospital, Cambridge, England and Macarthur Clinical School, Western Sydney University, Sydney, Australia."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the predictive value of mir 000000000016 000000000029a and 000000000134 for early identification of gestational diabetes a nested analysis of the dali cohort","src":["ku","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells10010170","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.93-044826","identifier":[{"id":"85100327142","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7830355","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33467738","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9f51c50c-83cc-4ee0-af05-1ca74a8d8065","ruc-3310861e-861b-4d68-8c5b-de34a58dcc3d","sdu-e96c02fd-1ae9-47bc-a9f1-2034eefa109c"],"keyword":["Circulating microRNA","Gestational diabetes mellitus","MiR-122-5p","MiR-134-5p","MiR-16-5p","MiR-29a-3p","MicroRNAs","Obesity","Predictive biomarker","Pregnancy","Randomized control trial","Serum"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-E8