16360f7a1","name":"Nyegaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-4973-8543","rank":30,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel F.","key":"gudbjartssondanielfpau","last":"Gudbjartsson","name":"Gudbjartsson, Daniel F.","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Hreinn","key":"stefanssonhreinnpau","last":"Stefansson","name":"Stefansson, Hreinn","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Kari","key":"stefanssonkaripau","last":"Stefansson","name":"Stefansson, Kari","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34079037"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s42003-021-02144-8","issn":["23993642"],"journal":"Communications Biology","pages":"655","paperid":"655","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Communications Biology","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85113872153"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b2efa0ac-88e6-429a-afeb-56a407fd08b7","au-e1c8c355-b7c3-4d98-8cf9-eaf7a5592e9e","cbs-3c5d4644-5aa3-4f46-93e4-8d7ba0d9556d","ku-83386a4b-46a8-436c-b10c-f948615123ca","sdu-2ca7a072-77ae-4c33-838d-406fde0ce7eb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","CBS Copenhagen Business School","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Eleven Genomic Loci Affect Plasma Levels of Chronic Inflammation Marker Soluble Urokinase-type Plasminogen Activator Receptor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-098.59-008622","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Recently, it has been established that the urine of a healthy adult bladder contains a microbiota and that urinary dysbiosis may be involved in the development of urinary tract diseases. The urinary microbiota and its relation to bladder health and disease in children is yet to be established. The objective of the present study was to investigate the voided urinary microbiota in asymptomatic prepubertal children. STUDY DESIGN: Thirty asymptomatic children (15 boys and 15 girls) participated in the study. Bacterial DNA in \"clean-catch\" midstream urine (CC MSU) samples was analysed using Illumina MiSeq sequencing of the V4 region of the bacterial 16 S rRNA gene. All children had normal bladder function as ensured by uroflowmetry, ultrasonic post-void residual, and frequency-volume charts. Bladder-related parameters and gender comparisons were analysed statistically by parametric and non-parametric tests. Alpha diversity, beta diversity, and a Venn diagram were used to analyse sequencing data. RESULTS: All CC MSU samples contained bacterial DNA. The voided urinary microbiota differed significantly between girls and boys in terms of operational taxonomic unit (OTU) richness, Shannon diversity index, and relative abundances of bacterial genera, but not for evenness. The urine of girls was dominated by Prevotella (18.2%), Porphyromonas (12.9%), Ezakiella (8.1%), Prevotella 6 (7.4%), and Dialister (7.0%). Porphyromonas (22.4%) was the most abundant genus in boys, followed by Ezakiella (12.0%), Campylobacter (11.6%), Prevotella (8.6%), and Dialister (3.7%). Girls had 10 unique core OTUs, whereas boys had no unique core OTUs. Porphyromonas appeared as a shared core OTU between genders. DISCUSSION: Contrary to previous findings, this study found significant differences in the voided urinary bacterial composition among asymptomatic prepubertal children. Moreover, the bacterial composition diverged from that found among healthy adults by other research groups. Among adults, the gender specific urinary microbiota has been hypothesised to be caused by anatomical differences in the reproductive organs and differences in sex hormone levels. This could also be evident for asymptomatic prepubertal children as sex hormone levels are different even at the prepubertal stage. The limitations of the study encompass small sample size and urine collection by CC MSU with risk of contamination from surrounding areas. CONCLUSIONS: This study documents that CC MSU samples of asymptomatic prepubertal children are not sterile. The composition of the voided urinary microbiota seems gender specific and unequal to that of healthy adults. The role of the urinary microbiota in paediatric urological disorders should be considered in future studies.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Fredsgaard, Lea","Thorsteinsson, Kristina","Bundgaard-Nielsen, Caspar","Ammitzbøll, Nadia","Leutscher, Peter Derek Christian","Chai, Qing","Jensen, Ann-Maria","Sørensen, Suzette","Pedersen, Lia Mendes","Hagstrøm, Søren","Arenholt, Louise Thomsen Schmidt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-069358"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thorsteinsson, Kristina"],"keyword":["Paediatric urology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"description of the voided urinary microbiota in asymptomatic prepubertal children a pilot study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85107017617&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-069358","identifier":[{"id":"85107017617","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34053859","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-42c169ff-1b61-483e-9bf2-7795c6b0a7b0"],"keyword":["Illumina MiSeq sequencing","Paediatric urology","Urinary microbiota"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACDA2E0D83A09A3B02DE1B649F9D8752"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for Clinical Research","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, North Denmark Regional Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lea","key":"fredsgaardpau","last":"Fredsgaard","locid":"1b4002df-d5b3-4187-bcc8-f2e21be7df27","name":"Fredsgaard, Lea","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"thorsteinssonpau","last":"Thorsteinsson","locid":"d1f7ae4e-6bbf-40a1-abd8-1ac37f2ac54c","name":"Thorsteinsson, Kristina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Caspar","key":"bundgaardnielsenpau","last":"Bundgaard-Nielsen","locid":"621f32eb-b0ed-4146-bed9-a4b793ee401d","name":"Bundgaard-Nielsen, Caspar","orcid":"0000-0002-2700-2378","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia","key":"ammitzbøllpau","last":"Ammitzbøll","locid":"998438bb-addc-4afc-b906-dcd21786cba2","name":"Ammitzbøll, Nadia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"leutscherpau","last":"Leutscher","locid":"56e8c48e-c3f9-4a4d-8b9b-0719c74da258","name":"Leutscher, Peter Derek Christian","name_org":"Leutscher, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-1168-4041","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qing","key":"chaipau","last":"Chai","locid":"16418fa2-cb26-4678-aeb4-d48ff6a8df55","name":"Chai, Qing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Maria","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b63dffe4-c4a2-410a-a9d9-5f75f27f0e0e","name":"Jensen, Ann-Maria","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Suzette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c96d8309-747c-403d-a858-2efad1aea498","name":"Sørensen, Suzette","orcid":"0000-0002-4201-1168","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lia M","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"3e66f6d1-fa95-4825-98fc-d44fcdb6e65c","name":"Pedersen, Lia Mendes","name_org":"Pedersen, Lia M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"hagstrømpau","last":"Hagstrøm","locid":"fe472f53-6bcd-4587-8287-df1539f689c3","name":"Hagstrøm, Søren","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise T S","key":"arenholtpau","last":"Arenholt","locid":"9fe53819-b8b7-4220-8f9f-125eb33881e8","name":"Arenholt, Louise Thomsen Schmidt","name_org":"Arenholt, Louise T S","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34053859"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpurol.2021.03.019","issn":["14775131","18734898"],"issn_org":["14775131"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Pediatric Urology","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Pediatric Urology","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107017617"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-42c169ff-1b61-483e-9bf2-7795c6b0a7b0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Description of the voided urinary microbiota in asymptomatic prepubertal children - A pilot study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-069358","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Helicopter emergency medical services (HEMS) are part of many emergency health care systems, ensuring specialized treatment on scene. An accurate use is important for improved resource utilization. The aim of this study was to describe patient characteristics, hospitalization, and mortality in trauma and nontrauma patients seen by the Danish HEMS teams. Methods: The study is a registry-based study presenting data from the national Danish HEMS database. We included all HEMS missions from October 1, 2014, to April 30, 2018. Results: A total of 13,391 HEMS entries were registered, and 5,524 cases were included in the study. Trauma patients were younger (38 vs. 63 years) and had a lower level of comorbidities (Charlson Comorbidity Index 0: 82% vs. 58%) compared with nontrauma patients. More nontrauma cases were classified with a severity score corresponding to a critical emergency. They also had a higher 30-day mortality compared with trauma patients (26% vs. 11%). Conclusion: This national study demonstrated differences in demographics, the severity profile, and mortality among trauma compared with nontrauma patients that could possibly indicate an overuse of HEMS for minor trauma cases. The results might suggest that educational efforts and a review of the current dispatch guidelines could be of importance when trying to improve the use of HEMS.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sørensen, Louise Marqvard","Rognås, Leif","Alstrup, Karen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-130354"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Alstrup, Karen"],"keyword":["Air Ambulances","Aircraft","Denmark epidemiology","Emergency Medical Services","Hospitalization","Humans","Injury Severity Score","Retrospective Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trauma versus nontrauma patients treated by the danish helicopter emergency medical service a register based study of patient characteristics hospitalization and mortality","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amj.2021.05.005","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-130354","identifier":[{"id":"85108515551","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34535240","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-01edcf4f-a819-4ee9-8f58-5373b69cc710"],"keyword":["Air Ambulances","Aircraft","Denmark/epidemiology","Emergency Medical Services","Hospitalization","Humans","Injury Severity Score","Retrospective Studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-12E375A166EEF306AEEF6475BB489BD4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amj.2021.05.005","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/273705547/1_s2.0_S1067991X21000936_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Marqvard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Louise Marqvard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leif","key":"rognåspau","last":"Rognås","locid":"982efaff-df9a-4a33-bd3d-c376879db4be","name":"Rognås, Leif","orcid":"0000-0002-2542-565X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"alstruppau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"4953db23-abb5-437d-933f-c6c0a22995b2","name":"Alstrup, Karen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34535240"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.amj.2021.05.005","issn":["1067991X","15326497"],"issn_org":["1067991X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Air Medical Journal","pages":"325-330","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Air Medical Journal","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108515551"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-01edcf4f-a819-4ee9-8f58-5373b69cc710"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Trauma Versus Nontrauma Patients Treated by the Danish Helicopter Emergency Medical Service : A Register-Based Study of Patient Characteristics, Hospitalization, and Mortality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-130354","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Linket til højre henviser til rapporten i trykt format til download. Dokumentet over linket er selve leveringen til ministeriet med følgebrev . Formålet med denne rapport er at dokumentere, hvordan Normtal for husdyrgødningens indhold af næringsstoffer beregnes. Normtallene udgør et gennemsnit for gødningens indhold af næringsstoffer for et stort antal kombinationer af husdyrart, dyrekategori, opstaldning og gødningsopbevaring. Beregningen af de nye normtal er sket efter de samme grundprincipper, som blev anvendt i DJF Rapport nr. 36 fra 2001. Selve beregningen af normtallene er foretaget som et massebalanceregnskab. Normtallene anvendes som grundlag for udformning af gødningsbekendtgørelser, som regulerer næringsstoftildelingen på markerne. Normtallene anvendes desuden til nationale opgørelser af næringsstofbalancer og emissioner. I fremtiden kommer der årligt opdateringer på https://anis.au.dk/forskning/sektioner/husdyrernaering-og-fysiologi/normtal/. Rapporten er udarbejdet efter opdrag fra ”Normudvalget vedr. kvælstofnormer, -prognoser og kvælstof i husdyrgødning”, der indstiller husdyrnormerne og relaterede data til Landbrugsstyrelsen. Normudvalget består på af repræsentanter fra Aarhus Universitet, Københavns Universitet, SEGES og Ministeriet for Fødevarer, Landbrug og Fiskeri, herunder Landbrugsstyrelsen.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Børsting, Christian Friis","Hellwing, Anne Louise Frydendahl","Sørensen, Martin Tang","Lund, Peter","van der Heide, Marleen Elise","Møller, Steen Henrik","Kai, Peter","Nyord, Tavs","Aaes, Ole","Clausen, Eric","Tybirk, Per","Holm, Michael","Hansen, Martin Nørregaard","Jensen, Henrik Bang","Bækgaard, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-201250"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["T0 2020"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":[