{"abstract":"Anbefalinger af faghistorisk litteratur og podcasts som er velegnede til at læse og lytte i sommertiden.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Nils Arne","Kallestrup, Louise Nyholm","Bregnsbo, Michael","Olesen, Niels Wium"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-641449"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sommerfornøjelser nok mest for historikere","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.facebook.com/temp.tidsskrift.for.historie/photos/pb.1426741127557434.-2207520000../2740256156205918/?type=3&theater","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-641449","ids":["sdu-ee30c035-7989-4d8d-87f1-cd04e5523a00"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8EEE23C0C7010346BB6994A08E276237"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.facebook.com/temp.tidsskrift.for.historie/photos/pb.1426741127557434.-2207520000../2740256156205918/?type=3&theater","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History, The History Programme in Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nils Arne","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"11525225-c9e5-4114-b748-d17ee6582c10","name":"Sørensen, Nils Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-7399-9386","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Nyholm","key":"kallestruppau","last":"Kallestrup","locid":"7713c2a5-db5f-48c1-8ecc-2caec0cac68c","name":"Kallestrup, Louise Nyholm","orcid":"0000-0002-4598-9401","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"bregnsbopau","last":"Bregnsbo","locid":"e8f5419c-975a-4484-8ec1-9e91e864cbd7","name":"Bregnsbo, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-1403-8718","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Wium","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Niels Wium","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["sdu-ee30c035-7989-4d8d-87f1-cd04e5523a00"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sommerfornøjelser - nok mest for historikere","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-641449","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Mutations in the genes encoding the highly conserved Ca2+-sensing protein calmodulin (CaM) cause severe cardiac arrhythmias, including catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia or long QT syndrome and sudden cardiac death. Most of the identified arrhythmogenic mutations reside in the C-terminal domain of CaM and mostly affect Ca2+-coordinating residues. One exception is the catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia-causing N53I substitution, which resides in the N-terminal domain (N-domain). It does not affect Ca2+ coordination and has only a minor impact on binding affinity toward Ca2+ and on other biophysical properties. Nevertheless, the N53I substitution dramatically affects CaM's ability to reduce the open probability of the cardiac ryanodine receptor (RyR2) while having no effect on the regulation of the plasmalemmal voltage-gated Ca2+ channel, Cav1.2. To gain more insight into the molecular disease mechanism of this mutant, we used NMR to investigate the structures and dynamics of both apo- and Ca2+-bound CaM-N53I in solution. We also solved the crystal structures of WT and N53I CaM in complex with the primary calmodulin-binding domain (CaMBD2) from RyR2 at 1.84-2.13 Å resolutions. We found that all structures of the arrhythmogenic CaM-N53I variant are highly similar to those of WT CaM. However, we noted that the N53I substitution exposes an additional hydrophobic surface and that the intramolecular dynamics of the protein are significantly altered such that they destabilize the CaM N-domain. We conclude that the N53I-induced changes alter the interaction of the CaM N-domain with RyR2 and thereby likely cause the arrhythmogenic phenotype of this mutation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Holt, Christian","Hamborg, Louise","Lau, Kelvin","Brohus, Malene","Sorensen, Anders B","Larsen, Kamilla Taunsig","Sommer, Cordula","Van Petegem, Filip","Overgaard, Michael Toft","Wimmer, Reinhard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-095429"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of British Columbia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the arrhythmogenic n000000000053i variant subtly changes the structure and dynamics in the calmodulin n terminal domain altering its interaction with the cardiac ryanodine receptor","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85085714994&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-095429","identifier":[{"id":"32317284","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85085714994","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9c766350-95e1-4e57-ae00-3cc86c14efcf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1F426A701EAEF86D46BBBF044B1DF9EB"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Medical Biotechnology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of british columbia","loc":["Canada","Ame