:"Schramm, Stine","orcid":"0000-0001-8039-8095","rank":43,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"sodemannoth","last":"Sodemann","locid":"e4e58879-7d72-4665-880c-38ad97d0ebe5","name":"Sodemann, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-8992-2500","rank":44,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"tarpoth","last":"Tarp","name":"Tarp, Jakob","rank":45,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Betina H.","key":"thuesenoth","last":"Thuesen","name":"Thuesen, Betina H.","rank":46,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Janne S.","key":"tolstrupoth","last":"Tolstrup","locid":"c03b1732-7c6e-404e-a542-e7d02e2b2575","name":"Tolstrup, Janne Schurmann","name_org":"Tolstrup, Janne S.","orcid":"0000-0002-9796-3967","rank":47,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian","key":"wangoth","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Qian","rank":48,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"wedderkoppoth","last":"Wedderkopp","locid":"bcfae344-0a75-458d-8ba2-4198ee915d40","name":"Wedderkopp, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-9660-6618","rank":49,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["33160572"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s0140-6736(20)31859-6","issn":["00995355","01406736"],"issn_org":["01406736"],"issue":"10261","journal":"The Lancet","pages":"1511-1524","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"The Lancet","title_org":"Lancet","volume":"396"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","UC SYD, University College South Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-902e3b9c-6afe-47e1-a3b7-05b41114debe","kp-c480e80b-4a60-4244-b369-c51a9ad2d13b","ku-8ec6726d-1542-4454-b3a6-c59c45205e5c","sdu-f477f297-a604-425c-aeac-6cfcbb3935bb","ucl-e250086c-202a-422c-a2fc-a8c37ceb21bd","ucsyd-0eabaa65-8f37-433e-b88c-be7efe8822e0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark","UC SYD University College South Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"Height and body-mass index trajectories of school-aged children and adolescents from 1985 to 2019 in 200 countries and territories : a pooled analysis of 2181 population-based studies with 65 million participants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S06-099.98-793348","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Fusarium pseudograminearum (Fp), the causative fungal pathogen of the diseases Fusarium crown rot, is an important constraint to cereals production in many countries including Australia. Fp produces a number of secondary metabolites throughout its life cycle. One of these metabolites, the cyclic lipopeptide fusaristatin A, is encoded by a specific gene cluster containing a polyketide synthase and a three-module non-ribosomal peptide synthetase. However, a recent survey of Fp populations across Australia suggests that this cluster may only be present in a subset of isolates from Western Australia (WA). In this study, we screened 319 Fp isolates from WA and 110 Fp isolates from the Australian eastern states of New South Wales, Victoria, Queensland and South Australia to examine the distribution of this gene cluster among Australian Fp populations. The fusaristatin A gene cluster was found to be present in ~50% of Fp isolates from WA but completely absent in Fp isolates from eastern states. To determine its potential function, mutants of the fusaristatin A gene cluster were generated by disrupting the non-ribosomal peptide synthetase and polyketide synthase genes simultaneously in two different parental backgrounds. The mutants showed increased growth rates and were significantly more aggressive than their respective parental strains on wheat in crown rot pathogenicity assays. This suggested that fusaristatin A has a negative effect on fungal development and aggressiveness. The possible reasons for the geographically restricted presence of the fusaristatin A gene cluster and its role in fungal biology are discussed.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Khudhair, Mohammed","Kazan, Kemal","Thatcher, Louise","Obanor, Friday","Rusu, Anca","Sørensen, Jens Laurids","Wollenberg, Rasmus","McKay, Alan","Giblot-Ducray, Daniéle","Simpfendorfer, Steven","Aitken, Elizabeth","Gardiner, Donald Max"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-051800"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Gardiner, Donald Max"],"country":["Australia","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Australian Government, Grains Research and Development Corporation","CSIRO","NSW Department of Primary Industries","South Australian Research and Development Institute","University of Perugia","University of Queensland"],"keyword":["Aggressiveness","Fusarium crown rot","Fusarium pseudograminearum","Polyketide","Secondary metabolites"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fusaristatin a production negatively affects the growth and aggressiveness of the wheat pathogen i fusarium pseudograminearum i","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85076249888&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-051800","identifier":[{"id":"85076249888","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0618124b-8e2b-4313-baa6-721e742c54b6"],"keyword":["Aggressiveness","Fusarium crown rot","Fusarium pseudograminearum","Head blight","Polyketide","Secondary metabolites","fusaristatin A gene cluster"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-08C4C095302E34515A3A62197F298741"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"csiro","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"CSIRO","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"university of queensland","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Queensland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"australian government grains research and development corporation","loc":