{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Martin Tang","Børsting, Christian Friis","Hellwing, Anne Louise Frydendahl","Kai, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-135461"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["T0 2020"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"udredning af mulighed for implementering af krav om reduceret råprotein i slagtesvin og malkekvægfoder i forbindelse med nec udvalgsarbejdet beregning af ammoniakreduktionseffekt samt udredning af sideeffekter besvarelse vedr slagtesvinefoder","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dme","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/190944028/Reduceret_protein_til_slagtesvin_100620.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-135461","ids":["au-0acc5242-8245-4eac-99d1-1e79b43e4d0d"],"keyword":["T0-2020"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3280D86B879236296F2C274AA23FA2E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/190944028/Reduceret_protein_til_slagtesvin_100620.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Tang","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"fefc1862-587c-4b1f-9e20-694246b18221","name":"Sørensen, Martin Tang","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-4282","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Friis","key":"børstingpau","last":"Børsting","locid":"335191b3-2ebe-47f4-b7c9-9fc3d198044e","name":"Børsting, Christian Friis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Louise Frydendahl","key":"hellwingpau","last":"Hellwing","locid":"ad65c0e8-8a1c-4f17-bb65-80aec2189e32","name":"Hellwing, Anne Louise Frydendahl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kaipau","last":"Kai","locid":"7503d031-8020-4d17-ae34-c18e11bd8f15","name":"Kai, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-5416-931X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0acc5242-8245-4eac-99d1-1e79b43e4d0d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Udredning af mulighed for implementering af krav om reduceret råprotein i slagtesvin- og malkekvægfoder i forbindelse med NEC-udvalgsarbejdet. Beregning af ammoniakreduktionseffekt samt udredning af sideeffekter. Besvarelse vedr. slagtesvinefoder","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-135461","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To assess the prevalence and type distribution of oral human papillomavirus (HPV) among renal transplant recipients (RTRs) and healthy controls and to examine risk factors for oral HPV among RTRs. Materials and Methods: During 2016-2017 we recruited 250 RTRs and 250 controls. Oral samples were tested for HPV DNA with INNO-LiPA HPV Genotyping Extra II. All participants answered a questionnaire on lifestyle and sexual behaviour, and characteristics of RTRs were obtained from medical files. We assessed prevalence and type distribution of oral HPV. Using logistic regression, the risk of oral HPV and risk factors for oral HPV among RTRs were estimated as odds ratios (OR) with 95% confidence intervals (CI). Results: Overall, 30 RTRs (12.1%) and 26 controls (10.4%) were oral HPV positive (OR = 1.14; 95% CI: 0.64–2.05). Female RTRs tended to have a higher oral HPV prevalence than controls (OR = 1.73; 95% CI: 0.63–4.77), while no difference was observed among men. HPV51 was the commonest genotype. Sexual behaviour tended to be associated with oral HPV among RTRs. Conclusions: There was no overall difference in oral HPV prevalence between RTRs and controls, but female RTRs tended to have a higher prevalence of oral HPV than controls.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Faber, Mette T.","Kjær, Alexander K.","Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","Thomsen, Louise T.","Haedersdal, Merete","Bonde, Jesper","Hansen, Jesper Melchior","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-419168"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human papillomavirus","Oral","Prevalence","Renal transplant recipients","Risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence type distribution and risk factors for oral hpv in danish renal transplant recipients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-419168","identifier":[{"id":"31742827","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85076424869","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2b28e10a-08d3-483b-aa4f-a2a7898cf958"],"keyword":["human papillomavirus","oral","prevalence","renal transplant recipients","risk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-97539470E7C6E12847BE7C5116E8F4A7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette T.","key":"fabermettetpau","last":"Faber","name":"Faber, Mette T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alexander K.","key":"kjæralexanderkpau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Alexander K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle K.","key":"larsenhellekiellbergpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cff32a53-c07d-466a-9bf3-cc621c1e2cb6","name":"Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","name_org":"Larsen, Helle K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise T.","key":"thomsenlouisetpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Louise T.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Merete","key":"haedersdalmeretepau","last":"Hædersdal","locid":"fef92f7f-7d21-4a42-903e-24071d35047b","name":"Haedersdal, Merete","name_org":"Hædersdal, Merete","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper","key":"bondejesperpau","last":"Bonde","name":"Bonde, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper M.","key":"hansenjespermelchiorpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3926a380-bc2a-42ca-b393-f1b9b464d1bc","name":"Hansen, Jesper Melchior","name_org":"Hansen, Jesper M.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren S.","key":"sørensensørenschwartzpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","name_org":"Sørensen, Søren S.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaersusannekpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjær, Susanne K.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31742827"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/odi.13240","issn":["1354523X","16010825"],"issn_org":["1354523X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Oral Diseases","pages":"484-488","status":"p","title":"Oral Diseases","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076424869"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2b28e10a-08d3-483b-aa4f-a2a7898cf958"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevalence, type distribution and risk factors for oral HPV in Danish renal transplant recipients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-419168","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Noninvasive prenatal testing (NIPT) has become a popular screening test for the most common fetal aneuploidies. The performance of NIPT is affected by several factors including maternal obesity, which results in a greater rate of no-calls for obese pregnant women. Guidelines regarding NIPT in prenatal screening have been published, but with few and divergent recommendations on the issue. We aimed to review the medical literature, guidelines from scientific societies and information material from commercial NIPT providers on no-calls and maternal obesity. We systematically identified medical literature and guidelines from scientific societies using the database MEDLINE. Information material from commercial NIPT providers was found via a systematic search on Google.com. Nine medical studies investigating the association between maternal obesity and NIPT no-calls were included. They all showed the same trend: increasing no-call rate with increasing maternal obesity. The no-call rate ranged from 0% to 4.2% for women with body mass index (BMI) 18.5-24.9 and from 5.4% to 70.1% for women BMI ≥40. We identified 17 scientific societies with guidelines and 13 commercial NIPT providers. All were checked for information material on no-calls and maternal obesity. To allow comparison, all guidelines were examined to answer the same three predefined questions. Of the 17 included scientific societies, 13 (76.5%) mentioned the association between maternal obesity and NIPT no-calls, two (11.8%) specified weight limits and three (17.6%) advised against NIPT for severely obese pregnant women. None of the 13 commercial NIPT providers provided specific recommendations, but four (30.8%) cite maternal obesity as a potential cause for a no-call. Because of the increasing number of patients in this group, we advocate updated recommendations to guide decision making in prenatal screening for obese pregnant women.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Juul, Laura A","Hartwig, Tanja S