{"abstract":"The authors regret “the lack of the abstract in the original version”. The authors have published the abstract now in this corrigendum. The authors would like to apologise for any inconvenience caused. Abstract Bypass grafting using autologous vessels or synthetic vascular conduits still has many limitations especially with small-diameter (SD) arteries, thus new approaches to produce alternative vascular grafts are required. Decellularization is a promising solution to produce tissue engineering vascular grafts. Herein, we aimed to test whether decellularized human umbilical artery (dHUA) remains a suitable scaffold for future use in vascular graft bioengineering. Human umbilical artery (HUA) was successfully decellularized as determined by the absence of visible nuclei, and reduction in DNA content, whereas Masson's Trichrome stains and quantitative proteomics showed preservation of the extracellular matrix components. Moreover, elimination of MHC class I and II in dHUA was verified by immunohistochemistry, and mechanical testing demonstrated no differences regarding ultimate tensile strength and suture retention strength between decellularized and native HUA. Human umbilical cord vascular endothelial cells (HUVECs) attached and grew well within the dHUA while maintained in a perfusion 3D-bioreactor, confirming dHUA cytocompatibility. Finally, in vivo implantation in sheep carotid bypass model confirmed that dHUA withstood arterial blood pressure in vivo with successful anastomosis. Sheep host immune blood cell count showed no obvious difference between dHUA and allogeneic sheep decellularized vessel. Yet, ultrasound examination and end-point histology, confirmed as expected that dHUA is prone to early (<day 7) thrombosis and immune cell infiltration (day 28) before the occurrence of re-endothelialization whereas allogeneic decellularized sheep carotid seems protected from this type of occlusion. Together this suggest that allogeneic dHUA in an autologous endothelialized version is an applicable strategy for developing SD vascular grafts.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Fang, Shu","Riber, Sara Schødt","Hussein, Kamal","Ahlmann, Alexander Høgsted","Harvald, Eva Bang","Khan, Fazal","Beck, Hans Christian","Weile, Louise Katrine Kjær","Sørensen, Jens Ahm","Sheikh, Søren Paludan","Riber, Lars","Andersen, Ditte Caroline"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-616330"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Ditte Caroline"],"country":["Egypt"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Assiut University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"corrigendum to decellularized human umbilical artery biocompatibility and in vivo functionality in sheep carotid bypass model mater sci eng c 000000000112 000000002020 000000110955 materials science amp engineering c 000000002020 000000000112 s928493119315206 000000000010 000000001016 j msec 000000002020 000000110955","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086437755","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-616330","identifier":[{"id":"85086437755","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32806232","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-96958854-a7fe-4eae-93dd-025603f1add1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-670820393741EB066DBE4A8A6ED5BC83"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Biochemistry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"eg","key":"assiut university","loc":["Egypt","Africa"],"name":"Assiut University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shu","key":"fangshupau","last":"Fang","locid":"7add42ac-1b35-4c13-8be6-2bd437324062","name":"Fang, Shu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Schødt","key":"ribersaraschødtpau","last":"Riber","locid":"e56152e3-16a6-4e1c-9a97-42b4184bac46","name":"Riber, Sara Schødt","orcid":"0000-0001-8001-2076","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kamal","key":"husseinkamalpau","last":"Hussein","locid":"cd7afed4-097b-4892-aef6-93a735333f99","name":"Hussein, Kamal","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander Høgsted","key":"ahlmannalexanderhøgstedpau","last":"Ahlmann","locid":"a8deee4b-acc8-481d-915d-7ba64b16bf7d","name":"Ahlmann, Alexander Høgsted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Bang","key":"harvaldevabangpau","last":"Harvald","locid":"3945633e-85f1-4318-990c-c0a854545dbf","name":"Harvald, Eva Bang","orcid":"0000-0002-3536-3886","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fazal","key":"khanfazalpau","last":"Khan","locid":"476978c5-4b86-478e-905e-c56b1e4750b8","name":"Khan, Fazal","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Christian","key":"beckhanschristianpau","last":"Beck","locid":"93687fda-7a9e-4e81-8cf0-49cc73c0fe73","name":"Beck, Hans Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-7763-3637","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Katrine Kjær","key":"weilelouisekatrinekjærpau","last":"Weile","locid":"2284a0db-35d7-49b6-b78a-bd64975db357","name":"Weile, Louise Katrine Kjær","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country"