au","last":"Vishwakarma","name":"Vishwakarma, Bramha Dutt","rank":84,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"wiesepau","last":"Wiese","name":"Wiese, David","rank":85,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"wiltonpau","last":"Wilton","name":"Wilton, David","rank":86,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"wagnerpau","last":"Wagner","name":"Wagner, Thomas","rank":87,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bert","key":"wouterspau","last":"Wouters","name":"Wouters, Bert","rank":88,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"wuitepau","last":"Wuite","name":"Wuite, Jan","rank":89,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"The IMBIE","key":"teampau","last":"Team","name":"Team, The IMBIE","rank":90,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31822019"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-019-1855-2","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["14764687"],"journal":"Nature","pages":"233-239","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"579"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078287272"],"sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-318b7aaa-a0e8-4942-87fe-8a45e677cec2","ku-f7167296-7c5c-4eaf-8b1b-045378c39166"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mass balance of the Greenland Ice Sheet from 1992 to 2018","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.58-033690","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Metformin is associated with increased insulin sensitivity, whereas oral contraceptive pills (OCP) could increase the risk for type 2 diabetes (T2D) in women with polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS). Certain microRNAs (miRNAs) might serve as biomarkers for the risk of T2D. The aim of this study was to investigate changes in circulating miRNA levels during treatment with metformin and OCP in women with PCOS. Sixty-five women with PCOS according to Rotterdam criteria were randomized to metformin (2g/d), metformin+OCP (150 mg desogestrel + 30 µg ethinylestradiol) or OCP alone for 12 months. Serum miRNA analysis was performed with individual RT-qPCR or Taqman Low Density Array cards of 22 selected miRNAs previously related to PCOS, glucose and/or lipid metabolism. MiR-122 and miR-29a levels were decreased after treatment with metformin compared with metformin+OCP and OCP group: miR-122: log2 difference -0.7 (p= 0.01) and -0.7 (p= 0.02), miR-29a: log2 difference -0.5 (p= 0.01) and -0.4 (p= 0.04), while miR-223 levels were decreased in the metformin+OCP group after treatment: log2 difference -0.5 (p=0.02). During the treatment period, a significant weight loss was observed in the metformin group compared with the OCP group. In the OCP group, miRNA levels were unchanged during the treatment period. Levels of circulating miRNAs associated with lipid and glucose metabolism decreased during metformin treatment. Changes in miRNA levels in the metformin group could be explained by the simultaneous weight loss in the same group. These results support the notion that metformin treatment alone may be superior for metabolic health compared with OCP.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bækgaard Udesen, Pernille","Glintborg, Dorte","Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Svendsen, Rikke","Frisk, Nanna Lond Skov","Wissing, Marie Louise Muff","Andersen, Marianne Skovsager","Mikkelsen Englund, Anne-Lis","Dalgaard, Louise Torp"],"cuid":["S02-095.08-048175"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Udesen, Pernille Bækgaard"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Metformin","Polycystic Ovary Syndrome","miR 122","microRNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["The Fertility Clinic"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metformin decreases mir 000000000122 mir 000000000223 and mir 000000000029a in women with polycystic ovary syndrome","src":["ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-20-0195","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This article is part of ReproUnion collaborative study, co-financed by the European Union, 阀nterreg V ?KS. The salary for P B U is funded by the grant from ReproUnion. A E S is funded by the Danish Diabetes Academy funded by Novo Nordisk Foundation. The funders had no influence on the design of the study, interpretation of results or decision to publish. The work of D G was supported by the Jacob Madsen’s and Olga Madsen’s Foundation, the Institute of Clinical Research, the Odense University Hospital, Kolding Hospital, the A. P. Møller’s Foundation, the Bernhard and Marie Kleins Foundation, The Novo Nordisk Foundation, and The Danish Medical Association. Oral contraceptive pills and metformin tablets were sponsored by Sandoz."],"id":"S02-095.08-048175","identifier":[{"id":"33112812","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7774773","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85097658293","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-202c42ef-1cb6-4c5c-9d3f-8c9a65f9c6c7","sdu-acbb78bd-1803-46d9-94e0-2756365621ce"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Metformin","Polycys