ss","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-071681","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"STUDY QUESTION: Is the fetal fraction (FF) of circulating cell-free DNA (cfDNA) affected in pregnancies following ART treatment with either fresh or frozen embryo transfer (ET) compared with natural conception? SUMMARY ANSWER: This study shows a significant reduction in the FF in ART patients compared with naturally conceived pregnancies, which seems to be more pronounced after fresh ET compared with frozen ET. WHAT IS KNOWN ALREADY: Non-invasive prenatal testing (NIPT) is based on cfDNA in maternal blood, of which about 10% is of placental origin and thus represents the fetal karyotype. Validation studies have demonstrated a high sensitivity, specificity and positive predictive value of NIPT for the detection of fetal trisomy 21, 18 and 13. Nevertheless, the FF of cfDNA is an important factor for NIPT test accuracy. Several studies have found a reduction in FF for pregnancies following ART in comparison with natural conception. However, knowledge on how the FF is affected in ART pregnancies after fresh ET compared with frozen ET is very limited. STUDY DESIGN, SIZE, DURATION: The study was designed as a case-control study. A total of 54 women with an ongoing pregnancy following ART treatment were included. After exclusion for different reasons, statistical analyses were based on 23 NIPT samples from pregnant women treated with fresh ET and 26 NIPT samples from pregnant women treated with frozen-thawed ET in a modified natural cycle. Women were included between February 2018 and November 2018. The results were compared with a control group of 238 naturally conceived pregnancies with a high-risk result from the combined first trimester screening (cFTS). PARTICIPANTS/MATERIALS, SETTING, METHODS: The study included women from the Fertility Clinics at Copenhagen University Hospital Hvidovre and Copenhagen University Hospital Rigshospitalet. Blood samples for NIPT analysis were drawn between 11 + 0 and 14 + 2 weeks of gestation and were all analyzed at the NIPT Center at Copenhagen University Hospital Hvidovre. The NIPT-test was performed by massive-parallel whole-genome sequencing. The FF was determined using the SeqFF algorithm. MAIN RESULTS AND THE ROLE OF CHANCE: We found a reduction in FF in ART patients compared with naturally conceived pregnancies, and the reduction was more pronounced for ART pregnancies after fresh ET (mean FF = 0.049) compared with frozen ET (mean FF = 0.063) (multivariate analysis adjusted for maternal BMI, P = 0.02). Another multivariate analysis, adjusted for BMI and multiples of median (MoM) values for pregnancy-associated plasma protein-A (PAPP-A), demonstrated a significantly reduced FF for ART pregnancies (mean FF = 0.056) compared with naturally conceived pregnancies (mean FF = 0.072) (P < 0.0001). We found that FF was significantly reduced with increasing maternal BMI (P < 0.0001) and with decreasing MoM values of PAPP-A (P = 0.003). LIMITATIONS, REASONS FOR CAUTION: A limitation of our study design was the relatively small sample size. Another limitation was that the control group was not matched with the ART-treated women. The majority of the women from the control group had a high risk from cFTS, thereby their biochemical markers were diverging. However, the biochemical markers for the ART-treated women with fresh or frozen ET were not divergent within the subgroups. WIDER IMPLICATIONS OF THE FINDINGS: Concurrent with other studies demonstrating a reduced FF for singleton pregnancies after ART treatment compared with naturally conceived pregnancies, we found a reduction in FF between the two groups. This is one of the first studies to examine FF in ART pregnancies after fresh ET compared with frozen ET, hence the existing knowledge is limited. We find that FF is even more reduced in pregnancies following fresh ET compared with frozen ET, which might possibly reflect the predisposition of being small for gestational age after fresh ET compared with natural cycle frozen ET. STUDY FUNDING/COMPETING INTEREST(S): The study was supported by the A.P. Møller og Hustru Chastine Mc-Kinney Møllers Fond til almene Formaal (the A.P. Møller Foundation for General Purposes). All authors declare no conflicts of interest.NA.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Talbot, Anna L.","Ambye, Louise","Hartwig, Tanja S.","Werge, Lene","Sørensen, Steen","Stormlund, Sacha","Prætorius, Lisbeth","Jørgensen, Henrik Løvendahl","Pinborg, Anja","Jørgensen, Finn Stener"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453642"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Assisted reproduction","non invasive prenatal testing NIPT"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fetal fraction of cell free dna in pregnancies after fresh or frozen embryo transfer following assisted reproductive technologies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85087110839&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-453642","identifier":[{"id":"85087110839","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32539141","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-64c26ab9-583a-42ec-b309-e1557901da1a"],"keyword":["assisted reproduction","fetal fraction (FF)","fresh embryo transfer (fresh ET)","frozen embryo transfer (frozen ET)","non-invasive prenatal testing (NIPT)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E91F5D558B5BD3F7DC0BE9AC4B82240F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anna L.","key":"talbotannalpau","last":"Talbot","name":"Talbot, Anna L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"ambyelouisepau","last":"Ambye","name":"Ambye, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tanja S.","key":"hartwigtanjaspau","last":"Hartwig","name":"Hartwig, Tanja S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"wergelenepau","last":"Werge","name":"Werge, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Steen","key":"sørensensteenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Steen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sacha","key":"stormlundsachapau","last":"Stormlund","name":"Stormlund, Sacha","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lisbeth","key":"prætoriuslisbethpau","last":"Prætorius","name":"Prætorius, Lisbeth","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik L.","key":"jørgensenhenrikløvendahlpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cf84c34a-16a5-4a24-9667-bc1c2481e1a5","name":"Jørgensen, Henrik Løvendahl","name_org":"Jørgensen, Henrik L.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anja","key":"pinborganjapau","last":"Pinborg","locid":"28eb0e05-b8d4-4063-9350-54ae5d522ed4","name":"Pinborg, Anja","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Finn S.","key":"jørgensenfinnstenerpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"af103a51-0399-4d0c-8377-db0260a8c6c8","name":"Jørgensen, Finn Stener","name_org":"Jørgensen, Finn S.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32539141"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/humrep/deaa110","issn":["02681161","14602350"],"issn_org":["02681161"],"issue":"6","journal":"Human Reproduction","pages":"1267-1275","status":"p","title":"Human Reproduction","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087110839"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-64c26ab9-583a-42ec-b309-e1557901da1a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fetal fraction of cell-free DNA in pregnancies after fresh or frozen embryo transfer following assisted reproductive technologies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453642","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Complications of atherosclerosis are the leading cause of morbidity and mortality worldwide. Various genetically modified mouse models are used to investigate disease trajectory with classical histology, currently the preferred methodology to elucidate plaque composition. Here, we show the strength of light-sheet fluorescence microscopy combined with deep learning image analysis for characterising and quantifying plaque burden and composition in whole aorta specimens. 3D imaging is a non-destructive method that requires minimal ex vivo handling and can be up-scaled to large sample sizes. Combined with deep learning, atherosclerotic plaque in mice can be identified without any ex vivo staining due to the autofluorescent nature of the tissue. The aorta and its branches can subsequently be segmented to determine how anatomical position affects plaque composition and progression. Here, we find the highest plaque accumulation in the aortic arch and brachiocephalic artery. Simultaneously, aortas can be stained for markers of interest (for example the pan immune cell marker CD45) and quantified. In ApoE−/− mice we observe that levels of CD45 reach a plateau after which increases in plaque volume no longer correlate to immune cell infiltration. All underlying code is made publicly available to ease adaption of the method.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jurtz, Vanessa Isabell","Skovbjerg, Grethe","Salinas, Casper Gravesen","Roostalu, Urmas","Pedersen, Louise","Hecksher-Sørensen, Jacob","Rolin, Bidda","Nyberg, Michael","van de Bunt, Martijn","Ingvorsen, Camilla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-481606"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GUB","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-GUB","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep learning reveals 000000000003d atherosclerotic plaque distribution and composition","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-78632-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-481606","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7726562","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33299076","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85097371003","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9390fb94-eca4-4223-b0ff-a9ce7e4e81fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EA7A79386399D3CCC97CDD75F9642470"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-78632-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/269506180/s41598_020_78632_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"gubra","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GUB","l3nl":"Gubra","l3nn":"Gubra","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Gubra","namevar":["Gubra"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GUB","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vanessa Isabell","key":"jurtzpau","last":"Jurtz","name":"Jurtz, Vanessa Isabell","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Grethe","key":"skovbjergpau","last":"Skovbjerg","name":"Skovbjerg, Grethe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Casper Gravesen","key":"salinaspau","last":"Salinas","name":"Salinas, Casper Gravesen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Urmas","key":"roostalupau","last":"Roostalu","name":"Roostalu, Urmas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Louise","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"d7bd27dd-f98a-4155-b0c3-95e9d1d188e3","name":"Pedersen, Louise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jacob","key":"heckshersørensenpau","last":"Hecksher-Sørensen","name":"Hecksher-Sørensen, Jacob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Bidda","key":"rolinpau","last":"Rolin","name":"Rolin, Bidda","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"nybergpau","last":"Nyberg","name":"Nyberg, Michael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martijn","key":"vandebuntpau","last":"van de Bunt","name":"van de Bunt, Martijn","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla","key":"ingvorsenpau","last":"Ingvorsen","name":"Ingvorsen, Camilla","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33299076"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-020-78632-4","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"21523","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097371003"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Gubra","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9390fb94-eca4-4223-b0ff-a9ce7e4e81fb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep learning reveals 3D atherosclerotic plaque distribution and composition","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-481606","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this registry-based cohort study, we estimated the risk of human papillomavirus (HPV)-related anogenital premalignancies and cancer in renal transplant recipients (RTRs) compared to a nontransplanted comparison cohort. We identified all first-time RTRs in Denmark during 1990-2015 in a nationwide nephrology register. For each RTR, we randomly selected 50 age- and sex-matched non-RTRs from the background population. The study population was followed for diagnoses of cervical, vaginal, vulvar, penile and anal intraepithelial neoplasia grades 2-3 (IN2/3) and cancer for up to 27 years. We estimated hazard ratios (HRs) of anogenital IN2/3 and cancer in RTRs vs. non-RTRs by Cox regression separately for men and women using age as underlying timescale, adjusting for income, education, HPV vaccination and immunocompromising conditions. We included 4,261 RTRs and 213,673 non-RTRs. RTRs had increased hazard of cervical (HR = 2.1, 95% CI: 1.7-2.8), vaginal (HR = 35.0, 95% CI: 13.9-87.7), vulvar (HR = 16.4, 95% CI: 10.4-25.8), penile (HR = 21.9, 95% CI: 11.1-43.5) and anal (women: HR = 51.1, 95% CI: 28.0-93.1; men: HR = 39.0, 95% CI: 16.7-91.1) IN2/3. The HRs of anogenital cancers were also increased at most sites. The HR of anogenital IN2/3 in female RTRs tended to be higher during graft function than during dialysis. In female RTRs aged <40 years at transplantation, 10-15% had cervical IN2/3 and 5-12% had vaginal/vulvar/anal IN2/3 within 20 years after transplantation, compared to 4-8 and 0.2-0.4%, respectively, of female non-RTRs. In conclusion, RTRs had substantially higher risk of HPV-related anogenital premalignancies and cancer than non-RTRs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Reinholdt, Kristian","Thomsen, Louise T","Dehlendorff, Christian","Larsen, Helle Kiellberg","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Haedersdal, Merete","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-528115"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"human papillomavirus related anogenital premalignancies and cancer in renal transplant recipients a danish nationwide registry based cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-528115","identifier":[{"id":"85081062537","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31291470","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e15ea1f4-dc4d-4485-ab2f-df24ca859eca"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-07E9674AB39A124C9A2C13A5898B9132"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Dermatovenerology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian","key":"reinholdtpau","last":"Reinholdt","name":"Reinholdt, Kristian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise T","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Th