{"abstract":"Recent studies indicate that microbial enterotypes may influence the beneficial effects of wholegrain enriched diets including bodyweight regulation. In a 4-week intervention trial, overweight subjects were randomized to consume either arabinoxylan-oligosaccharides (AXOS) (10.4 g/d) from wheat bran or polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFA) (3.6 g/d). In the present study, we have stratified the subjects participating in the intervention (n = 29) according to the baseline Prevotella-to-Bacteroides (P/B) ratios through a post-hoc analysis and applied a linear mixed model analysis to identify the influence of this P/B ratio on the differences in weight changes in the intervention arms. Following AXOS consumption (n = 15), the high P/B group showed no bodyweight changes [-0.14 kg (95% CI: -0.67; 0.38, p = .59)], while the low P/B group gained 0.65 kg (95% CI: 0.16; 1.14, p = .009). Consequently, a difference of -0.79 kg was found between P/B groups (95% CI: -1.51; -0.08, p = .030). No differences were found between P/B groups following PUFA consumption (0.61 kg, 95% CI: -0.13; 1.35, p = .10). Among the Bacteroides species, B. cellulosilyticus relative abundance exhibited the highest positive rank correlation (Kendall's tau = 0.51, FDR p = .070) with 4-week weight change on AXOS, and such association was further supported by using supervised classification methods (Random Forest). We outlined several carbohydrate-active enzyme (CAZy) genes involved in xylan-binding and degradation to be enriched in B. cellulosilyticus genomes, as well as multiple accessory genes, suggesting a supreme AXOS-derived glycan scavenging role of such species. This post-hoc analysis, ensuring species and strain demarcation at the human gut microbiota, permitted to uncover the predictive role of Bacteroides species over P/B enterotype in weight gain during a fiber-based intervention. The results of this pilot trial pave the way for future assessments on fiber fermentation outputs from Bacteroides species affecting lipid metabolism in the host and with direct impact on adiposity, thus helping to design personalized interventions.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars","Sørensen, Claudia Vodstrup","Wøhlk, Frederikke U","Kjølbæk, Louise","Astrup, Arne","Sanz, Yolanda","Hjorth, Mads Fiil","Benítez-Páez, Alfonso"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527121"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centro de Investigacion Principe Felipe","The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC)"],"keyword":["Arabinoxylans","Bacteroides","Enterotype","Faculty of Science","Obesity","Overweight","Prevotella"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microbial enterotypes beyond genus level i bacteroides i species as a predictive biomarker for weight change upon controlled intervention with arabinoxylan oligosaccharides in overweight subjects","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/19490976.2020.1847627","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-527121","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7781564","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33319645","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85098534323","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-dfc8e4a6-282e-4e96-bd83-9a4ca77f375f"],"keyword":["Arabinoxylans","B. cellulosilyticus","Bacteroides","Enterotype","Faculty of Science","Obesity","Overweight","Prevotella"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25B6D1A2635DE0567BE85F9E92F19095"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/19490976.2020.1847627","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/257282332/Christensen_et_al_Gut_Microbes_2020_Vol_12_1_e1847627.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"the spanish national research council","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"centro de investigacion principe felipe","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Centro de Investigacion Principe Felipe","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"d87ec11e-b7a7-481a-a376-8e7a1c56dc81","name":"Christensen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-2251-6713","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claudia Vodstrup","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"8e197cb3-59fa-4017-bd9b-195b1d8d12a4","name":"Sørensen, Claudia Vodstrup","orcid":"0000-0003-1411-1812","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederikke U","key":"wøhlkpau","last":"Wøhlk","name":"Wøhlk, Frederikke U","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"kjølbækpau","last":"Kjølbæk","locid":"704b196a-527d-4a0b-9a32-7dcdfdb8a3fd","name":"Kjølbæk, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-4310-9332","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"5d943631-c9fc-4b63-8aaa-263ba4248735","name":"Astrup, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-8968-8996","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yolanda","key":"sanzpau","last":"Sanz","name":"Sanz, Yolanda","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Fiil","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"00918fa0-7b1e-4128-919e-a0af9497026b","name":"Hjorth, Mads Fiil","orcid":"0000-0001-9440-2737","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Alfonso","key":"benítezpáezpau","last":"Benítez-Páez","name":"Benítez-Páez, Alfonso","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33319645"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/19490976.2020.1847627","issn":["19490976","19490984"],"issn_org":["19490976"],"journal":"Gut Microbes","paperid":"1847627","status":"p","title":"Gut Microbes","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098534323"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dfc8e4a6-282e-4e96-bd83-9a4ca77f375f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microbial enterotypes beyond genus level: <i>Bacteroides</i> species as a predictive biomarker for weight change upon controlled intervention with arabinoxylan oligosaccharides in overweight subjects","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527121","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To investigate associations between age, lifestyle and erectile dysfunction (ED) in the general population and to explore associations between age, lifestyle and contact with a general practitioner (GP) regarding ED.Design: Cross-sectional web-based questionnaire study.Setting: The general Danish population.Subjects: A randomly selected sample of 48,910 men aged 20 years and older.Main outcome measures: Prevalence of ED and probability of contacting a GP regarding ED. In logistic regression models we analysed associations between age, smoking status, alcohol consumption, body mass index (BMI), and self-rated physical fitness on both ED and GP contact.Results: A total of 22,198 men (47.6%) completed the question regarding ED. The overall prevalence of ED was 19.3%, varying from 2.3% among men aged 20-29 years to 55.3% among men aged 80 years and above. 31.8% of men reporting ED had contacted a GP regarding ED. Increasing age, current or former smoking, complete alcohol abstinence or alcohol consumption above seven units per week, high BMI, and poor self-rated physical fitness were significantly associated with reporting ED. The proportion of GP contacts was significantly associated with age. Overall, no significant associations between lifestyle and healthcare seeking were observed, although lower odds of GP contact were found when physical fitness was rated as poor.Conclusion: Reporting ED and GP contact were significantly associated with age. Furthermore, lifestyle was significantly associated with reporting ED, but largely not associated with healthcare seeking. These findings are important for future interventions aiming to improve diagnosis and treatment of ED.Key pointsExperiencing erectile dysfunction is frequent in the general population, especially among older men.  • In this large-scale national survey, age and lifestyle were significantly associated with reporting erectile dysfunction.  • Healthcare seeking with erectile dysfunction was significantly associated with age, but not with lifestyle.  • Diagnosis and treatment of erectile dysfunction might be challenged when erectile dysfunction does not lead to healthcare seeking.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Paulsen, Louise Herluf","Sørensen Bakke, Louise","Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","Balasubramaniam, Kirubakaran","Hansen, Dorte Gilså"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-583297"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Erectile Dysfunction","General population","General practice","Healthcare seeking","Lifestyle","Self Report"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations between lifestyle erectile dysfunction and healthcare seeking a population based study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02813432.2020.1753347","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-583297","identifier":[{"id":"85083707406","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32314631","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8570741","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-2349bc0c-f497-4c78-871d-523f853d32e8"],"keyword":["Erectile dysfunction","general population","general practice","healthcare seeking","lifestyle","self-report"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B985946C967FA2972CBEF04835E7CD8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02813432.2020.1753347","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170573644/Associations_between_lifestyle_erectile_dysfunction_and_healthcare_seeking_a_population_based_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Herluf","key":"paulsenpau","last":"Paulsen","locid":"9fdb22bf-b93d-448f-b6ac-ab15ebaa199d","name":"Paulsen, Louise Herluf","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"sørensenbakkepau","last":"Sørensen Bakke","locid":"e176eb9a-ad6b-4454-b389-dc591f200a6a","name":"Sørensen Bakke, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Ejg","key":"jarbølpau","last":"Jarbøl","locid":"42ad7b79-3390-486b-840a-94cadacfeaef","name":"Jarbøl, Dorte Ejg","orcid":"0000-0002-3241-4190","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirubakaran","key":"balasubramaniampau","last":"Balasubramaniam","locid":"3a38228d-1757-46a2-b5f9-fafafb3a17c4","name":"Balasubramaniam, Kirubakaran","orcid":"0000-0002-3612-1731","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Gilså","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2826791-eb97-4bca-8af7-448b0940e6e5","name":"Hansen, Dorte Gilså","orcid":"0000-0002-5946-9968","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32314631"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/02813432.2020.1753347","issn":["02813432","15027724"],"issn_org":["02813432"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Primary Health Care","pages":"176-183","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Primary Health Care","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083707406"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2349bc0c-f497-4c78-871d-523f853d32e8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations between lifestyle, erectile dysfunction and healthcare seeking - a population-based study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-583297","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
