, Anne","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"IEH","key":"madsenidaehpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"7bad9fdb-4af4-46fa-846a-9a16db2a2419","name":"Madsen, Ida E H","name_org":"Madsen, IEH","orcid":"0000-0003-3635-3900","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"ruguliesreinerpau","last":"Rugulies","locid":"4684d49a-5fe6-43e0-b3a6-5959f3d2f472","name":"Rugulies, Reiner","name_org":"Rugulies, R.","orcid":"0000-0002-7752-131X","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["988779043749"],"place":"København","publisher":"Det Nationale Forskningscenter for Arbejdsmiljø","repno":"NFA-rapport","series":"NFA-rapport","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-8c045335-6161-493c-85f7-eaf4df7d715e","nfa-d6d47e39-0f95-4b03-a3ad-2dab111f2dd6"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Litteraturgennemgang med supplerende analyser af årsagerne til ufrivillig, førtidig tilbagetrækning fra arbejdsmarkedet. Appendiks til afslutningsrapport til Arbejdsmiljøforskningsfonden","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.36-769532","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Maladaptive plasticity involving increased expression of AMPA-type glutamate receptors is involved in several pathologies, including neuropathic pain, but direct inhibition of AMPARs is associated with side effects. As an alternative, we developed a cell-permeable, high-affinity (~2 nM) peptide inhibitor, Tat-P4 -(C5)2 , of the PDZ domain protein PICK1 to interfere with increased AMPAR expression. The affinity is obtained partly from the Tat peptide and partly from the bivalency of the PDZ motif, engaging PDZ domains from two separate PICK1 dimers to form a tetrameric complex. Bivalent Tat-P4 -(C5)2 disrupts PICK1 interaction with membrane proteins on supported cell membrane sheets and reduce the interaction of AMPARs with PICK1 and AMPA-receptor surface expression in vivo. Moreover, Tat-P4 -(C5)2 administration reduces spinal cord transmission and alleviates mechanical hyperalgesia in the spared nerve injury model of neuropathic pain. Taken together, our data reveal Tat-P4 -(C5)2 as a novel promising lead for neuropathic pain treatment and expand the therapeutic potential of bivalent inhibitors to non-tandem protein-protein interaction domains.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Christensen, Nikolaj R","De Luca, Marta","Lever, Michael B","Richner, Mette","Hansen, Astrid B","Noes-Holt, Gith","Jensen, Kathrine L","Rathje, Mette","Jensen, Dennis Bo","Erlendsson, Simon","Bartling, Christian Ro","Ammendrup-Johnsen, Ina","Pedersen, Sofie E","Schönauer, Michèle","Nissen, Klaus B","Midtgaard, Søren R","Teilum, Kaare","Arleth, Lise","Sørensen, Andreas T","Bach, Anders","Strømgaard, Kristian","Meehan, Claire F","Vægter, Christian Bjerggaard","Gether, Ulrik","Madsen, Kenneth L"],"cuid":["S02-099.42-014909"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biopharmaceuticals","Maladaptive plasticity","Scaffold proteins","Synaptic plasticity","calcium permeable AMPARs"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a high affinity bivalent pdz domain inhibitor complexes pick000000000001 to alleviate neuropathic pain","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.15252/emmm.201911248","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.42-014909","identifier":[{"id":"32352640","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85084202280","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7278562","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000529633900001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-1f97eff6-28ca-4b06-a6fe-7e8ac62e3100","ku-be3d9f21-e7d4-4ae8-955c-071a249267b3"],"keyword":["biopharmaceuticals","calcium permeable AMPARs","maladaptive plasticity","scaffold proteins","synaptic plasticity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BBEACEB997DB3AF349D4BDFEE421E664"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/243006394/A_high_affinity_bivalent_PDZ_domain_inhibitor_complexes_PICK1_to_alleviate_neuropathic_pain.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.15252/emmm.201911248","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Biopharmaceuticals","Københavns Universitet, Facul