ntu, Pawinee","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"chopau","last":"Cho","name":"Cho, Louise","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ashminder","key":"kaurpau","last":"Kaur","name":"Kaur, Ashminder","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Mats","key":"bengtssonpau","last":"Bengtsson","name":"Bengtsson, Mats","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jason","key":"dehnpau","last":"Dehn","name":"Dehn, Jason","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31970929"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/tan.13811","issn":["20592302","20592310"],"issn_org":["20592302"],"issue":"6","journal":"HLA","pages":"516-531","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"HLA","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078839466"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a582979e-57c0-44f2-83db-e372d27de7c4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Common, intermediate and well-documented HLA alleles in world populations : CIWD version 3.0.0","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-223662","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The Barents Sea is situated on a continental margin and was home to a large ice sheet at the Last Glacial Maximum. Studying the solid Earth response to the removal of this ice sheet (glacial isostatic adjustment; GIA) can give insight into the subsurface rheology of this region. However, because the region is currently covered by ocean, uplift measurements from the center of the former ice sheet are not available. The Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment (GRACE) gravity data have been shown to be able to constrain GIA. Here we analyze GRACE data for the period 2003-2015 in the Barents Sea and use the data to constrain GIA models for the region. We study the effect of uncertainty in non-tidal ocean mass models that are used to correct GRACE data and find that it should be taken into account when studying solid Earth signals in oceanic areas from GRACE. We compare GRACE-derived gravity disturbance rates with GIA model predictions for different ice deglaciation chronologies of the last glacial cycle and find that best-fitting models have an upper mantle viscosity equal or higher than 3×1020 Pa s. Following a similar procedure for Fennoscandia we find that the preferred upper mantle viscosity there is a factor 2 larger than in the Barents Sea for a range of lithospheric thickness values. This factor is shown to be consistent with the ratio of viscosities derived for both regions from global seismic models. The viscosity difference can serve as constraint for geodynamic models of the area.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rovira-Navarro, Marc","Van Der Wal, Wouter","Barletta, Valentina Roberta","C. Root, Bart","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340219"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rovira-Navarro, Marc"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"grace constraints on earth rheology of the barents sea and fennoscandia","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/se-11-379-2020","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340219","identifier":[{"id":"85082578146","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-77695c23-d78f-4520-8cec-d29c8cec6121"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D66B1384F660867D9266B58C9F30C188"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/se-11-379-2020","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/210077477/se_11_379_2020.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodesy and Earth Observation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"roviranavarropau","last":"Rovira-Navarro","name":"Rovira-Navarro, Marc","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wouter","key":"vanderwalpau","last":"Van Der Wal","name":"Van Der Wal, Wouter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina R.","key":"barlettapau","last":"Barletta","locid":"9662b7b8-5901-45b2-bba3-dd8e3879f864","name":"Barletta, Valentina Roberta","name_org":"Barletta, Valentina R.","orcid":"0000-0003-4427-0830","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bart","key":"crootpau","last":"C. Root","name":"C. Root, Bart","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/se-11-379-2020","issn":["18699510","18699529"],"issn_org":["18699510"],"issue":"2","journal":"Solid Earth","pages":"379-395","publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","status":"p","title":"Solid Earth","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082578146"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-77695c23-d78f-4520-8cec-d29c8cec6121"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"GRACE constraints on Earth rheology of the Barents Sea and Fennoscandia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340219","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background Food processing, including heat‐treatment, can affect protein structure and stability, and consequently affect protein immunogenicity and allergenicity. A few studies have shown that structural changes induced by heat‐treatment impact the intestinal protein uptake and suggest this as a contributing factor for altered allergenicity. Objective To investigate the impact of heat‐treatment of a whey‐based protein product on allergenicity and tolerogenicity as well as on intestinal uptake in various animal models. Methods Immunogenicity and sensitising capacity of the heat‐treated whey product was compared to that of the unmodified product by intraperitoneal and oral exposure studies, while tolerogenic properties were assessed by oral primary prevention and desensitisation studies in high‐IgE responder Brown Norway rats. Results Heat‐treatment of whey induced partial protein denaturation and aggregation, which reduced the intraperitoneal sensitising capacity but not immunogenicity. In contrast, heat‐treatment did not influence the oral sensitising capacity, but the heat‐treated whey showed a significantly reduced eliciting capacity compared to unmodified whey upon oral challenge. Heat‐treatment did not reduce the tolerogenic properties of whey, as both products were equally good at preventing sensitisation in naïve rats as well as desensitising already sensitised rats. Results from inhibitory ELISA and immunoblots with sera from sensitised rats demonstrated that heat‐treatment caused an altered protein and epitope reactivity. Protein uptake studies showed that heat‐treatment changed the route of uptake with less whey being absorbed through the epithelium but more into the payer's patches. Conclusion & Clinical Relevance These results support the notion that the physicochemical features of proteins affect their route of uptake and that the route of uptake may affect the protein allergenicity. Furthermore, the study highlights the potential for heat‐treatment in the production of efficient and safe cow's milk protein‐based products for prevention and treatment of cow's milk allergy.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Graversen, Katrine Bækby","Ballegaard, Anne-Sofie Ravn","Kræmer, Louise H","Hornslet, Sofie Emilie","Sørensen, Laila V","Christoffersen, Heidi F.","Jacobsen, Lotte N.","Untersmayr, Eva","Smit, Joost J","Bøgh, Katrine Lindholm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352924"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bøgh, Katrine Lindholm"],"country":["Austria","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Medical University of Vienna","Utrecht University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cow s milk allergy prevention and treatment by heat treated whey a study in brown norway rats","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cea.13587","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352924","identifier":[{"id":"85081729931","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32077177","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-a212d93b-8a03-4576-b76c-47c2b60d9892"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C72AC37D4482AA7D7EA33470627C4D68"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cea.13587","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/206932827/Graversen_et_al_2020_Clinical_Experimental_Allergy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/215275143/cea.13587.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai"