 Sofie Emilie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laila V","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Laila V","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Heidi F.","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","name":"Christoffersen, Heidi F.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte N.","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Lotte N.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"untersmayrpau","last":"Untersmayr","name":"Untersmayr, Eva","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Joost J","key":"smitpau","last":"Smit","name":"Smit, Joost J","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrine Lindholm","key":"bøghpau","last":"Bøgh","locid":"69dcdef2-7e2a-4c8c-966b-dd14c90e6419","name":"Bøgh, Katrine Lindholm","orcid":"0000-0002-5266-0372","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32077177"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/cea.13587","issn":["09547894","09602178"],"issn_org":["09547894"],"issue":"6","journal":"Clinical and Experimental Allergy","pages":"708-721","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Clinical and Experimental Allergy","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081729931"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a212d93b-8a03-4576-b76c-47c2b60d9892"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Cow's milk allergy prevention and treatment by heat-treated whey - a study in Brown Norway rats","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352924","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Actions to improve healthy aging and delay morbidity are crucial, given the global aging population. We believe that biological age estimation can help promote the health of the general population. Biological age reflects the heterogeneity in functional status and vulnerability to disease that chronological age cannot. Thus, biological age assessment is a tool that provides an intuitively meaningful outcome for the general population, and as such, facilitates our understanding of the extent to which lifestyle can increase health span. OBJECTIVE: This interdisciplinary study intends to develop a biological age model and explore its usefulness. METHODS: The model development comprised three consecutive phases: (1) conducting a cross-sectional study to gather candidate biomarkers from 100 individuals representing normal healthy aging people (the derivation cohort); (2) estimating the biological age using principal component analysis; and (3) testing the clinical use of the model in a validation cohort of overweight adults attending a lifestyle intervention course. RESULTS: We completed the data collection and analysis of the cross-sectional study, and the initial results of the principal component analysis are ready. Interpretation and refinement of the model is ongoing. Recruitment to the validation cohort is forthcoming. We expect the results to be published by December 2021. CONCLUSIONS: We expect the biological age model to be a useful indicator of disease risk and metabolic risk, and further research should focus on validating the model on a larger scale.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Husted, Karina Louise Skov","Fogelstrøm, Mathilde","Hulst, Pernille","Brink-Kjær, Andreas","Henneberg, Kaj-Åge","Sørensen, Helge Bjarup Dissing","Dela, Flemming","Helge, Jørn Wulff"],"cuid":["S02-088.45-036281"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biological age","Body Mass Index","CARDIOVASCULAR RESPONSES","Health promotion","Healthy aging","Insulin Resistance","Life style intervention","Metabolic syndrome","Physical activity","Principal component analysis","Protocol","Waist Circumference","lower extremity function","skin autofluorescence"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a biological age model designed for health promotion interventions protocol for an interdisciplinary study for model development","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/19209","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.45-036281","identifier":[{"id":"33104001","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7652682","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000582576000022","type":"wos"},{"id":"85095846848","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a2b1809d-e4b3-463f-8106-cc3530724de7","ku-2946802b-66c3-4cfb-b9d1-aebfc84c8b02"],"keyword":["BODY-MASS INDEX","CARDIOVASCULAR-RESPONSES","CLINICAL BIOMARKERS","INSULIN-RESISTANCE","LIFE-STYLE INTERVENTION","LOWER-EXTREMITY FUNCTION","METABOLIC SYNDROME","PHYSICAL-ACTIVITY","SKIN AUTOFLUORESCENCE","WAIST CIRCUMFERENCE","biological age","health promotion","healthy aging","principal component analysis","protocol"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A4CA253FC105D5644338B8A366CD19A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/222714641/JMIR.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/19209","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.k