Kristjansen","name":"Kristjansen, Helene Saltoft","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"hartvigpedh","last":"Hartvig","name":"Hartvig, Peter","rank":15,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Steen","key":"sørensenpedh","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Steen","rank":16,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788793787421"],"isbn":["9788793787414"],"issn":["22451684"],"pages":"103-107","place":"Tjele","publisher":"DCA - Nationalt Center for Fødevarer og Jordbrug","series":"DCA rapport","status":"p","title":"Applied Crop Protection 2018"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e8188a0c-5b5c-478d-a5dc-438ef8b756f8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Results of crop protection trials in minor crops in 2018","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-261786","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Despite improved treatment and care, children and adolescents diagnosed with cancer continue to die, while many of those cured are burdened by treatment-related sequelae. The best clinical management of children and adolescents with cancer depends on healthcare professionals with various skills and expertise. Complex treatment, care and rehabilitation require collaboration between healthcare professionals. The purpose of this scoping review is to identify and evaluate existing interprofessional education in paediatric cancer. METHODS: We utilised the scoping review methodology and searched PubMed, Scopus and Education Resources Information Center. Inclusion criteria were postgraduate studies targeting more than one profession and evaluation of the educational intervention. We applied Kirkpatrick's modified interprofessional education outcomes model to systematise outcomes. RESULTS: Of 418 references, nine studies fulfilled the inclusion criteria. The design, strategy and content of all the studies were heterogeneous. None of the interprofessional educations systematically evaluated knowledge, skills, attitudes or the effects on patient outcomes or quality of care. CONCLUSION: There is a lack of well-structured, interprofessional education in paediatric cancer that has undergone evaluation. Paediatric cancer may benefit from systematic education and evaluation frameworks since interprofessional education could potentially strengthen the treatment, care and rehabilitation for children and adolescents with cancer.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Topperzer, Martha Krogh","Hoffmann, Marianne","Roug, Louise Ingerslev","Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","Lausen, Birgitte","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Sørensen, Jette Led"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-424323"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unmet need for interprofessional education in paediatric cancer a scoping review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00520-019-04856-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-424323","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6726701","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85067638752","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31127437","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-33ed9579-97eb-4116-8e06-7958151796d5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-92950FE640F0AFFB6FB97B834F32247F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/237512324/Unmet_need_for_interprofessional_education_in_paediatric_cancer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00520-019-04856-4","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Martha Krogh","key":"topperzerpau","last":"Topperzer","name":"Topperzer, Martha Krogh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marianne","key":"hoffmannpau","last":"Hoffmann","name":"Hoffmann, Marianne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise Ingerslev","key":"rougpau","last":"Roug","name":"Roug, Louise Ingerslev","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne Bækgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Hanne Bækgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte","key":"lausenpau","last":"Lausen","name":"Lausen, Birgitte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kjeld","key":"schmiegelowpau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"6ce2f948-244d-4f19-82aa-f08a71289674","name":"Schmiegelow, Kjeld","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jette Led","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"84ce4092-8277-45c1-89d5-afedea9c65f0","name":"Sørensen, Jette Led","orcid":"0000-0002-7320-2784","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31127437"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00520-019-04856-4","issn":["09414355","14337339"],"issn_org":["09414355"],"journal":"Supportive Care in Cancer","pages":"3627-3637","status":"p","title":"Supportive Care in Cancer","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067638752"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-33ed9579-97eb-4116-8e06-7958151796d5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unmet need for interprofessional education in paediatric cancer : a scoping review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-424323","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Thromboelastography (TEG) is a global whole blood hemostasis assay which includes plasma as well as cellular components of hemostasis in the analysis and follows the quality and dynamics of clot development, stabilization, and lysis. In human medicine TEG is also a valuable asset in the therapeutic setting, allowing evaluation of the effect of transfusion therapy in vitro. This case series describes the use of TEG as a guiding tool for transfusion therapy in four dogs with hypocoagulable hemostatic disorders. Case presentation: Four dogs presented with hypocoagulable disorders of hemostasis, diagnosed as rodenticide intoxication, angiostrongylosis, disseminated intravascular coagulation following severe systemic inflammation, and immune-mediated thrombocytopenia, respectively. TEG was used as a diagnostic tool as well as a guiding tool in the decision of whether or not, and in what dose, fresh frozen plasma would be of benefit in the treatment protocol for each dog. Conclusions: TEG may be applied in the therapeutic setting as a means to tailor individual patient transfusion therapy in critically ill dogs with hypocoagulable states.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Langhorn, Rebecca","Bochsen, Louise","Willesen, Jakob","Sørensen, Tina Møller","Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-535796"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bleeding","Dog","Hemostasis","Thromboelastography","Transfusion medicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thromboelastography guided transfusion in dogs with hypocoagulable disorders a case series","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13028-019-0469-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-535796","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6647138","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85069781165","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31331398","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ee7fffbb-ae2e-49a6-ac12-e03aa492e766"],"keyword":["Bleeding","Dog","Hemostasis","Thromboelastography","Transfusion medicine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B5FB20E0CC8BFB846FC030717ABDA3BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/226536460/s13028_019_0469_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13028-019-0469-x","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Section for Internal Medicine, Oncology and Clinical Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rebecca","key":"langhornpau","last":"Langhorn","locid":"9d62c730-7ad4-4563-8f55-1bcaa1b83574","name":"Langhorn, Rebecca","orcid":"0000-0001-7833-5191","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"bochsenpau","last":"Bochsen","locid":"b595f878-0a10-410f-8f51-dd391dd816d7","name":"Bochsen, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Lundgreen","key":"willesenpau","last":"Willesen","locid":"ebd8eab4-49c2-4419-aa32-e40fa79791b7","name":"Willesen, Jakob","name_org":"Willesen, Jakob Lundgreen","orcid":"0000-0002-2851-9264","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tina Møller","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c127bc51-ef4a-4a52-822d-86684e030d69","name":"Sørensen, Tina Møller","orcid":"0000-0001-6325-4970","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annemarie Thuri","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"a7007b3a-f743-46be-8a05-6473fd440756","name":"Kristensen, Annemarie Thuri","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31331398"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13028-019-0469-x","issn":["0044605X","17510147"],"issn_org":["0044605X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","paperid":"35","status":"p","title":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069781165"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ee7fffbb-ae2e-49a6-ac12-e03aa492e766"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Thromboelastography-guided transfusion in dogs with hypocoagulable disorders : A case series","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-535796","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The multifunctional protein - tissue inhibitor of metalloproteinases-1 (TIMP-1) - has been associated with a poor prognosis in several types of cancers including glioblastomas. In addition, TIMP-1 has been associated with decreased response to chemotherapy, and especially the efficacy of the family of topoisomerase (TOP) inhibitors has been related to TIMP-1. As a second line treatment of glioblastomas, the vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) antibody bevacizumab is administered in combination with the TOP1 inhibitor irinotecan and glioblastoma cell levels of TIMP-1 could therefore potentially influence the efficacy of such treatment. In the present study, we aimed to investigate whether a high TIMP-1 expression in glioblastoma cell lines would affect the sensitivity to TOP inhibitors, and whether TIMP-1 overexpressing cells would have alterered growth and invasion. We established TIMP-1 overexpressing subclones from two human glioblastoma cell lines. TIMP-1 overexpressing U87MG cells were significantly more resistant than low TIMP-1 expressing clones and parental cells when exposed to SN-38 (TOP1 inhibitor) or epirubicin (TOP2 inhibitor). No significant differences were observed for the TIMP-1 transfected A172 cells. Implantation of both U87MG and A172 spheroids into organotypic brain slice cultures revealed a reduced growth of TIMP-1 overexpressing U87MG spheroids, however, no significant differences in invasion were observed. The present study suggests that TIMP-1 overexpression reduces the effect of TOP inhibitors in glioblastoma. TIMP-1 also appeared to reduce spheroid growth, but did not influence invasion. Whether TIMP-1 plays a role in irinotecan resistance and has a predictive potential in glioblastoma patients remains to be elucidated.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aaberg-Jessen, Charlotte","Fogh, Louise","Sørensen, Mia Dahl","Halle, Bo","Brünner, Nils","Kristensen, Bjarne Winther"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-621951"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kristensen, Bjarne Winther"],"keyword":["Chemosensitivity","Glioblastoma","TIMP 1"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overexpression of timp 000000000001 and sensitivity to topoisomerase inhibitors in glioblastoma cell lines","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85030155716","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-621951","identifier":[{"id":"28963609","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85030155716","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-aa3536b5-4d39-4b99-9a0d-24aae282d1dc"],"keyword":["Chemosensitivity","Glioblastoma","TIMP-1","TOP inhibitors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9475BB40FE93684945D6085C1709B2C9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Pathology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"aabergjessenpau","last":"Aaberg-Jessen","locid":"1498c754-add7-41ce-90c9-1e24c1265a50","name":"Aaberg-Jessen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1407-7976","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"foghpau","last":"Fogh","name":"Fogh, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mia Dahl","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"3524a591-0bd0-4849-b735-4b916b84defb","name":"Sørensen, Mia Dahl","orcid":"0000-0002-0105-2940","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"hallepau","last":"Halle","locid":"fda27d18-0472-456b-9b4b-2eeea9fcec94","name":"Halle, Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-9930-4490","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"brünnerpau","last":"Brünner","name":"Brünner, Nils","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne Winther","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"42dfd2da-9280-417b-a660-1b1cbd918867","name":"Kristensen, Bjarne Winther","orcid":"0000-0002-6352-0826","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28963609"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12253-017-0312-5","issn":["12194956","15322807"],"issn_org":["12194956"],"issue":"1","journal":"Pathology and Oncology Research","pages":"59-69","publisher":"Frontiers Media","status":"p","title":"Pathology and Oncology Research","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030155716"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-aa3536b5-4d39-4b99-9a0d-24aae282d1dc"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Overexpression of TIMP-1 and Sensitivity to Topoisomerase Inhibitors