{"abstract":"Objective The aim of this study was to examine the association between musculoskeletal (MSK) pain, insomnia, anxiety and depressive symptoms in patients from general practice. Design This is a cross-sectional study. Setting This study was conducted in general practice in Denmark. Participants A consecutive sample of 390 general practice patients (aged 12 years or older) were included; 183 patients with MSK pain and 207 patients without MSK pain. To be included in the MSK pain group, participants with MSK pain were required to report MSK pain at least weekly during the preceding month, which had a negative impact on daily activities. Primary and secondary outcomes measures The primary outcome was insomnia evaluated by the Athens Insomnia Scale. The secondary outcomes were psychological symptoms assessed by the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale. Results Patients with MSK pain had a significantly higher prevalence of insomnia (difference 25.5%, p<0.0001), anxiety (difference 24.3%, p<0.0001) and depressive symptoms (difference 11%, p<0.0001) compared with patients without MSK pain. Furthermore, patients with MSK pain and comorbid insomnia had significantly higher levels of anxiety and symptoms of depression compared with patients with MSK pain without insomnia (p<0.0001). These relationships remained robust when controlling for age, sex and body mass index in linear regression. Conclusion One in two patients in general practice report MSK pain. Comorbid MSK pain and insomnia are common and are associated with a higher prevalence of anxiety and depression. This highlights the importance of establishing the presence of insomnia and affective disorders as potentially modifiable factors during treatment of MSK pain in general practice.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Louise","Jensen, Morten Sig Ager","Rathleff, Michael Skovdal","Holden, Sinead"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-064060"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Family Practice","Musculoskeletal disorders","Pain","Sleep medicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comorbid insomnia psychological symptoms and widespread pain among patients suffering from musculoskeletal pain in general practice a cross sectional study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-031971","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-064060","identifier":[{"id":"31256044","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068919624","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-306bfd0f-9594-49cf-8702-b3d893b869a2"],"keyword":["family practice","musculoskeletal disorders","pain","sleep medicine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-51390EB6D57487739248332E81EB40B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/312436635/e031971.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-031971","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for General Practice at Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"316b41aa-fa02-4b9a-a1c9-fb5cf748bb47","name":"Sørensen, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Sig Ager","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"de4051ce-fce4-4bfc-b3b7-b215597e93c4","name":"Jensen, Morten Sig Ager","orcid":"0000-0002-3075-882X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Skovdal","key":"rathleffpau","last":"Rathleff","locid":"90c1260f-4cd4-497f-88ca-a98f412bbe7b","name":"Rathleff, Michael Skovdal","orcid":"0000-0003-1173-0335","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sinead","key":"holdenpau","last":"Holden","locid":"8cd76341-9177-4b45-b939-3c487530e766","name":"Holden, Sinead","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31256044"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2019-031971","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"6","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e031971","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068919624"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-306bfd0f-9594-49cf-8702-b3d893b869a2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comorbid insomnia, psychological symptoms and widespread pain among patients suffering from musculoskeletal pain in general practice : a cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-064060","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Artiklen er en del af antologien Kunst, kultur og deltagelse redigeret af Birgit Eriksson, Mette Houlberg Rung og Anne Scott Sørensen. Bogen omhandler: Deltagelse er et nøgleord i samtidens kunst- og kulturliv. Både kunstnere og kulturinstitutioner eksperimenterer med at udvikle kommunikationsformer, der inddrager publikum på nye måder. Museer, teatre og biblioteker arbejder med at lade borgerne komme til orde og styrke deres medbestemmelse og medskabelse. Bag initiativerne ligger ofte et ønske om et mere åbent og tilgængeligt kulturliv og et mere lige og demokratisk samfund. En vigtig konsekvensens er, at institutionerne selv forandres. Kunst, kultur og deltagelse præsenterer en række aktuelle eksperimenter med deltagelse i kunst- og kulturlivet. Bogens forfattere stiller skarpt på de teoretiske og metodiske udfordringer, der ligger i at udvikle, designe, facilitere og evaluere deltagelsesprojekter. Eksemplerne spænder fra Aarhus 2017 og Kbh Læser til et biblioteksprojekt i Østjylland og et byudviklingsprojekt i Greve, fra europæiske kulturhuse til store kulturinstitutioner som ARoS, Trapholt, Det Kgl. Teater og Statens Museum for Kunst.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hansen, Louise Ejgod"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-191642"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"en målestok for deltagelse evaluering af forskellige deltagelsesformer under aarhus 000000002017","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-191642","ids":["au-6d3fd89b-9110-4604-8b47-90cd0d7a3595"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3EEBA7AAD7608611690982FA6F50BE92"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Dramaturgy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise Ejgod","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2ffe90e-58e0-4efe-974c-5e84e0ac697d","name":"Hansen, Louise Ejgod","orcid":"0000-0002-3476-4717","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgit","key":"erikssonpedh","last":"Eriksson","name":"Eriksson, Birgit","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette Houlberg","key":"rungpedh","last":"Rung","name":"Rung, Mette Houlberg","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"scottsørensenpedh","last":"Scott Sørensen","name":"Scott Sørensen, Anne","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["978 87 7184 531 0"],"pages":"206-225","publisher":"Aarhus Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"Kunst, kultur og deltagelse"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6d3fd89b-9110-4604-8b47-90cd0d7a3595"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"En målestok for deltagelse : Evaluering af forskellige deltagelsesformer under Aarhus 2017","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-191642","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Satellite gravimetry data acquired by the Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment (GRACE) allows to derive the temporal evolution in ice mass for both the Antarctic Ice Sheet (AIS) and the Greenland Ice Sheet (GIS). Various algorithms have been used in a wide range of studies to generate Gravimetric Mass Balance (GMB) products. Results from different studies may be affected by substantial differences in the processing, including the applied algorithm, the utilised background models and the time period under consideration. This study gives a detailed description of an assessment of the performance of GMB algorithms using actual GRACE monthly solutions for a prescribed period as well as synthetic data sets. The inter-comparison exercise was conducted in the scope of the European Space Agency’s Climate Change Initiative (CCI) project for the AIS and GIS, and was, for the first time, open to everyone. GMB products generated by different groups could be evaluated and directly compared against each other. For the period from 2003-02 to 2013-12, estimated linear trends in ice mass vary between -99 Gt/yr and -108 Gt/yr for the AIS and between -252 Gt/yr and -274 Gt/yr for the GIS, respectively. The spread between the solutions is larger if smaller drainage basins or gridded GMB products are considered. Finally, findings from the exercise formed the basis to select the algorithms used for the GMB product generation within the AIS and GIS CCI project.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Groh, Andreas","Horwath, Martin","Horvath, Alexander","Meister, Rakia","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Barletta, Valentina Roberta","Forsberg, René","Wouters, Bert","Ditmar, Pavel","Ran, Jiangjun","Klees, Roland","Su, Xiaoli","Shang, Kun","Guo, Junyi","Shum, C. K.","Schrama, Ernst","Shepherd, Andrew"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-367234"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Groh, Andreas"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Ohio State University","Technical University of Munich","Technische Universität Dresden","University of Bristol","University of Leeds"],"keyword":["Antarctica","GRACE","Greenland","Methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluating grace mass change time series for the antarctic and greenland ice sheet methods and results","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/geosciences9100415","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-367234","identifier":[{"id":"85073453027","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d1c16b1f-543e-4f57-b869-72bf44fc8fc3"],"keyword":["Antarctica","GRACE","Greenland","Ice mass change","Methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2EC46D0C402FE5D55A70829924CFB5BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/geosciences9100415","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/197303436/geosciences_09_00415_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technische universität dresden","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technische Universität Dresden","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities"