{"abstract":"Circulating MFAP4 is a relevant biomarker to identify COPD patients at risk of death and cardiovascular comorbidity after smoking cessation http://ow.ly/6vnL30o8t1g.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Johansson, Sofie Lock","Johansson, Helle Wulf","Schlosser, Anders","Titlestad, Ingrid Louise","Miller, Bruce","Tal-Singer, Ruth","Holmskov, Uffe","Vestbo, Jørgen","Sorensen, Grith Lykke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614254"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sorensen, Grith Lykke"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GlaxoSmithKline","University of Manchester"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plasma microfibrillar associated protein 000000000004 is not prognostic of emphysema progression but is associated with cardiovascular disease history and mortality in copd patients","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1183/23120541.00021-2019","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["6MWD: 6-min walking distance; mMRC: modified Medical Research Council dyspnoea score; SGRQ: St George’s Respiratory Questionnaire score; BODE: body mass index, obstruction, dyspnoea, exercise capacity; PD: post-bronchodilator; GOLD: Global Initiative for Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease; FEV1: forced expiratory volume in 1 s; LAA%: percentage of low-attenuation areas; CVD: cardiovascular disease; MFAP4: microfibrillar-associated protein 4; IL: interleukin; FVC: forced vital capacity; Δ: change in; PD15: provocative dose causing a 15% fall in FEV1; NS: nonsignificant. #: n=966; ¶: n=629; +: n=367; §: odds ratio (not β-coefficient). Conflict of interest: S.L. Johansson has nothing to disclose. H. Wulf-Johansson has nothing to disclose. A. Schlosser is an inventor of US Patent No. 9,988,442 and EP17199552.5 owned by University of Southern Denmark. I.L. Titlestad has nothing to disclose. B. Miller is an employee and shareholder of GSK. R. Tal-Singer is an employee and shareholder of GSK. U. Holmskov is an inventor of US Patent No. 9,988,442 and EP17199552.5 owned by University of Southern Denmark. J. Vestbo reports consultancy fees for COPD Phase 2 and 3 programmes and payment for lectures including service in speaker bureaus from GlaxoSmithKline, Chiesi Pharmaceuticals, Boehringer-Ingelheim, Novartis and AstraZeneca, and an unconditional grant for biomarker research at Manchester University Hospital NHS Foundation Trust from Boehringer Ingelheim, outside the submitted work. G.L. Sørensen is an inventor of US Patent No. 9,988,442 and EP17199552.5 owned by University of Southern Denmark. Support statement: The study was sponsored by the Danish Strategic Research Council. J. Vestbo is supported by the NIHR Manchester Biomedical Research Centre. The ECLIPSE study (SCO104960, NCT00292552) was funded by GSK. Funding information for this article has been deposited with the Crossref Funder Registry."],"id":"S01-000.00-614254","identifier":[{"id":"85114076873","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6469069","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31024964","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-8f43ceb8-a54f-45e9-a484-77753fcb23dd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1514B388271C4E3D4086EDD5F6FDE3FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151043257/Plasma_microfibrillar_associated_protein_4_is_not_prognostic_of_emphysema_progression_but_is_associated_with_cardiovascular_disease_history_and_mortality_in_COPD_patients.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license"