d, Romy","rank":86,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"V. W. V.","key":"jaddoevwvpau","last":"Jaddoe","name":"Jaddoe, V. W. V.","rank":87,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 43","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincent W V","key":"jaddoevincentwvpau","last":"Jaddoe","name":"Jaddoe, Vincent W V","rank":87,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30786138"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1471-0528.15661","issn":["01407686","14700328"],"issn_org":["14700328"],"issue":"8","journal":"BJOG: An International Journal of Obstetrics and Gynaecology","pages":"984-995","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"BJOG: An International Journal of Obstetrics and Gynaecology","volume":"126"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065645885"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-55b9d83c-ea54-49a0-8a9f-ef519db70738","sdu-a9242972-28b2-49df-ad73-582ccf336a3b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of maternal body mass index and gestational weight gain on pregnancy complications : An individual participant data meta-analysis of European, North American and Australian cohorts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.31-666843","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND:: Hyponatremia is associated with increased mortality and is frequently induced by diuretic use. It is uncertain whether diuretic use is linked to mortality risk in patients with hyponatremia. STUDY QUESTION:: To measure the prognostic impact of diuretic use on 30-day mortality among patients hospitalized with hyponatremia. STUDY DESIGN:: Using population-based registries, we identified all patients with a serum sodium measurement <135 mmol/L within 24 hours after acute hospital admission in western Denmark from 2006 to 2012 (cumulative population of 2.2 million). We categorized patients as current diuretic users (new and long-term), former users or nonusers, and followed them until death, migration or up to 30 days which ever came first. MEASURES AND OUTCOMES:: Thirty-day cumulative mortality and relative risk with 95% confidence interval (CI) controlled for demographics, previous morbidity, renal function, and co-medications. Calculations were also divided by the diuretic type and were repeated after propensity score matching. RESULTS:: Thirty-day mortality was 11.4% among current diuretic users (n = 14,635) compared with 6.2% among nonusers, yielding an adjusted relative risk of 1.4 (95% CI, 1.2–1.5). New users were at higher risk (1.7, 95% CI, 1.5–2.0) than long-term users (1.3, 95% CI, 1.2–1.4). In particular, the use of loop diuretics (1.6, 95% CI, 1.4–1.8), potassium-sparing diuretics (1.6, 95% CI, 1.2–2.2), and diuretic polytherapy (1.5, 95% CI, 1.3–1.7) were associated with increased risk, whereas thiazide use was not (1.0, 95% CI, 0.9–1.2). Propensity score–matched analyses confirmed the results. CONCLUSIONS:: Diuretic use except from thiazides, and particularly if newly initiated, is a negative prognostic factor in patients admitted with hyponatremia.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Holland-Bill, Louise","Christiansen, Christian F","Ulrichsen, Sinna P","Ring, Troels","Lunde Jørgensen, Jens O","Sørensen, Henrik T"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-011793"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Holland-Bill, Louise"],"keyword":["Comorbidity","Hyponatremia","Internal Medicine","Mortality","Pharmacoepidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preadmission diuretic use and mortality in patients hospitalized with hyponatremia a propensity score matched cohort study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85007153079&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-011793","identifier":[{"id":"85007153079","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28005557","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f6d425b7-726f-486a-8f44-bec19d1bb8b9","au-14306032-93be-4c31-95cb-efb9ee7be8f3"],"keyword":["comorbidity","diuretic use","hyponatremia","internal medicine","mortality","pharmacoepidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C980B4BE0EF478DC1E53EE5DC5755CD1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anaesthesiology and Operation, Intensive care","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Nephrology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"hollandbillpau","last":"Holland-Bill","locid":"578d785d-8e78-4933-9ba4-3db0ec2b4c29","name":"Holland-Bill, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian F","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"b1104ec4-1322-428f-af8f-7771361930bb","name":"Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","name_org":"Christiansen, Christian F","orcid":"0000-0002-0727-953X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sinna P","key":"ulrichsenpau","last":"Ulrichsen","locid":"28d145ca-92b9-49f2-8be2-e6d9f59c01ce","name":"Ulrichsen, Sinna Pilgaard","name_org":"Ulrichsen, Sinna P","orcid":"0000-0001-8679-5163","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels","key":"ringpau","last":"Ring","locid":"6efec618-81ab-4b8d-a0b0-21545f7c9336","name":"Ring, Troels","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens O","key":"lundejørgensenpau","last":"Lunde Jørgensen","locid":"303ebe86-6861-4b19-b4d7-6bda0526b27e","name":"Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","name_org":"Lunde Jørgensen, Jens O","orcid":"0000-0001-7408-1526","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik T","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","name_org":"Sørensen, Henrik T","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28005557"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/mjt.0000000000000544","issn":["10752765","15363686"],"issn_org":["10752765"],"issue":"1","journal":"American Journal of Therapeutics","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Therapeutics","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85007153079"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f6d425b7-726f-486a-8f44-bec19d1bb8b9","au-14306032-93be-4c31-95cb-efb9ee7be8f3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Preadmission Diuretic Use and Mortality in Patients Hospitalized With Hyponatremia : A Propensity Score-Matched Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-011793","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Surface area is an important input parameter for reactive transport modelling and it changes with time when rocks dissolve. Here we show direct observations of increased surface area due to chalk (predominantly CaCO3) dissolution, using 3D in situ X-ray microtomography. This transient increase cannot be explained by changes in fluid accessibility or by surface roughening that arises from preferential leaching. We use model simulations to explain how this increase in surface area correlates with the size of the Damköhler space, defined macroscopically using a phenomenological dissolution rate law and the cumulative surface of the microstructure. We attribute this transient increase to the coupling between fluid flow and mineral dissolution and argue that the extent is determined by the advective penetration distance of the reactants. We conclude that using a macroscopic dimensionless number as a qualitative indicator for microstructure evolution has limited applicability.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Yang, Y.","Rogowska, M.","Zheng, Yi","Bruns, Stefan","Gundlach, Carsten","Stipp, S.L.S.","Sørensen, Henning Osholm"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-034923"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Yang, Y."],"keyword":["Chalk dissolution","In situ imaging","Microstructure evolution","X ray tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transient increase in reactive surface and the macroscopic damköhler number in chalk dissolution","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/167600249/HYDROL29401R1_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["YY is supported by the European Union’s Horizon 2020 Research and Innovation Programme under the Marie Sklodowska-Curie Action project OMNICS (Grant Agreement No 653241) and by the Independent Research Fund Denmark under the Council of Technology and Production grant ConFiG (no. 8022-00162). Additional funding was provided by the Innovation Fund Denmark through the CINEMA project and the Innovation Fund Denmark and Maersk Oil and Gas A/S through the P 3 project. Parts of this work were also supported by funding from the European Commission for the CO2-REACT project, Grant No: FP7-317235, to MR. We gratefully acknowledge the Danish Agency for Science, Technology and Innovation for travel support via Danscatt . Appendix A"],"id":"S02-100.00-034923","identifier":[{"id":"85061191617","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-661fdd35-e88f-4249-95b1-819107029ba7","ku-bb0f5f42-1afb-4044-a182-2e65baaede5f"],"keyword":["Chalk Dissolution","Damköhler number","In situ imaging","Microstructure evolution","Reactive surface area","X-ray tomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8ED4AD034B894F520F80A4A16F321402"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1709.07784","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/167600249/HYDROL29401R1_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"a