":"Rose, S. K.","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"C. J.","key":"merchantpau","last":"Merchant","name":"Merchant, C. J.","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"macintoshpau","last":"MacIntosh","name":"MacIntosh, C.","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"vonschuckmannpau","last":"von Schuckmann","name":"von Schuckmann, K.","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"B. D.","key":"gutknechtpau","last":"Gutknecht","name":"Gutknecht, B. D.","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"novotnypau","last":"Novotny","name":"Novotny, K.","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"grohpau","last":"Groh","name":"Groh, A.","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. O.","key":"willenpau","last":"Willen","name":"Willen, M. O.","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"restanopau","last":"Restano","name":"Restano, M.","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"benvenistepau","last":"Benveniste","name":"Benveniste, J.","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-109491df-b86c-4ee7-8a6c-43055de8f97d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Global Sea Level Budget and Ocean Mass Budget, with Focus on New Data Products and Uncertainty Characterization.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309586","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background Drug-eluting stents (DES) have proven superior to bare-metal stents (BMS) in terms of safety and efficacy. However, inference to the female subgroup has been limited by low enrolment rates of women in clinical trials. The objective of this study was to investigate the safety and efficacy of DES versus BMS in women and men. Methods In a pooled analysis of two all-comers randomised trials (Basel Stent Kosten-Effektivitäts Trial-Prospective Validation Examination (BASKET-PROVE) and BASKET-PROVE II) (n=4605), we examined safety and efficacy of DES versus BMS according to sex. Patients were followed 2 years for a composite endpoint of cardiac death, non-fatal myocardial infarction (MI) and clinically driven target-vessel revascularisation not related to MI. Results Among the 1076 women and 3529 men included in the analysis, 65.6% of the women and 67.2% of the men were randomised to receive DES. At baseline, men had more complex coronary artery disease than women. After 2 years, DES reduced rates of major adverse cardiac events (MACE) compared with BMS in both women (cumulative incidence, 6.1% vs 14.7%; adjusted HR 0.36 (95% CI 0.24 to 0.54)) and men (7.7 vs 12.1%, HR 0.62 (0.50 to 0.77)), although the reduction in MACE rates was more pronounced in women (adjusted p=0.02 for sex-stent interaction). Event rates were lower in DES for both safety and efficacy outcomes, with the largest effect seen for non-MI TVR, in both women (2.3 vs 9.2%, adjusted HR 0.24 (0.13 to 0.44)) and men (4.0 vs 7.8%, adjusted HR 0.48 (0.36 to 0.64)) (adjusted p=0.049 for sex-stent interaction). Conclusions In patients requiring stenting of large coronary arteries, DES were associated with improved safety in women and superior efficacy in both sexes as compared with BMS.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bjerking, Louise Hougesen","Hansen, Kim Wadt","Sørensen, Rikke","Prescott, Eva","Biering-Sørensen, Tor","Jeger, Raban","Kaiser, Christoph","Pfisterer, Matthias","Galatius, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417088"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Basel"],"keyword":["Coronary Angiography","Coronary artery disease","Gender","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drug eluting stents in large coronary vessels improve both safety and efficacy compared with bare metal stents in women a pooled analysis of the basket prove i and ii trials","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/openhrt-2018-000986","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-417088","identifier":[{"id":"31217999","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85065965166","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6546185","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-27888fde-ad76-4e97-9917-7791746f1efa"],"keyword":["Coronary angiography","Coronary artery disease","Coronary stenting","Gender","Percutaneous coronary intervention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F47B73610C1CDD50ED37B8EF1F92FF75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/openhrt-2018-000986","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/236318640/e000986.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3