{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Houlberg Rung, Mette","Springborg, Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-549250"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deltagelse","Forandring","Kunst"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deltagelse som forstyrrelse og forandring","src":["kum"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-549250","ids":["kum-75882d22-348d-4eda-bb66-f471083b70cd"],"keyword":["Deltagelse","Forandring","Kunst"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6D7F2251EB1DF909C5C317C6194C6232"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kum ministry of culture archives museums and royal library denmark","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-KUM","l3nn":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","namevar":["Ministry of Culture Denmark, SMK National Gallery of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-KUM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"houlbergrungpau","last":"Houlberg Rung","locid":"47201f5f-62de-4d76-bc90-a52d52cbdb45","name":"Houlberg Rung, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8493-6601","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"springborgpau","last":"Springborg","name":"Springborg, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette Houlberg","key":"rungpedh","last":"Rung","name":"Rung, Mette Houlberg","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Scott","key":"sørensenpedh","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Anne Scott","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgit","key":"erikssonpedh","last":"Eriksson","name":"Eriksson, Birgit","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771845310"],"pages":"107-130","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"Kunst, kultur og deltagelse"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kum-75882d22-348d-4eda-bb66-f471083b70cd"],"src":["KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"Deltagelse som forstyrrelse og forandring","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-549250","year":"2019","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Human islet isolation is a cost-/resource-intensive program generating islets for cell therapy in Type 1 diabetes. However, only a third of cadaveric pancreas get to clinical transplantation due to low quality/number of islets. There is a need to identify biomarker(s) that predict the quality of islets, prior to initiating their isolation. Here, we sequenced transcriptome from 18 human islet preparations stratified into three groups (Gr.1: Best quality/transplantable islets, Gr.2: Intermediary quality, Gr.3: Inferior quality/non-transplantable islets) based on routine measurements including islet purity/viability. Machine-learning algorithms involving penalized regression analyses identified 10 long-non-coding(lnc)RNAs significantly different across all group-wise comparisons (Gr1VsGr2, Gr2vsGr3, Gr1vsGr3). Two variants of Metastasis-Associated Lung Adenocarcinoma Transcript-1(MALAT1) lncRNA were common across all comparisons. We confirmed RNA-seq findings in a \"validation set\" of 75 human islet preparations. Finally, in 19 pancreas samples, we demonstrate that assessing the levels of MALAT1 variants alone (ROC curve AUC: 0.83) offers highest specificity in predicting post-isolation islet quality and improves the predictive potential for clinical islet transplantation when combined with Edmonton Donor Points/Body Mass Index(BMI)/North American Islet Donor Score(NAIDS). We present this resource of islet-quality-stratified lncRNA transcriptome data and identify MALAT1 as a biomarker that significantly enhances current selection methods for clinical (GMP)-grade islet isolation.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Wong, Wilson W.K.","Jiang, Guochi","Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Chew, Yi Vee","Lee-Maynard, Cody","Liuwantara, David","Williams, Lindy","O'Connell, Phillip","Dalgaard, Louise Torp","Ma, Ronald C.","Hawthorne, Wayne J.","Joglekar, Mugdha","Hardikar, Anandwardhan Awadhoot"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-560619"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The Chinese University of Hong Kong","University of Sydney"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the long noncoding rna malat000000000001 predicts human islet isolation quality","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://insight.jci.org/articles/view/129299","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-560619","identifier":[{"id":"85071524274","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-454c37e8-6abb-481c-92c9-cd6e01254f13"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2A69FB10F75596D0F1332DEA6BC1F1F6"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Sydney","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"the chinese university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The Chinese University of Hong Kong","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Wilson W.K.","key":"wongpau","last":"Wong","name":"Wong, Wilson W.K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Guochi","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Guochi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Anja Elaine","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7e5d1e2c-5d4b-4436-bb66-acdca4058c08","name":"Sørensen, Anja Elaine","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-5376","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yi Vee","key":"chewpau","last":"Chew","name":"Chew, Yi Vee","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cody","key":"leemaynardpau","last":"Lee-Maynard","name":"Lee-Maynard, Cody","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"David","key":"liuwantarapau","last":"Liuwantara","name":"Liuwantara, David","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lindy","key":"williamspau","last":"Williams","name":"Williams, Lindy","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Phillip","key":"oconnellpau","last":"O'Connell","name":"O'Connell, Phillip","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Louise Torp","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"a219fdaf-f994-4a7a-beb8-1f353846ed5a","name":"Dalgaard, Louise Torp","orcid":"0000-0002-3598-2775","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ronald C.","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Ronald C.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wayne J.","key":"hawthornepau","last":"Hawthorne","name":"Hawthorne, Wayne J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mugdha","key":"joglekarpau","last":"Joglekar","name":"Joglekar, Mugdha","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anandwardhan Awadhoot","key":"hardikarpau","last":"Hardikar","name":"Hardikar, Anandwardhan Awadhoot","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1172/jci.insight.129299","issn":["23793708"],"issue":"16","journal":"JCI Insight","paperid":"e129299","status":"p","title":"JCI Insight","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071524274"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-454c37e8-6abb-481c-92c9-cd6e01254f13"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"The long noncoding RNA MALAT1 predicts human islet isolation quality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-560619","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Study question: Can we identify microRNAs associated with an altered metabolic proﬁle in women with Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS), which can serve as biomarkers for early diabetes? Summary answer: Circulating miR-122-5p is a possible marker of prediabetes in women with PCOS and is associated with the severity of metabolic disease. What is known already:It is well established that women with PCOS are at greater risk of developing metabolic syndrome and type 2 diabetes. Recent discoveries indicate that miRNAs play an important role in development of diabetes in general and reﬂect the clinical status of patients. However, to date there are no existing studies of circulating miRNAs as biomarkers for a challenged metabolism and a prediabetic phenotype in women with PCOS. Study design,size,duration:A prospective follow-up-study with a cohort of 46 women with PCOS diagnosed according to Rotterdam 2003 criteria and nine healthy controls, aged 18 to 39 years. The women were examined twice 6 yearsapart.CirculatingmiRNAlevelswereanalyzedatbothvisitsandcompared with clinical data. A cross sectional cohort of 162 PCOS patients (133 PCOS and 29 controls) were investigated for biological validation of ﬁndings. Participants/materials,setting,methods:Relevant clinical data of PCOS status and measurements of metabolic disease were obtained at both visits. Peripheral fasting serum samples collected at both time points were used for microRNA analysis. Total RNA was extracted using TriReagent. MiRNA levels were measured using custom Taqman® Array cards of 96 selected miRNAs. MiRNArelativelevelswerequantiﬁedbythe2-Ct method.MiR-122-5pwere analyzed with individual qRT-PCR in the validation cohort. Main results and the role of chance:During the 6-year follow-up, more participants became prediabetic (deﬁned by Impaired Glucose Tolerance (IGT) or Impaired Fasting Glucose (IFG)) (Six (10.9%) participants at baseline vs 10 (18.2%) participants at follow-up). Analysis of miRNA did not reveal signiﬁcant differences in circulating levels of any of the tested miRNAs comparing PCOS Abstracts of the 35th Annual Meeting of the ESHRE,Vienna,Austria 24 to 26 June 2019 i431 with controls neither at baseline nor at follow-up. However, comparing the non-prediabetic with prediabetic, we found that miR-122-5p was signiﬁcantly upregulatedintheprediabeticgroupbothatfollow-up(p=0.03)andatbaseline, as predictor of prediabetic status at follow-up (p=0.03, OR=7.7 (95%CI: 1.251.3)adjustedforBMI,smokingandage).Next,theparticipantswereevaluated for degree of metabolic disease by numbers of metabolic factors present (0-5: hypertension, dyslipidemia, triglyceridemia, increased waist circumference and IGT or IFG). Applying linear regression on the levels of miR-122-5p vs the degree of metabolic disease, the models were statistically signiﬁcant both at baseline(R2=0.10,B=0.51,p=0.05)andfollow-up(R2=0.17B=0.9,p<0.01).In thevalidationof ﬁndingsinthecohortof 162participants,wefoundsigniﬁcantly elevated levels of miR-122-5p in participants with IFG both in PCOS patients alone(p<0.05)andinthecohortasawhole(p<0.01)afteradjustmentforBMI and age. Limitations,reasons for caution:Few participants with prediabetes in the follow-up study causes weak modelling. Wider implications of the ﬁndings: Our results are in line with earlier studies of miR-122-5p, which have demonstrated strong correlation with both metabolic and hepatic disease. Further, validation in the larger cohort strengthen the ﬁndings, but suggests that miR-122-5p is probably more a generalmarkerof metabolicdisease,thanaPCOS-speciﬁcmarkerof metabolic disease. Trial registration number:ClinicalTrials.gov. Identiﬁer: NCT03142633","author_count":7,"contributors":["Udesen, P.B.","Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Svendsen, Rikke","Frisk, Nanna Lond Skov","Wissing, Marie Louise Muff","Dalgaard, Louise Torp","Mikkelsen, Anne Lis Englund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-572667"],"event":{"end":"2019-06-26","place":"Wien, at","start":"2019-06-23","title":"35th Annual Meeting of the ESHRE","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of micrornas associated with an impaired metabolic profile in women with polycystic ovary syndrome","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.eshre.eu/-/media/sitecore-files/Annual-meeting/Vienna/Abstract-book-2019-v2.pdf?la=en&hash=F4F40E984DD06A3F0206C13495105ECFA9D92FF0","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-572667","ids":["ruc-f7b47deb-09c1-4d3a-8991-bd46a1abea87"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7347BF772A754FD2BD7786F50DFDFBE4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Køge Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"P.B.","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","name":"Udesen, P.B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Anja Elaine","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7e5d1e2c-5d4b-4436-bb66-acdca4058c08","name":"Sørensen, Anja Elaine","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-5376","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"64c98108-e41d-4368-a5ef-8b49c0ecde50","name":"Svendsen, Rikke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Nanna Louise Skov","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"25f309b3-6a87-40f7-8fe6-7475e7ecce58","name":"Frisk, Nanna Lond Skov","name_org":"Nielsen, Nanna Louise Skov","orcid":"0000-0001-6150-2408","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Louise Muff","key":"wissingpau","last":"Wissing","name":"Wissing, Marie Louise Muff","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Louise Torp","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"a219fdaf-f994-4a7a-beb8-1f353846ed5a","name":"Dalgaard, Louise Torp","orcid":"0000-0002-3598-2775","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Lis Englund","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","name":"Mikkelsen, Anne Lis Englund","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["02681161","14602350"],"issn_org":["02681161"],"issue":"Suppl","journal":"Human Reproduction","status":"p","title":"Human Reproduction","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-f7b47deb-09c1-4d3a-8991-bd46a1abea87"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Identification of microRNAs associated with an impaired metabolic profile in women with polycystic ovary syndrome","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-572667","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The decision to limit or discontinue treatment is a difficult issue, which all physicians will face. Timely communication with information on treatment possibilities and limitations, respectful listening to patients‘ and informal caregivers‘ wishes and early palliation is recommended in a stable phase. In some situations, it is better to stop life-prolonging treatment and optimise quality of life in patients with benign pulmonary diseases. Decision on treatment limitations or discontinuation is best taken at a conference and should be based on the patient’s wishes, the disease stage and progression and potential reversible components.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Sørensen, Anita Rath","Bendstrup, Elisabeth","Løkke, Anders","Titlestad, Ingrid Louise","Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr","Thomsen, Laura Hohwu","Roberts, Nassim Bazeghi","Gjørup, Pia Holland","Shaker, Saher Burhan","Gundestrup, Svend","Wilcke, Jon Torgny Rostrup","Weinreich, Ulla Moller","Marsaa, Kristoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-621967"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Advance care planning","Caregivers","Humans","Lung Diseases Interstitial therapy","Palliative care","Patient Preference","Physician Patient Relations","Pulmonary Disease Chronic Obstructive therapy","Quality of Life","Terminal Care","Withholding Treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"behandlingsniveau og behandlingsstop ved benign lungesygdom","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/behandlingsniveau-og-behandlingsstop-ved-benign-lungesygdom","ve