{"abstract":"Purpose: The aims of this study were to examine associations between substitutions of poultry and red meat intake with fish (total, lean or fatty) and the risk of peripheral arterial disease (PAD). We hypothesised that a higher intake of fish and a concomitant lower intake of poultry or red meat were associated with a lower risk of incident PAD. Methods: We used data from a Danish cohort where middle-aged participants filled in food frequency and lifestyle questionnaires at baseline. During follow-up, we identified participants with valid diagnoses of PAD and analysed data by multivariable Cox regression analyses. Substitutions of 150 g/week of either poultry, red meat (processed or unprocessed) with 150 g/week of fish (total, lean or fatty) were explored. Results: We followed the cohort (n = 54,597) for a median of 13.6 years and identified 897 cases with PAD. We found modest lower rates of PAD when intake of fish replaced a concomitant lower intake of unprocessed (HR 0.94, 95% CI 0.88–1.01) and processed red meat (HR 0.94, 95% CI 0.87–1.02). Replacing unprocessed (HR 0.89, 95% CI 0.79–1.00) or processed red meat (HR 0.88, 95% CI 0.78–1.01) with fatty fish was associated with lower rates of PAD. No associations were observed when fish intake replaced poultry or when lean fish replaced red meat. Conclusions: This study suggests that substituting red meat with fish and especially fatty fish may be associated with a lower risk of PAD, although not statistically significant. Replacing poultry with fish was not associated with the risk of PAD.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lasota, Anne N","Grønholdt, Marie-Louise","Bork, Christian Sørensen","Lundbye-Christensen, Søren","Schmidt, Erik Berg","Overvad, Kim"],"cuid":["S02-089.66-000586"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cohort study","Fish","Meat","Peripheral arterial disease","Substitution"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"substitution of poultry and red meat with fish and the risk of peripheral arterial disease a danish cohort study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85053772188&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.66-000586","identifier":[{"id":"85053772188","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30238314","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-0b236e63-baaf-4404-8b0b-82324af9051e","au-3ad6e447-077c-4449-b2c7-f8f4bfbf45f5"],"keyword":["Cohort study","Fish","Meat","Peripheral arterial disease","Substitution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2345423719E021A6E4A2536F3F847B94"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Vascular Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne N.","key":"lasotapau","last":"Lasota","locid":"bc00a0f0-eaac-44f2-bd2d-148ad7da49a5","name":"Lasota, Anne N","name_org":"Lasota, Anne N.","orcid":"0000-0001-6489-3213","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie-Louise Moes","key":"grønholdtpau","last":"Grønholdt","locid":"a1169867-75a1-47b4-aa1c-aea1b408226d","name":"Grønholdt, Marie-Louise","name_org":"Grønholdt, Marie-Louise Moes","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Sørensen","key":"borkpau","last":"Bork","locid":"9a5f5510-7213-4e16-88c2-74a3af7aa2d9","name":"Bork, Christian Sørensen","orcid":"0000-0001-5233-2902","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"lundbyechristensenpau","last":"Lundbye-Christensen","locid":"d2639b0b-0785-456c-8c8d-57e9e79e0569","name":"Lundbye-Christensen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-9420-2783","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Berg","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"3eff6ccc-90b4-48ee-b121-8df4865f0342","name":"Schmidt, Erik Berg","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-5666","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"overvadpau","last":"Overvad","locid":"7ca4bfca-d3a3-484e-8ee5-d7cb6ad7314b","name":"Overvad, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-6429-7921","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30238314"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00394-018-1822-y","issn":["14366207","14366215"],"issn_org":["14366207"],"issue":"7","journal":"European Journal of Nutrition","pages":"2731-2739","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Nutrition","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053772188"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0b236e63-baaf-4404-8b0b-82324af9051e","au-3ad6e447-077c-4449-b2c7-f8f4bfbf45f5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Substitution of poultry and red meat with fish and the risk of peripheral arterial disease : a Danish cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.66-000586","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background & Aims: We recently showed that the functional capacity for ureagenesis is deficient in non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) patients. The aim of this study was to assess expression of urea cycle-related genes to elucidate a possible gene regulatory basis to the functional problem. Methods: Liver mRNA expression analyses within the gene pathway governing hepatic nitrogen conversion were performed in 20 non-diabetic, biopsy-proven NAFLD patients (8 simple steatosis; 12 non-alcoholic steatohepatitis [NASH]) and 12 obese and 14 lean healthy individuals. Sixteen NAFLD patients were included for gene expression validation. Relationship between gene expressions and functional capacity for ureagenesis was described. Results: Gene expression of most urea cycle-related enzymes were downregulated in NAFLD vs both control groups; markedly so for the urea cycle flux-generating carbamoyl phosphate synthetase (CPS1) (~3.5-fold, P <.0001). In NASH, CPS1 downregulation paralleled the deficit in ureagenesis (P =.03). Additionally, expression of several genes involved in amino acid uptake and degradation, and the glucagon receptor gene, were downregulated in NAFLD. Conversely, glutamine synthetase (GS) expression increased >1.5-fold (P ≤.03), inversely related to CPS1 expression (P =.004). Conclusions: NAFLD downregulated the expression of urea cycle-related genes. Downregulation of urea cycle flux-generating CPS1 correlated with the loss of functional capacity for ureagenesis in NASH. On gene level, these changes coincided with an increase in the major ammonia scavenging enzyme GS. The effects seemed related to a fatty liver as such rather than NASH or obesity. The findings support gene regulatory mechanisms involved in the deficient ureagenesis of NAFLD, but it remains unexplained how hepatocyte fat accumulation exerts these effects.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Eriksen, Peter Lykke","Vilstrup, Hendrik","Rigbolt, Kristoffer","Suppli, Malte Palm","Sørensen, Michael","Heebøll, Sara","Veidal, Sanne Skovgård","Knop, Fillip Krag","Thomsen, Karen Louise"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-027073"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Amino acid transport","Amino acids","Ammonia","Cirrhosis","Component","Elimination","Glucagon","Glutamine synthetase","In vivo","Induction","Non alcoholic steatohepatitis","Resistance","Steatosis","Stimulation","Urea","Urea cycle"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GUB"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-GUB","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non alcoholic fatty liver disease alters expression of genes governing hepatic nitrogen conversion","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85071855933","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-027073","identifier":[{"id":"000485856700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85071855933","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31386258","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c6b899ea-6b3b-4c39-a902-abc69812b63e","ku-a3d8707d-0d87-4930-a831-1b7255dfd724"],"keyword":["AMINO-ACID-TRANSPORT","CIRRHOSIS","COMPONENT","ELIMINATION","IN-VIVO","INDUCTION","RESISTANCE","STEATOSIS","STIMULATION","UREA CYCLE","amino acids","ammonia","glucagon","glutamine synthetase","non-alcoholic steatohepatitis","urea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-838F251B64324FF8CDCB85162A06290C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hepatology and Gastroenterology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"gubra","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GUB","l3nl":"Gubra","l3nn":"Gubra","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Gubra","namevar":["Gubra ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GUB","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Lykke","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"02b5f3f7-8692-403b-9a17-1dc588d638e7","name":"Eriksen, Peter Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-1115-8308","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hendrik","key":"vilstruppau","last":"Vilstrup","locid":"9e1905f3-3094-4aea-bbde-7178733bf6cb","name":"Vilstrup, Hendrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristoffer","key":"rigboltpau","last":"Rigbolt","name":"Rigbolt, Kristoffer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Malte P.","key":"supplipau","last":"Suppli","name":"Suppli, Malte P.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"52635821-2c0d-418e-848d-e3e1f1175e12","name":"Sørensen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-8750-4329","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"heebøllpau","last":"Heebøll","locid":"4cc44596-c83a-4e5d-bbd3-b2f7beb0958e","name":"Heebøll, Sara","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne Skovgård","key":"veidalpau","last":"Veidal","name":"Veidal, Sanne Skovgård","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Fillip K.","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","name_org":"Knop, Fillip K.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen Louise","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"32baa31f-0b93-4c6d-af7e-0da0519f574f","name":"Thomsen, Karen Louise","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31386258"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/liv.14205","issn":["13991698","14783223"],"issn_org":["14783223"],"issue":"11","journal":"Liver International","pages":"2094-2101","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Liver International","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071855933"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Gubra","Hospitals","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c6b899ea-6b3b-4c39-a902-abc69812b63e","ku-a3d8707d-0d87-4930-a831-1b7255dfd724"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Non-alcoholic fatty liver disease alters expression of genes governing hepatic nitrogen conversion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-027073","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The Programme for Monitoring of the Greenland Ice Sheet (PROMICE) has measured ice-sheet elevation and thickness via repeat airborne surveys circumscribing the ice sheet at an average elevation of 1708 ± 5 m (Sørensen et al. 2018). We refer to this 5415 km survey as the ‘PROMICE perimeter’. Here, we assess ice-sheet mass balance following the input-output approach of Andersen et al. (2015). We estimate ice-sheet output, or the ice discharge across the ice-sheet grounding line, by applying downstream corrections to the ice flux across the PROMICE perimeter. We subtract this ice discharge from ice-sheet input, or the area-integrated, ice sheet surface mass balance, estimated by a regional climate model. While Andersen et al. (2015) assessed ice-sheet mass balance in 2007 and 2011, this updated input-output assessment now estimates the annual sea-level rise contribution from eighteen sub-sectors of the Greenland ice sheet over the 1995–2015 period.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Colgan, William","Mankoff, Kenneth D.","Kjeldsen, Kristian K.","Bjørk, Anders A.","Box, Jason E.","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Khan, Shfaqat Abbas","Solgaard, Anne M.","Forsberg, René","Skourup, Henriette","Stenseng, Lars","Kristensen, Steen Savstrup","Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","Citterio, Michele","Karlsson, Nanna","Fettweis, Xavier","Ahlstrøm, Andreas P.","Andersen, Signe B.","Van As, Dirk","Fausto, Robert"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-032853"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Colgan, William"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Liege"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greenland ice sheet mass balance assessed by promice 000000001995 000000002015","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.34194/GEUSB-201943-02-01","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-032853","identifier":[{"id":"85071306593","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0bad55d7-5103-4f11-9206-14153c7983b6","ku-81f5dba2-6bb9-481e-bb4d-61d53d9d8de3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-407886B63786C421ACCBBD51E604C505"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/189369608/geusb_201943_02_01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/225429226/Greenland_ice_sheet_mass_balance_assessed_by_PROMICE_1995_2015_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.34194/GEUSB-201943-02-01","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for