{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To update tonsillectomy incidence rates in Denmark and identify whether the incidence rates vary between geographical areas in the country during the period 1991-2012. DESIGN: This was a retrospective nationwide cohort study using data from the comprehensive Danish patient registries. Data included surgical code, gender and date of birth, date and place of surgery. SETTING: Hospitals and private oto-, rhino-, laryngology (ORL) offices. PARTICIPANTS: Danes who underwent tonsillectomy in the period 1991-2012. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE: Tonsillectomy. RESULTS: In the 22-year period, 177 211 tonsillectomies were conducted, and the overall incidence of tonsillectomy decreased significantly over time. The overall annual incidence of tonsillectomies decreased from 155.7 per 100 000 inhabitants in 1991 to 129.4 per 100 000 inhabitants in 2012. In 1991, 5.5% of tonsillectomies were performed in office settings, while in 2012, it had increased to 26.6% (P < .01). The highest incidence of tonsillectomy was found in children between 3 and 4 years of age (predominance of males, P < .01) and in 15- to 19-year-olds (predominance of females, P < .01). Each year, 0.44% of children underwent tonsillectomy, and by the age of 20, 7.7% of the Danish people has had a tonsillectomy. There were significant regional differences in the number of tonsillectomies. CONCLUSION: The incidence rate of tonsillectomies in Denmark decreased significantly in the study period, but with great regional variance.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Juul, Marie Louise","Rasmussen, Eva Rye","Rasmussen, Stig Hebbelstrup Rye","Sørensen, Christian Hjort","Howitz, Michael Frantz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-510032"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Child","Child Preschool","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Follow Up Studies","Forecasting","Humans","Incidence","Infant","Infant Newborn","Male","Population Surveillance methods","Registries","Retrospective Studies","Tonsillectomy statistics numerical data","Tonsillitis epidemiology","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a nationwide registry based cohort study of incidence of tonsillectomy in denmark 000000001991 000000002012","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-510032","identifier":[{"id":"85040833998","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28851039","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c34d7007-5214-4f61-ac8c-6d09bc2c7f46"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Child","Child, Preschool","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Forecasting","Humans","Incidence","Infant","Infant, Newborn","Male","Population Surveillance/methods","Registries","Retrospective Studies","Tonsillectomy/statistics & numerical data","Tonsillitis/epidemiology","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-06C62773F405DA3B55E8EECD17E7DA3E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Marie Louise","key":"juulmarielouisepau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Marie Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva Rye","key":"rasmussenevaryepau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Eva Rye","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stig Hebbelstrup Rye","key":"rasmussenstighebbelstrupryepau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Stig Hebbelstrup Rye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Hjort","key":"sørensenchristianhjortpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c6f2ec98-9856-4e9d-8757-e5b0d6978778","name":"Sørensen, Christian Hjort","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael Frantz","key":"howitzmichaelfrantzpau","last":"Howitz","name":"Howitz, Michael Frantz","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28851039"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/coa.12959","issn":["17494478","17494486"],"issn_org":["17494478"],"issue":"1","journal":"Clinical Otolaryngology","pages":"274-284","status":"p","title":"Clinical Otolaryngology","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040833998"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c34d7007-5214-4f61-ac8c-6d09bc2c7f46"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A nationwide registry-based cohort study of incidence of tonsillectomy in Denmark, 1991-2012","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-510032","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Peters, Rikke","Sørensen, Christina Louise","Lauridsen, Poul Kjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-649916"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Læring pædagogik og undervisning"],"level":"edu","oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"svenskerne nabovenner eller arvefjender","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://historielab.dk/til-undervisningen/kildebank/svenskerne-nabovenner-arvefjender/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-649916","ids":["ucl-f7ef4ffc-4416-4549-9a2a-251dd2ce7a52"],"keyword":["Læring, pædagogik og undervisning"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","noi":["Local-1-1-00D19BC130A015F05A1DDD0C76A9E45B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://historielab.dk/til-undervisningen/kildebank/svenskerne-nabovenner-arvefjender/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Rektor, Rektor, Videncenter for Historie og Kulturformidling"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Louise Alberg","key":"peterspau","last":"Peters","locid":"c08a1671-9716-48a1-a1b9-2f07a47a57e9","name":"Peters, Rikke","name_org":"Peters, Rikke Louise Alberg","orcid":"0000-0003-0120-370X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Louise","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c4715900-2e37-4a8f-9c8b-77690089c2c4","name":"Sørensen, Christina Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul Kjær","key":"lauridsenppu","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"d50179d4-5a35-4a3c-b628-ad1543edeff8","name":"Lauridsen, Poul Kjær","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-f7ef4ffc-4416-4549-9a2a-251dd2ce7a52"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Svenskerne - nabovenner eller arvefjender?","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-649916","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The dissertation Beyond Periphery – Dissensual Artistic Representations of Danish Provinces 2005-2015 examines how certain artistic representations of the provinces have the potential to make the Danish provinces sensible as something other than simply periphery. The outset of the dissertation is the one-sided debate about the Danish provinces, which, after the turn of the millennium, has made itself manifest through terms such as ‘the rotten banana’ (‘den rådne banan’) and ‘Peripheral Denmark’ (‘Udkantsdanmark’). This negative and – as argued in this dissertation – politically based and media generated framing of the provinces as periphery (which in this dissertation is termed periphery policing) forms the background of the analyses. Following the aesthetic-political theories of Jacques Rancière, aesthetic representations of the provinces from 2005 to 2015 (even those not explicitly participating in the discussion of the Danish provinces or referencing peripheral areas) are comprehended as having a genuine political potential to create new ways of perceiving areas popularly termed ‘Peripheral Denmark’. Thus, my thesis’s proposition is that the selected artistic representations of the provinces have a political potential related to the prevailing policing of the periphery. These representations create new ways of making the provinces sensible accessible through what this dissertation terms dissensus of the periphery. The opening chapter of the dissertation is an introductory chapter, in which the debate about the so-called ‘Peripheral Denmark’ outlined and the analytical field of the dissertation is presented. This chapter points to two fundamental conditions of the emergence of ‘Peripheral Denmark’. Firstly, using Malene Brandt Winther and Gunnar Lind Haase Svenden as a starting point, ‘Peripheral Denmark’ is revealed as a new and singularly negative discourse about the provinces, whose emergence can be connected to the agenda of centralisation practised after the change of government in 2001. Secondly, focusing on the term ‘the rotten banana’, it is described how the media – the news media in particular – has been a deciding factor in the manifestation of the discourse. 225 Chapter 2 opens with a presentation of Rancière’s most important concepts: Firstly, the distribution of the sensible, policing, and dissensus, and then the three art regimes and aesthetic dissensus. As such, the chapter consists of two parts: One concerning the ‘aesthetics of politics’ and one concerning ‘the politics aesthetics’, a move from the socio-political domain to the domain of art theory. This two-fold clarification of terms serves the purpose of conceptualising ‘Peripheral Denmark’ – using Rancière’s theories of society – as a repressive societal discourse, a specific framing or distribution of the sensible, which supresses any perceptions of the provinces as anything but periphery. This dissertation thereby term this the policing of the periphery. Terming ‘Peripheral Denmark’ as a type of policing of the periphery is the foundation of the second part of the chapter, in which I argue - based on Rancière’s art regimes - that creative representations of the provinces can be understood as possessing a peripheral political potential in relation to the prevailing policing of the periphery. Chapter 3 uses Rancière’s art regimes to focus on what this dissertation term ‘art in the service of the periphery’. This chapter focuses on artworks which have the explicit intention to debate or even change the conditions in ’Peripheral Denmark’. This chapter of the dissertation is unique in dealing with analytical case material explicitly expressing a political agenda. Here I highlight and discuss the problems related to art trying to ‘save the periphery’ through strategies of participation. At the end of the chapter an analysis of the place specific artwork “Skivevej 13” (2013) concludes, that it is certainly possible to create artistic interactions and place specific artworks in the provinces that have a potential for creating a dissensus of the periphery. However, this type of art cannot simply create local change. It has to mediate the local or make it sensible accessible anew. Chapter 4 establishes the dissertation’s method, which partly serves as a way of scanning the extensive creative material, and partly provides methods of globalisation and place theory that can be used to locate and analyse a dissensus of the periphery. The chapter is divided into three sections. First, the reception in which this dissertation focuses, is outlined and discussed, and thereafter, the field of globalisation theory is presented. It is argued that ‘Peripheral Denmark’ must be understood as a particular way (out of several alternative ways) of viewing the areas of the provinces as a product of globalisation. Finally, based on Doreen Massey’s concept ‘a global sense of place’ it is suggested that the analytical case material can be sorted in conjuncture with the ‘sense of place’ distributed in the artworks. Chapter 5 analyses the novel Naturlige fjender (Natural Enemies, 2008) by Lone Hørslev which serves as an example of a work distributing a global sense of place or a ‘glocal dissensus of the periphery’. The chapter argues that Naturlige fjender can be interpreted as radical glocal literature, which enforces an expanded sense of the provincial place on three levels. One through a trope of traffic, which depicts Vejby (Road Town) as a junction of larger and wider connections; another through a distinct stream of consciousness style equipping local inhabitants with a global outlook, and also in a non-hierarchic syntax which distributes a flat ontology. Chapter 6 undertakes a close reading of the novel Stigninger og fald (Ascents and Descents, 2010) by Josefine Klougart, which distinguishes itself as being an active and reflective remembrance novel. This chapter examines how Stigninger og fald opens the provincial childhood in an active and dynamic way through literary experiments that continually open and rewrite the place and landscape of Mols. In this analysis it is argued that the use of linked metaphors in particular possess a political peripheral potential by creating entirely new sensible connections in the perception, but also by distributing an open sense of place through the expansive power of metonymic displacement. Chapter 7 examines the art photography exhibition Uden for myldretid (Beyond the Rush, 2013-2015) focusing on Carsten Ingemann’s contribution entitled “Mørke” (“Darkness”). Ingemann’s tactile night photographies, which at times seem more like paintings than photographs, bring about a dissensual pensiveness, a zone of perceptual indetermination between the prevailing codes of representation of the provinces and new distributions of the sensible. In this analysis, I argue that “Mørke” works as a ‘minor’ photography which challenges the ‘major’ codes of representing the provinces in photography. Ingemann’s images of darkness make common ways of perceiving the periphery as ‘stutter’ or ‘stop making sense’ by use of its haptic shape, but also (as seen in the Hørdum227 photograph) by embedding a critical reflection on the ‘larger’ photography. In the final analytical chapter (8) the analytical main points of the dissertation are gathered in an analysis of the music film An Island (2010). In a close reading of selected sections of the film, and in cohesion to the preceding analysis’ of the previous chapters, it is argued that aesthetic peripheral dissensus can be identified and analysed in 1) the breaks with prevailing matrices of provincial presentation, 2) in the bringing about new distributions of the sensible, and finally 3) in a glocal distribution of the local. The conclusion of the dissertation briefly outlines the evolvement from 2015 to present day, during which the policing of the periphery seems to have lost momentum. As a continuation of this, the conclusion draws perspectives to some of the assertions proposed by this dissertation on the changed political context, which includes new culture and branding initiatives such as Cold Hawaii and increased political disagreement following the general election of 2015.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sørensen, Tina Louise Hove"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-694265"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hinsides udkant alternative kunstneriske sanseliggørelser af dansk provins 000000002005 000000002015","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dtd","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-694265","ids":["au-c988d224-a3ed-4984-b852-449926133cdf"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-433D471FFB4E8D9A0ECA56065A45B032"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Department of Art History, Aesthetics & Culture and Museology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Louise Hove","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"2560cc73-3cc9-4077-85b7-55dc78426422","name":"Sørensen, Tina Louise Hove","orcid":"0009-0000-0392-0767","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"244","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c988d224-a3ed-4984-b852-449926133cdf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hinsides udkant : Alternative kunstneriske sanseliggørelser af dansk provins 2005-2015","type":"Thesis Doctoral","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-694265","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The decision to limit or discontinue treatment is a difficult issue, which all physicians will face. Timely communication with information on treatment possibilities and limitations, respectful listening to patients' and informal caregivers' wishes and early palliation is recommended in a stable phase. In some situations, it is better to stop life-prolonging treatment and optimise quality of life in patients with benign pulmonary diseases. Decision on treatment limitations or discontinuation is best taken at a conference and should be based on the patient's wishes, the disease stage and progression and potential reversible components.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Sørensen, Anita Rath","Bendstrup, Elisabeth","Løkke, Anders","Titlestad, Ingrid Louise","Jensen, Jens Ulrik","Thomsen, Laura","Roberts, Nassim","Gjørup, Pia Holland","Shaker, Saher","Gundestrup, Svend","Wilcke, Torgny","Weinreich, Ulla","Marsaa, Kristoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745120"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"treatment limitations or discontinuation in patients with benign pulmonary diseases","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85054090930","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745120","identifier":[{"id":"85054090930","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30274574","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b141323a-0ef0-4113-bd9a-9c65b9e519f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0DE1495B3B30DB791B31C57197CD0833"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":