{"abstract":"As the demand for product customization increases globally, companies must increasingly manufacture individually configured products, which stresses the traditional business processes and manufacturing systems. Although previous research indicates potentials in integrating product and process models, few practical implementations of this are found partly due to lacking systems integration. This paper proposes a framework for integrating existing information repositories for manufacturing system and product family model information. By integrating this information, manufacturing information can improve the product configuration process and product configuration information can support the manufacturing process.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","Sorensen, Daniel G. H.","Andersen, Ann-Louise","Nielsen, Kjeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-104692"],"event":{"end":"2018-05-18","place":"Stockholm, se","start":"2018-05-16","title":"51st CIRP Conference on Manufacturing Systems, CIRP CMS 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Brunø, Thomas Ditlev"],"keyword":["Mass customization","Ontology","Process model","Product Model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"framework for integrating production system models and product family models","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procir.2018.03.020","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-104692","identifier":[{"id":"85049577467","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bc882fbc-ac57-4439-8dc7-2e8f8b2b643b"],"keyword":["co-platforming","mass customization","ontology","process model","product model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F485603FC534CEB42E5EF67E2AC5BB92"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/287532474/1_s2.0_S2212827118301197_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procir.2018.03.020","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Manufacturing Systems research group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Ditlev","key":"brunoepau","last":"Brunoe","locid":"b75a6b6d-0181-4141-b951-6f7f70bae83f","name":"Brunø, Thomas Ditlev","name_org":"Brunoe, Thomas Ditlev","orcid":"0000-0002-9847-6562","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Grud","key":"hellerupsørensenpau","last":"Hellerup Sørensen","locid":"7c8e8d62-a3ee-4398-8d8a-c4c514667546","name":"Sorensen, Daniel G. H.","name_org":"Hellerup Sørensen, Daniel Grud","orcid":"0000-0001-9395-2411","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann Louise","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"73d5c9b6-ff83-41c1-b16e-43f380f384d9","name":"Andersen, Ann-Louise","name_org":"Andersen, Ann Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7923-6301","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ffae8343-8516-499e-89a3-2f0d6179a5fc","name":"Nielsen, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3720-167X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.procir.2018.03.020","issn":["22128271"],"journal":"Procedia CIRP","pages":"592-597","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Procedia CIRP","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049577467"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bc882fbc-ac57-4439-8dc7-2e8f8b2b643b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Framework for Integrating Production System Models and Product Family Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-104692","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To examine the risks of myocardial infarction, stroke (ischaemic and haemorrhagic), peripheral artery disease, venous thromboembolism, atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter, and heart failure in patients with migraine and in a general population comparison cohort. DESIGN: Nationwide, population based cohort study. SETTING: All Danish hospitals and hospital outpatient clinics from 1995 to 2013. PARTICIPANTS: 51 032 patients with migraine and 510 320 people from the general population matched on age, sex, and calendar year. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: Comorbidity adjusted hazard ratios of cardiovascular outcomes based on Cox regression analysis. RESULTS: Higher absolute risks were observed among patients with incident migraine than in the general population across most outcomes and follow-up periods. After 19 years of follow-up, the cumulative incidences per 1000 people for the migraine cohort compared with the general population were 25v17 for myocardial infarction, 45v25 for ischaemic stroke, 11v6 for haemorrhagic stroke, 13v11 for peripheral artery disease, 27v18 for venous thromboembolism, 47v34 for atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter, and 19v18 for heart failure. Correspondingly, migraine was positively associated with myocardial infarction (adjusted hazard ratio 1.49, 95% confidence interval 1.36 to 1.64), ischaemic stroke (2.26, 2.11 to 2.41), and haemorrhagic stroke (1.94, 1.68 to 2.23), as well as venous thromboembolism (1.59, 1.45 to 1.74) and atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter (1.25, 1.16 to 1.36). No meaningful association was found with peripheral artery disease (adjusted hazard ratio 1.12, 0.96 to 1.30) or heart failure (1.04, 0.93 to 1.16). The associations, particularly for stroke outcomes, were stronger during the short term (0-1 years) after diagnosis than the long term (up to 19 years), in patients with aura than in those without aura, and in women than in men. In a subcohort of patients, the associations persisted after additional multivariable adjustment for body mass index and smoking. CONCLUSIONS: Migraine was associated with increased risks of myocardial infarction, ischaemic stroke, haemorrhagic stroke, venous thromboembolism, and atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter. Migraine may be an important risk factor for most cardiovascular diseases.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Adelborg, Kasper","Szépligeti, Szimonetta Komjáthiné","Holland-Bill, Louise","Ehrenstein, Vera","Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","Henderson, Victor W","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-237604"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"keyword":["Adult","Atrial Fibrillation epidemiology","Body Mass Index","Cardiovascular Diseases epidemiology","Cohort Studies","Comorbidity","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Heart Failure epidemiology","Humans","Incidence","Intracranial Hemorrhages epidemiology","Male","Middle Aged","Migraine Disorders complications","Myocardial Infarction epidemiology","Outcome Assessment Health Care","Peripheral Arterial Disease epidemiology","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Smoking epidemiology","Stroke epidemiology","Venous Thromboembolism epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"migraine and risk of cardiovascular diseases danish population based matched cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/167779988/bmj.k96.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-237604","identifier":[{"id":"85042744452","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29386181","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5791041","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-bda5dc78-5f60-40c3-a007-6a0ad5a5cc83"],"keyword":["Adult","Atrial Fibrillation/epidemiology","Body Mass Index","Cardiovascular Diseases/epidemiology","Cohort Studies","Comorbidity","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Heart Failure/epidemiology","Humans","Incidence","Intracranial Hemorrhages/epidemiology","Male","Middle Aged","Migraine Disorders/complications","Myocardial Infarction/epidemiology","Outcome Assessment (Health Care)","Peripheral Arterial Disease/epidemiology","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Smoking/epidemiology","Stroke/epidemiology","Venous Thromboembolism/epidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-88E46A820BD87D5ADA35EFB056D4193C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/167779988/bmj.k96.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"adelborgpau","last":"Adelborg","locid":"2744cdbf-8516-46f6-ad71-f99fee1afaa0","name":"Adelborg, Kasper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Szimonetta Komjáthiné","key":"szépligetipau","last":"Szépligeti","locid":"1cfc05bd-ca1a-4a09-8c9b-398a0cdff68d","name":"Szépligeti, Szimonetta Komjáthiné","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first"