{"abstract":"Denne video \"Takt og tone i tiden\" er en triggerfilm, skabt til kildebankemnet \"Kærlighed, køn og seksualitet\". Filmen kan anvendes som en igangsætter til at arbejde problemorienteret med kilder i historieundervisningen i udskolingen.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sørensen, Christina Louise","Peters, Rikke","Lauridsen, Poul Kjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-649343"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Børn og unge","Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Skoler fag og institutioner"],"level":"edu","oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kildebanken kærlighed køn og seksualitet triggerfilm til arbejde med historielabs kildebank","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tzsfkk5WA8U","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-649343","ids":["ucl-cc586d49-6624-4b8c-90a8-3e6da230c300"],"keyword":["Børn og unge","Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","Skoler, fag og institutioner"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","noi":["Local-1-1-9FB5D61A77683651F60DC82B01748C1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tzsfkk5WA8U","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Rektor, Rektor, Videncenter for Historie og Kulturformidling"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Louise","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c4715900-2e37-4a8f-9c8b-77690089c2c4","name":"Sørensen, Christina Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Louise Alberg","key":"peterspau","last":"Peters","locid":"c08a1671-9716-48a1-a1b9-2f07a47a57e9","name":"Peters, Rikke","name_org":"Peters, Rikke Louise Alberg","orcid":"0000-0003-0120-370X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul Kjær","key":"lauridsenppu","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"d50179d4-5a35-4a3c-b628-ad1543edeff8","name":"Lauridsen, Poul Kjær","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Nationalt Videnscenter for Historie- og Kulturformidling","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-cc586d49-6624-4b8c-90a8-3e6da230c300"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Kildebanken - Kærlighed, køn og seksualitet : Triggerfilm til arbejde med HistorieLabs Kildebank","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-649343","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Sea-ice ecosystems are among the most extensive of Earth’s habitats; yet its autotrophic and heterotrophic activities remain poorly constrained. We employed the in situ aquatic eddy-covariance (AEC) O2 flux method and laboratory incubation techniques (H14CO3−, [3H] thymidine and [3H] leucine) to assess productivity in Arctic sea-ice using different methods, in conditions ranging from land-fast ice during winter, to pack ice within the central Arctic Ocean during summer. Laboratory tracer measurements resolved rates of bacterial C demand of 0.003–0.166 mmol C m−2 day−1 and primary productivity rates of 0.008–0.125 mmol C m−2 day−1 for the different ice floes. Pack ice in the central Arctic Ocean was overall net autotrophic (0.002–0.063 mmol C m−2 day−1), whereas winter land-fast ice was net heterotrophic (− 0.155 mmol C m−2 day−1). AEC measurements resolved an uptake of O2 by the bottom-ice environment, from ~ − 2 mmol O2 m−2 day−1 under winter land-fast ice to~ − 6 mmol O2 m−2 day−1 under summer pack ice. Flux of O2-deplete meltwater and changes in water flow velocity masked potential biological-mediated activity. AEC estimates of primary productivity were only possible at one study location. Here, productivity rates of 1.3 ± 0.9 mmol O2 m−2 day−1, much larger than concurrent laboratory tracer estimates (0.03 mmol C m−2 day−1), indicate that ice algal production and its importance within the marine Arctic could be underestimated using traditional approaches. Given careful flux interpretation and with further development, the AEC technique represents a promising new tool for assessing oxygen dynamics and sea-ice productivity in ice-covered regions.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Attard, Karl M.","Søgaard, Dorte H.","Piontek, Judith","Lange, Benjamin A.","Katlein, Christian","Sørensen, Heidi L.","McGinnis, Daniel F.","Rovelli, Lorenzo","Rysgaard, Søren","Wenzhöfer, Frank","Glud, Ronnie N."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-023726"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Attard, Karl M."],"country":["Canada","Finland","Germany","Greenland","Japan","Switzerland"],"glorg":["Alfred Wegener Institute","All Global Affiliations","GEOMAR Helmholtz Centre for Ocean Research Kiel","Greenland Climate Research Centre","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Leibnitz Institute for Freshwater Ecology and Inland Fisheries","Leibniz-Institute of Freshwater Ecology and Inland Fisheries","Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology","Tokyo University of Marine Science and Technology","University of Geneva","University of Hamburg","University of Helsinki","University of Manitoba"],"keyword":["Bacterial production","Carbon cycling","Eddy covariance","Primary production","Sea ice"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oxygen fluxes beneath arctic land fast ice and pack ice towards estimates of ice productivity","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00300-018-2350-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-023726","identifier":[{"id":"85048370474","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-97e4804a-5cac-4d33-b05b-a972aea775f2","sdu-e0513e76-34fb-451b-939e-9d9810fcdcd8"],"keyword":["Bacterial production","Carbon cycling","Eddy-covariance","Primary production","Sea-ice"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-53B753BBDF98C7B7F9ECD2377F772B75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/143470028/Attard2018_Article_OxygenFluxesBeneathArcticLand_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00300-018-2350-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/134318444/10.1007_s00300_018_2350_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gl","key":"greenland climate research centre","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Climate Research Centre","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"helmholtz association of german research centres","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"geomar helmholtz centre for ocean research kiel","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"GEOMAR Helmholtz Centre for Ocean Research Kiel","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"university of hamburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hamburg","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"de","key":"alfred wegener institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","