{"abstract":"Tightened restrictions call for cleaner transportation fuels to minimize environmental and societal problems caused by the presence of sulfur in transportation fuels. This emphasizes the need for new and better catalysts in the field of hydrodesulfurization (HDS), which aims at removing the refractory sulfur from different petroleum streams mostly found in the form of the alkyl-substituted dibenzothiophenes (β-DBTs). In this work we demonstrate how a setup dedicated to testing minute amounts (nanogram) of well-defined catalytic systems in μ-reactors can be used in the gas-phase HDS of the model compounds DBT and 4,6-dimethyldibenzothiophene (4,6-DMDBT) and the reaction pathways revealed by time-of-flight mass spectrometry. Specifically, we investigate HDS of DBT and 4,6-DMDBT on mass-selected Pt nanoparticles and show that only the direct desulfurization products are formed.The setup is a means to bridge the gap between structural characterization of model catalysts and their related activity in the HDS of DBT and 4,6-DMDBT.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Ann-Louise N.","Bodin, Anders","Elkjær, Christian F.","Sørensen, Jakob Ejler","Kibsgaard, Jakob","Chorkendorff, Ib"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-377572"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Chorkendorff, Ib"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-HLT"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-HLT","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ambient pressure hydrodesulfurization of refractory sulfur compounds in highly sensitive μ reactor platform coupled to a time of flight mass spectrometer","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/197365681/Ambient_Pressure_Hydrodesulfurization_of_Refractory_Sulfur_Compounds_in_Highly_Sensitive_Reactor_Platform_Coupled_to_a_Time_of_Flight_Mass_Spectrometer.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-377572","identifier":[{"id":"85041236352","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f3f62563-b76b-4628-a98d-a897175bfd01"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6994C11CB9439FB4A054A65ED8BEBD2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/197365681/Ambient_Pressure_Hydrodesulfurization_of_Refractory_Sulfur_Compounds_in_Highly_Sensitive_Reactor_Platform_Coupled_to_a_Time_of_Flight_Mass_Spectrometer.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Surface Physics and Catalysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"topsoe","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-HLT","l3nl":"Haldor Topsoe","l3nn":"Topsoe","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Topsoe","namevar":["Haldor Topsoe AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-HLT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann-Louise N.","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"6889385e-988e-4467-b81b-b4581ee5a883","name":"Christoffersen, Ann-Louise N.","orcid":"0000-0002-6476-9439","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"bodinpau","last":"Bodin","locid":"9d327b0c-bdbc-4be0-8dd0-2c1e24164f39","name":"Bodin, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0904-3800","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian F.","key":"elkjærpau","last":"Elkjær","name":"Elkjær, Christian F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Ejler","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f89ae815-acb1-48d4-8756-1366692b516a","name":"Sørensen, Jakob Ejler","orcid":"0000-0001-8834-1616","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"kibsgaardpau","last":"Kibsgaard","locid":"d69dab5c-453b-4638-8bef-a4359b6a4ef2","name":"Kibsgaard, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-9219-816X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ib","key":"chorkendorffpau","last":"Chorkendorff","locid":"17d73156-a1b3-436c-ba6c-a8bfe5b2f5d6","name":"Chorkendorff, Ib","orcid":"0000-0003-2738-0325","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jpcc.7b11089","issn":["19327447","19327455"],"issn_org":["19327447"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","pages":"1699-1705","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Chemistry C","volume":"122"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041236352"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Haldor Topsoe","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f3f62563-b76b-4628-a98d-a897175bfd01"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Ambient Pressure Hydrodesulfurization of Refractory Sulfur Compounds in Highly Sensitive μ-Reactor Platform Coupled to a Time-of-Flight Mass Spectrometer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-377572","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Protein interacting with C-kinase 1 (PICK1) is a widely expressed scaffold protein known to interact via its PSD-95/discs-large/ZO-1 (PDZ)-domain with several membrane proteins including the dopamine (DA) transporter (DAT), the primary target for cocaine's reinforcing actions. Here, we establish the importance of PICK1 for behavioral effects observed after both acute and repeated administration of cocaine. In PICK1 knock-out (KO) mice, the acute locomotor response to a single injection of cocaine was markedly attenuated. Moreover, in support of a role for PICK1 in neuroadaptive changes induced by cocaine, we observed diminished cocaine intake in a self-administration paradigm. Reduced behavioral effects of cocaine were not associated with decreased striatal DAT distribution and most likely not caused by the ∼30% reduction in synaptosomal DA uptake observed in PICK1 KO mice. The PICK1 KO mice demonstrated preserved behavioral responses to DA receptor agonists supporting intact downstream DA receptor signaling. Unexpectedly, we found a prominent increase in striatal DA content and levels of striatal tyrosine hydroxylase (TH) in PICK1 KO mice. Chronoamperometric recordings showed enhanced DA release in PICK1 KO mice, consistent with increased striatal DA pools. Viral-mediated knock-down (KD) of PICK1 in cultured dopaminergic neurons increased TH expression, supporting a direct cellular effect of PICK1. In summary, in addition to demonstrating a key role of PICK1 in mediating behavioral effects of cocaine, our data reveal a so far unappreciated role of PICK1 in DA homeostasis that possibly involves negative regulation of striatal TH levels.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Jensen, Kathrine Louise","Sørensen, Gunnar","Dencker, Ditte","Owens, William Anthony","Rahbek-Clemmensen, Troels","Brett Lever, Michael","Runegaard, Annika H","Christensen, Nikolaj Riis","Weikop, Pia","Wörtwein, Gitta","Fink-Jensen, Anders","Madsen, Kenneth Lindegaard","Daws, Lynette","Gether, Ulrik","Rickhag, Mattias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-397481"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pick000000000001 deficient mice exhibit impaired response to cocaine and dysregulated dopamine homeostasis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1523/ENEURO.0422-17.2018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-397481","identifier":[{"id":"29911172","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6001137","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85050202309","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-06b1a5f5-313d-42ee-bd90-c4fa90cc4eb2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7C36EDAD83926FABB5F419361FAFF64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1523/ENEURO.0422-17.2018","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/208958092/PICK1_Deficient_Mice_Exhibit_Impaired_Response_to_Cocaine_and_Dysregulated_Dopamine_Homeostasis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Neuropharm and Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kathrine Louise","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d16cc237-89d