{"abstract":"AimTo assess the impact of head motion artefacts and an automated artefact-correction system on CBCT image quality andinterpretability for simulated diagnostic tasks.Material and MethodsA partially dentate human skull was mounted on a robot simulating four types of head movement (antero-posteriortranslation/APT, nodding/NOD, lateral rotation/ROT, and tremor/TRM), at three distances (0.75, 1.5, and 3 mm) basedon two movement patterns (skull returning/not returning to the initial position). Two diagnostic tasks were simulated:dental implant planning/IP, and detection of a periapical lesion/AP. Three CBCT units were used to examine the skullduring the movements and no-motion (control): Cranex 3Dx/CRA, Orthophos SL 3D/ORT, and the X1 without (X1wo)and with (X1wi) an automated motion artefact-correction system. Eighty-eight examinations were performed for eachdiagnostic task. Three observers, blinded to unit and movement, scored image quality: presence of stripe artefacts(present/absent), overall unsharpness (present/absent), and image interpretability (interpretable/non-interpretable).Kappa statistics assessed interobserver agreement, and descriptive statistics summarized the findings.ResultsInterobserver agreement for image interpretability was good (average kappa=0.68). Regarding IP, X1wi images wereinterpretable by all observers, while for the other units mainly the cases with TRM were non-interpretable. RegardingAP, besides TRM, some cases with APT, NOD, and ROT at 3 mm distance and the “not returning” pattern were also noninterpretablefor CRA, ORT, and X1wo. For X1wi, two observers scored 1.5 mm TRM and one observer scored 3 mm TRMas non-interpretable.ConclusionThe automated motion artefact-correction system significantly enhanced CBCT image quality and interpretability.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Spin-Neto, Rubens","Schropp, Lars","Matzen, Louise Hauge","Sørensen, T.S.","Wenzel, Ann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-138301"],"event":{"end":"2018-06-16","place":"Luzern, ch","start":"2018-06-13","title":"European Congress of DentoMaxilloFacial Radiology 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"automated motion artefact correction and the impact on cone beam computed tomography image quality and interpretability an ex vivo study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-138301","ids":["au-0f97d22d-35fa-48a8-9649-32b07e7093ed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B8F9D6BF9713F5CFB48499F9E634A45B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Radiology and Endodontics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rubens","key":"spinnetopau","last":"Spin-Neto","locid":"242a9551-55e4-4564-afdd-f51a3ad8947b","name":"Spin-Neto, Rubens","orcid":"0000-0002-9562-0610","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"schropppau","last":"Schropp","locid":"3ae0d2fd-2662-499f-8d5e-5246156d138f","name":"Schropp, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-4897-1554","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise Hauge","key":"matzenpau","last":"Matzen","locid":"6d2056e0-6343-4b7e-94d0-f3c63475edd4","name":"Matzen, Louise Hauge","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"T.S.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, T.S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann","key":"wenzelpau","last":"Wenzel","locid":"314cf777-b5eb-4d7c-a49e-cf3a36431859","name":"Wenzel, Ann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0f97d22d-35fa-48a8-9649-32b07e7093ed"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Automated Motion Artefact Correction and the Impact on Cone Beam Computed Tomography Image Quality and Interpretability. An Ex Vivo Study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-138301","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":16,"contributors":["Hartvig, Peter","Hjelmroth, Louise","Madsen, Lis","Nielsen, Magnus Gammelgaard","Schiøtt, Uffe Vincentz","Sørensen, Jakob","Ingvordsen, Kaspar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-242769"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"results from crop protection trials in minor crops in 000000002017","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/131007269/XIII_Results_from_crop_protection_trials_in_minor_crops_in_2017.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-242769","ids":["au-c6b4072e-52cf-4ae0-b98b-432ad3b00a9f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-413123681AE61B2C26D7D1D291DE38E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/131007269/XIII_Results_from_crop_protection_trials_in_minor_crops_in_2017.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"hartvigpau","last":"Hartvig","locid":"3b364808-01b2-4c22-9252-384824fca1ed","name":"Hartvig, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"hjelmrothpau","last":"Hjelmroth","locid":"93abfbbd-