{"abstract":"Decreased quality of life is described more often in hypothyroid patients, who are treated with a synthetic form of thyroxine (L-T4), than in euthyroid controls. A combination of L-T4 and a synthetic form of triiodothyronine (L-T3) has been suggested; however, previous meta-analyses on unselected patients did not find any effect. Recent studies demonstrate, that the overall hypothalamic-pituitary-thyroid-tissue homeostasis could be more complex than previously suggested. Polymorphisms in deiodinase and thyroid hormone transporter genes could theoretically explain, why a minor subgroup of hypothyroid patients seem to have an effect of L-T4/L-T3 combination therapy.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rath Sørensen, Anita","Brendstrup, Elisabeth","Titlestad, Ingrid Louise","Stæhr Jensen, Jens Ulrik","Hohwu Thomsen, Laura","Roberts, Nassim Bazeghi","Gjørup, Pia Holland","Shaker, Saher","Gundestrup, Svend","Wilcke, Torgny Rostrup","Weinreich, Ulla Møller","Marså, Kristoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-092985"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"behandlingsniveau og behandlingsstop ved benign lungesygdom","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://ugeskriftet.dk.auh.aub.aau.dk/videnskab/behandlingsniveau-og-behandlingsstop-ved-benign-lungesygdom","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-092985","ids":["aau-9415cd74-c202-40f3-83c9-559f820d5524"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EC2F66D4E8F1CA4EFBBF66EEE72B9E04"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Respiratory Diseases","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anita","key":"rathsørensenpau","last":"Rath Sørensen","name":"Rath Sørensen, Anita","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"brendstruppau","last":"Brendstrup","name":"Brendstrup, Elisabeth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid Louise","key":"titlestadpau","last":"Titlestad","name":"Titlestad, Ingrid Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ulrik","key":"stæhrjensenpau","last":"Stæhr Jensen","name":"Stæhr Jensen, Jens Ulrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"hohwuthomsenpau","last":"Hohwu Thomsen","name":"Hohwu Thomsen, Laura","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nassim Bazeghi","key":"robertspau","last":"Roberts","name":"Roberts, Nassim Bazeghi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia Holland","key":"gjøruppau","last":"Gjørup","name":"Gjørup, Pia Holland","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Saher","key":"shakerpau","last":"Shaker","name":"Shaker, Saher","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Svend","key":"gundestruppau","last":"Gundestrup","name":"Gundestrup, Svend","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Torgny Rostrup","key":"wilckepau","last":"Wilcke","name":"Wilcke, Torgny Rostrup","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulla Møller","key":"weinreichpau","last":"Weinreich","locid":"dd46b672-1843-46f2-8fdd-a338cf5c6621","name":"Weinreich, Ulla Møller","orcid":"0000-0003-1975-3654","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristoffer","key":"marsåpau","last":"Marså","name":"Marså, Kristoffer","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"2-6","paperid":"V04180270","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"180"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9415cd74-c202-40f3-83c9-559f820d5524"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Behandlingsniveau og behandlingsstop ved benign lungesygdom","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-092985","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To assess the impact of head motion artefacts and an automated artefact-correction system on cone beam CT (CBCT) image quality and interpretability for simulated diagnostic tasks. METHODS: A partially dentate human skull was mounted on a robot simulating four types of head movement (anteroposterior translation, nodding, lateral rotation, and tremor), at three distances (0.75, 1.5, and 3 mm) based on two movement patterns (skull returning/not returning to the initial position). Two diagnostic tasks were simulated: dental implant planning and detection of a periapical lesion. Three CBCT units were used to examine the skull during the movements and no-motion (control): Cranex 3Dx (CRA), Orthophos SL 3D (ORT), and X1 without (X1wo) and with (X1wi) an automated motion artefact-correction system. For each diagnostic task, 88 examinations were performed. Three observers, blinded to unit and movement, scored image quality: presence of stripe artefacts (present/absent), overall unsharpness (present/absent), and image interpretability (interpretable/non-interpretable). κ statistics assessed interobserver agreement, and descriptive statistics summarized the findings. RESULTS: Interobserver agreement for image interpretability was good (average κ = 0.68). Regarding dental implant planning, X1wiimages were interpretable by all observers, while for the other units mainly the cases with tremor were non-interpretable. Regarding detection of a periapical lesion, besides tremor, most of the 3 mm movements based on the \"not returning\" pattern were also non-interpretable for CRA, ORT, and X1wo. For X1wi, two observers scored 1.5 mm tremor and one observer scored 3 mm tremor as non-interpretable. CONCLUSIONS: The automated motion artefact-correction system significantly enhanced CBCT image quality and interpretability.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Spin-Neto, Rubens","Matzen, Louise Hauge","Schropp, Lars","Sørensen, Thomas S","Wenzel, Ann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-181210"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artifacts","CBCT scan","Computed tomography","Cone Beam Computed Tomography methods","Cone beam CT","Head Movements","Humans","Image quality","In Vitro Techniques","Models Anatomic","Motion artefacts","Patient movement","Radiographic Image Enhancement methods","Reduction","Simulation","Video observation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an ex vivo study of automated motion artefact correction and the impact on cone beam ct image quality and interpretability","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6196041/pdf/dmfr.20180013.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-181210","identifier":[{"id":"85049254166","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29537303","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6196041","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-5b08115b-76bc-43dc-8467-2474461da801"],"keyword":["Artifacts","CBCT SCAN","COMPUTED-TOMOGRAPHY","Cone beam CT","Cone-Beam Computed Tomography/methods","HEAD MOVEMENTS","Humans","Image quality","In Vitro Techniques","Models, Anatomic","Motion artefacts","Patient movement","REDUCTION","Radiographic Image Enhancement/methods","SIMULATION","TRACKING SYSTEM","VIDEO OBSERVATION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-330B7568D6824848B56439A79C08D70A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6196041/pdf/dmfr.20180013.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Radiology and Endodontics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rubens","key":"spinnetopau","last":"Spin-Neto","locid":"242a9551-55e4-4564-afdd-f51a3ad8947b","name":"Spin-Neto, Rubens","orcid":"0000-0002-9562-0610","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise H","key":"matzenpau","last":"Matzen","locid":"6d2056e0-6343-4b7e-94d0-f3c63475edd4","name":"Matzen, Louise Hauge","name_org":"Matzen, Louise H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars W","key":"schropppau","last":"Schropp","locid":"3ae0d2fd-2662-499f-8d5e-5246156d138f","name":"Schropp, Lars","name_org":"Schropp, Lars W","orcid":"0000-0003-4897-1554","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas S","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Thomas S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann","key":"wenzelpau","last":"Wenzel","locid":"314cf777-b5eb-4d7c-a49e-cf3a36431859","name":"Wenzel, Ann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29537303"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1259/dmfr.20180013","issn":["0250832X","0349490X"],"issn_org":["0250832X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Dentomaxillofacial Radiology","paperid":"20180013","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Dentomaxillofacial Radiology","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049254166"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5b08115b-76bc-43dc-8467-2474461da801"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"An ex vivo study of automated motion artefact correction and the impact on cone beam CT image quality and interpretability","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-181210","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Hyponatremia has recently been associated with subsequent cancer risk. This population-based nationwide study assessed whether the diagnosis of hyponatremia can predict a cancer diagnosis within most common cancers. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Using Danish medical registries, we identified 16,220 patients with a first-time diagnosis of hyponatremia, without a cancer diagnosis, from January 2006 through November 2013. We quantified the relative risk of a subsequent cancer diagnosis by standardized incidence ratios (SIRs), comparing observed cancer incidence among patients diagnosed with hyponatremia to that expected, based on national cancer incidence during that period. RESULTS: During 40,207 person-years of follow-up, we observed 1546 cancer diagnoses compared to 956 expected (SIR: 1.62; 95% confidence interval (CI), 1.54-1.70). The increase in risk of a cancer diagnosis following a hyponatremia diagnosis was most pronounced within 0-6 months of follow-up (SIR 4.16; 95% CI, 3.85-4.48) and in the younger age group; 0-29 years (SIR 8.71; 95% CI, 2.82-20.28), 30-49 years (SIR 3.16; 95% CI, 2.26-4.31), 50-69 years (SIR 2.29; 95% CI, 2.10-2.48) and 70 + years (SIR 1.35; 95% CI, 1.27-1.44). Within six months after a hyponatremia diagnosis, the SIRs increased 10-fold for cancers of the lung (SIR 17.14; 95% CI, 15.15-19.32), brain (SIR 13.52; 95% CI, 8.90-19.66) and liver (SIR 13.26; 95% CI, 7.57-21.53) and increased 5 to 10-fold for cancers of the pancreas (SIR 8.25; 95% CI, 5.72-11.53), esophagus (SIR 6.59; 95% CI, 3.15-12.12), kidney (SIR 6.36; 95% CI, 3.39-10.88), pharynx (SIR 6.15; 95% CI, 1.27-17.97) and non-Hodgkin lymphoma (SIR 6.10; 95% CI, 4.17-8.61). The rate increased across virtually all types of cancers, except melanoma and basal cell carcinomas. CONCLUSIONS: A diagnosis of hyponatremia may be a marker of occult neoplasms, especially cancers of the lung, brain, liver, pancreas, esophagus, kidney, pharynx and non-Hodgkin lymphoma. Hyponatremia may aid in early detection of cancer.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Holland-Bill, Louise","Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","Farkas, Dóra Körmendiné","Donskov, Frede","Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-211925"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnosis of hyponatremia and increased risk of a subsequent cancer diagnosis results from a nationwide population based cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85029604127","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-211925","identifier":[{"id":"85029604127","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28920509","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-90cfe188-2407-499c-84e1-79a3bd9e39d6"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F30228003D85D61E733AB22E1190191C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anaesthesiology and Operation, Intensive care","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"hollandbillpau","last":"Holland-Bill","locid":"578d785d-8e78-4933-9ba4-3db0ec2b4c29","name":"Holland-Bill, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Fynbo","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"b1104ec4-1322-428f-af8f-7771361930bb","name":"Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","orcid":"0000-0002-0727-953X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dóra Körmendiné","key":"farkaspau","last":"Farkas","locid":"573f7202-6799-4977-bf11-f1e017ac21a2","name":"Farkas, Dóra Körmendiné","orcid":"0000-0002-8577-048X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frede","key":"donskovpau","last":"Donskov","locid":"51fdc715-1b4d-4639-9b26-5dbf474dbec7","name":"Donskov, Frede","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Otto L","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"303ebe86-6861-4b19-b4d7-6bda0526b27e","name":"Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","name_org":"Jørgensen, Jens Otto L","orcid":"0000-0001-7408-1526","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28920509"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2017.1378430","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"522-527","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029604127"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-90cfe188-2407-499c-84e1-79a3bd9e39d6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Diagnosis of hyponatremia and increased risk of a subsequent cancer diagnosis : results from a nationwide population-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-211925","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Global mean sea level is an integral of changes occurring in the climate system in response to unforced climate variability as well as natural and anthropogenic forcing factors. Its temporal evolution allows changes (e.g., acceleration) to be detected in one or more components. Study of the sea-level budget provides constraints on missing or poorly known contributions, such as the unsurveyed deep ocean or the still uncertain land water component. In the context of the World Climate Research Programme Grand Challenge entitled \"Regional Sea Level and Coastal Impacts\", an international effort involving the sea-level community worldwide has been recently initiated with the objective of assessing the various datasets used to estimate components of the sea-level budget during the altimetry era (1993 to present). These datasets are based on the combination of a broad range of space-based and in situ observations, model estimates, and algorithms. Evaluating their quality, quantifying uncertainties and identifying sources of discrepancies between component estimates is extremely useful for various applications in climate research. This effort involves several tens of scientists from about 50 research teams/institutions worldwide (www.wcrp-climate.org/grand-challenges/gc-sea-level, last access: 22 August 2018). The results presented in this paper are a synthesis of the first assessment performed during 2017–2018. We present estimates of the altimetry-based global mean sea level (average rate of 3.1±0.3mmyr−1 and acceleration of 0.1mmyr−2 over 1993–present), as well as of the different components of the sea-level budget (http://doi.org/10.17882/54854, last access: 22 August 2018). We further examine closure of the sea-level budget, comparing the observed global mean sea level with the sum of components. Ocean thermal expansion, glaciers, Greenland and Antarctica contribute 42%, 21%, 15% and 8% to the global mean sea level over the 1993–present period. We also study the sea-level budget over 2005–present, using GRACE-based ocean mass estimates instead of the sum of individual mass components. Our results demonstrate that the global mean sea level can be closed to within 0.3mmyr−1 (1σ). Substantial uncertainty remains for the land water storage component, as shown when examining individual mass contributions to sea level.","author_count":91,"contributors":["Group, WCRP Global Sea Level Budget","Cazenave, Anny","Meyssignac, Benoit","Ablain, Michael","Balmaseda, Magdalena","Bamber, Jonathan","Barletta, Valentina Roberta","Beckley, Brian","Benveniste, Jérôme","Berthier, Etienne","Blazquez, Alejandro","Boyer, Tim","Caceres, Denise","Chambers, Don P.","Champollion, Nicolas","Chao, Ben","Chen, Jianli","Cheng, Lijing","Church, John A.","Chuter, Stephen","Cogley, J. Graham","Dangendorf, Soenke","Desbruyères, Damien","Döll, Petra","Domingues, Catia","Falk, Ulrike","Famiglietti, James","Fenoglio-Marc, Luciana","Forsberg, René","Galassi, Gaia","Gardner, Alex","Groh, Andreas","Hamlington, Benjamin","Hogg, Anna","Horwath, Martin","Humphrey, Vincent","Husson, Laurent","Ishii, Masayoshi","Jaeggi, Adrian","Jevrejeva, Svetlana","Johnson, Gregory","Kolodziejczyk, Nicolas","Kusche, Jürgen","Lambeck, Kurt","Landerer, Felix","Leclercq, Paul","Legresy, Benoit","Leuliette, Eric","Llovel, William","Longuevergne, Laurent","Loomis, Bryant D.","Luthcke, Scott B","Marcos, Marta","Marzeion, Ben","Merchant, Chris","Merrifield, Mark","Milne, Glenn","Mitchum, Gary","Mohajerani, Yara","Monier, Maeva","Monselesan, Didier","Nerem, Steve","Palanisamy, Hindumathi","Paul, Frank","Pérez, Begona","Piecuch, Christopher G.","Ponte, Rui M.","Purkey, Sarah G.","Reager, John T.","Rietbroek, Roelof","Rignot, Eric","Riva, Riccardo","Roemmich, Dean H.","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Sasgen, Ingo","Schram, E.J.O.","Seneviratne, Sonia I.","Shum, C.K.","Spada, Giorgio","Stammer, Detlef","van de Wal, Roderic","Velicogna, Isabella","von Schuckmann, Karina","Wada, Yoshihide","Wang, Yiguo","Watson, Christopher S.","Wiese, David","Wijffels, Susan","Westaway, Richard","Woppelmann, Guy","Wouters, Bert"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-341163"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Cazenave, Anny"],"country":["Australia","Canada","China","France","Germany","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Switzerland","Taiwan","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Academia Sinica - Institute of Earth Sciences","Aerodyne Research, Inc.","Alfred Wegener Institute - Helmholtz Centre for Polar and Marine Research","All Global Affiliations","Australian National University","Bjerknes Centre for Climate Research","CSIRO","California Institute of Technology","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Collecte Localisation Satellites","Delft University of Technology","European Centre for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts","European Space Agency - ESA","Goethe University Frankfurt","Institut français de recherche pour l'exploitation de la mer","Laboratoire d’Études en Géophysique et Océanographie Spatiales","Laboratory for Ocean Physics and Satellite Remote Sensing","Mercator Océan","Meteorological Research Institute","NASA Goddard Space Flight Center","National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration","National Oceanography Centre","Ohio State University","Old Dominion University","Puertos del Estados","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich","Technische Universität Dresden","Trent University","Universitat de les Illes Balears","University of Bern","University of Bonn","University of Bremen","University of Bristol","University of California at Irvine","University of California at San Diego","University of Colorado Boulder","University of Grenoble","University of Hamburg","University of Leeds","University of New South Wales","University of Oslo","University of Ottawa","University o