{"abstract":"In this review, we provide an overview of the current knowledge on the role of different classes of non-coding RNAs for islet and β-cell development, maturation and function. MicroRNAs (miRNAs), a prominent class of small RNAs, have been investigated for more than two decades and patterns of the roles of different miRNAs in pancreatic fetal development, islet and β-cell maturation and function are now emerging. Specific miRNAs are dynamically regulated throughout the period of pancreas development, during islet and β-cell differentiation as well as in the perinatal period, where a burst of β-cell replication takes place. The role of long non-coding RNAs (lncRNA) in islet and β-cells is less investigated than for miRNAs, but knowledge is increasing rapidly. The advent of ultra-deep RNA sequencing has enabled the identification of highly islet- or β-cell-selective lncRNA transcripts expressed at low levels. Their roles in islet cells are currently only characterized for a few of these lncRNAs, and these are often associated with β-cell super-enhancers and regulate neighboring gene activity. Moreover, ncRNAs present in imprinted regions are involved in pancreas development and β-cell function. Altogether, these observations support significant and important actions of ncRNAs in β-cell development and function.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wong, Wilson W.K.","Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Joglekar, Mugdha","Hardikar, Anandwardhan Awadhoot","Dalgaard, Louise Torp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-562112"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sydney"],"keyword":["CELL","Circular RNAs","Fetal Development","Islets of Langerhans","Long non coding RNAs","Pancreas","microRNA","non coding RNAs","small nucleolar RNAs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non coding rna in pancreas and β cell development","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ncrna4040041","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-562112","identifier":[{"id":"85058942934","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-5bf4ec50-8881-49a0-a743-eea502bfd838"],"keyword":["circular RNAs","fetal development","islets of Langerhans","long intergenic non-coding RNAs","long non-coding RNAs","microRNA","non-coding RNAs","pancreas","piwi associated RNAs","small nucleolar RNAs","α-cell","β-cell"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-774E25491461A836D97E4E07842FD7BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ncrna4040041","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/63757258/Non_Coding_RNA_in_Pancreas_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Sydney","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Molecular and Medical Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Wilson W.K.","key":"wongpau","last":"Wong","name":"Wong, Wilson W.K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","fi