{"abstract":"Key points and policy recommendations from a joint seminar hosted by the Danish Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Danish Institute for International Studies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Funder, Mikkel","Fugl, Jens","Sørensen, Louise Kronborg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-301142"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Climate change","Displacement","Fragility","Migration"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-DIIS"],"OT":["Udenrigsministeriet"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-DIIS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"climate change migration and fragility towards evidence based policy and practice","src":["diis"],"src-code":["DI-GV-DIIS"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.diis.dk/ws/files/1233296/2016_Climate_change_seminar_summary_report.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-301142","ids":["diis-593842a9-9f04-48d8-8f25-44940c59bcca"],"keyword":["Climate change","Displacement","Fragility","Migration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F78A18B911FD5C6B9A41AC1918F84D6F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.diis.dk/ws/files/1233296/2016_Climate_change_seminar_summary_report.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"diis danish institute for international studies","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-DIIS","l3nn":"DIIS Danish Institute for International Studies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DIIS Danish Institute for International Studies","namevar":["Danish Institute for International Studies, Natural Resources and Development"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-DIIS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Udenrigsministeriet"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"funderpau","last":"Funder","locid":"96c82c5f-9fb1-436b-86b2-697ee89c9cab","name":"Funder, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-3808-919X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"fuglpau","last":"Fugl","name":"Fugl, Jens","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Kronborg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Louise Kronborg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"4","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"Udenrigsministeriet, Danida","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["diis-593842a9-9f04-48d8-8f25-44940c59bcca"],"src":["DIIS Danish Institute for International Studies"],"title":"Climate Change, Migration and Fragility : Towards Evidence-based Policy and Practice","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-301142","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Thirteen years of GRACE data provide an excellent picture of the current mass changes of Greenland and Antarctica, with mass loss in the GRACE period 2002–2015 amounting to 265 ± 25 GT/year for Greenland (including peripheral ice caps), and 95 ± 50 GT/year for Antarctica, corresponding to 0.72 and 0.26 mm/year average global sea level change. A significant acceleration in mass loss rate is found, especially for Antarctica, while Greenland mass loss, after a corresponding acceleration period, and a record mass loss in the summer of 2012, has seen a slight decrease in short-term mass loss trend. The yearly mass balance estimates, based on point mass inversion methods, have relatively large errors, both due to uncertainties in the glacial isostatic adjustment processes, especially for Antarctica, leakage from unmodelled ocean mass changes, and (for Greenland) difficulties in separating mass signals from the Greenland ice sheet and the adjacent Canadian ice caps. The limited resolution of GRACE affects the uncertainty of total mass loss to a smaller degree; we illustrate the “real” sources of mass changes by including satellite altimetry elevation change results in a joint inversion with GRACE, showing that mass change occurs primarily associated with major outlet glaciers, as well as a narrow coastal band. For Antarctica, the primary changes are associated with the major outlet glaciers in West Antarctica (Pine Island and Thwaites Glacier systems), as well as on the Antarctic Peninsula, where major glacier accelerations have been observed after the 2002 collapse of the Larsen B Ice Shelf.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Forsberg, René","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-309485"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CryoSat","Envisat","GRACE","Greenland Ice Sheet"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greenland and antarctica ice sheet mass changes and effects on global sea level","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128885687/icesheets_sealevel_issi_v3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-309485","identifier":[{"id":"85009278907","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-103f839f-fa22-4fb1-ae81-4c439c41cc43"],"keyword":["Antarctica mass loss","CryoSat","Envisat","GRACE","Greenland ice sheet"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DAD493F99D7EE3E0FAD31DA0547F111C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128885687/icesheets_sealevel_issi_v3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10712-016-9398-7","issn":["01693298","15730956"],"issn_org":["01693298"],"journal":"Surveys in Geophysics","pages":"89-104","publisher":"Springer Netherlands","status":"p","title":"Surveys in Geophysics","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009278907"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-103f839f-fa22-4fb1-ae81-4c439c41cc43"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Greenland and Antarctica Ice Sheet Mass Changes and Effects on Global Sea Level","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309485","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Long-term observations of surface elevation change of the Greenland ice sheet (GrIS) is of utmost importance when assessing the state of the ice sheet. Satellite radar altimetry offers a long time series of data over the GrIS, starting with ERS-1 in 1991. ESA's Cryosat-2 mission, launched in 2010, provides an invaluable radar altimetry dataset for monitoring the current changes of the ice sheets due to its dense spatial and temporal coverage of these areas. Here, we investigate the effects of including different parameters which describe the shape of the return radar waveform (waveform parameters) in the elevation change algorithm, to correct for temporal changes in the ratio between surface- and volume-scatter in Cryosat-2 observations. We present elevation and volume changes for the Greenland ice sheet in the period from 2010 until 2014. The waveform parameters considered here are the backscatter coefficient, and the leading edge width, which are both available in the ESA Cryosat-2 Level-2i data product. Investigations into relocation of radar reflection points are also included. Inter-comparison of the Cryosat-2 derived elevation changes with those derived from Operation IceBridge laser data suggests waveform parameters to be applicable for correcting for changes in volume scattering. The best results in the Synthetic Aperture Radar Interferometric mode area of the GrIS are found when applying only the backscatter correction, whereas the best result in the Low Resolution Mode area is obtained by only applying a leading edge width correction. Using this approach to correct for the scattering properties, a volume loss of −292±38 km3 yr −1 is found for the GrIS for the time span November 2010 until November 2014. The inclusion of waveform parameter corrections and improved relocation for the GrIS, helps to reconcile the satellite-derived elevation changes with those observed by Operation IceBridge. However, the bias of temporal changes in the scattering horizons of Cryosat-2 is not entirely removed and suggests that future improvements could be made by including climate data and/or additional waveform parameters to make additional corrections in the Cryosat-2 radar altimetry.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343254"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CryoSat 2","Greenland Ice Sheet","Radar altimetry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"implications of changing scattering properties on greenland ice sheet volume change from cryosat 000000000002 altimetry","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85008211293","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343254","identifier":[{"id":"85008211293","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-817ef1cf-cc4d-4c40-ab64-0acf8ace2bcc"],"keyword":["Cryosat-2","Cryospheric changes","Greenland ice sheet","Radar altimetry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6141807EA8459C49F763BE60F51D3D59"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.rse.2016.12.012","issn":["00344257"],"journal":"Remote Sensing of Environment","pages":"207-216","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Remote Sensing of Environment","volume":"190"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85008211293"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-817ef1cf-cc4d-4c40-ab64-0acf8ace2bcc"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Implications of changing scattering properties on Greenland ice sheet volume change from Cryosat-2 altimetry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343254","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Beslutninger om at anbringe et barn uden for hjemmet eller ej er nogle af de kommunale beslutninger, som har de allerstørste konsekvenser. Både her og nu og på længere sigt. Og både for barnet, forældre og netværk – og for samfundet. Derfor er der brug for at vide noget mere om, hvordan beslutningerne træffes. Hvilke forhold spiller ind, hvilken vægt tillægges de? Af hvem, hvordan og hvorfor? Det er denne form for viden, denne antologi giver indblik i. Den er relevant for socialrådgivere, ledere og andre, der arbejder på området, og er rettet mod undervisningen på grunduddannelsen til socialrådgiver og mod de forskellige diplommaster- og kandidatuddannelser på velfærdsområdet, men den kan også være relevant på andre uddannelser. Antologien er delt ind i to overordnede dele. Del I – som omfatter kapitlerne 1 til 5 – handler om rammerne omkring de konkrete beslutninger, dvs. om kommunale strukturer, strategier, udviklingen på området i tal og det retlige grundlag. Del II – som omfatter kapitlerne 6 til 10 – handler om de konkrete beslutninger i praksis, dvs. hvordan træffer sagsbehandlere, ledere og andre aktører beslutninger i praksis. Kapitlerne er mere indgående præsenteret i kapitel 1. Bogens ti kapitler kan læses for sig eller indgå som et mere samlet hele. Kapitlerne belyser tal, regler og praksis på området, men de kan også bruges til at belyse de forskellige måder, disse forhold kan undersøges på. Centrale begreber er forklaret i oversigten til sidst, hvor man også kan finde en liste over de anvendte kilder, et stikordsregister og en forfatteroversigt. Der er ikke brugt slutnoter, men i et vist omfang er begreber og supplerende oplysninger givet i fodnoter i de enkelte kapitler.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Svendsen, Idamarie Leth","Ebsen, Frank Cloyd","Bengtsson, Tea Torbenfeldt","Ejrnæs, Mette","Gørtz, Mette","Laugesen, Laura Louise","Thiele, Sarah","Loehr, Gry Malling","Sørensen, Tove Holmgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-387797"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Afmagt","Anbringelse","Beslutninger","Børn og unge","Kvantitative data","Magt","Signs of Safety","Tid","kvalitative data","retsgrundlag","skalering"],"level":"sci","oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"den svære beslutning en antologi om beslutninger om anbringelse af børn og unge hvornår hvorfor og hvordan","src":["kp"],"src-code":["DI-UC-KP"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/41377986/Den_Sv_re_Beslutning_2017._Print_kvalitet.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-387797","ids":["kp-55fcb308-252b-4931-b92a-233ed7bb36b8"],"keyword":["Børn og unge","Signs of Safety","afmagt","anbringelse","beslutninger","kommunale politikker","kvalitative data","kvantitative data","magt","retsgrundlag","skalering","tid"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-1E8A543A2AF0298391FF99E358D5DC6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/41377986/Den_Sv_re_Beslutning_2017._Print_kvalitet.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for pædagogiske og samfundsfaglige uddannelser-Dekan, Socialrådgiveruddannelsen 4","Socialt Arbejde - Institut for Socialrådgiveruddannelse","Socialt Arbejde - Institut for Socialrådgiveruddannelse, Udsathed blandt børn, unge og familier"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Idamarie Leth","key":"svendsenped","last":"Svendsen","locid":"8e4aa626-1aa8-4645-a7a4-9bc6c5f66ba0","name":"Svendsen, Idamarie Leth","orcid":"0000-0003-0799-8590","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank Cloyd","key":"ebsenpau","last":"Ebsen","locid":"50924a42-ec83-4a2f-8491-1624ed4bc550","name":"Ebsen, Frank Cloyd","orcid":"0000-0003-0279-4169","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tea Torbenfeldt","key":"bengtssonpau","last":"Bengtsson","name":"Bengtsson, Tea Torbenfeldt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"ejrnæspau","last":"Ejrnæs","name":"Ejrnæs, Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"gørtzpau","last":"Gørtz","name":"Gørtz, Mette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura Louise","key":"laugesenpau","last":"Laugesen","name":"Laugesen, Laura Louise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"thielepau","last":"Thiele","name":"Thiele, Sarah","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gry Malling","key":"loehrpau","last":"Loehr","name":"Loehr, Gry Malling","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tove Holmgaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Tove Holmgaard","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["13977725"],"issn":["13977725"],"pages":"248","place":"København","publisher":"Professionshøjskolen Metropol","series":"Skriftserien Socialt Arbejde","status":"p","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-55fcb308-252b-4931-b92a-233ed7bb36b8"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Den svære beslutning : En antologi om beslutninger om anbringelse af børn og unge - hvornår, hvorfor og hvordan","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-387797","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In humans, biofilm is a well-known cause of delayed healing and low-grade inflammation of chronic wounds. In horses, biofilm formation in wounds has been studied to a very limited degree. The objective of this study was thus to investigate the occurrence of biofilm in equine experimental wounds healing by secondary intention. Tissue biopsies from non-contaminated, experimental excisional shoulder and limb wounds were obtained on day 1–2, day 7–10 and day 14–15 post-wounding. Limb wounds were either un-bandaged or bandaged to induce exuberant granulation tissue (EGT) formation and thereby impaired healing. Presence of biofilm in tissue biopsies was assessed by peptide nucleic acid fluorescence in situ hybridization (PNA FISH) and confocal laser scanning microscopy (CLSM). Bandaged limb wounds developed EGT and displayed delayed healing, while shoulder and un-bandaged limb wounds healed normally. Biofilm was detected in limb wounds only. At day 14–15 biofilm was significantly more prevalent in bandaged limb wounds than in un-bandaged limb wounds (P = 0.003). Further, bandaged limb wounds had a statistically significant increase in biofilm burden from day 7–10 to day 14–15 (P = 0.009). The finding that biofilm was most prevalent in bandaged limb wounds with EGT formation suggests that biofilm may be linked to delayed wound healing in horses, as has been observed in humans. The inability to clear bacteria could be related to hypoxia and low-grade inflammation in the EGT, but the interaction between biofilm forming bacteria and wound healing in horses needs further elucidation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Elin Lisby Kastbjerg","Bay, Lene","Bjarnsholt, Thomas","Bundgaard, Louise","Sørensen, Mette Aamand","Jacobsen, Stine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-512245"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the occurrence of biofilm in an equine experimental wound model of healing by secondary intention","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-512245","identifier":[{"id":"85018725563","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28532812","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c70d7b53-0532-40d9-8925-331d41e79dd4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B7454493D24F34A9F981692CBE303199"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Section for Medicine and Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Elin Lisby Kastbjerg","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"f9bc7815-bf97-4662-90d5-a74dcb6c5dbb","name":"Jørgensen, Elin Lisby Kastbjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-4314-2602","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"baypau","last":"Bay","locid":"22f49c41-e569-43c4-8978-94bc9e411869","name":"Bay, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-4164-5900","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"bjarnsholtpau","last":"Bjarnsholt","locid":"cb3ccb7d-0415-40e5-9bba-c9bc26b6316d","name":"Bjarnsholt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-8003-7414","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"bundgaardpau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"fac2f738-731c-4ca5-9369-45d6f4486fe2","name":"Bundgaard, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-0396-883X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Aamand","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c3ce4ae2-7fda-40ef-8fa7-ff09dc2da244","name":"Sørensen, Mette Aamand","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"f3957428-a0cc-46ad-a05c-b85ca7d03e9e","name":"Jacobsen, Stine","orcid":"0000-0002-2380-4576","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28532812"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vetmic.2017.03.011","issn":["03781135","18732542"],"issn_org":["03781135"],"journal":"Veterinary Microbiology","pages":"90-95","status":"p","title":"Veterinary Microbiology","volume":"204"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018725563"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c70d7b53-0532-40d9-8925-331d41e79dd4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The occurrence of biofilm in an equine experimental wound model of healing by secondary intention","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-512245","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: High-protein diets increase weight loss (WL) during energy restriction; therefore, it has been suggested that additional protein intake may improve weight maintenance (WM) after WL.Objective: We investigated the effect of protein supplements from either whey with or without calcium or soy on WM success after WL compared with that of a control.Design: In a randomized, controlled, double-blinded trial, 220 participants aged 18-60 y with body mass index (in kg/m(2)) from 27.6 to 40.4 were included. The study was initiated with an 8-wk WL period followed by a 24-wk WM period. During WM, participants consumed the following isocaloric supplements (45-48 g/d): whey and calcium (whey+), whey, soy, or maltodextrin (control). Data were collected at baseline, before WM, and after WM (weeks 0, 8, and 32, respectively) and included body composition, blood biochemistry, and blood pressure. Meal tests were performed to investigate diet-induced-thermogenesis (DIT) and appetite sensation. Compliance was tested by 24-h urinary nitrogen excretion.Results: A total of 151 participants completed the WM period. The control and 3 protein supplements did not result in different mean ± SD weight regains (whey+: 2.19 ± 4.6 kg; whey: 2.01 ± 4.6 kg; soy: 1.76 ± 4.7 kg; and control: 2.23 ± 3.8 kg; P = 0.96), fat mass regains (whey+: 0.46 ± 4.5 kg; whey: 0.11 ± 4.1 kg; soy: 0.15 ± 4.1 kg; and control: 0.54 ± 3.3 kg; P = 0.96), or improvements in lean body mass (whey+: 1.87 ± 1.7 kg; whey: 1.94 ± 1.3 kg; soy: 1.58 ± 1.4 kg; and control: 1.74 ± 1.4 kg; P = 0.50) during WM. Changes in blood pressure and blood biochemistry were not different between groups. Compared with the control, protein supplementation resulted in higher DIT (∼30 kJ/2.5 h) and resting energy expenditure (243 kJ/d) and an anorexigenic appetite-sensation profile.Conclusion: Protein supplementation does not result in improved WM success, or blood biochemistry after WL compared with the effects of normal dietary protein intake (0.8-1.0 g · kg(-1) · d(-1)). This trial was registered at clinicaltrials.gov as NCT01561131.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kjølbæk, Louise","Sørensen, Lone Brinkmann","Søndertoft, Nadja Buus","Rasmussen, Carrie Klestrup","Lorenzen, Janne Kunchel","Serena, Anja","Astrup, Arne","Larsen, Lesli Hingstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-534491"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["BMI","Calcium","Fat mass","Lean body mass","Protein","Soy","Weight loss","Weight maintenance","Whey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protein supplements after weight loss do not improve weight maintenance compared with recommended dietary protein intake despite beneficial effects on appetite sensation and energy expenditure a randomized controlled double blinded trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-534491","identifier":[{"id":"28679554","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85026669890","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ec4676e5-8a61-4b2a-98ca-54e264f60aa0"],"keyword":["BMI","Calcium","Fat mass","Lean body mass","Protein","Soy","Weight loss","Weight maintenance","Whey"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9FDB50191BC1D308E63B0E9E58A19BCB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"kjølbækpau","last":"Kjølbæk","locid":"704b196a-527d-4a0b-9a32-7dcdfdb8a3fd","name":"Kjølbæk, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-4310-9332","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lone Brinkmann","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"9940bf35-5cfb-40a1-af6a-5d0c58cf6163","name":"Sørensen, Lone Brinkmann","orcid":"0000-0002-8991-695X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Nadja Buus","key":"søndertoftpau","last":"Søndertoft","name":"Søndertoft, Nadja Buus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carrie Klestrup","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"8e7e5bf6-1349-439f-a417-090e4a4dc631","name":"Rasmussen, Carrie Klestrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janne Kunchel","key":"lorenzenpau","last":"Lorenzen","locid":"d8755162-ea5d-46be-b486-15f75a00b42b","name":"Lorenzen, Janne Kunchel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anja","key":"serenapau","last":"Serena","name":"Serena, Anja","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"5d943631-c9fc-4b63-8aaa-263ba4248735","name":"Astrup, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-8968-8996","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lesli Hingstrup","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cf1fc793-3fd4-4dca-ab8e-ee3ed914ec04","name":"Larsen, Lesli Hingstrup","orcid":"0000-0001-8827-7992","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28679554"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3945/ajcn.115.129528","issn":["00029165","19383207"],"issn_org":["00029165"],"issue":"2","journal":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","pages":"684-697","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","volume":"106"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026669890"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ec4676e5-8a61-4b2a-98ca-54e264f60aa0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Protein supplements after weight loss do not improve weight maintenance compared with recommended dietary protein intake despite beneficial effects on appetite sensation and energy expenditure : a randomized, controlled, double-blinded trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-534491","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Serial measurements of high-sensitivity troponin are used to rule out acute myocardial infarction (AMI) with an assay specific cutoff at the 99th percentile. Here, we evaluated the performance of a single admission troponin with a lower cutoff combined with a low risk electrocardiogram (ECG) to rule out AMI. METHODS: Troponin I measured with a high-sensitivity assay (hs-TnI) was determined at admission in 1040 patients presenting with suspected AMI (BACC study). To rule out AMI we calculated the negative predictive value (NPV) utilizing the optimal hs-TnI cutoff combined with a low risk ECG. The results were validated in 3566 patients with suspected AMI [2-h Accelerated Diagnostic Protocol to Assess Patients With Chest Pain Symptoms Using Contemporary Troponins as the Only Biomarker (ADAPT) studies]. Patients were followed for 6 or 12 months. RESULTS: 184 of all patients were diagnosed with AMI. An hs-TnI cutoff of 3 ng/L resulted in a NPV of 99.3% (CI 97.3-100.0), ruling out 35% of all non-AMI patients. Adding the information of a low riskECGresulted in a 100% (CI 97.5-100.0) NPV (28% ruled out). The 2 validation cohorts replicated the high NPV of this approach. The follow-up mortality in the ruled out population was low (0 deaths in BACC and Stenocardia, 1 death in ADAPT). CONCLUSIONS: A single hs-TnI measurement on admission combined with a low risk ECG appears to rule out AMI safely without need for serial troponin testing. Trial Registration: www.clinicaltrials.gov (NCT02355457).","author_count":23,"contributors":["Neumann, Johannes Tobias","Sörensen, Nils Arne","Ojeda, Francisco","Schwemer, Tjark","Lehmacher, Jonas","Gönner, Saskia","Jarsetz, Nikolas","Keller, Till","Schaefer, Sarina","Renné, Thomas","Landmesser, Ulf","Clemmensen, Peter","Makarova, Nataliya","Schnabel, Renate B.","Zeller, Tanja","Karakas, Mahir","Pickering, John W.","Than, Martin","Parsonage, William","Greenslade, Jaimi","Cullen, Louise","Westermann, Dirk","Blankenberg, Stefan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-626632"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Neumann, Johannes Tobias"],"country":["Australia","Germany","New Zealand","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Christchurch Hospital","Goethe University Frankfurt","Karolinska Institute","Partner Site Hamburg/Kiel/Lübeck","Royal Brisbane and Women’s Hospital","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immediate rule out of acute myocardial infarction using electrocardiogram and baseline high sensitivity troponin i","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85008472877","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-626632","identifier":[{"id":"85008472877","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27903616","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-ba568a75-9cfe-40e6-9c10-61be41836609"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE32016075ADD721779594FDD91F8043"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university medical center hamburg eppendorf","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"partner site hamburg kiel lübeck","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Partner Site Hamburg/Kiel/Lübeck","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"goethe university frankfurt","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Goethe University Frankfurt","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"karolinska institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institute","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"charité university medicine berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité - University Medicine Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS – Nykøbing Falster Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"nz","key":"christchurch hospital","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Christchurch Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"au","key":"royal brisbane and women s hospital","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Royal Brisbane and Women’s Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johannes Tobias","key":"neumannpau","last":"Neumann","name":"Neumann, Johannes Tobias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils Arne","key":"sörensenpau","last":"Sörensen","name":"Sörensen, Nils Arne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Francisco","key":"ojedapau","last":"Ojeda","name":"Ojeda, Francisco","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tjark","key":"schwemerpau","last":"Schwemer","name":"Schwemer, Tjark","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"lehmacherpau","last":"Lehmacher","name":"Lehmacher, Jonas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Saskia","key":"gönnerpau","last":"Gönner","name":"Gönner, Saskia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolas","key":"jarsetzpau","last":"Jarsetz","name":"Jarsetz, N