{"abstract":"Background: This review focuses on the treatment of pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) with selexipag and compares its drug-related therapeutic effects with those of prostacyclin analogues. Methods: We searched the relevant literature and summarized the current clinical trials concerning selexipag and PAH. Results: With only few cases per million, PAH is a rare disease, but when untreated it can be life-threatening. PAH is linked to elevated levels of endothelin (ET-1) and decreased levels of nitric oxide (NO) and prostacyclin (PGI 2 ). PAH-specific therapeutic approaches concentrate on these characteristics with drugs targeting the endo-thelin-receptor (e.g. bosentan), phosphodiesterase-5 (e.g. sildenafil) or the prostacyclin-receptor (e.g. treprostinil). Recently, the new drug selexipag acting as a non-prostanoid IP 2 -receptor agonist has been approved for PAH therapy. The active form of selexipag (ACT-333679) was designed by the help of a medicinal chemistry program and it was further modified by replacing the terminal carboxyl group with an N-acylsulfonamide group to form the more stable oral drug, selexipag. Selexipag has a high selectivity for the IP 2 -receptor and differs from conventional prostacyclin analogues in its chemical structure. In the GRIPHON trial selexipag was demonstrated to significantly improve the primary composite endpoint of death or complications related to PAH (hazard ratio 0.6, 99% confidence interval, 0.46 to 0.78; P < 0.001) as well as exercise capacity in the form of the 6-minute walk distance (12.0 m treatment effect, 99% confidence interval, 1 to 24; P = 0.003). However, no significant reduction in all-cause mortality was achieved. Selexipag has also shown promising results in combination therapy with phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors (PDE-5i) and/or endothelin receptor antagonists (ERA). The most common adverse effects (AEs), associated with selexipag, are headache, diarrhea, jaw pain, and nausea. Nevertheless, Selexipag was generally well tolerated during the GRIPHON trial. Conclusions: Selexipag is a valuable addition to PAH therapeutics especially by reducing the PAH-related hospitalizations and thus improving quality of life in PAH patients.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sørensen, Louise Marqvard","Wehland, Markus","Krüger, Marcus","Simonsen, Ulf","Nassef, Mohamed Zakaria","Infanger, Manfred","Grimm, Daniela"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-266997"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Otto von Guericke University Magdeburg"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a special focus on selexipag treatment of pulmonary arterial hypertension","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85042763820","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-266997","identifier":[{"id":"85042763820","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28891448","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f142dff4-8dcb-4de4-9d59-5c83db099799"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-71AE5E365ACED23F07D353D380D3B7BD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"otto von guericke university magdeburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Otto von Guericke University Magdeburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Marqvard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"8072d291-4fd1-4307-88ea-6d9706b3cd55","name":"Sørensen, Louise Marqvard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Markus","key":"wehlandpau","last":"Wehland","name":"Wehland, Markus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus","key":"krügerpau","last":"Krüger","name":"Krüger, Marcus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulf","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"eed8d0f5-bdc4-462e-9638-d2e314b2363c","name":"Simonsen, Ulf","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohamed Zakaria","key":"nassefpau","last":"Nassef","name":"Nassef, Mohamed Zakaria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Manfred","key":"infangerpau","last":"Infanger","name":"Infanger, Manfred","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniela","key":"grimmpau","last":"Grimm","locid":"734dee11-f808-49ec-a6e6-3e75123d84aa","name":"Grimm, Daniela","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28891448"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2174/1381612823666170908114227","issn":["13816128","18734286"],"issn_org":["13816128"],"issue":"34","journal":"Current Pharmaceutical Design","pages":"5191-5199","publisher":"Bentham Science Publishers","status":"p","title":"Current Pharmaceutical Design","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042763820"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f142dff4-8dcb-4de4-9d59-5c83db099799"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A Special Focus on Selexipag - Treatment of Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-266997","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
