42d58cba-8c56-4d5e-8646-22c8a3aaf95e"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Energikrisen i 1973 : Historie 6-7 klasse 6-7 lektioner","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-647436","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: Dietary and endogenously formed long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acids (LCPUFAs) are hypothesized to improve cognitive development, but results are inconclusive, with suggestions of sex specificity. One study suggested that single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) rs1535 and rs174448 in the fatty acid desaturase (FADS) gene cluster have opposite effects on erythrocyte LCPUFAs at 9 mo.Objective: To explore whether SNPs in FADS and elongase (ELOVL) genes were associated with school performance in a sex-specific manner, we performed a Mendelian randomization study using data from the Optimal well-being, development and health for Danish children through a healthy New Nordic Diet (OPUS) School Meal Study with 765 Danish schoolchildren 8-11 y old.Design: Associations between selected FADS1/2 SNPs (rs1535, rs174448, and rs174468) and ELOVL5 rs2397142, whole-blood fatty acid composition, and performance in the d2 Test of Attention and a reading test were analyzed in multiple regression models including all SNPs, SNP-sex interactions, and covariates related to testing conditions.Results:FADS, rs1535 minor allele carriage associated with lower whole-blood arachidonic acid (P ≤ 0.002), and minor alleles of rs174448 tended to associate with lower docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) (P = 0.052). We identified sex interactions in 50% of the SNP performance sets. Sex-dependent associations were observed for rs174448 and rs1535 on the d2 Test of Attention outcomes (P < 0.03) and for the associations between reading scores and rs174448 and rs2397142 (P < 0.01). All of the sex-specific analyses showed associations in opposite directions in girls and boys. The minor allele carriage of rs174448 was associated with lower d2 Test of Attention performance (P < 0.02) and reading scores (P < 0.001) in boys but with better reading scores in girls (P ≤ 0.002). The associations were consistently the opposite for rs1535 minor allele carriage (P < 0.05). Associations with rs2397142 also appeared to be opposite of those of rs174448, but only for reading and not significant after adjustment for parental educational level and whole-blood DHA.Conclusions: This study showed associations between rs1535 minor allele homozygosity and rs174448 major allele carriage and improved performance in 8- to 11-y-old boys but not in girls, thereby counteracting existing sex differences. This may be a consequence of increased endogenous DHA synthesis in infancy but not at school-age. This trial was registered at clinicaltrials.gov as NCT01457794.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Lauritzen, Lotte","Sorensen, Louise B.","Harslof, Laurine B.","Ritz, Christian","Stark, Ken D.","Astrup, Arne","Dyssegaard, Camilla Brørup","Egelund, Niels","Michaelsen, Kim F.","Damsgaard, Camilla T."],"cuid":["S02-095.14-020607"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Lauritzen, Lotte"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["Docosahexaenoic acid","ELOVL","FADS","Fatty acid metabolism","Fish intake","Grundskole","Køn","NEURODEVELOPMENTAL OUTCOMES","Neurodevelopment","Nordic diet","Pregnancy","School performance","controlled trial","n 3 Fatty acids"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mendelian randomization shows sex specific associations between long chain pufa related genotypes and cognitive performance in danish schoolchildren","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85021822044","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.14-020607","identifier":[{"id":"000404593900013","type":"wos"},{"id":"28515069","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85021822044","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6c98f734-c6f6-4af2-9e2d-2d41acc653fc","ku-08280aa9-6427-4db6-8bfb-762660bd38dc"],"keyword":["CONTROLLED-TRIAL","DHA SUPPLEMENTATION","DOCOSAHEXAENOIC ACID","ELOVL","FADS","FADS2 POLYMORPHISMS","FATTY-ACID-METABOLISM","FISH INTAKE","Grundskole","Køn","NEURODEVELOPMENTAL OUTCOMES","NORDIC DIET","OPUS SCHOOL MEAL","PREGNANCY","n-3 fatty acids","neurodevelopment","school performance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3BF6B3C5294064C30731C0A304E9883D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Lifecourse Nutrition & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of waterloo","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Waterloo","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Sociology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte","key":"lauritzenpau","last":"Lauritzen","locid":"4263561d-003a-4d4c-9f05-06a8f88155e8","name":"Lauritzen, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0001-7184-5949","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise B","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"b86d9af7-ea09-4925-a863-ea