r Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021822044"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6c98f734-c6f6-4af2-9e2d-2d41acc653fc","ku-08280aa9-6427-4db6-8bfb-762660bd38dc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mendelian randomization shows sex-specific associations between long-chain PUFA-related genotypes and cognitive performance in Danish schoolchildren","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.14-020607","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Both hypoglycemia and severe hyperglycemia constitute known risk factors for cardiac repolarization changes potentially leading to malignant arrhythmias. Patients with loss of function mutations in KCNQ1 are characterized by long QT syndrome (LQTS) and may be at increased risk for glucose-induced repolarization disturbances. OBJECTIVE: The purpose of this study was to test the hypothesis that KCNQ1 LQTS patients are at particular risk for cardiac repolarization changes during the relative hyperglycemia that occurs after an oral glucose load. METHODS: Fourteen KCNQ1 LQTS patients and 28 control participants matched for gender, body mass index, and age underwent a 3-hour oral 75-g glucose tolerance test with ECGs obtained at 7 time points. Fridericia corrected QT interval (QTcF), Bazett corrected QT interval (QTcB), and the Morphology Combination Score (MCS) were calculated. RESULTS: QTc and MCS increased in both groups. MCS remained elevated until 150 minutes after glucose ingestion, and the maximal change from baseline was larger among KCNQ1 LQTS patients compared with control subjects (0.28 ± 0.27 vs 0.15 ± 0.13; P <.05). CONCLUSION: Relative hyperglycemia induced by ingestion of 75-g glucose caused cardiac repolarization disturbances that were more severe in KCNQ1 LQTS patients compared with control subjects.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hyltén-Cavallius, Louise","Iepsen, Eva W.","Christiansen, Michael","Graff, Claus","Linneberg, Allan","Pedersen, Oluf","Holst, Jens J.","Hansen, Torben","Torekov, Signe S.","Kanters, Jørgen K."],"cuid":["S03-100.00-008985"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Kanters, Jørgen K."],"keyword":["Administration Oral","Adult","Blood Glucose metabolism","Cardiac arrhythmia","Denmark epidemiology","Dose Response Relationship Drug","Electrocardiography drug effects","Female","Glucose administration dosage","Heart Rate drug effects","Humans","Hypoglycemia blood","Incidence","Journal Article","KCNQ1","Long QT Syndrome","Male","Middle Aged","Morphology combination score","Oral glucose tolerance test","QT interval","Risk Factors","T wave morphology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glucose ingestion causes cardiac repolarization disturbances in type 000000000001 long qt syndrome patients and healthy subjects","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85019944507","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was supported by grants from the Danish Research Council; Danish Strategic Research Foundation; Fraenkel Foundation; Novo Nordisk Foundation; Lundbeck Foundation Centre for Applied Medical Genomics for Personalised Disease Prediction, Prevention and Care (www.lucamp.org); University of Copenhagen; and University Investment Capital: Food, Fitness & Pharma for Health and Disease from the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation and the Danish Diabetes Academy supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation. The Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research is an independent research center at the University of Copenhagen partially funded by an unrestricted donation from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (www.metabol.ku.dk). Drs. Graff and Kanters are inventors of a patent regarding T-wave morphology. All other authors have reported that they have no relationships relevant to the contents of this paper to disclose. Drs. Torekov and Kanters contributed equally to this manuscript."],"id":"S03-100.00-008985","identifier":[{"id":"000406496700014","type":"wos"},{"id":"85019944507","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28400316","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-ba4e4ed6-f780-4299-b090-d85b86b4f4ec","ku-e05b4e29-e5ae-4be6-bf4e-08ff961eb11a","sdu-150ba651-b32b-4cbb-a73b-7b510d7b1e9b"],"keyword":["Administration, Oral","Adult","Blood Glucose/metabolism","Cardiac arrhythmia","Denmark/epidemiology","Dose-Response Relationship, Drug","Electrocardiography/drug effects","Female","Glucose/administration & dosage","Heart Rate/drug effects","Humans","Hypoglycemia/blood","Incidence","Journal Article","KCNQ1","Long QT syndrome","Male","Middle Aged","Morphology Combination Score","Oral glucose tolerance test","QT interval","Risk Factors","Romano-Ward Syndrome/complications","Sweetening Agents/administration & dosage","T-wave morphology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-894774A777082EC3B038E330B843216B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University",