{"abstract":"For the Greenland ice sheet, the period from 2007-2015 is characterized by a large variability in climate conditions, with record-breaking melt in 2010 and 2012 and minor net mass loss in 2013. As a part of the Programme for Monitoring of the Greenland Ice Sheet (PROMICE) funded by the Danish Energy Agency, repeat airborne LiDAR surveys have been conducted in 2007, 2011 and 2015. The surveys were conducted around the entire margin of Greenland ice sheet. In addition to LiDAR measurements, ice-penetrating radar measurements were carried out in 2007 and 2011, to estimate ice sheet thickness along the flight-path. As the only one of its kind, the repeat surveys have been performed in late summer, to coincide with the end of the balance year. With the third survey successfully conducted in 2015, a unique opportunity for evaluating elevation changes at a consistent and tailored circum-Greenland fluxgate consist with this PROMICE dataset. Here, we combine available satellite observations of elevation changes of the Greenland ice sheet, with the PROMICE dataset, to estimate the state of the Greenland ice sheet seen from the PROMICE fluxgate. The PROMICE LiDAR snapshots will guide the contemporary observations from satellites to target the balance year.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Forsberg, René","Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","Nielsen, Jens Emil","Skourup, Henriette","Stenseng, Lars","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-364936"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-13","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2016-05-09","title":"ESA Living Planet Symposium 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"snapshots of circum greenland elevation change viewed from the promice airborne surveys in 000000002007 000000002011 and 000000002015","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session185.php#869p","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-364936","ids":["dtu-ca1842b5-edf6-4dea-83b6-045b2ebf44f4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E4927D41B54E51104649B6642283FF15"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session185.php#869p","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sine Munk","key":"hvidegaardpau","last":"Hvidegaard","locid":"92b07d8f-692c-4ebb-bc40-f44224f3f143","name":"Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","orcid":"0000-0001-8159-6499","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Emil","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c1ed0703-31fb-4d2b-8c22-eb1566cb603f","name":"Nielsen, Jens Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-8422-6901","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette","key":"skouruppau","last":"Skourup","locid":"f5fe613f-20e5-4a69-9eff-f03779801182","name":"Skourup, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-4468-8033","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"stensengpau","last":"Stenseng","locid":"c0f908ca-1192-4239-b399-ad14c4d9bc6d","name":"Stenseng, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-4690-4200","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ca1842b5-edf6-4dea-83b6-045b2ebf44f4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Snapshots of circum-Greenland elevation change, viewed from the PROMICE airborne surveys in 2007, 2011, and 2015","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-364936","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"As the Greenland ice sheet warms, a change in the structure of the upper snow/firn occurs. This change further induces changes in the reflective properties of the firn seen from satellite radar altimetry. If not identified as changes in the reflective properties of the firn, these may be interpreted as actual surface elevation changes seen from the satellite radar altimetry (Nilsson et al., 2015).Here, we investigate how to correct the elevation change observed from the ESA Cryosat-2 radar altimetry mission to derive elevation change of the air/snow interface of the Greenland ice sheet. The elevation change of this “real” physical surface is crucial, if the goal is to derive Greenland mass balance as done for LiDAR missions.The investigations look into waveform parameters to correct for the observed bias between Radar and LiDAR observations when using Croysat-2 level-2 data. Based on the knowledge gained by analyzing the elevation change derived from the inclusion of various waveform parameters, we pinpoint the challenges associated with the using Croysat-2 observation in mass balance studies. As for mass balance studies utilizing LiDAR observation (ICESat), a strong firn-modeling component is needed; here the information gained from running such models may also provide input for the correction of radar elevation in to surface elevation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Forsberg, René","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-372177"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-13","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2016-05-09","title":"ESA Living Planet Symposium 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenges for greenland wide mass balance from cryosat 000000000002 radar altimetry","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session185.php#935p","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-372177","ids":["dtu-e229e0e6-5b5a-41de-af2a-f21997da8cc5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1071EB866DB3DC450765B53018E3F154"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session185.php#935p","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e229e0e6-5b5a-41de-af2a-f21997da8cc5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Challenges for Greenland-wide mass balance from Cryosat-2 radar-altimetry","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-372177","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Glyceryl trinitrate induces headache during infusion to man and migraine patients develop an additional migraine attack a few hours after the infusion. Recently, we have moved this model into rat with the intention of developing an animal model predictive of migraine therapy. In the current paper we have studied the effect of glyceryl trinitrate infusion on three different rat behaviors. Methods: The stability of burrowing behavior, running wheel activity and light sensitivity towards repeated testing was evaluated also with respect to estrous cycle. Finally, the effect of glyceryl trinitrate on these behaviors in female rats was observed. Results: Burrowing behavior and running wheel activity were stable in the individual rat between experiments. The burrowing behavior was significantly affected by the stage of estrous cycle. The other assays were stable throughout the cycle. None of the three behavioral tests were altered by glyceryl trinitrate infusion. In the light-dark box, some batches of rats showed light sensitivity after treatment with glyceryl trinitrate but it could not be repeated in other batches of rats. Discussion: We have investigated the stability towards repeated testing and the effect of i.v. glyceryl trinitrate infusion to awake rats in three behavioral assays. Of the assays evaluated, only light sensitivity was capable of detecting changes after glyceryl trinitrate infusion but, this was not repeatable. Thus, the infusion of a low dose glyceryl trinitrate to concious rats together with the chosen behavioral tests is not a robust setup for studying immediate GTN induced headache behavior in rats","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christensen, Sarah Louise T","Petersen, Steffen","Sørensen, Dorte Bratbo","Jansen-Olesen, Inger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-523061"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animal model","Burrowing","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Glyceryl trinitrate","Light sensitivity","Methods","Migraine","Rat","Running wheel"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infusion of low dose glyceryl trinitrate has no consistent effect on burrowing behavior running wheel activity and light sensitivity in female rats","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-523061","identifier":[{"id":"27066766","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84964370048","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d9004896-06b6-44ad-adee-0c1af516c4d6"],"keyword":["Animal model","Burrowing","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Glyceryl trinitrate","Light sensitivity","Methods","Migraine","Oestrous cycle","Rat","Running wheel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77B768EFC35E91D64ABBE403DEEC8F76"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah Louise T","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Sarah Louise T","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steffen","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Steffen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dorte Bratbo","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"b4b02b58-e75f-4c0d-a4ce-907b714484f4","name":"Sørensen, Dorte Bratbo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger","key":"jansenolesenpau","last":"Jansen-Olesen","name":"Jansen-Olesen, Inger","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27066766"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vascn.2016.04.004","issn":["10568719","1873488X"],"issn_org":["10568719"],"journal":"Journal of Pharmacological and Toxicological Methods","pages":"43-50","status":"p","title":"Journal of Pharmacological and Toxicological Methods","volume":"80"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964370048"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d9004896-06b6-44ad-adee-0c1af516c4d6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infusion of low dose glyceryl trinitrate has no consistent effect on burrowing behavior, running wheel activity and light sensitivity in female rats","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-523061","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND/OBJECTIVES: We previously found that the OPUS School Meal Study improved reading and increased errors related to inattention and impulsivity. This study explored whether the cognitive effects differed according to gender, household education and reading proficiency at baseline. SUBJECTS/METHODS: This is a cluster-randomised cross-over trial comparing Nordic school meals with packed lunch from home (control) for 3 months each among 834 children aged 8 to 11 years. At baseline and at the end of each dietary period, we assessed children's performance in reading, mathematics and the d2-test of attention. Interactions were evaluated using mixed models. Analyses included 739 children. RESULTS: At baseline, boys and children from households without academic education were poorer readers and had a higher d2-error%. Effects on dietary intake were similar in subgroups. However, the effect of the intervention on test outcomes was stronger in boys, in children from households with academic education and in children with normal/good baseline reading proficiency. Overall, this resulted in increased socioeconomic inequality in reading performance and reduced inequality in impulsivity. Contrary to this, the gender difference decreased in reading and increased in impulsivity. Finally, the gap between poor and normal/good readers was increased in reading and decreased for d2-error%. CONCLUSIONS: The effects of healthy school meals on reading, impulsivity and inattention were modified by gender, household education and baseline reading proficiency. The differential effects might be related to environmental aspects of the intervention and deserves to be investigated further in future school meal trials.European Journal of Clinical Nutrition advance online publication, 15 June 2016; doi:10.1038/ejcn.2016.99.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Dyssegaard, Camilla Brørup","Egelund, Niels","Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","Damsgaard, Camilla Trab","Petersen, Rikke A.","Dalskov, Stine-Mathilde","Hjorth, Mads Fiil","Tetens, Inge","Astrup, Arne","Lauritzen, Lotte","Michaelsen, Kim F."],"cuid":["S03-100.00-021514"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Cognitive performance","Dansk læse skrive","Grundskole","Kognitionspsykologi","Køn","Nutrition","School meals","Social udsathed arv"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differences in the effects of school meals on children s cognitive performance according to gender household education and baseline reading skills","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84974851799","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-021514","identifier":[{"id":"27302673","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84974851799","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-79272e52-36f8-41ff-9896-f7866ccd8519","dtu-c53b658b-0aa3-4aa1-8ff1-70d7be64a424","ku-e2bc8058-507b-46fe-bc0b-d5f5ab4413c9"],"keyword":["Cognitive performance","Dansk/læse/skrive","Grundskole","Household education","Kognitionspsykologi","Køn","Nutrition","Reading sklls","School meals","Social udsathed/arv"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-14E5F98C1455ED1B09BC8280300E4BF5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namev