ey":"evensbergetpau","last":"Evensberget","name":"Evensberget, Dag","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth","key":"hauglundpau","last":"Hauglund","name":"Hauglund, Kenneth","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirill","key":"khvorostovskypau","last":"Khvorostovsky","name":"Khvorostovsky, Kirill","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Andy","key":"shepherdpau","last":"Shepherd","name":"Shepherd, Andy","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"hoggpau","last":"Hogg","name":"Hogg, Anna","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Signe","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Christine","key":"hvidbergpau","last":"Hvidberg","name":"Hvidberg, Christine","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Synne","key":"svensenpau","last":"Svensen","name":"Svensen, Synne","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus","key":"engdahlpau","last":"Engdahl","name":"Engdahl, Marcus","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-718878ce-7c30-45d9-acdb-b8520f3a7ad1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Spaceborne measurement of Greenland ice sheet changes: the ESA Greenland CCI project","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-338451","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Both the Antarctic Ice Sheet (AIS) and the Greenland Ice Sheet (GIS) have been identified as key parameters, so called Essential Climate Variables (ECV), in the climate system. Within the framework of the Climate Change Initiative (CCI) of the European Space Agency (ESA), reliable long-term satellite-based data products are generated for selected ECVs. Since ice sheet mass balance is an ECV parameter of highest interest, both the AIS_cci and the GIS_cci project will provide mass balance products based on satellite gravimetry data: (a) time series of monthly mass changes for individual drainage basins, and (b) gridded mass changes covering the entire ice sheet.Gravimetry Mass Balance (GMB) products are derived from data acquired by the GRACE (Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment) mission. Although GRACE data have the advantage of being directly sensitive to mass changes, their limited spatial resolution and complex error structures place particular demands on the applied processing strategy. To choose the most suitable algorithm which minimizes the impact of GRACE errors and signal leakage errors on GMB products, an open Round Robin experiment was set up. Participants were asked to provide GMB products according to the specifications of the official products by the ESA CCI using their preferred processing strategy and GRACE release. In addition, the same algorithms should be applied to a series of synthetic datasets, which realistically mimic mass variations in various subsystems of the Earth (e.g. cryoshpere, ocean, continental hydrology). By comparing the derived synthetic mass changes with the a priori known 'synthetic truth', leakage errors can be quantified.Here we inter-compare the Round Robin results from six individual contributions, relying on different processing strategies, including regional integration approaches, mass inversion strategies, and a forward modeling approach. Time series of basin averaged and gridded products are compared with respect to their specific noise level. The minimization of leakage errors is assessed from the synthetic results. Finally, for selected drainage basins the GMB time series are compared to independent mass balance products based on satellite altimetry and firn densification information from a regional climate model. This inter-comparison has aided the algorithm definition for the operational ECV production.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Groth, A.","Horwath, M.","Horvath, A.","Meister, Rakia","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Forsberg, René","Su, X","Shang, K.","Shum, C.K.","Ditmar, P.","Ran, J.","Klees, R.","Wouters, B.","Schrama, E.","Shepherd, A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-372957"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-13","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2016-05-09","title":"ESA Living Planet Symposium 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Dresden University of Technology","Ohio State University","Ohio University","Technical University of Munich","University of Bristol"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inter comparison of ice sheet mass balance products from grace esa cci round robin results","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session185.php#1689p","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-372957","ids":["dtu-e4c9dc96-70af-4d62-98dd-736b4bda4c55"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8A39DB0D3EBC42B0071A421CC4CD43DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session185.php#1689p","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"dresden university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Dresden University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"ohio state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ohio State University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"ohio university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ohio University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"university of bristol","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bristol","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"grothpau","last":"Groth","name":"Groth, A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"horwathpau","last":"Horwath","name":"Horwath, M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"horvathpau","last":"Horvath","name":"Horvath, A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rakia","key":"meisterpau","last":"Meister","locid":"4f1baadc-6017-47d8-a7b6-38877d9cdc20","name":"Meister, Rakia","orcid":"0000-0001-8519-5502","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"X","key":"supau","last":"Su","name":"Su, X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"shangpau","last":"Shang","name":"Shang, K.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"C.K.","key":"shumpau","last":"Shum","name":"Shum, C.K.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"ditmarpau","last":"Ditmar","name":"Ditmar, P.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"ranpau","last":"Ran","name":"Ran, J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"kleespau","last":"Klees","name":"Klees, R.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"wouterspau","last":"Wouters","name":"Wouters, B.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"schramapau","last":"Schrama","name":"Schrama, E.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"shepherdpau","last":"Shepherd","name":"Shepherd, A.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e4c9dc96-70af-4d62-98dd-736b4bda4c55"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Inter-comparison of ice sheet mass balance products from GRACE: ESA CCI Round Robin results","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-372957","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Based on evident sex-related differences in the invasive management of patients presenting with acute myocardial infarction (AMI), we sought to identify predictors of diagnostic coronary angiography (DCA) and to investigate reasons for opting out an invasive strategy in women and men. Methods: The study was designed as a matched cohort study. We randomly selected 250 female cases from a source population of 4000 patients hospitalized with a first AMI in a geographically confined region of Denmark from January 2010 to November 2011. Each case was matched to a male control on age and availability of cardiac invasive facilities at the index hospital. We systematically reviewed medical records for risk factors, comorbid conditions, clinical presentation, and receipt of DCA. Clinical justifications, as stated by the treating physician, were noted for the subset of patients who did not receive a DCA. Results: Overall, 187 women and 198 men received DCA within 60 days (75 % vs. 79 %, hazard ratio: 0.82 [0.67-1.00], p = 0.047).In the subset of patients who did not receive a DCA (n = 114), clinical justifications for opting out an invasive strategy was not documented for 21 patients (18.4 %). Type 2 myocardial infarction was noted in 11 patients (women versus men; 14.5 % vs. 3.8 %, p = 0.06) and identified as a potential confounder of the sex-DCA relationship. Receipt of DCA was predicted by traditional risk factors for ischaemic heart disease (family history of cardiovascular disease, hypercholesterolemia, and smoking) and clinical presentation (chest pain, ST-segment elevations). Although prevalent in both women and men, the presence of relative contraindications did not prohibit the use of DCA. Conclusion: In this matched cohort of patients with a first AMI, women and men had different clinical presentations despite similar age. However, no differences in the distribution of relative contraindications for DCA were found between the sexes. Type 2 MI posed a potentiel confounder for the sex-related differences in the use of DCA. Importantly,clinical justification for opting out an invasive strategy was not documented in almost one fifth of patients not receiving a DCA.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bjerking, Louise Hougesen","Hansen, Kim Wadt","Madsen, Mette","Jensen, Jan Skov","Madsen, Jan K","Sørensen, Rikke","Galatius, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-531173"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Cardiac Catheterization","Coronary Angiography","Gender"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of diagnostic coronary angiography in women and men presenting with acute myocardial infarction a matched cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12872-016-0248-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-531173","identifier":[{"id":"000376842600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"84975308025","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27250115","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4888313","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-e6a226c8-1c19-4917-9048-7e5b4e0fc3a0"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Cardiac catheterization","Coronary angiography","Gender"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D6D489A550D4F4F158F46DC6CBFB1A4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12872-016-0248-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/188915190/s12872_016_0248_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016