{"abstract":"Beam-limited footprints from conventional satellite radar altimeters have diameters of up to tens of kilometers. Topography within the footprint results in a displacement of the reflecting point from Nadir to the point of closest approach relative to the satellite. Several methods exist for correcting for such mispointing errors. Here, two techniques are applied to observations near Jakobshavn Isbræ, acquired with Envisat’s Radar Altimeter(RA-2). The apriori knowledge on the surface topography is obtained from a digital elevation model. The methods relocate the measurement location horizontally to agree with the measured range. One method assumes a constant surface slope within the footprint and uses this and the surface aspect to estimate the displacement parameter; the other locates the optimal relocation point using local topography. The results of the two methods are evaluated against airborne laser-scanner data from the airborne topographic mapper. We find that the accuracy of the relocation depends on both the technique and the spatial resolution of the digital elevation model, and that this dependency varies with surface roughness. Thus, the relocation may be associated with significant errors, which will lower the accuracy of cryospheric studies based on radar altimetry data. We find that the most accurate results are obtained when assessing the full local topography. Furthermore, errors in data over the steep margin are minimized the most when using a spatial resolution of 2 km; the effect of the resolution overregions with a smoother topography is minor.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fredenslund Levinsen, Joanna","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Forsberg, René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-320330"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital Elevation Models","Satellite radar altimetry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Ministry of Energy, Utilities and Climate"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of dem resolution on relocating radar altimetry data over ice sheets","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84983410337","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-320330","identifier":[{"id":"84983410337","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-34eb68a4-f403-4c18-87fd-7bd2b10d35bb"],"keyword":["Digital Elevation Models","Relocation errors","Satellite radar altimetry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8C4D7DD13654BB0597F5A322CA569EDB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Ministry of Energy, Utilities and Climate"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"fredenslundlevinsenpau","last":"Fredenslund Levinsen","name":"Fredenslund Levinsen, Joanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/jstars.2016.2587684","issn":["19391404","21511535"],"issn_org":["19391404"],"issue":"7","journal":"IEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Applied Earth Observations and Remote Sensing","pages":"3158-3163","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Applied Earth Observations and Remote Sensing","title_org":"I E E E Journal of Selected Topics in Applied Earth Observations and Remote Sensing","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84983410337"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-34eb68a4-f403-4c18-87fd-7bd2b10d35bb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The Impact of DEM Resolution on Relocating Radar Altimetry Data Over Ice Sheets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-320330","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Earlier studies on seasonality in growth reported the largest height gains during spring and largest body weight gains during autumn. We examined seasonality in height, body weight, BMI, fat mass index (FMI) and fat-free mass index (FFMI) among contemporary Danish 8-11-year-olds. METHODS: 760 children from the OPUS School Meal Study provided >2200 measurements on height, body weight and composition between September-June. Average velocities were calculated using change-score analyses based on three-month intervals. As a complementary analysis, point velocities derived from estimated growth curves were fitted using semi-parametric regression that included covariate adjustment and allowed flexible modelling of the time trend. RESULTS: Average velocities showed the following trends: Height was higher than the average (6.10 cm/year) in January-April. Body weight was below the average (4.02 kg/year) August-January and above January-May; BMI (average: 0.49 kg/ m(2)/year) and FFMI (average: 0.17 kg/m(2)/year) showed similar trends. In contrast, FMI was above the average (0.38 kg/m(2)/year) November-March. Similar trends were seen for point velocities. CONCLUSIONS: Our findings suggest seasonality in growth and body composition of Danish children. We recovered the well-known height velocity peak during spring time, but unlike earlier studies we found coincident peaks in body weight, BMI, and FFMI velocities.Pediatric Research (2015); doi:10.1038/pr.2015.206.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Dalskov, Stine-Mathilde","Ritz, Christian","Larnkjær, Anni","Damsgaard, Camilla Trab","Petersen, Rikke Agnete","Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","Hjorth, Mads Fiil","Ong, Ken K","Astrup, Arne","Mølgaard, Christian","Michaelsen, Kim F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-474743"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"seasonal variations in growth and body composition of 000000000008 000000000011 year old danish children","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-474743","identifier":[{"id":"26488554","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84982266831","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-87f1db78-8311-41f1-817e-279b787de3b6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B2404D4BFFD43E6914259AA4E6DE2638"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Lifecourse Nutrition & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stine-Mathilde","key":"dalskovpau","last":"Dalskov","locid":"56222bcb-fb52-4111-8cfa-0264a3fef7e5","name":"Dalskov, Stine-Mathilde","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"ritzpau","last":"Ritz","locid":"c881424f-d529-443e-b60e-bc2edb674ede","name":"Ritz, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5095-0624","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anni","key":"larnkjærpau","last":"Larnkjær","locid":"988a7c84-01db-4679-8549-d375f2f92cd1","name":"Larnkjær, Anni","orcid":"0000-0002-7790-7888","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Trab","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","locid":"5ea9cc09-17f1-46a3-9e4e-fa5490abd815","name":"Damsgaard, Camilla Trab","orcid":"0000-0002-5013-0562","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke Agnete","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"7ec167a6-8982-42dc-87de-53c245802653","name":"Petersen, Rikke Agnete","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Bergmann","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"b86d9af7-ea09-4925-a863-eadc0c0e26ee","name":"Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Fiil","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"00918fa0-7b1e-4128-919e-a0af9497026b","name":"Hjorth, Mads Fiil","orcid":"0000-0001-9440-2737","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ken K","key":"ongpau","last":"Ong","name":"Ong, Ken K","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"5d943631-c9fc-4b63-8aaa-263ba4248735","name":"Astrup, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-8968-8996","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"mølgaardpau","last":"Mølgaard","locid":"240d0bd3-4221-4d27-bfdb-8fd6887cdb30","name":"Mølgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5311-9457","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim F.","key":"michaelsenpau","last":"Michaelsen","locid":"c29a2565-4c7e-4a5b-ab39-899baedae963","name":"Michaelsen, Kim F.","orcid":"0000-0003-0449-0839","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26488554"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/pr.2015.206","issn":["00313998","15300447"],"issn_org":["00313998"],"issue":"2","journal":"Pediatric Research","pages":"358-363","status":"p","title":"Pediatric Research","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84982266831"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-87f1db78-8311-41f1-817e-279b787de3b6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Seasonal variations in growth and body composition of 8-11-year-old Danish children","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-474743","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS) is a frequent endocrine disorder in women. PCOS is associated with altered features of androgen metabolism, increased insulin resistance and impaired fertility. Furthermore, PCOS, being a syndrome diagnosis, is heterogeneous and characterized by polycystic ovaries, chronic anovulation and evidence of hyperandrogenism, as well as being associated with chronic lowgrade inflammation and an increased life time risk of type 2 diabetes. A number of androgen species contribute to the symptoms of increased androgen exposure seen in many, though not all, cases of PCOS: Testosterone, androstenedione, dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA) and dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate (DHEAS), where the quantitatively highest amount of androgen is found as DHEAS. The sulfation of DHEA to DHEAS depends on a number of enzymes, and altered sulfate metabolism may be associated with and contribute to the pathogenesis of PCOS. MicroRNAs (miRNAs) are small, non-coding RNAs that are able to regulate gene expression at the posttranscriptional level. Altered miRNA levels have been associated with diabetes, insulin resistance, inflammation and various cancers. Studies have shown that circulating miRNAs are present in whole blood, serum, plasma and the follicular fluid of PCOS patients and that these might serve as potential biomarkers and a new approach for the diagnosis of PCOS. In this review, recent work on miRNAs with respect to PCOS will be summarized. Our understanding of miRNAs, particularly in relation to PCOS, is currently at a very early stage, and additional studies will yield important insight into the molecular mechanisms behind this complex and heterogenic syndrome.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sørensen, Anja Elaine","Udesen, Pernille Bækgaard","Wissing, Marie Louise","Englund, Anne Lis Mikkelsen","Dalgaard, Louise Torp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-558894"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Androgens","Biomarker","DHEA","DHEAS","Polycystic Ovary Syndrome","microRNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"micrornas related to androgen metabolism and polycystic ovary syndrome","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-558894","identifier":[{"id":"84995810373","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-2bb32b12-14d4-4aa9-b938-d7eb69a51784"],"keyword":["Androgens","Biomarker","DHEA","DHEAS","MicroRNA","Ovarian steroid metabolism","Polycystic ovary syndrome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-42A203D98BD2AE11AA21BDBFCB08E1A5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Holbæk Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Anja Elaine","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7e5d1e2c-5d4b-4436-bb66-acdca4058c08","name":"Sørensen, Anja Elaine","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-5376","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Pernille Bækgaard","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","name":"Udesen, Pernille Bækgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Marie Louise","key":"wissingpau","last":"Wissing","name":"Wissing, Marie Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anne Lis Mikkelsen","key":"englundpau","last":"Englund","name":"Englund, Anne Lis Mikkelsen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Louise Torp","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"a219fdaf-f994-4a7a-beb8-1f353846ed5a","name":"Dalgaard, Louise Torp","orcid":"0000-0002-3598-2775","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cbi.2016.06.008","issn":["00092797","18727786"],"issn_org":["00092797"],"journal":"Chemico-Biological Interactions","pages":"8-16","status":"p","title":"Chemico-Biological Interactions","volume":"259"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84995810373"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-2bb32b12-14d4-4aa9-b938-d7eb69a51784"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"MicroRNAs related to androgen metabolism and polycystic ovary syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-558894","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"I mere end 250 år var Danmark en stor kolonimagt. Skt. Jan, Skt. Thomas og Skt. Croix, eller U.S. Virgin Islands, som de kaldes i dag, var danske kolonier, hvor der bl.a. blev dyrket sukkerrør og bomuld. Det hårde arbejde blev udført af slaver, som man fra slutningen af 1600-tallet begyndte at transportere over Atlanterhavet. Hvorfor havde Danmark øer, der lå så lagt væk – og hvorfor solgte man dem i 1917? Det kan eleverne læse om i bogen, ligesom de også kan få svar på, hvor-dan befolkningen på de danske kolonier levede, og hvornår slaveriet blev afskaffet. I bogen per-spektivers samtidig til forhold i Europa og Amerika, der påvirkede udviklingen på øerne – fx krige, storpolitik og politiske ideer. Teksten giver eleverne et overblik over slaveriet i Vestindien, men den er samtidig ”åben”, idet den skaber nysgerrighed, påpeger dilemmaer og i det hele taget motiverer eleverne til at reflektere og søge yderligere information om emnet.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Peters, Rikke","Brunbech, Peter Johan Yding","Poulsen, Jens Aage","Sørensen, Christina Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-647250"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Danske Kolonier","Historie","Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Slaveri"],"level":"pop","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"da danmark var en slavenation om slaveriet og de vestindiske øer fra 000000001600 tallet til nu","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-647250","ids":["ucl-3512ab3f-3140-4e34-a439-2e9b92cffee0"],"keyword":["Danske kolonier","Historie","Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","Slaveri","kolonimagt"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-1-5163B65871581D02BFD9C6278B86E324"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Rektor, Rektor, Videncenter for Historie og Kulturformidling"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Louise Alberg","key":"peterspau","last":"Peters","locid":"c08a1671-9716-48a1-a1b9-2f07a47a57e9","name":"Peters, Rikke","name_org":"Peters, Rikke Louise Alberg","orcid":"0000-0003-0120-370X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Johan Yding","key":"brunbechpau","last":"Brunbech","name":"Brunbech, Peter Johan Yding","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Aage","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"2fe2921a-cbaa-4e8f-b6f0-fdf98dda45ae","name":"Poulsen, Jens Aage","orcid":"0000-0001-9617-4336","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Louise","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c4715900-2e37-4a8f-9c8b-77690089c2c4","name":"Sørensen, Christina Louise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788799736393"],"pages":"60","place":"Jelling","publisher":"Nationalt Videnscenter for Historie- og Kulturformidling","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-3512ab3f-3140-4e34-a439-2e9b92cffee0"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Da Danmark var en slavenation : Om slaveriet og De Vestindiske Øer fra 1600-tallet til nu","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-647250","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Sufficient summer/autumn vitamin D status appears important to mitigate winter nadirs at northern latitudes. We conducted a cross-sectional study to evaluate autumn vitamin D status and its determinants in 782 Danish 8-11-year-old children (55°N) using baseline data from the Optimal well-being, development and health for Danish children through a healthy New Nordic Diet (OPUS) School Meal Study, a large randomised controlled trial. Blood samples and demographic and behavioural data, including 7-d dietary recordings, objectively measured physical activity, and time spent outdoors during school hours, were collected during September-November. Mean serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D (25(OH)D) was 60·8 (sd 18·7) nmol/l. Serum 25(OH)D levels ≤50 nmol/l were found in 28·4 % of the children and 2·4 % had concentrations <25 nmol/l. Upon multivariate adjustment, increasing age (per year) (β -2·9; 95 % CI -5·1, -0·7 nmol/l), female sex (β -3·3; 95 % CI -5·9, -0·7 nmol/l), sampling in October (β -5·2; 95 % CI -10·1, -0·4 nmol/l) and November (β -13·3; 95 % CI -17·7, -9·1), and non-white ethnicity (β -5·7; 95 % CI -11·1, -0·3 nmol/l) were negatively associated with 25(OH)D (all P<0·05). Likewise, immigrant/descendant background was negatively associated with 25(OH)D, particularly in females (β -16·3; 95 % CI -21·9, -10·7) (P<0·001) (P interaction=0·003). Moderate-to-vigorous physical activity (MVPA) (min/d) (β 0·06; 95 % CI 0·01, 0·12), outdoor walking during school hours (min/week) (β 0·4; 95 % CI 0·1, 0·6) and intake of vitamin D-containing supplements ≥3 d/week (β 8·7; 95 % CI 6·4, 11·0) were positively associated with 25(OH)D (all P<0·05). The high proportion of children with vitamin D status below the recommended sufficiency level of 50 nmol/l raises concern as levels expectedly drop further during winter months. Frequent intake of vitamin D supplements was strongly associated with status. MVPA and outdoor activity during school hours should be investigated further in interventions to improve autumn vitamin D status in children at northern latitudes.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Petersen, Rikke A","Damsgaard, Camilla T","Dalskov, Stine-Mathilde","Sørensen, Louise B","Hjorth, Mads F","Ritz, Christian","Kjølbæk, Louise","Andersen, Rikke","Tetens, Inge","Krarup, Henrik","Astrup, Arne","Michaelsen, Kim F","Mølgaard, Christian"],"cuid":["S04-091.57-008325"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"keyword":["Children","Determinants","Northern latitudes","Nutrition","Vitamin D"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vitamin d status and its determinants during autumn in children at northern latitudes a cross sectional analysis from the optimal well being development and health for danish children through a healthy new nordic diet opus school meal study","src":["aau","dtu","ku","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S000711451500433X","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-091.57-008325","identifier":[{"id":"000367236200005","type":"wos"},{"id":"84951559107","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26563915","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-acfbcc7b-c369-422b-91f1-44fd68b56c11","dtu-16f7d7c9-c8d4-4327-b552-6bef74aacc5d","ku-0d09b975-b6b6-432e-be12-8b9e03830ce4","ucl-c972e0c2-59fc-4f3d-9a75-1ec12a248298"],"keyword":["Children","Determinants","Northern latitudes","Vitamin D","nutrition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-99A98C9EFC5ECC0BAEED9576F8469B8A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S000711451500433X","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/269991123/vitamin_d_status_and_its_determinants_during_autumn_in_children_at_northern_latitudes_a_crosssectional_analysis_from_the_optimal_wellbeing_development_and_health_for_danish_children_through_a_healthy_new_nordic_diet_opus_schoo.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucl.dk/ws/files/33442316/Petersen_et_al_2015_Vitamin_D_status_and_its_determinants_during_autumn_in_children_at_northern_latitudes.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Lifecourse Nutrition & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen i Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of D