{"abstract":"The project focussed on validating RNA based methods as potential genomic tools in assessment of agricultural soil ecosystems. It was shown that the mRNA based technique was very sensitive and the effects was seen in the same situations as when the OECD nitrification assay showed an effect. 16S rRNA based pyrosequencing of bacterial communities in soil was shown to report different than just DNA based analysis and indicated unlike the DNA measurement that the community was developing. Finally microarray analysis was compared to traditional test for toxicity testing of Folsomia candida and showed a more sensitive response to the pesticide exposure.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jacobsen, Carsten Suhr","Feld, Louise","Hjelmsø, Mathis Hjort","Nielsen, Morten Schostag","Rønn, Regin","Ekelund, Flemming","Johnsen, Anders","Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","Krogh, Paul Henning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-253527"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genepease genomic tools for assessment of pesticide effects on the agricultural soil ecosystem","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www2.mst.dk/Udgiv/publications/2016/06/978-87-93283-27-5.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-253527","ids":["au-d9975dea-35dd-4980-ab20-931eea8c4fa7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-96189F80A8C145DD2D560EC01A3152A2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Suhr","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"133780bc-c017-4476-9545-8e1ce69c200a","name":"Jacobsen, Carsten Suhr","orcid":"0000-0003-1041-0823","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"feldpau","last":"Feld","name":"Feld, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathis Hjort","key":"hjelmsøpau","last":"Hjelmsø","name":"Hjelmsø, Mathis Hjort","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Schostag","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Morten Schostag","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Regin","key":"rønnpau","last":"Rønn","name":"Rønn, Regin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"ekelundpau","last":"Ekelund","name":"Ekelund, Flemming","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J G","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ad745dfe-7c3b-4bbc-90df-4217c1b9ca92","name":"Sørensen, Jesper Givskov","name_org":"Sørensen, J G","orcid":"0000-0002-9149-3626","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Paul Henning","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"afaf03ea-44d9-4c45-b081-ce7e524cad38","name":"Krogh, Paul Henning","orcid":"0000-0003-2033-553X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793283275"],"pages":"53","publisher":"Bekæmpelsesmiddelforskning fra Miljøstyrelsen","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d9975dea-35dd-4980-ab20-931eea8c4fa7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"GENEPEASE Genomic tools for assessment of pesticide effects on the agricultural soil ecosystem","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-253527","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The combination of GRACE and altimetry data may yield a high resolution mass balance time series of the Greenlandice sheet, highlighting the varying individual mass loss behaviour of major glaciers. By including the Canadian arctic ice caps in the estimation, a more reliable estimate of the mass loss of both Greenlandand the Canadian ice caps may be obtained, minimizing the leakage errors otherwise unavoidable by GRACE. Actually, the absolute value of the Greenlandice sheet mass loss is highly dependent on methods and how the effects of Arctic Canadian ice caps are separated in the GRACE signal; here altimetry data and firn models may provide important constraints.In the presentation we outline the basis of the joint estimation method, including corrections for firn density and compaction, and use CryoSat and EnviSat data together with GRACE data to provide composite time series of mass loss of the ice caps and ice sheet basins for the period 2003-15. This period shows a marked increase of ice sheet melt, especially in NW and NE Greenland, but also show large variability, with the melt anomaly year of 2012 showing a record mass loss, followed by 2013 with essentially no Greenland mass loss at all, and lately return to the “normal” mass loss rate. While GRACE sees these later year anomalies quite clearly, the CryoSat data are affected strongly by the icesheet-wide 2012 melt event, where change in CryoSat radar penetration in the firn results in an erroneous mass gain estimate over central parts of theGreenlandice sheet. The overall estimate of mass loss trend forGreenlandduring the CryoSat period yields values around -280 GT/yr, with the Canadian ice cap mass loss estimated at around -40 GT/yr and -25 GT/yr for the Baffin and Ellesmere regions, respectively. The used estimation methods can readily be extended to other altimetry mission data, such as Sentinel-3 and AltiKa, and could also potentially be used to further integrate other EO parameters such as ice velocity changes of the major outlet glaciers, as produced e.g. in the ESA Greenland Ice Sheet CCI project.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Forsberg, René","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Nilsson, Johan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-339837"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-13","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2016-05-09","title":"ESA Living Planet Symposium 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mass balance of greenland and the canadian ice caps from combined altimetry and grace inversion","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session132.php#1741p","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-339837","ids":["dtu-7614530d-9068-445f-b723-44826a9f24f9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-826D4B6D298AB8BDB26DBCBFBCB94D04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session132.php#1741p","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"nasa jet propulsion laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johan","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","name":"Nilsson, Johan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7614530d-9068-445f-b723-44826a9f24f9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Mass balance of Greenland and the Canadian Ice Caps from combined altimetry and GRACE inversion","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-339837","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A novel method, Spin-State-Selective (S3) HMBC, for accurate measurement of homonuclear coupling constants is introduced. As characteristic for S3 techniques, S3 HMBC yields independent subspectra corresponding to particular passive spin states and thus allows determination of coupling constants between detected spins and homonuclear coupling partners along with relative signs. In the presented S3 HMBC experiment, spin-state selection occurs via large one-bond coupling constants ensuring high editing accuracy and unequivocal sign determination of the homonuclear long-range relative to the associated one-bond coupling constant. The sensitivity of the new experiment is comparable to that of regular edited HMBC and the accuracy of the J/RDC measurement is as usual for E.COSY and S3-type experiments independent of the size of the homonuclear coupling constant of interest. The merits of the method are demonstrated by an application to strychnine where thirteen JHH coupling constants not previously reported could be measured.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kjærulff, Louise","Benie, Andrew J.","Hoeck, Casper","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Sørensen, Ole W."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-341056"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["HMBC","J coupling constants","RDC","Small molecules"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-NOVO","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"s sup 000000000003 sup hmbc spin state selective hmbc for accurate measurement of homonuclear coupling constants application to strychnine yielding thirteen hitherto unreported jhh","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84954515795","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-341056","identifier":[{"id":"84954515795","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26774647","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-7a3db2c4-c785-47e1-a569-441e13cf3dac"],"keyword":["HMBC","J coupling constants","RDC","S3 HMBC","Small molecules"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B666A060E66D41D1CA5254086164F363"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, Organic Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-NOVO","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk Foundation","namevar":["Novo Nordisk Foundation"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"kjaerulffpau","last":"Kjaerulff","locid":"840d3acf-77d5-4323-84ed-14a6ff8aabfc","name":"Kjærulff, Louise","name_org":"Kjaerulff, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew J.","key":"beniepau","last":"Benie","name":"Benie, Andrew J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Casper","key":"hoeckpau","last":"Hoeck","locid":"b0666407-58d2-4154-bec3-3c1d14be9f4a","name":"Hoeck, Casper","orcid":"0000-0001-5372-9821","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Held","key":"gotfredsenpau","last":"Gotfredsen","locid":"1cf4df84-2d0e-4693-bf47-e9932e3bf0e3","name":"Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","orcid":"0000-0002-7386-119X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole W.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"7b2b9372-1af4-432b-8994-12b1f6faa56b","name":"Sørensen, Ole W.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26774647"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmr.2015.11.007","issn":["10907807","10960856"],"issn_org":["10907807"],"journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","pages":"101-107","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","volume":"263"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84954515795"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7a3db2c4-c785-47e1-a569-441e13cf3dac"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"S<sup>3</sup> HMBC: Spin-State-Selective HMBC for accurate measurement of homonuclear coupling constants. Application to strychnine yielding thirteen hitherto unreported JHH","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-341056","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Lauritzen, Lotte","Sørensen, Louise Bergmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-513182"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ernæringens betydning for børns kognition og indlæring","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-513182","ids":["ku-c88dc43c-411b-4658-b112-9dd51130120b"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-33B292F35B1AE7EA68F8025C4091A254"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Lifecourse Nutrition & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte","key":"lauritzenpau","last":"Lauritzen","locid":"4263561d-003a-4d4c-9f05-06a8f88155e8","name":"Lauritzen, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0001-7184-5949","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Bergmann","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"b86d9af7-ea09-4925-a863-eadc0c0e26ee","name":"Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Rikke","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sanna","key":"fiskerpedh","last":"Fisker","name":"Fisker, Sanna","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788762814585"],"pages":"212-222","place":"København","publisher":"Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Livscyklusernæring"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c88dc43c-411b-4658-b112-9dd51130120b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ernæringens betydning for børns kognition og indlæring","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-513182","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"We examined fat-independent associations of hormones with height and whole-body bone size and mineral content in 633 school children. IGF-1 and osteocalcin predict growth in height, while fat, osteocalcin, and in girls also, IGF-1 predict growth in bone size. Leptin and ghrelin are inversely associated with bone size in girls. INTRODUCTION: Obesity causes larger bone size and bone mass, but the role of hormones in this up-regulation of bone in obesity is not well elucidated. We examined longitudinal associations between baseline body fat mass (FM), and fat-independent fasting levels of ghrelin, adiponectin, leptin, insulin, insulin-like growth factor-I (IGF-1), osteocalcin, and intact parathyroid hormone, and subsequent changes in height and in whole-body height-adjusted bone area \"BAheight\" and size-adjusted bone mineral content \"BMCsize\" in 8- to 11-year-olds. METHODS: Analyses were carried out separately for boys (n = 325) and girls (n = 308) including data from baseline, 3 and 6 months from OPUS School Meal Study. RESULTS: In both sexes: gain in BAheight was positively associated with baseline FM (≥2.05 cm(2)/kg, both p ≤ 0.003). Furthermore, gain in height was positively associated with baseline IGF-1 (≥0.02 cm/ng/ml, p = 0.001) and osteocalcin (≥0.13 cm/ng/ml, p ≤ 0.009); and gain in BAheight was positively associated with baseline osteocalcin (≥0.35 cm(2)/ng/ml, p ≤ 0.019). In girls only, gain in BAheight was also positively associated with baseline IGF-1 (0.06 cm(2)/ng/ml, p = 0.017) and inversely associated with both baseline ghrelin (-0.01 cm(2)/pg/ml, p = 0.001) and leptin (-1.21 cm(2)/μg/ml, p = 0.005). In boys, gain in BMCsize was positively associated with osteocalcin (0.18 g/ng/ml, p = 0.030). CONCLUSIONS: This large longitudinal study suggests that in 8- to 11-year-old children, IGF-1 and osteocalcin predict growth in height, while FM, osteocalcin, and in girls also, IGF-1 predict growth in BAheight. Fat-independent inverse associations of leptin and ghrelin with BAheight in girls' are contrary to proposed growth-stimulating effects of leptin. Osteocalcin in boys predicts gain in BMCsize.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Dalskov, Stine-Mathilde","Ritz, Christian","Larnkjær, Anni","Damsgaard, Camilla Trab","Petersen, Rikke Agnete","Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","Ong, Ken K","Astrup, Arne","Michaelsen, Kim F.","Mølgaard, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518030"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations between adiposity hormones and gains in height whole body height adjusted bone size and size adjusted bone mineral content in 000000000008 to 000000000011 year old children","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-518030","identifier":[{"id":"26667245","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84961138180","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d08bdfb8-ef9f-4a27-a7fc-5bd1a33552b2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A47D52C447521A550D82D4104A7136D3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Lifecourse Nutrition & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stine-Mathilde","key":"dalskovpau","last":"Dalskov","locid":"56222bcb-fb52-4111-8cfa-0264a3fef7e5","name":"Dalskov, Stine-Mathilde","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"ritzpau","last":"Ritz","locid":"c881424f-d529-443e-b60e-bc2edb674ede","name":"Ritz, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5095-0624","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anni","key":"larnkjærpau","last":"Larnkjær","locid":"988a7c84-01db-4679-8549-d375f2f92cd1","name":"Larnkjær, Anni","orcid":"0000-0002-7790-7888","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Trab","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","locid":"5ea9cc09-17f1-46a3-9e4e-fa5490abd815","name":"Damsgaard, Camilla Trab","orcid":"0000-0002-5013-0562","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke Agnete","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"7ec167a6-8982-42dc-87de-53c245802653","name":"Petersen, Rikke Agnete","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Bergmann","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"b86d9af7-ea09-4925-a863-eadc0c0e26ee","name":"Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ken K","key":"ongpau","last":"Ong","name":"Ong, Ken K","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"5d943631-c9fc-4b63-8aaa-263ba4248735","name":"Astrup, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-8968-8996","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim F.","key":"michaelsenpau","last":"Michaelsen","locid":"c29a2565-4c7e-4a5b-ab39-899baedae963","name":"Michaelsen, Kim F.","orcid":"0000-0003-0449-0839","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"mølgaardpau","last":"Mølgaard","locid":"240d0bd3-4221-4d27-bfdb-8fd6887cdb30","name":"Mølgaard, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5311-9457","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26667245"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00198-015-3428-z","issn":["0937941X","14332965"],"issn_org":["0937941X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Osteoporosis International","pages":"1619-1629","status":"p","title":"Osteoporosis International","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961138180"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d08bdfb8-ef9f-4a27-a7fc-5bd1a33552b2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Associations between adiposity, hormones, and gains in height, whole-body height-adjusted bone size, and size-adjusted bone mineral content in 8- to 11-year-old children","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518030","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
