{"abstract":"DNA origami provides rapid access to easily functionalized, nanometer-sized structures making it an intriguing platform for the development of defined drug delivery and sensor systems. Low cellular uptake of DNA nanostructures is a major obstacle in the development of DNA-based delivery platforms. Herein, significant strong increase in cellular uptake in an established cancer cell line by modifying a planar DNA origami structure with the iron transport protein transferrin (Tf) is demonstrated. A variable number of Tf molecules are coupled to the origami structure using a DNA-directed, site-selective labeling technique to retain ligand functionality. A combination of confocal fluorescence microscopy and quantitative (qPCR) techniques shows up to 22-fold increased cytoplasmic uptake compared to unmodified structures and with an efficiency that correlates to the number of transferrin molecules on the origami surface.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Schaffert, David Henning","Okholm, Anders Hauge","Sørensen, Rasmus Schøler","Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","Tørring, Thomas","Rosen, Christian Bech","Kodal, Anne Louise Bank","Mortensen, Michael Rosholm","Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager","Kjems, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-246757"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intracellular delivery of a planar dna origami structure by the transferrin receptor internalization pathway","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84979490376","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-246757","identifier":[{"id":"27032044","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84979490376","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cd6eed6e-eba8-4559-a30d-ab450fc75ea3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DAD65E0DDC2DC3E9AFC360A0CD8709B0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David Henning","key":"schaffertpau","last":"Schaffert","locid":"680e746e-7ceb-488c-af97-2385ce6479d3","name":"Schaffert, David Henning","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Hauge","key":"okholmpau","last":"Okholm","locid":"f264fed0-c43e-4f71-843a-7787595ad043","name":"Okholm, Anders Hauge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Schøler","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"dd13ff30-6bd7-4512-bc60-efa5c5b0ebdd","name":"Sørensen, Rasmus Schøler","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"721272e9-869d-48f0-b183-980b58848b68","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"tørringpau","last":"Tørring","locid":"b03df36b-0252-4e5a-aeee-7113f77cad12","name":"Tørring, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-5257-2121","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Bech","key":"rosenpau","last":"Rosen","locid":"90fa292f-d20b-421f-8c8e-e7df0ffcf3eb","name":"Rosen, Christian Bech","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Louise Bank","key":"kodalpau","last":"Kodal","locid":"765efe10-0aa6-4d31-9803-fb5e322fcf3e","name":"Kodal, Anne Louise Bank","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Rosholm","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"89380d2c-7022-4063-bce8-c6a92811aebd","name":"Mortensen, Michael Rosholm","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kurt Vesterager","key":"gothelfpau","last":"Gothelf","locid":"8ca43d09-e887-432e-8775-ab2f38db1e6d","name":"Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager","orcid":"0000-0003-2399-3757","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"kjemspau","last":"Kjems","locid":"f5915d75-aca3-437a-9a9d-f4fdfef7accd","name":"Kjems, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-9317","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27032044"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/smll.201503934","issn":["16136810","16136829"],"issn_org":["16136810"],"issue":"19","journal":"Small","pages":"2634-2640","publisher":"Wiley-VCH Verlag","status":"p","title":"Small","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979490376"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cd6eed6e-eba8-4559-a30d-ab450fc75ea3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Intracellular Delivery of a Planar DNA Origami Structure by the Transferrin-Receptor Internalization Pathway","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-246757","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"DTU Space have collected surface elevation observations of the Arctic sea ice and land ice since 1998 using laser scanning and radar altimetry from a small fixed‐wing Twin‐Otter aircraft. The observations provide unique datasets for studying ongoing changes, and support the analysis of satellite measurements of ice sheet changes. The majority of the campaigns have been sponsored by the European Space Agency, ESA, as part of the CryoSat Validation Experiments – CryoVEx. These have been internationally coordinated efforts to collect coincident space‐borne, airborne, and in‐situ data for pre‐ and post‐launch validation studies, with several aircraft and international in‐situ ground teams participating, both in Greenland, Arctic Canada, and Svalbard. The methods and campaigns are outlined together with examples of results.The campaigns focused on five main validation sites: Devon ice cap (Canada), Austfonna ice cap (Svalbard), the EGIG line crossing the Greenland Ice Sheet, as well as the sea ice north of Alert and sea ice around Svalbard in the Fram Strait. Selected tracks were planned to match CryoSat‐2 passes and a few of them were flown in formation flight with the Alfred Wegener Institute (AWI) Polar‐5 carrying an EM‐bird. The poster will outline the methods and campaigns, as well as show examples of the results.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","Skourup, Henriette","Forsberg, René","Nielsen, Jens Emil","Olesen, Arne Vestergaard","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Davidson, Malcolm","Casal, Tania"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343679"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-13","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2016-05-09","title":"ESA Living Planet Symposium 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Space Agency - ESA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"airborne observations of changes of ice sheet and sea ice in the arctic using cryovex campaign data","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session185.php#490p","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343679","ids":["dtu-82fad4d5-c3a8-4a8a-a382-bf6afe2dd802"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-004406C459113526B4F5ED05C6789E02"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lps16.esa.int/page_session185.php#490p","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"european space agency esa","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"European Space Agency - ESA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sine Munk","key":"hvidegaardpau","last":"Hvidegaard","locid":"92b07d8f-692c-4ebb-bc40-f44224f3f143","name":"Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","orcid":"0000-0001-8159-6499","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette","key":"skouruppau","last":"Skourup","locid":"f5fe613f-20e5-4a69-9eff-f03779801182","name":"Skourup, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-4468-8033","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Emil","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c1ed0703-31fb-4d2b-8c22-eb1566cb603f","name":"Nielsen, Jens Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-8422-6901","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Arne Vestergaard","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"113a87aa-f48a-4bcd-802f-b63662d87564","name":"Olesen, Arne Vestergaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9555-9787","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Malcolm","key":"davidsonpau","last":"Davidson","name":"Davidson, Malcolm","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tania","key":"casalpau","last":"Casal","name":"Casal, Tania","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-82fad4d5-c3a8-4a8a-a382-bf6afe2dd802"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Airborne observations of changes of ice sheet and sea ice in the Arctic using CryoVEx campaign data","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343679","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A new methodology for retrieval of glacier and ice sheet elevations and elevation changes from CryoSat-2 data is presented. Surface elevations and elevation changes determined using this approach show significant improvements over ESA's publicly available CryoSat-2 elevation product (L2 Baseline-B). The results are compared to near-coincident airborne laser altimetry from NASA's Operation IceBridge and seasonal height amplitudes from the Ice, Cloud, and Elevation Satellite (ICESat). Applying this methodology to CryoSat-2 data collected in interferometric synthetic aperture mode (SIN) over the high-relief regions of the Greenland Ice Sheet we find an improvement in the root-mean-square error (RMSE) of 27 and 40% compared to ESA's L2 product in the derived elevation and elevation changes, respectively. In the interior part of the ice sheet, where CryoSat-2 operates in low-resolution mode (LRM), we find an improvement in the RMSE of 68 and 55% in the derived elevation and elevation changes, respectively. There is also an 86% improvement in the magnitude of the seasonal amplitudes when compared to amplitudes derived from ICESat data. These results indicate that the new methodology provides improved tracking of the snow/ice surface with lower sensitivity to changes in near-surface dielectric properties. To demonstrate the utility of the new processing methodology we produce elevations, elevation changes, and total volume changes from CryoSat-2 data for the Greenland Ice Sheet during the period January 2011 to January 2015. We find that the Greenland Ice Sheet decreased in volume at a rate of 289 ± 20km3 a-1, with high interannual variability and spatial heterogeneity in rates of loss. This rate is 65km3 a-1 more negative than rates determined from ESA's L2 product, highlighting the importance of CryoSat-2 processing methodologies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nilsson, Johan","Gardner, Alex","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Forsberg, René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360278"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","California Institute of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved retrieval of land ice topography from cryosat 000000000002 data and its impact for volume change estimation of the greenland ice sheet","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127858023/tc_10_2953_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-360278","identifier":[{"id":"85002323059","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ba584952-c3de-4b93-b535-01a9f5644e0b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1D0D6AEBE80AA536DC1CA66D9FA3AC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127858023/tc_10_2953_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"california institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"California Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Johan","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","name":"Nilsson, Johan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alex","key":"gardnerpau","last":"Gardner","name":"Gardner, Alex","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/tc-10-2953-2016","issn":["19940416","19940424"],"issn_org":["19940416"],"issue":"6","journal":"Cryosphere","pages":"2953-2969","publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","status":"p","title":"Cryosphere","title_org":"The Cryosphere","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85002323059"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ba584952-c3de-4b93-b535-01a9f5644e0b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improved retrieval of land ice topography from CryoSat-2 data and its impact for volume-change estimation of the Greenland Ice Sheet","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-360278","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Birth weight (BW) has been shown to be influenced by both fetal and maternal factors and in observational studies is reproducibly associated with future risk of adult metabolic diseases including type 2 diabetes (T2D) and cardiovascular disease. These life-course associations have often been attributed to the impact of an adverse early life environment. Here, we performed a multi-ancestry genome-wide association study (GWAS) meta-analysis of BW in 153,781 individuals, identifying 60 loci where fetal genotype was associated with BW (P < 5 × 10(-8)). Overall, approximately 15% of variance in BW was captured by assays of fetal genetic variation. Using genetic association alone, we found strong inverse genetic correlations between BW and systolic blood pressure (Rg = -0.22, P = 5.5 × 10(-13)), T2D (Rg = -0.27, P = 1.1 × 10(-6)) and coronary artery disease (Rg = -0.30, P = 6.5 × 10(-9)). In addition, using large -cohort datasets, we demonstrated that genetic factors were the major contributor to the negative covariance between BW and future cardiometabolic risk. Pathway analyses indicated that the protein products of genes within BW-associated regions were enriched for diverse processes including insulin signalling, glucose homeostasis, glycogen biosynthesis and chromatin remodelling. There was also enrichment of associations with BW in known imprinted regions (P = 1.9 × 10(-4)). We demonstrate that life-course associations between early growth phenotypes and adult cardiometabolic disease are in part the result of shared genetic effects and identify some of the pathways through which these causal genetic effects are mediated.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Horikoshi, Momoko","Beaumont, Robin N","Day, Felix R","Warrington, Nicole M","Kooijman, Marjolein N","Fernandez-Tajes, Juan","Feenstra, Bjarke","van Zuydam, Natalie R","Gaulton, Kyle J","Grarup, Niels","Bradfield, Jonathan P","Strachan, David P","Li-Gao, Ruifang","Ahluwalia, Tarun Veer Singh","Kreiner, Eskil","Rueedi, Rico","Lyytikäinen, Leo-Pekka","Cousminer, Diana L","Wu, Ying","Thiering, Elisabeth","Wang, Carol A","Have, Christian Theil","Hottenga, Jouke-Jan","Vilor-Tejedor, Natalia","Joshi, Peter K","Boh, Eileen Tai Hui","Ntalla, Ioanna","Pitkänen, Niina","Mahajan, Anubha","van Leeuwen, Elisabeth M","Joro, Raimo","Lagou, Vasiliki","Nodzenski, Michael","Diver, Louise A","Zondervan, Krina T","Bustamante, Mariona","Marques-Vidal, Pedro","Mercader, Josep M","Appel, Emil Vincent Rosenbaum","Waage, Johannes","Sørensen, Thorkild I A","Melbye, Mads","Kadarmideen, Haja","Holm, Jens-Christian","Hansen, Torben","Bønnelykke, Klaus","Bisgaard, Hans","Pisinger, Charlotta","Pedersen, Oluf","Vaag, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-433144"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["CHARGE Consortium Hematology Working Group"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide associations for birth weight and correlations with adult disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-433144","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5164934","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27680694","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84991665514","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-42769b1e-80e0-4344-86c7-eb8f68bfd04e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-26A9023CC25FEB188F7C0134E7959164"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Grarup Group","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Human Genomics and Metagenomics in Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"charge consortium hematology working group","name":"CHARGE Consortium Hematology Working Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Momoko","key":"horikoshipau","last":"Horikoshi","name":"Horikoshi, Momoko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Robin N","key":"beaumontpau","last":"Beaumont","name":"Beaumont, Robin N","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Felix R","key":"daypau","last":"Day","name":"Day, Felix R","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicole M","key":"warringtonpau","last":"Warrington","name":"Warrington, Nicole M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marjolein N","key":"kooijmanpau","last":"Kooijman","name":"Kooijman, Marjolein N","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan","key":"fernandeztajespau","last":"Fernandez-Tajes","name":"Fernandez-Tajes, Juan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bjarke","key":"feenstrapau","last":"Feenstra","name":"Feenstra, Bjarke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Natalie R","key":"vanzuydampau","last":"van Zuydam","name":"van Zuydam, Natalie R","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kyle J","key":"gaultonpau","last":"Gaulton","name":"Gaulton, Kyle J","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"graruppau","last":"Grarup","locid":"824a7159-a059-4de1-bf3f-e116ef59e0de","name":"Grarup, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5526-1070","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonathan P","key":"bradfieldpau","last":"Bradfield","name":"Bradfield, Jonatha