en, Michael","orcid":"0000-0001-6089-9781","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Heidi Amalie Rosendahl","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e4859f19-a267-4bdc-9588-8a48889704bd","name":"Jensen, Heidi Amalie Rosendahl","orcid":"0000-0001-7171-7429","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie Thorning","key":"rydpau","last":"Ryd","locid":"94ecab58-53bc-4be8-80ec-127fd7a33fe0","name":"Ryd, Julie Thorning","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leise","key":"strøbækpau","last":"Strøbæk","locid":"4e2f4047-e8a7-4b07-93d8-0965f0348fd7","name":"Strøbæk, Leise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emily Dibba","key":"whitepau","last":"White","locid":"81de8c54-4a1e-4e36-9cde-aefac1ea566c","name":"Dibba, Emily Petros","name_org":"White, Emily Dibba","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Jan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud","key":"juelpau","last":"Juel","locid":"95a22bf7-54de-48e0-ab33-855002b210be","name":"Juel, Knud","orcid":"0000-0002-4134-1173","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771047929"],"pages":"396","place":"København","publisher":"Sundhedsstyrelsen","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ec8e099b-1c2f-43f2-a8d9-942b95507cf0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sygdomsbyrden i Danmark : Risikofaktorer","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-640972","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"I efteråret 2015 gennemførte Lederforeningen i DSR og DSR’s analyseafdeling en landsdækkende spørgeskemaundersøgelse om ledende sygeplejerskers arbejdsliv. Formålet var at få øget viden om ledende sygeplejerskers arbejdsmiljø og ledelsesvilkår. Dette notat dykker ned i den del af undersøgelsen, der kigger på sammenhænge mellem sygeplejerskernes jobtilfredshed og deres oplevelse af ledelsesvilkår i form af arbejdspres, klarhed om ledelsesrollen, modstridende forventninger og klare mål for arbejdet. Notatet ser også på, om der er sammenhænge med lederanciennitet, placering i ledelseshierarkiet med eller uden ledere under sig, samt om deres ansættelsessted er i kommuner eller regioner.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Holm-Petersen, Christina","Sørensen, Louise Kryspin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-662301"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ledende sygeplejerskers jobtilfredshed set i relation til deres ledelsesvilkår i form af arbejdspres og klarhed om roller forventninger og mål","src":["vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/2033683/rapport-ledende-sygeplejerskers-jobtilfredshed.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-662301","ids":["vive-0e544be4-a11a-4d18-88b0-d1ffdb49aa10"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-94E5F7CB86DF03FE1359E016CA00D080"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/2033683/rapport-ledende-sygeplejerskers-jobtilfredshed.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["VIVE - The Danish Center for Social Science Research, VIVE Governance and Management"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christina","key":"holmpetersenpau","last":"Holm-Petersen","locid":"46bd96cc-a8b5-4d71-bc3e-da488711cc13","name":"Holm-Petersen, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Kryspin","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Louise Kryspin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Lederforeningen, Dansk Sygeplejeråd","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["vive-0e544be4-a11a-4d18-88b0-d1ffdb49aa10"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Ledende sygeplejerskers jobtilfredshed : Set i relation til deres ledelsesvilkår i form af arbejdspres og klarhed om roller, forventninger og mål","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-662301","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: Integration of physical activity (PA) into the classroom may be an effective way of promoting the learning and academic achievement of children at elementary school. This paper describes the research design and methodology of an intervention study examining the effect of classroom-based PA on mathematical achievement, creativity, executive function, body mass index and aerobic fitness. Methods: The study was designed as a school-based cluster-randomized controlled trial targeting schoolchildren in 1st grade, and was carried out between August 2012 and June 2013. Eligible schools in two municipalities in the Region of Southern Denmark were invited to participate in the study. After stratification by municipality, twelve schools were randomized to either an intervention group or a control group, comprising a total of 505 children with mean age 7.2 ± 0.3 years. The intervention was a 9-month classroom-based PA program that involved integration of PA into the math lessons delivered by the schools' math teachers. The primary study outcome was change in math achievement, measured by a 45-minute standardized math test. Secondary outcomes were change in executive function (using a modified Eriksen flanker task and the Behavior Rating Inventory of Executive Function (BRIEF) questionnaire filled out by the parents), creativity (using the Torrance Tests of Creative Thinking, TTCT), aerobic fitness (by the Andersen intermittent shuttle-run test) and body mass index. PA during math lessons and total PA (including time spent outside school) were assessed using accelerometry. Math teachers used Short Message Service (SMS)-tracking to report on compliance with the PA intervention and on their motivation for implementing PA in math lessons. Parents used SMS-tracking to register their children's PA behavior in leisure time. Discussion: The results of this randomized controlled trial are expected to provide schools and policy-makers with significant new insights into the potential of classroom-based PA to improve cognition and academic achievement in children. Trial registration: Clinicaltrials.gov: NCT02488460 (06/29/2015)","author_count":11,"contributors":["Have, Mona","Nielsen, Jacob Have","Gejl, Anne Kær","Thomsen Ernst, Martin","Fredens, Kjeld","Støckel, Jan Toftegaard","Wedderkopp, Niels","Domazet, Sidsel Louise","Gudex, Claire","Grøntved, Anders","Kristensen, Peter Lund"],"cuid":["S02-096.72-001625"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Have, Mona"],"keyword":["Academic achievement","Classroom based PA","Embodied cognition","Executive functions","Methods","RCT","School children"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rationale and design of a randomized controlled trial examining the effect of classroom based physical activity on math achievement","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-016-2971-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.72-001625","identifier":[{"id":"84963831020","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000373711600002","type":"wos"},{"id":"27068574","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4827169","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-203eab71-d616-4e5c-bf50-e68c378f4696","sdu-d8c8939f-1339-466c-b6f2-7c8bd9adf241"],"keyword":["Academic achievement","Classroom-based PA","Embodied cognition","Executive Functions","Methods","RCT","School children"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F8FD4FFE642225AEBA4482B93AD8F2F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-016-2971-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129522928/Rationale_and_design_of_a_randomized_controlled_trial_examining_the_effect_of_classroom_based_physical_activity_on_math_achievement.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, RICH - Research In Childhood Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, reCreate - Research Center for Creative and Immersive Learning Environments (Learning)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mona Have","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1ba6651e-b2fa-4de5-80e8-2aa9c1365966","name":"Sørensen, Mona Have","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Have","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"60dbd694-056c-423f-8146-ec9e56361639","name":"Nielsen, Jacob Have","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Kær","key":"gejlpau","last":"Gejl","locid":"275fae7f-a794-4f46-b268-8a68caf1c8ab","name":"Gejl, Anne Kær","orcid":"0000-0001-6781-2263","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Thomsen","key":"ernstpau","last":"Ernst","locid":"8ff79b27-ae57-47dd-b099-4c3f53d10528","name":"Ernst, Martin Thomsen","orcid":"0000-0001-9003-3823","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"fredenspau","last":"Fredens","locid":"095edd9c-1868-417e-b9ea-cc02690e435e","name":"Fredens, Kjeld","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Toftegaard","key":"støckelpau","last":"Støckel","locid":"b4917a37-7c99-483e-921e-53a102ef1941","name":"Støckel, Jan Toftegaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2471-8549","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"wedderkopppau","last":"Wedderkopp","locid":"bcfae344-0a75-458d-8ba2-4198ee915d40","name":"Wedderkopp, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-9660-6618","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sidsel Louise","key":"domazetpau","last":"Domazet","locid":"bc55ec0f-c267-4f39-b481-130141c0177f","name":"Domazet, Sidsel Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3128-1875","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claire","key":"gudexpau","last":"Gudex","locid":"f3926977-0fd9-4dc0-9456-8baf5c4ffafe","name":"Gudex, Claire","orcid":"0000-0003-3881-9890","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"grøntvedpau","last":"Grøntved","locid":"393b1ca1-e658-437c-9ca3-73aea925ad58","name":"Grøntved, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1584-679X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Lund","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"751d26de-66d4-4ef9-8183-880c48c96dc7","name":"Kristensen, Peter Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-5666-9614","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27068574"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12889-016-2971-7","issn":["14712458"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Public Health","paperid":"304","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Public Health","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963831020"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-203eab71-d616-4e5c-bf50-e68c378f4696","sdu-d8c8939f-1339-466c-b6f2-7c8bd9adf241"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Rationale and design of a randomized controlled trial examining the effect of classroom-based physical activity on math achievement","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.72-001625","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background/objectives Aside from the health consequences, observational studies indicate that being overweight may also negatively affect cognitive function. However, existing evidence has to a large extent not controlled for the possible confounding effect of having different lifestyles. Therefore, the objective was to examine the independent associations between weight status and lifestyle indicators with cognitive performance in 8–11 year old Danish children. Subjects/methods The analyses included 828 children (measured in 2011–2012) each having one to three measurement occasions separated by approximately 100 days. Dietary intake, physical activity, sedentary time, and sleep duration were measured using dietary records and accelerometers. The Children's Sleep Habits Questionnaire was used to access sleep problems and the Andersen test was carried out to estimate cardio-respiratory fitness (CRF). Weight status (underweight, normal weight, and overweight/obese) was defined according to body mass index and cognitive performance was assessed using the d2-test of attention, a reading test, and a math test. A linear mixed model including a number of fixed and random effects was used to test associations between lifestyle indicators as well as BMI category and cognitive performance. Results After adjustment for demographics, socioeconomics, and multiple lifestyle indicators, normal weight children had higher cognitive test scores than overweight/obese and underweight children of up to 89% and 48% of expected learning within one school year (P < 0.05). Daily breakfast consumption, fewer sleep problems, higher CRF, less total physical activity, more sedentary time, and less light physical activity were associated with higher cognitive performance independently of each other in at least one of the three cognitive tests (P < 0.05). Conclusions Normal weight children had higher cognitive performance compared to overweight/obese as well as underweight children, independent of multiple lifestyle indicators.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Dyssegaard, Camilla Brørup","Egelund, Niels","Hjorth, Mads Fiil","Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","Andersen, Rikke","Ritz, Christian","Tetens, Inge","Michaelsen, Kim F","Astrup, Arne","Sjödin, Anders Mikael"],"cuid":["S03-097.68-026976"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Behavior","Behavioral Neuroscience","Børnekultur","Cognitive performance","Diet","Experimental and Cognitive Psychology","Hverdagsliv","Læring","Overweight","Philosophy","Physical activity","Pædagogisk psykologi","Sleep"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"normal weight children have higher cognitive performance independent of physical activity sleep and diet","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84984823934","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.68-026976","identifier":[{"id":"84984823934","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27570193","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c560aa4e-3190-4779-ab4c-b80cd0d85eae","dtu-4defe94e-55a7-45c2-9072-1c68c0464d4c","ku-a04588e5-6ab8-4eb8-94fd-e7c7fc7c2a93"],"keyword":["Behavior","Behavioral Neuroscience","Børnekultur","Cognitive performance","Diet","Experimental and Cognitive Psychology","Hverdagsliv","Læring","Overweight","Philosophy","Physical activity","Pædagogisk psykologi","sleep"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-F175C7256CDE88A5A917312A8AAE9382"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPu