{"abstract":"Children's vitamin D intake can be optimized to meet recommendations. We investigated if nutritionally balanced school meals with weekly fish servings affected serum 25-hydroxuvitamin D and markers related to bone in 8-11-year-old Danish children. A cluster-randomized cross-over trial with secondary outcome analyses from the OPUS School Meal Study.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Petersen, Rikke Agnete","Damsgaard, Camilla T","Dalskov, Stine-Mathilde","Sørensen, Louise B","Hjorth, Mads Fiil","Andersen, Rikke","Tetens, Inge","Krarup, Henrik","Ritz, Christian","Astrup, Arne","F. Michaelsen, Kim","Mølgaard, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-649294"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Children","Nutrition","School meals","Vitamin D"],"level":"sci","oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of school meals with weekly fish servings on vitamin d status in danish children secondary outcomes from the opus school meal study","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/jns.2015.15","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-649294","identifier":[{"id":"84994560210","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ucl-c946b0af-7121-4098-9e44-ade849b704f9"],"keyword":["Children","School Meals","Vitamin D","nutrition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Global-Local-3-7-DBF2BB3152770BF8014C6714B62D8DD1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucl.dk/ws/files/33442191/Petersen_et_al_2015_Effects_of_school_meals_with_weekly_fish_servings_on_vitamin_D_status.pdf","version":"Publish