121-4098-9e44-ade849b704f9"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Effects of school meals with weekly fish servings on vitamin D status in Danish children: secondary outcomes from the OPUS School Meal Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-649294","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT: Blooms of the marine dictyochophyte Pseudochattonella farcimen have been Associated with fish kills, but attempts to verify ichthyotoxicity of this microalga under experimental conditions have not been successful. In the early spring of 2009 and 2011, P. farcimen bloomed in the inner Danish waters. The blooms occurred at a seawater temperature of ~2°C and correlated with extensive kills of farmed salmonid fish (2009) and wild populations (2011). Several strains of P. farcimen were isolated from the 2009 bloom. However, exposure of rainbow trout Oncorhynchus mykiss to laboratory-grown P. farcimen cultures did not reveal any toxic effects. During the 2011 bloom, fish were exposed to bloom water under both laboratory and field conditions. While no clinical effect was observed on fish incubated in bloom water in the aboratory trial, a remarkable difference was seen in the field trial between rainbow trout kept in tanks supplied with a continuous flow of filtered versus non-filtered bloom water. Histological examination of the gill tissue revealed karyorrhexis and epithelial loosening in the affected fish. Microscopy analysis of algal cell morphology suggested that mucocysts detected on the cell surface only in freshly sampled bloom water might be associated with ichtyotoxicity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Andersen, Nikolaj Gedsted","Hansen, Per Juel","Engell-Sørensen, Kirsten","Nørremark, Louise Hjorth","Andersen, Per","Lorenzen, Ellen","Lorenzen, Niels"],"cuid":["S02-099.78-018004"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Harmful algae","Pseudochattonella farcimen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-WSP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-WSP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ichthyotoxicity of the microalga em pseudochattonella farcimen em under laboratory and field conditions in danish waters","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3354/dao02916","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.78-018004","identifier":[{"id":"84946016825","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26503770","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-49789d1f-d2eb-4a41-9683-0f4da27a90b1","ku-46671580-e71f-4b83-905a-0911997d164a"],"keyword":["Dictyochophytes","Harmful algae","Ichthyotoxicity","Mucocysts","Pseudochattonella farcimen"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E01E860965E38E105643F162F03B895B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3354/dao02916","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Marine Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Fishlab"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"wsp danmark","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-WSP","l3nl":"WSP Danmark A/S","l3nn":"WSP Danmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"WSP Danmark","namevar":["Orbicon"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-WSP","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nikolaj Gedsted","key":"andersennikolajgedstedpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"98400236-5e22-4bcc-a520-43ba77f3af7c","name":"Andersen, Nikolaj Gedsted","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per Juel","key":"hansenperjuelpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5484a61d-edd3-4242-8267-e66e5b4aed4e","name":"Hansen, Per Juel","orcid":"0000-0003-0228-9621","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"engellsørensenkirstenpau","last":"Engell-Sørensen","name":"Engell-Sørensen, Kirsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Hjorth","key":"nørremarklouisehjorthpau","last":"Nørremark","name":"Nørremark, Louise Hjorth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"andersenperpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Per","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellen","key":"lorenzenellenpau","last":"Lorenzen","locid":"d2880b21-e9a7-4e69-9b67-1151ca30b23f","name":"Lorenzen, Ellen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"lorenzennielspau","last":"Lorenzen","locid":"392bd7b0-ffa8-4227-923c-f5d043e76fd2","name":"Lorenzen, Niels","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26503770"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3354/dao02916","issn":["01775103","16161580"],"issn_org":["01775103"],"issue":"3","journal":"Diseases of Aquatic Organisms","pages":"165-172","publisher":"Inter-Research","status":"p","title":"Diseases of Aquatic Organisms","volume":"116"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84946016825"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","WSP Danmark A/S","fishlab"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-49789d1f-d2eb-4a41-9683-0f4da27a90b1","ku-46671580-e71f-4b83-905a-0911997d164a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ichthyotoxicity of the microalga Pseudochattonella farcimen under laboratory and field conditions in Danish waters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.78-018004","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: We aimed to investigate the impact of hyponatremia severity on mortality risk and assess any evidence of a dose-response relation, utilizing prospectively collected data from population-based registries. DESIGN: Cohort study of 279 508 first-time acute admissions to Departments of Internal Medicine in the North and Central Denmark Regions from 2006 to 2011. METHODS: We used the Kaplan-Meier method (1 - survival function) to compute 30-day and 1-year mortality in patients with normonatremia and categories of increasing hyponatremia severity. Relative risks (RRs) with 95% CIs, adjusted for age, gender and previous morbidities, and stratified by clinical subgroups were estimated by the pseudo-value approach. The probability of death was estimated treating serum sodium as a continuous variable. RESULTS: The prevalence of admission hyponatremia was 15% (41 803 patients). Thirty-day mortality was 3.6% in normonatremic patients compared to 7.3, 10.0, 10.4 and 9.6% in patients with serum sodium levels of 130-134.9, 125-129.9, 120-124.9 and <120 mmol/l, resulting in adjusted RRs of 1.4 (95% CI: 1.3-1.4), 1.7 (95% CI: 1.6-1.8), 1.7 (95% CI: 1.4-1.9) and 1.3 (95% CI: 1.1-1.5) respectively. Mortality risk was increased across virtually all clinical subgroups, and remained increased by 30-40% 1 year after admission. The probability of death increased when serum sodium decreased from 139 to 132 mmol/l. No clear increase in mortality was observed for lower concentrations. CONCLUSIONS: Hyponatremia is highly prevalent among patients admitted to Departments of Internal Medicine and is associated with increased 30-day and 1-year mortality risk, regardless of underlying disease. This risk seems independent of hyponatremia severity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Holland-Bill, Louise","Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","Heide-Jørgensen, Uffe","Ulrichsen, Sinna Pilgaard","Ring, Troels","Jørgensen, Jens Otto L","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-008542"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyponatremia and mortality risk a danish cohort study of 000000000279 000000000508 acutely hospitalized patients","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EJE-15-0111","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-008542","identifier":[{"id":"26036812","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84935082158","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000358947700016","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-b1396c64-196a-4708-9011-88878b0f4394","au-7748bcc6-6bb6-4576-ba3a-be4207960141"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6F32558D1C99101780DCA95FF9BEBA61"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EJE-15-0111","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinical Skills Laboratory","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","n