{"abstract":"Engelsk version af Pernille Welents, Tine Eibyes og mit undervisningsmateriale, oversat og taget i anvendelse af Slingsby Theatre Company i Australien","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, Louise Ejgod","Welent Sørensen, Pernille","Eibye, Tine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-185854"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experiencing theatre and drama developing a space for communication with children and young people","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.slingsby.net.au/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/Experiencing-Drama-and-Theatre.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-185854","ids":["au-62ff9121-62f4-41f6-a60a-3cfcd2931cfc"],"lang":"English","level":"Educational","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-66CE87986148CD81E95F6058291970D6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.slingsby.net.au/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/Experiencing-Drama-and-Theatre.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Dramaturgy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise Ejgod","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"a2ffe90e-58e0-4efe-974c-5e84e0ac697d","name":"Hansen, Louise Ejgod","orcid":"0000-0002-3476-4717","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"welentsørensenpau","last":"Welent Sørensen","name":"Welent Sørensen, Pernille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine","key":"eibyepau","last":"Eibye","name":"Eibye, Tine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["au-62ff9121-62f4-41f6-a60a-3cfcd2931cfc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Experiencing Theatre and Drama : Developing a space for communication with children and young people","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-185854","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This paper seeks to demonstrate the central role of making and creating models in what we call “designerly and human-centred entrepreneurship”. We refer to empirics from studies of Danish entrepreneurs working on how to develop their businesses. In Drucker´s (2001) “Management Challenges for the 21st Century” he predicts the new paradigms of management will change and continue to change our basic assumptions about the practices and principles of management. One of the key influences is that of design. 10 years later Johansson & Woodilla argue there is a need for a paradigmatic widening within Design Management, since, if it stays within the current Functionalist paradigm, it is difficult or even impossible to embrace the ambiguous aspects of praxis-based design knowledge (Johansson & Woodilla, 2011). We believe this paper contributes to the more humanist and interpretive paradigm, by bringing forward examples from design research with entrepreneurs, clearly indicating the power of design processes in business. Our paper focuses specifically on how design processes, here defined as ‘reflective-conversation-with-materials’ (Bamberger & Schön, 1983), can act as strong ‘inner dialogues’ (Sørensen, 2011) about personal values in life and in business. Thus, our outline of ‘designerly and human-centred entrepreneursip’ builds on designerly ways of knowing (Cross,1982), Drucker’s idea about value clarification and self-management (2000), as well as Sheldon’s idea about ‘motivation’ (2012). We frame this within Goleman & Senge´s recent concept “The Triple Focus” - in this paper emphasizing the ‘inner focus’ (2013, 2014). We briefly refer to experiential and aesthetic learning experiences that leads not only to value clarification, but also to changes in the entrepreneurs’ self-awareness, values and identity. Thus we highlight, and suggest the current design management discourse to promote, the strong role design processes with materials can play in business modelling and entrepreneurship.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sørensen, Kirsten Bonde","Evers, Winie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-622773"],"event":{"end":"2015-11-26","place":"Kolding, dk","start":"2015-11-25","title":"Design Research Society (DRS)","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Entrepreneurship","Experiential learning","Reflective conversation with materials","The Triple Focus","Values"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of doing and making models with materials outlining designerly and human centred entrepreneurship","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://experientialknowledge.org.uk/proceedings_2015_files/EKSIG2015_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-622773","identifier":[{"id":"85053521719","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ad122587-57ea-4ee1-a4e6-5d76a74efe5e"],"keyword":["Entrepreneurship","Experiential Learning","The Triple Focus","Values","‘reflective conversation with materials’"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F5E550E6A0D86DE9FA4E480F0699DBBB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://experientialknowledge.org.uk/proceedings_2015_files/EKSIG2015_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["University College Lillebælt"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design and Communication, SDU Design","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business and Sustainability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten Bonde","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Kirsten Bonde","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Winie","key":"everspau","last":"Evers","locid":"28268332-c08b-42f0-b7b6-f8fa34cfe0ed","name":"Evers, Winie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Louise","key":"bangpedh","last":"Bang","name":"Bang, Anne Louise","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob","key":"buurpedh","last":"Buur","name":"Buur, Jacob","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Irene","key":"almalønnepedh","last":"Alma Lønne","name":"Alma Lønne, Irene","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nithikul","key":"nimkulratpedh","last":"Nimkulrat","name":"Nimkulrat, Nithikul","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788790775902"],"pages":"185-199","publisher":"Design School Kolding","status":"p","subtitle":"EKSIG 2015 - International Conference of the Design Research Society Special Interest Group on Experiential Knowledge, Conference Proceedings","title":"Tangible Means: Experiential Knowledge Through Materials"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053521719"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ad122587-57ea-4ee1-a4e6-5d76a74efe5e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The role of doing and making models with materials : Outlining “designerly and human-centred entrepreneurship”","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-622773","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This chapter investigates the construction of the battlefield of Dybbøl, Denmark, as a memorial site with particular changes of connotations and cultural and political meanings over time. Dybbøl is the site of a decisive battle in the Schleswig-Holstein war of 1864, won by Prussia and used by Bismarck to initiate his campaign of creating Greater Germany. After the war, a large part of the Danish monarchy was lost to Germany including the area where the battle occurred. This political situation lasted until 1920 when some of the area, including the battlefield, was incorporated with Denmark as a result of a plebiscite (agreed upon as part of the Treaty of Versailles). This introduced a period of re-nationalisation of the battlefield as a Danish memorial landscape (Adriansen 2003, 2010a, 2010c). After Germany’s entry into NATO in 1955 and Denmark’s entry into the EU in 1973 the old animosity between the two warring partners was officially forgotten, and rapprochement between the two sides within the border region began; the effect of this on the usage of Dybbøl has been seen especially since 2000. The chapter proposes that the concept of ‘biography’ – with its implication of progression through different phases as well as formative junctures, transitions, and gradual transformation – can be used as an effective means of exploring the afterlife of the battlefield and the changes in the meanings of the site. In the particular case, this approach helps to show how the degree of access to the site matters, stressing the difference between a site that is physically controlled and one that exists only as a place within the imagination and through emotional linkages. The chapter accordingly argues that the connotations of a place are influenced by the kinds of relations that can be constructed, making the difference between political and legal control as opposed to emotional claims significant for memorialisation purposes and practices.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Marie Louise Stig","Adriansen, Inge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-645278"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leiden University","University of Cambridge"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dybbøl the construction and reconstruction of a memorial landscape","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84952790189","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-645278","identifier":[{"id":"84952790189","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-fbedb2c9-1bca-452c-891c-00c5fa78680b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-19EC86261A398318DF1D15A38E147C5A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"leiden university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leiden University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Institut for Grænseregionsforskning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise Stig","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Marie Louise Stig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Inge","key":"adriansenpau","last":"Adriansen","locid":"94287761-67ae-486a-beab-c6b03d7ffba0","name":"Adriansen, Inge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marie Louise Stig","key":"sørensenpedh","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Marie Louise Stig","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dacia","key":"viejorosepedh","last":"Viejo-Rose","name":"Viejo-Rose, Dacia","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/cbo9781107444911.002","eisbn":["9781107444911"],"isbn":["9781107059337","9781107665057"],"pages":"18-45","place":"Cambridge","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Biographies of Place","title":"War and Cultural Heritage"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-84952790189"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fbedb2c9-1bca-452c-891c-00c5fa78680b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Dybbøl : The construction and reconstruction of a memorial landscape","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-645278","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this thesis is to show how the Morality Police in Copenhagen regulated prostitution and sexual promiscuity from 1906-1940. The final decades of the nineteenth century saw intense discussion on how to cope with the danger of the widespread venereal diseases. Prostitutes were seen as disease carriers and at the same time, prostitution was considered immoral and scandalous. The solution to both the problem of the dissemination of sexually transmitted diseases and the grounds of public morality and decency were resolved through regulation of the sale of sex. This implied regular medical examinations and strict rules laid down for the behavior of the prostitutes. However in 1906 a new legislation concerning public indecency and venereal diseases, Lov af 30te Marts 1906 om Modarbejdelse af offentlig Usædelighed og venerisk Smitte, was passed by the Danish Parliament. The Law of 1906 was adopted as a break with the previous system which had received criticism for police arbitrariness and legal issues. In this thesis The Law of 1906 is being analyzed to illustrate how the legislation was interpreted and used in practice by the Morality Police in Copenhagen from 1906-1940. In the analysis of both the legislation and police practice, exemplified in different kinds of material, “Beretningerne” and “Rapporterne” this thesis demonstrates a link between women, venereal diseases, sexual promiscuity, vagrancy, and prostitution. According to The Law of 1906 prostitution was not illegal, but the legislation forbade vagrancy. My investigation shows that it was illegal to sustain oneself by prostitution and therefore women who made a living as a prostitute came afoul of the law.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sørensen, Christina Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-648645"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hun vides ikke at have andet erhverv end erhverv ved utugt en undersøgelse af sædelighedspolitiets praksis i reguleringen af prostitution og usædelighed i københavn 000000001906 000000000040","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-648645","ids":["ucl-9c8ef6f0-cf93-4d26-992c-14a1e0a414d1"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-19C1BF568AF4504644D84E009C321FF2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Rektor, Rektor, Videncenter for Historie og Kulturformidling"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Louise","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c4715900-2e37-4a8f-9c8b-77690089c2c4","name":"Sørensen, Christina Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"80","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-9c8ef6f0-cf93-4d26-992c-14a1e0a414d1"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"\"Hun vides ikke at have andet erhverv end erhverv ved utugt\" : En undersøgelse af sædelighedspolitiets praksis i reguleringen af prostitution og usædelighed i København, 1906-40.","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-648645","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this paper is to reveal how to support and enhance all students' self directed learning activities outside the campus. The data collection has been carried out among radiography students and students from Hospitality and Tourism Management at University College North (UCN) in Denmark. By the use of participatory design based research, following the Collaborative E-learning Design method (CoED), the students have generated descriptions of new tools and activities to handle the challenges of self directed study activities. Based on the findings from the two workshops and a content analysis, the result reveals values as engagement and motivation to be taken into consideration. Moreover, students stress that the learning management system must provide tools for ubiquitous learning, peer-support, collaboration and feedback.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dau, Susanne","Falk, Lars","Jensen, Louise Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-650724"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"technology enhanced self directed and self regulated learning outside the campus an inclusion of students as designers","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.d4l.aau.dk/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-650724","ids":["ucn-414c55ce-c856-4a42-99a8-d504553284e2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-287662338765D71A7B996AE4BCD233CD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, UCN Forskning og Udvikling"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"daupau","last":"Dau","locid":"3bbc0a28-2694-45fa-86db-78ecaf3a8b72","name":"Dau, Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-5798-0519","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"falkpau","last":"Falk","locid":"79426a99-8081-418c-bec7-6a1c18149361","name":"Falk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1729-8555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Bach","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a7cb5a8a-64c4-4f87-8d52-51d666b2d0b9","name":"Jensen, Louise Bach","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elsebeth","key":"soerensenpedh","last":"Soerensen","name":"Soerensen, Elsebeth","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andras","key":"szucspedh","last":"Szucs","name":"Szucs, Andras","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Md. Saifuddin","key":"khalidpedh","last":"Khalid","name":"Khalid, Md. Saifuddin","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788771124026"],"pages":"146-151","place":"Aalborg University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Innovations in Digital Learning for Inclusion (D4L)","title":"1st D4Learning International Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-414c55ce-c856-4a42-99a8-d504553284e2"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Technology enhanced self directed and self regulated learning outside the campus : An inclusion of students as designers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-650724","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"CryoSat-2 data are used to study elevation changes over an area in the interior part of the Greenland Ice Sheet during the extreme melt event in July 2012. The penetration of the radar signal into dry snow depends heavily on the snow stratigraphy, and the rapid formation of refrozen ice layers can bias the surface elevations obtained from radar altimetry. We investigate the change in CryoSat-2 waveforms and elevation estimates over the melt event and interpret the findings by comparing in situ surface and snow pit observations from the North Greenland Eemian Ice Drilling Project camp. The investigation shows a major transition of scattering properties around the area, and an apparent elevation increase of 56±26 cm is observed in reprocessed CryoSat-2 data. We suggest that this jump in elevation can be explained by the formation of a refrozen melt layer that raised the reflective surface, introducing a positive elevation bias.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Nilsson, Johan","Vallelonga, Paul Travis","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Forsberg, René","Dahl-Jensen, Dorthe","Hirabayashi, Motohiro","Goto-Azuma, Kumiko","Hvidberg, Christine S.","Kjær, Helle A.","Satow, Kazuhide"],"cuid":["S02-093.40-666693"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KU Leuven","Nagaoka National College of Technology","Research Organization of Information and Systems, National Institute of Polar Research"],"keyword":["Altimetry","CryoSat 2","Elevation change","Greenland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greenland 000000002012 melt event effects on cryosat 000000000002 radar altimetry","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2015GL063296","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-093.40-666693","identifier":[{"id":"000356631300037","type":"wos"},{"id":"84931565745","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ae2aad7a-9e10-4693-9652-ee19b1c1762c","ku-1d6f319a-9e68-43db-8411-766c62bc6c4e"],"keyword":["CryoSat-2","Greenland","altimetry","elevation change","melt event"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6512012AE1EE0C805CDD17E0E16C5D42"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2015GL063296","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate and Earth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"be","key":"ku leuven","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"KU Leuven","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"jp","key":"research organization of information and systems national institute of polar research","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Research Organization of Information and Systems, National Institute of Polar Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"jp","key":"nagaoka national college of technology","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Nagaoka National College of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johan","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"65e62cc4-51ed-4231-8c7d-415bfcbefbab","name":"Nilsson, Johan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Paul","key":"vallelongapau","last":"Vallelonga","locid":"51df0666-60ac-46fe-8fdd-ae4ab41f3fef","name":"Vallelonga, Paul","orcid":"0000-0003-1055-7235","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","name":"Sorensen, Louise Sandberg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dorthe","key":"dahljensenpau","last":"Dahl-Jensen","locid":"6d9a0017-8123-40da-8570-d3071cf77133","name":"Dahl-Jensen, Dorthe","orcid":"0000-0002-1474-1948","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Motohiro","key":"hirabayashipau","last":"Hirabayashi","name":"Hirabayashi, Motohiro","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Kumiko","key":"gotoazumapau","last":"Goto-Azuma","name":"Goto-Azuma, Kumiko","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christine S.","key":"hvidbergpau","last":"Hvidberg","locid":"21bdf16f-aeb9-452e-bc06-56442fd393af","name":"Hvidberg, Christine S.","orcid":"0000-0002-9665-1339","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle A.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"72d1fab5-0bb7-4976-8b8c-66524e523876","name":"Kjær, Helle Astrid","name_org":"Kjaer, Helle A.","orcid":"0000-0002-3781-9509","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Kazuhide","key":"satowpau","last":"Satow","name":"Satow, Kazuhide","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/2015gl063296","issn":["00948276","19448007"],"issn_org":["19448007"],"issue":"10","journal":"Geophysical Research Letters","pages":"3919-3926","status":"p","title":"Geophysical Research Letters","title_org":"Geophysical Research Letters (Online)","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84931565745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ae2aad7a-9e10-4693-9652-ee19b1c1762c","ku-1d6f319a-9e68-43db-8411-766c62bc6c4e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Greenland 2012 melt event effects on CryoSat-2 radar altimetry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.40-666693","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The microstructure of many echinoid species has long fascinated scientists because of its high porosity and outstanding mechanical properties. We have used X-ray microtomography to examine the test of Echinocardium cordatum (heart urchin), a burrowing cousin of the more commonly known sea urchins. Three dimensional imaging demonstrates that the bulk of the test is composed of only two distinct, highly porous, fenestrated regions (stereom), in which the thickness of the struts is constant. Different degrees of porosity are achieved by varying the spacing of the struts. Drawing an analogy to vertebrate trabecular bone, where for example, human bone has a connectivity density of ≈1/mm3, we measure up to 150,000 strut connections per mm3. Simulations of mechanical loading using finite element calculations indicate that the test performs at very close to the optimum expected for foams, highlighting the functional link between structure and mechanical properties.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Müter, D.","Sørensen, H. O.","Oddershede, Jette","Dalby, K. N.","Stipp, S. L. S."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-034411"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Echinoids","Finite element modelling","X Ray Microtomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microstructure and micromechanics of the heart urchin test from x ray tomography","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actbio.2015.05.007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-034411","identifier":[{"id":"25983316","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84938209596","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-513878fb-19dc-403c-acf3-2e2768d4f1b4","ku-3cbc2b85-914f-4a85-ab71-b3715703e793"],"keyword":["Biomineralisation","Echinoids","Finite element modelling","X-ray microtomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3E5C74394A285B55C7E374DDE0BA1B55"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actbio.2015.05.007","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Neutrons and X-rays for Materials Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Dirk","key":"müterpau","last":"Müter","locid":"76c859c0-2a33-42c0-9933-0cab85960fbc","name":"Müter, Dirk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henning Osholm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"e1bf7bae-7f0e-445e-99ea-12eb242407fb","name":"Sørensen, Henning Osholm","orcid":"0000-0002-7004-547X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jette","key":"oddershedepau","last":"Oddershede","locid":"1c2a7108-b610-4a71-a642-c7fb71129275","name":"Oddershede, Jette","orcid":"0000-0003-2319-7419","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim Nicole","key":"dalbypau","last":"Dalby","locid":"d4a52fb2-4967-4539-933a-cf2d04a0acb4","name":"Dalby, Kim Nicole","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susan Louise Svane","key":"stipppau","last":"Stipp","locid":"b907e7ef-d26a-4093-836b-9b7c9238d956","name":"Stipp, Susan Louise Svane","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25983316"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.actbio.2015.05.007","issn":["17427061","18787568"],"issn_org":["17427061"],"journal":"Acta Biomaterialia","pages":"21-26","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Acta Biomaterialia","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938209596"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-513878fb-19dc-403c-acf3-2e2768d4f1b4","ku-3cbc2b85-914f-4a85-ab71-b3715703e793"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microstructure and micromechanics of the heart urchin test from X-ray tomography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-034411","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Bias in self-reported dietary intake is important when evaluating the effect of dietary interventions, particularly for intervention foods. However, few have investigated this in children, and none have investigated the reporting accuracy of fish intake in children using biomarkers. In a Danish school meal study, 8- to 11-year-old children (n 834) were served the New Nordic Diet (NND) for lunch. The present study examined the accuracy of self-reported intake of signature foods (berries, cabbage, root vegetables, legumes, herbs, potatoes, wild plants, mushrooms, nuts and fish) characterising the NND. Children, assisted by parents, self-reported their diet in a Web-based Dietary Assessment Software for Children during the intervention and control (packed lunch) periods. The reported fish intake by children was compared with their ranking according to fasting whole-blood EPA and DHA concentration and weight percentage using the Spearman correlations and cross-classification. Direct observation of school lunch intake (n 193) was used to score the accuracy of food-reporting as matches, intrusions, omissions and faults. The reporting of all lunch foods had higher percentage of matches compared with the reporting of signature foods in both periods, and the accuracy was higher during the control period compared with the intervention period. Both Spearman's rank correlations and linear mixed models demonstrated positive associations between EPA+DHA and reported fish intake. The direct observations showed that both reported and real intake of signature foods did increase during the intervention period. In conclusion, the self-reported data represented a true increase in the intake of signature foods and can be used to examine dietary intervention effects.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Biltoft-Jensen, Anja Pia","Damsgaard, Camilla Trab","Andersen, Rikke","Ygil, Karin Hess","Andersen, Elisabeth Wreford","Ege, Majken","Christensen, Tue","Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","Stark, Ken D.","Tetens, Inge","Thorsen, Anne Vibeke"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-037964"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["Faults","Intrusions","Omissions","n 3 Fatty acids"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accuracy of self reported intake of signature foods in a school meal intervention study comparison between control and intervention period","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/115331329/S0007114515002020a.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-037964","identifier":[{"id":"84939564099","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26189886","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-f16fe7a4-6682-499e-b561-ee9d177787d5","ku-1bc5f342-8130-448d-bc8e-0d471f094aa6"],"keyword":["Direct observation","Faults","Intrusions","Matches","Omissions","Web-based food diaries","n-3 fatty acids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-01507503F4965485582BF8EBBCA4F5CD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/s0007114515002020","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/115331329/S0007114515002020a.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Risk Assessment and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Lifecourse Nutrition & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of waterloo","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Waterloo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja Pia","key":"biltoftjensenanjapiapau","last":"Biltoft-Jensen","locid":"6a9984ca-23c7-46b0-9c65-03977f80cae0","name":"Biltoft-Jensen, Anja Pia","orcid":"0000-0002-6607-7575","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Camilla Trab","key":"damsgaardcamillatrabpau","last":"Damsgaard","locid":"5ea9cc09-17f1-46a3-9e4e-fa5490abd815","name":"Damsgaard, Camilla Trab","orcid":"0000-0002-5013-0562","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"andersenrikkepau","last":"Andersen","locid":"4906b97e-828c-48ec-9440-08178d4d8c5a","name":"Andersen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-5091-6995","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin Hess","key":"ygilkarinhesspau","last":"Ygil","locid":"5ed70c95-b9f2-49d0-892f-a067f8ac4142","name":"Ygil, Karin Hess","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elisabeth Wreford","key":"andersenelisabethwrefordpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"0d3105eb-61c0-4faa-bedd-ebb927bcb75b","name":"Andersen, Elisabeth Wreford","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Majken","key":"egemajkenpau","last":"Ege","locid":"b1391664-847a-431a-9444-922e697ca330","name":"Ege, Majken","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tue","key":"christensentuepau","last":"Christensen","locid":"189d4073-9f5b-4f14-95ad-31a1e1a382c8","name":"Christensen, Tue","orcid":"0000-0001-7693-7359","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Louise Bergmann","key":"sørensenlouisebergmannpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"b86d9af7-ea09-4925-a863-eadc0c0e26ee","name":"Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ken D.","key":"starkkendpau","last":"Stark","name":"Stark, Ken D.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inge","key":"tetensingepau","last":"Tetens","locid":"471bd31c-6fe2-423c-a500-8ffab1993a2e","name":"Tetens, Inge","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Vibeke","key":"thorsenannevibekepau","last":"Thorsen","locid":"f27504cc-5fd8-44e0-a177-1e497cf8f681","name":"Thorsen, Anne Vibeke","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26189886"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0007114515002020","issn":["00071145","14752662"],"issn_org":["00071145"],"issue":"4","journal":"British Journal of Nutrition","pages":"635-644","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Nutrition","volume":"114"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84939564099"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f16fe7a4-6682-499e-b561-ee9d177787d5","ku-1bc5f342-8130-448d-bc8e-0d471f094aa6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Accuracy of self-reported intake of signature foods in a school meal intervention study: comparison between control and intervention period","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-037964","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Fe and n-3 long-chain PUFA (n-3 LCPUFA) have both been associated with cognition, but evidence remains inconclusive in well-nourished school-aged children. In the Optimal Well-Being, Development and Health for Danish Children through a Healthy New Nordic Diet (OPUS) School Meal Study, the 3-month intervention increased reading performance, inattention, impulsivity and dietary intake of fish and Fe. This study investigated whether the intervention influenced n-3 LCPUFA and Fe status and, if so, explored how these changes correlated with the changes in cognitive performance. The study was a cluster-randomised cross-over trial comparing school meals with packed lunch (control). At baseline and after each treatment, we measured serum ferritin, whole-blood n-3 LCPUFA and Hb, and performance in reading, mathematics and d2-test of attention. Data were analysed using mixed models (n 726) and principal component analysis of test performances (n 644), which showed two main patterns: 'school performance' and 'reading comprehension'. The latter indicated that children with good reading comprehension were also more inattentive and impulsive (i.e. higher d2-test error%). The intervention improved 'school performance' (P=0·015), 'reading comprehension' (P=0·043) and EPA+DHA status 0·21 (95 % CI 0·15, 0·27) w/w % (P<0·001), but it did not affect serum ferritin or Hb. At baseline, having small Fe stores was associated with poorer 'school performance' in girls, but with better 'reading comprehension' in both boys and girls. Both baseline EPA+DHA status and the intervention-induced increase in EPA+DHA status was positively associated with 'school performance', suggesting that n-3 LCPUFA could potentially explain approximately 20 % of the intervention effect. These exploratory associations indicate that increased fish intake might explain some of the increase in reading performance and inattention in the study.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Egelund, Niels","Dyssegaard, Camilla Brørup","Sørensen, Louise Bergmann","Damsgaard, Camilla Trapholt","Damsgaard, Stine Mathilde","Petersen, Rikke","Stark, Ken","Andersen, Rikke","Tetens, Inge","Astrup, arne","Michaelsen, Kin Fleicher","Lauritzen, Lotte"],"cuid":["S03-096.35-017598"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["CRP C reactive protein","Cognitive performance","Ernæring","Iron","PCA principal component analysis","RCT randomised controlled trial","School meals","School performance","Sundhedspædagogik","Trivsel","kognitionspsykologi opmærksomhed hukommelse tænkning","n 3 PUFA"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diet induced changes in iron and em n em 000000000003 fatty acid status and associations with cognitive performance in 000000000008 000000000011 year old danish children secondary analyses of the optimal well being development and health for danish children through a healthy new nordic diet school meal study","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/117488606/S0007114515003323a.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-096.35-017598","identifier":[{"id":"26359192","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84945465566","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-43c94ebc-397c-48ab-99a7-e19eee3e1c1c","dtu-316b605d-e798-49ee-a068-2820515c4c00","ku-08259325-f4ab-451d-8819-29be151fa30a"],"keyword":["CP concentration performance","CRP C-reactive protein","Cognitive performance","Ernæring","ID Fe deficiency","IDA ID with anaemia","Iro