{"abstract":"Mannose-binding lectin (MBL) is a C-type serum lectin of importance in innate immunity. Low serum concentrations of MBL have been associated with greater susceptibility to infections. In this study, binding of purified chicken MBL (cMBL) to Salmonella enterica subsp. enterica (S. enterica) serotypes B, C1 and D was investigated by flow cytometry, and Staphylococcus aureus (S. aureus) was used for comparison. For S. enterica the C1 serotypes were the only group to exhibit binding to cMBL. Furthermore, functional studies of the role of cMBL in phagocytosis and complement activation were performed. Spiking with cMBL had a dose-dependent effect on the HD11 phagocytic activity of S. enterica subsp. enterica serovar Montevideo, and a more pronounced effect in a carbohydrate competitive assay. This cMBL dose dependency of opsonophagocytic activity by HD11 cells was not observed for S. aureus. No difference in complement-dependent bactericidal activity in serum with high or low cMBL concentrations was found for S. Montevideo. On the other hand, serum with high concentrations of cMBL exhibited a greater bactericidal activity to S. aureus than serum with low concentrations of cMBL. The results presented here emphasise that chicken cMBL exhibits functional similarities with its mammalian counterparts, i.e. playing a role in opsonophagocytosis and complement activation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ulrich-Lynge, Sofie Louise","Dalgaard, Tina Sørensen","Norup, Liselotte Rothmann","Song, Xiaokai","Sørensen, Poul","Juul-Madsen, Helle Risdahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-192117"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antibacterial activity","Host pathogen interaction","Mannose Binding Lectin","Phagocytosis","Salmonella enterica","Staphylococcus aureus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chicken mannose binding lectin function in relation to antibacterial activity towards i salmonella enterica i","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.imbio.2014.12.007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-192117","identifier":[{"id":"84940166803","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25623031","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6e08caee-c6b9-486e-9a6d-9f68f9479eb3"],"keyword":["HD11 cells","Mannose-Binding Lectin","Staphylococcus aureus","antibacterial activity","host-pathogen interaction","phagocytosis","salmonella enterica"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF3DEECDCEC0E491ECA81D73086DE175"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.imbio.2014.12.007","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Louise","key":"ulrichlyngepau","last":"Ulrich-Lynge","locid":"9934f350-7a13-499b-8bcb-5877dc7558d9","name":"Ulrich-Lynge, Sofie Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Sørensen","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"78918005-837a-4b5c-b5f9-3f71d33f8047","name":"Dalgaard, Tina Sørensen","orcid":"0000-0002-3424-6047","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liselotte Rothmann","key":"noruppau","last":"Norup","locid":"0bb0f5f6-3402-45f9-83f7-488dbdcbdf1f","name":"Norup, Liselotte Rothmann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaokai","key":"songpau","last":"Song","locid":"69d67d3b-d34c-4571-bf52-5bc3eeddc310","name":"Song, Xiaokai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"3172d2c3-ef30-4475-9921-e8fd8f8dad8a","name":"Sørensen, Poul","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Risdahl","key":"juulmadsenpau","last":"Juul-Madsen","locid":"3829e4a9-b29d-474f-9d37-c83a72fc564c","name":"Juul-Madsen, Helle Risdahl","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25623031"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.imbio.2014.12.007","issn":["01712985","07226365"],"issn_org":["01712985"],"issue":"5","journal":"Immunobiology","pages":"555-563","publisher":"Elsevier GmbH","status":"p","title":"Immunobiology","volume":"220"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84940166803"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6e08caee-c6b9-486e-9a6d-9f68f9479eb3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Chicken mannose-binding lectin function in relation to antibacterial activity towards <i>Salmonella enterica</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-192117","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"As the rapid reduction in ice volume of the Greenland ice sheet (GrIS) continues, increased melt water flux from the GrIS enters the deep Greenlandic fjords. This increased freshwater flux may change the salinity and eventually the ecology of the fjords. Here, we present a case study in which we, from various remote-sensing data sets, estimate the freshwater flux from the GrIS into a specific fjord system, the Godthåbsfjord, in southwest Greenland. The area of the GrIS draining into Godthåbsfjord covers approximately 36,700 km2. The large areal extent and the multiple outlets from the GrIS hamper in situ observations. Here, we evaluate available data from remote sensing and find a drainage basin in rapid change. An analysis of data from the Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment (GRACE) satellites shows a mean seasonal freshwater flux into Godthåbsfjord of 18.2 ± 1.2 Gt, in addition to an imbalance in the mass balance of the drainage basin from 2003 to 2013 of 14.4 ± 0.2 Gt year−1. Altimetry data from air and spaceborne missions also suggest rapid changes in the outlet glacier dynamics. We find that only applying data from the Ice, Cloud, and land Elevation Satellite (ICESat) mission the mass change of the Godthåbsfjord drainage basin is significantly underestimated. When including additional laser-altimetry surveys, to account for changes in the outlet glaciers elevation, not captured by ICESat, the altimetry data were able to reconcile the basin mass balance with the gravimetric estimate and provide a higher spatial resolution of the mass changes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Barletta, Valentina Roberta","Forsberg, René","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-313393"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reconciled freshwater flux into the godthåbsfjord system from satellite and airborne remote sensing","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01431161.2014.995277","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-313393","identifier":[{"id":"84920983092","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1d92dc7e-65c7-42e8-9bdf-90b1378c6a26"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-116EE7C6BBC168DBC57A5AE52FB7E29B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01431161.2014.995277","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Bjerregaard","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"d088b945-224e-4fd3-a871-022cc71c5cb1","name":"Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0001-9569-1294","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina Roberta","key":"barlettapau","last":"Barletta","locid":"9662b7b8-5901-45b2-bba3-dd8e3879f864","name":"Barletta, Valentina Roberta","orcid":"0000-0003-4427-0830","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01431161.2014.995277","issn":["01431161","13665901"],"issn_org":["01431161"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Remote Sensing","pages":"361-374","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Remote Sensing","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84920983092"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1d92dc7e-65c7-42e8-9bdf-90b1378c6a26"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Reconciled freshwater flux into the Godthåbsfjord system from satellite and airborne remote sensing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313393","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The mass balance of glaciers and ice caps is sensitive to changing climate conditions. The mass changes derived n this study are determined from elevation changes derived measured by the Ice, Cloud, and land Elevation Satellite (ICESat) for the time period 2003–2009. Four methods, based on interpolation and extrapolation, are used to regionalize these elevation changes to areas without satellite coverage. A constant density assumption is then applied to estimate the mass change by integrating over the entire glaciated region.The main purpose of this study is to investigate the sensitivity of the regional mass balance of Arctic ice caps and glaciers to different regionalization schemes. The sensitivity analysis is based on studying the spread of mass changes and their associated errors, and the suitability of the different regionalization techniques is assessed through cross validation.The cross-validation results shows comparable accuracies for all regionalization methods, but the inferred mass changein individual regions, such as Svalbard and Iceland, can vary up to 4 Gt a-1, which exceeds the estimated errors by roughly50 % for these regions. This study further finds that this spread in mass balance is connected to the magnitude of the elevation change variability. This indicates that care should be taken when choosing a regionalization method, especially for areas which exhibit large variability in elevation change.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nilsson, Johan","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Barletta, Valentina Roberta","Forsberg, René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-324852"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mass changes in arctic ice caps and glaciers implications of regionalizing elevation changes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/105417717/Nilsson2015_TC.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-324852","identifier":[{"id":"84921719465","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-443316ce-2f53-49a0-a624-6ccf1a50ac58"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1DD5E356B4CEF2661E18C6EFD05CC185"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/105417717/Nilsson2015_TC.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/tc-9-139-2015","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johan","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"65e62cc4-51ed-4231-8c7d-415bfcbefbab","name":"Nilsson, Johan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina Roberta","key":"barlettapau","last":"Barletta","locid":"9662b7b8-5901-45b2-bba3-dd8e3879f864","name":"Barletta, Valentina Roberta","orcid":"0000-0003-4427-0830","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/tc-9-139-2015","issn":["19940416","19940424"],"issn_org":["19940416"],"journal":"Cryosphere","pages":"139-150","publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","status":"p","title":"Cryosphere","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84921719465"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-443316ce-2f53-49a0-a624-6ccf1a50ac58"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Mass changes in Arctic ice caps and glaciers: implications of regionalizing elevation changes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-324852","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"For more than two decades, radar altimetry missions have provided continuous elevation estimates of the Greenland ice sheet (GrIS). Here, we propose a method for using such data to estimate ice-sheet-wide surface elevation changes (SECs). The final data set will be based on observations acquired from the European Space Agency’s Environmental Satellite (ENVISAT), European Remote Sensing (ERS)-1 and -2, CryoSat-2, and, in the longer term, Sentinel-3 satellites. In order to find the best-performing method, an intercomparison exercise has been carried out in which the scientific community was asked to provide their best SEC estimates as well as feedback sheets describing the applied method. Due to the hitherto few radar-based SEC analyses as well as the higher accuracy of laser data, the participants were asked to use either ENVISAT radar or ICESat (Ice, Cloud, and land Elevation Satellite) laser altimetry over the Jakobshavn Isbræ drainage basin. The submissions were validated against airborne laser-scanner data, and intercomparisons were carried out to analyse the potential of the applied methods and to find whether the two altimeters were capable of resolving the same signal. The analyses found great potential of the applied repeat-track and cross-over techniques, and, for the first time over Greenland, that repeat-track analyses from radar altimetry agreed well with laser data. Since topography-related errors can be neglected in cross-over analyses, it is expected that the most accurate, ice-sheet-wide SEC estimates are obtained by combining the cross-over and repeat-track techniques. It is thus possible to exploit the high accuracy of the former and the large spatial data coverage of the latter. Based on CryoSat’s different operation modes, and the increased spatial and temporal data coverage, this shows good potential for a future inclusion of CryoSat-2 and Sentinel-3 data to continuously obtain accurate SEC estimates both in the interior and margin ice sheet.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Fredenslund Levinsen, Joanna","Khvorostovsky, Kirill","Ticconi, F.","Shepherd, A.","Forsberg, René","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Muir, A.","Pie, N.","Felikson, D.","Flament, T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-376012"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nansen Environmental and Remote Sensing Center","University College London","University of Leeds","University of Texas at Dallas"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"esa ice sheet cci derivation of the optimal method for surface elevation change detection of the greenland ice sheet round robin results","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01431161.2014.999385","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-376012","identifier":[{"id":"84961290319","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-eed2e6d8-8430-4b5b-ba46-1af527205dbc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-83B6B97033840A9E9211BF2790C35371"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01431161.2014.999385","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"nansen environmental and remote sensing center","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nansen Environmental and Remote Sensing Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of leeds","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Leeds","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of texas at dallas","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Texas at Dallas","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Joanna","key":"fredenslundlevinsenpau","last":"Fredenslund Levinsen","locid":"55f307d3-198e-4dd1-9f7f-2305c650f50d","name":"Fredenslund Levinsen, Joanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirill","key":"khvorostovskypau","last":"Khvorostovsky","name":"Khvorostovsky, Kirill","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"ticconipau","last":"Ticconi","name":"Ticconi, F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"shepherdpau","last":"Shepherd","name":"Shepherd, A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"muirpau","last":"Muir","name"