2"],"journal":"Månedsskrift for Almen Praksis","pages":"232-38","status":"p","title":"Månedsskrift for Almen Praksis","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d54b90de-00e6-4861-b60c-395ec04e4817"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risikofri screening af gravide for Downs syndrom og andre hyppige kromosomfejl","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-520886","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: We tested the controversial hypothesis that vitamin D depletion aggravates hypertension and target-organ damage by influencing renin. METHODS AND RESULTS: Four-week-old double-transgenic rats (dTGR) with excess angiotensin (Ang) II production due to overexpression of the human renin (hREN) and angiotensinogen (hAGT) genes received vitamin D-depleted (n=18) or standard chow (n=15) for 3 weeks. The depleted group had very low serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D levels (mean±SEM; 3.8±0.29 versus 40.6±1.19 nmol/L) and had higher mean systolic BP at week 5 (158±3.5 versus 134.6±3.7 mm Hg, P<0.001), week 6 (176.6±3.3 versus 162.3±3.8 mm Hg, P<0.01), and week 7 (171.6±5.1 versus 155.9±4.3 mm Hg, P<0.05). Vitamin D depletion led to increased relative heart weights and increased serum creatinine concentrations. Furthermore, the mRNAs of natriuretic peptides, neutrophil gelatinase-associated lipocalin, hREN, and rRen were increased by vitamin D depletion. Regulatory T cells in the spleen and in the circulation were not affected. Ang metabolites, including Ang II and the counter-regulatory breakdown product Ang 1 to 7, were significantly up-regulated in the vitamin D-depleted groups, while ACE-1 and ACE-2 activities were not affected. CONCLUSIONS: Short-term severe vitamin D depletion aggravated hypertension and target-organ damage in dTGR. Our data suggest that even short-term severe vitamin D deficiency may directly promote hypertension and impacts on renin-angiotensin system components that could contribute to target-organ damage. The findings add to the evidence that vitamin D deficiency could also affect human hypertension.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Andersen, Louise Bjørkholt","Przybyl, Lukasz","Haase, Nadine","von Versen-Höynck, Frauke","Qadri, Fatimunnisa","Jørgensen, Jan Stener","Sorensen, Grith Lykke","Fruekilde, Palle Bach Nielsen","Poglitsch, Marko","Szijarto, István","Gollasch, Maik","Peters, Joerg","Muller, Dominik N","Christesen, Henrik Thybo","Dechend, Ralf"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-596382"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vitamin d depletion aggravates hypertension and target organ damage","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129633302/Vitamin_D_depletion_aggravates_hypertension_and_target_organ_damage.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-596382","identifier":[{"id":"85005784382","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4345870","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"25630909","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-50dff13b-96f5-4a94-8e0f-c1b70dd53cb8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-32DB15139BFACBA2166498BE748D0E20"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129633302/Vitamin_D_depletion_aggravates_hypertension_and_target_organ_damage.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.114.001417","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Bjørkholt","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"26e