{"abstract":"Mannose-binding lectin (MBL) is a key protein in innate immunity. MBL binds to carbohydrates on the surface of pathogens, where it initiates complement activation via the lectin-dependent pathway or facilitates opsonophagocytosis. In vitro studies have shown that human MBL is able to bind to Salmonella, but knowledge in relation to chicken MBL and Salmonella is lacking. In order to study this relation day-old chickens from two selected lines L10H and L10L, differing in MBL serum concentration, were either orally infected with S. Infantis (S.123443) or kept as non-infected controls. The differences between healthy L10H and L10L chicken sublines were more profound than differences caused by the S. Infantis infection. The average daily body weight was higher for L10H than for L10L, regardless of infection, indicating beneficial effects of MBL selection on growth. Salmonella was detected in cloacal swabs and the number of Salmonella positive chickens during the experiment was significantly higher in L10L than L10H, indicating that MBL may affect the magnitude of Salmonella colonisation in day-old chickens. MBL expression was determined in ceca tissue by real-time RT-PCR. L10H chickens showed a significantly higher relative expression than L10L at days 1 and 41 pi, regardless of infection. Finally, flow cytometric analysis of whole blood from infected chickens showed that L10H had a significantly higher count of all assessed leucocyte subsets on day 5 pi, and also a higher count of monocytes on day 12 pi than L10L. No difference was observed between infected and non-infected L10L chicken.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ulrich-Lynge, Sofie Louise","Dalgaard, Tina Sørensen","Norup, Liselotte Rothmann","Kjærup, Rikke Brødsgaard","Olsen, John Elmerdahl","Sørensen, Poul","Juul-Madsen, Helle Risdahl"],"cuid":["S02-095.81-020105"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Chicken","Innate immune defence","Mannose Binding Lectin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the consequence of low mannose binding lectin concentration in chickens in relation to susceptibility to i salmonella i infantis in chickens","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vetimm.2014.11.003","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.81-020105","identifier":[{"id":"84919422507","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25487759","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-66068c23-df71-4ac3-8e7d-de8abb8974b7","ku-5a8223ea-115f-46c7-b6f7-d33a9c39a36e"],"keyword":["Chicken","Innate immune defence","Mannose-binding lectin;","Salmonella enterica Infantis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6C966DBB0032C99EBF46FD7CB6012EF8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vetimm.2014.11.003","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Institut for Husdyrvidenskab - Immunologi og mikrobiologi"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Louise","key":"ulrichlyngepau","last":"Ulrich-Lynge","locid":"9934f350-7a13-499b-8bcb-5877dc7558d9","name":"Ulrich-Lynge, Sofie Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Sørensen","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"78918005-837a-4b5c-b5f9-3f71d33f8047","name":"Dalgaard, Tina Sørensen","orcid":"0000-0002-3424-6047","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liselotte Rothmann","key":"noruppau","last":"Norup","locid":"0bb0f5f6-3402-45f9-83f7-488dbdcbdf1f","name":"Norup, Liselotte Rothmann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Munkholm","key":"kjæruppau","last":"Kjærup","locid":"0770c615-8e70-4201-aa98-cf459c0a02e7","name":"Kjærup, Rikke Brødsgaard","name_org":"Kjærup, Rikke Munkholm","orcid":"0000-0001-7798-5483","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"John Elmerdahl","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d7f792e1-ac2c-4d67-8887-3615a3a98edb","name":"Olsen, John Elmerdahl","orcid":"0000-0001-6225-6587","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"3172d2c3-ef30-4475-9921-e8fd8f8dad8a","name":"Sørensen, Poul","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Risdahl","key":"juulmadsenpau","last":"Juul-Madsen","locid":"3829e4a9-b29d-474f-9d37-c83a72fc564c","name":"Juul-Madsen, Helle Risdahl","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25487759"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vetimm.2014.11.003","issn":["01652427","18732534"],"issn_org":["01652427"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Veterinary Immunology and Immunopathology","pages":"23-32","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Veterinary Immunology and Immunopathology","volume":"163"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84919422507"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-66068c23-df71-4ac3-8e7d-de8abb8974b7","ku-5a8223ea-115f-46c7-b6f7-d33a9c39a36e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The consequence of low mannose-binding lectin concentration in chickens in relation to susceptibility to <i>Salmonella</i> Infantis in chickens","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.81-020105","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Calmodulin (CaM)(1) is the central mediator of intracellular Ca(2+) signalling in cardiomyocytes, where it conveys the intricate Ca(2+) transients to the proteins controlling cardiac contraction. We recently linked two separate mutations in CaM (N53I and N97S) to dominantly inherited catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia (CPVT), an arrhythmic disorder in which exercise or acute emotion can lead to syncope and sudden cardiac death. Given the ubiquitous presence of CaM in all eukaryote cells, it is particular intriguing that carriers of either mutation show no additional symptoms. Here, we investigated the effects of the CaM CPVT mutations in a zebrafish animal model. Three-days old embryos injected with either CaM mRNA showed no detectable pathologies or developmental abnormalities. However, embryos injected with CPVT CaM mRNA displayed increased heart rate compared to WT CaM mRNA under β-adrenergic stimulation, demonstrating a conserved dominant cardiac specific effect between zebrafish and human carriers of these mutations. Motivated by the highly similar physiological phenotypes, we compared the effects of the N53I and N97S mutations on the biophysical and functional properties of CaM. Surprisingly, the mutations have opposing effects on CaM C-lobe Ca(2+) binding affinity and kinetics, and changes to the CaM N-lobe Ca(2+) binding are minor and specific to the N53I mutation. Furthermore, both mutations induce differential perturbations to structure and stability towards unfolding. Our results suggest different molecular disease mechanisms for the CPVT (N53I and N97S mutations), and strongly support that cardiac contraction is the physiological process most sensitive to CaM integrity. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Søndergaard, Mads Toft","Sorensen, Anders B","Skov, Louise L","Kjaer-Sorensen, Kasper","Bauer, Mikael C","Nyegaard, Mette","Linse, Sara","Oxvig, Claus","Overgaard, Michael Toft"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-000337"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calmodulin mutations causing catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia confer opposing functional and biophysical molecular changes","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/febs.13184","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-000337","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000350288300012","type":"wos"},{"id":"84923176771","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25557436","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-06674a8f-9f6e-43b8-a543-923b654539ea","au-9df2db2a-3cec-4fff-824f-6cdadff82d53"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7D54D1C6C5E455BD705B3DAE13B5AABE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/febs.13184","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","us