{"abstract":"Sea-ice diatoms are known to accumulate in large aggregates in and under sea ice and in melt ponds. There is recent evidence from the Arctic that such aggregates can contribute substantially to particle export when sinking from the ice. The role and regulation of microbial aggregation in the highly seasonal, nutrient-and light-limited Arctic sea-ice ecosystem is not well understood. To elucidate the mechanisms controlling the formation and export of algal aggregates from sea ice, we investigated samples taken in late summer 2011 and 2012, during two cruises to the Eurasian Basin of the Central Arctic Ocean. Spherical aggregates densely packed with pennate diatoms, as well as filamentous aggregates formed by Melosira arctica showed sign of different stages of degradation and physiological stoichiometries, with carbon to chlorophyll a ratios ranging from 110 to 66700, and carbon to nitrogen molar ratios of 8-35 and 9-40, respectively. Sub-ice algal aggregate densities ranged between 1 and 17 aggregates m 22, maintaining an estimated net primary production of 0.4-40 mg C m(-2) d(-1), and accounted for 3-80% of total phototrophic biomass and up to 94% of local net primary production. A potential factor controlling the buoyancy of the aggregates was light intensity, regulating photosynthetic oxygen production and the amount of gas bubbles trapped within the mucous matrix, even at low ambient nutrient concentrations. Our data-set was used to evaluate the distribution and importance of Arctic algal aggregates as carbon source for pelagic and benthic communities.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fernandez-Mendez, Mar","Wenzhöfer, Frank","Peeken, Ilka","Sørensen, Heidi L.","Glud, Ronnie N.","Boetius, Antje"],"cuid":["S02-082.93-015734"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fernandez-Mendez, Mar"],"country":["Germany","Greenland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Alfred Wegener Institute","All Global Affiliations","Greenland Climate Research Centre","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology","The Scottish Association for Marine Science","University of Bremen"],"keyword":["Carbon","Diatom","Dynamics","Fram Strait","Marine phytoplankton","Temperature","Transport"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"composition buoyancy regulation and fate of ice algal aggregates in the central arctic ocean","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0107452","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-082.93-015734","identifier":[{"id":"000342030300083","type":"wos"},{"id":"84925254023","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4160247","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"25208058","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-2ae88dd8-e341-4f1f-9969-8e920191ff18","sdu-076d3557-03f6-498b-9f03-67014a7dcf72"],"keyword":["CARBON","DIATOM","DYNAMICS","EXOPOLYMERIC SUBSTANCES","FRAM STRAIT","MARINE-PHYTOPLANKTON","MELTING SEA-ICE","PARTICLES TEP","TEMPERATURE","TRANSPORT"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-26F49F07EF0FB8025AD29AD094E0DB46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0107452","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"helmholtz association of german research centres","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"alfred wegener institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Alfred Wegener Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for marine microbiology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of bremen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bremen","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Nordcee"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gl","key":"greenland climate research centre","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Climate Research Centre","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"gb","key":"the scottish association for marine science","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Scottish Association for Marine Science","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mar","key":"fernandezmendezpau","last":"Fernandez-Mendez","name":"Fernandez-Mendez, Mar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mar","key":"fernándezméndezpau","last":"Fernández-Méndez","name":"Fernández-Méndez, Mar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"wenzhöferpau","last":"Wenzhöfer","name":"Wenzhöfer, Frank","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"