{"abstract":"Perinatal exposure to endocrine disrupting chemicals with estrogenic activity can adversely affect reproductive development, but few studies evaluating estrogen-sensitive endpoints have been performed in Wistar rats. Therefore, time-mated Wistar rats (n=10) were gavaged during gestation and lactation with 0, 5, 15 or 50μg/kg bw/day of ethinyl estradiol.This potent estrogen was found to induce an increased number of nipples and reduced ovary weight in female offspring. Malformations of female genitalia were found in young as well as adult offspring, as an increased AGD was seen at birth and a deeper urethral slit length was seen in adulthood. In prepubertal male offspring, estrogen-regulated gene expression in ventral prostate was increased dose-dependently and a decreased ventral prostate weight was seen at 15μg/kg.Female external sexual characteristics and prostate development were found to be targets for exposure to estrogenic compounds and may be of interest in studies on estrogenic environmental compounds.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Egebjerg, Karen Mandrup","Jacobsen, Pernille Rosenskjold","Isling, Louise Krag","Petersen, Marta Axelstad","Sørensen, Karin Dreisig","Hadrup, Niels","Vinggaard, Anne Marie","Hass, Ulla","Boberg, Julie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-328063"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anogenital distance","Endocrine disruption","Estrogen","Gene expression","Genital malformations","Mammary gland","Nipples","Onset of puberty"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of perinatal ethinyl estradiol exposure in male and female wistar rats","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.reprotox.2013.09.001","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-328063","identifier":[{"id":"84878819555","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24036065","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-4ef9f2d1-cd9c-4639-8bde-da428fc1da5d"],"keyword":["Anogenital distance","Endocrine disruption","Estrogen","Gene expression","Genital malformations","Mammary gland","Nipples","Onset of puberty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5DD365C558145DAA24FB9D9932B3C4C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.reprotox.2013.09.001","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Toxicology and Risk Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen","key":"mandruppau","last":"Mandrup","locid":"8970bf81-c563-45b9-b882-7e9bea3811be","name":"Egebjerg, Karen Mandrup","name_org":"Mandrup, Karen","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-6882","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Rosenskjold","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"5df258c6-3f28-4013-8b1c-a053aea5a039","name":"Jacobsen, Pernille Rosenskjold","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Krag","key":"islingpau","last":"Isling","locid":"c250e61f-a839-416d-a4c8-140b83730547","name":"Isling, Louise Krag","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marta Axelstad","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"28964548-221c-4138-b266-abe3d6d0bc2d","name":"Petersen, Marta Axelstad","orcid":"0000-0002-2375-0918","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin Dreisig","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"0a5be222-101b-45b4-a02c-1b0350c04205","name":"Sørensen, Karin Dreisig","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"hadruppau","last":"Hadrup","locid":"4384548f-118a-4c3c-aedf-f0d203046277","name":"Hadrup, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-1188-445X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Marie","key":"vinggaardpau","last":"Vinggaard","locid":"c6459d83-f7f1-417a-ac8f-2ab00cb0f432","name":"Vinggaard, Anne Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-6822-3572","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulla","key":"hasspau","last":"Hass","locid":"7ca26739-77b7-4ee6-86eb-ae2b326d2af8","name":"Hass, Ulla","orcid":"0000-0001-5309-167X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Julie","key":"bobergpau","last":"Boberg","locid":"0a6dd5db-7b41-4b80-87f8-589a2e3e5fd8","name":"Boberg, Julie","orcid":"0000-0003-2255-1201","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24036065"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.reprotox.2013.09.001","issn":["08906238","18731708"],"issn_org":["08906238"],"journal":"Reproductive Toxicology","pages":"180-191","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Reproductive Toxicology","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878819555"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4ef9f2d1-cd9c-4639-8bde-da428fc1da5d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Effects of perinatal ethinyl estradiol exposure in male and female Wistar rats","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-328063","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We present a full-length a1b2c2 GABA receptor model optimized for agonists and benzodiazepine (BZD) allosteric modulators. We propose binding hypotheses for the agonists GABA, muscimol and THIP and for the allosteric modulator diazepam (DZP). The receptor model is primarily based on the glutamate-gated chloride channel (GluCl) from C. elegans and includes additional structural information from the prokaryotic ligand-gated ion channel ELIC in a few regions. Available mutational data of the binding sites are well explained by the model and the proposed ligand binding poses. We suggest a GABA binding mode similar to the binding mode of glutamate in the GluCl X-ray structure. Key interactions are predicted with residues a1R66, b2T202, a1T129, b2E155, b2Y205 and the backbone of b2S156. Muscimol is predicted to bind similarly, however, with minor differences rationalized with quantum mechanical energy calculations. Muscimol key interactions are predicted to be a1R66, b2T202, a1T129, b2E155, b2Y205 and b2F200. Furthermore, we argue that a water molecule could mediate further interactions between muscimol and the backbone of b2S156 and b2Y157. DZP is predicted to bind with interactions comparable to those of the agonists in the orthosteric site. The carbonyl group of DZP is predicted to interact with two threonines a1T206 and c2T142, similar to the acidic moiety of GABA. The chlorine atom of DZP is placed near the important a1H101 and the N-methyl group near a1Y159, a1T206, and a1Y209. We present a binding mode of DZP in which the pending phenyl moiety of DZP is buried in the binding pocket and thus shielded from solvent exposure. Our full length GABAA receptor is made available as Model S1.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bergmann, Rikke","Kongsbak, Kristine Grønning","Sørensen, Pernille Louise","Sander, Tommy","Balle, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-421355"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a unified model of the gabaa receptor comprising agonsit and benzodiazepine binding sites","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0052323","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-421355","identifier":[{"id":"84872033261","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3538749","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23308109","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2ee436be-9151-440c-9b7b-5afff830894f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-03E935795C7790031AE37B1C5603E171"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0052323","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Biostructural Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l