{"abstract":"We demonstrate temperature-controlled encapsulation and release of the enzyme horseradish peroxidase using a preassembled and covalently closed three-dimensional DNA cage structure as a controllable encapsulation device. The utilized cage structure was covalently closed and composed of 12 double-stranded B-DNA helices that constituted the edges of the structure. The double stranded helices were interrupted by short single-stranded thymidine linkers constituting the cage corners except for one, which was composed by four 32 nucleotide long stretches of DNA with a sequence that allowed them to fold into hairpin structures. As demonstrated by gel-electrophoretic and fluorophore-quenching experiments this design imposed a temperature-controlled conformational transition capability to the structure, which allowed entrance or release of an enzyme cargo at 37 °C while ensuring retainment of the cargo in the central cavity of the cage at 4 °C. The entrapped enzyme was catalytically active inside the DNA cage and was able to convert substrate molecules penetrating the apertures in the DNA lattice that surrounded the central cavity of the cage.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Juul, Sissel","Iacovelli, Federico","Falconi, Mattia","Kragh, Sofie Louise","Christensen, Brian Søndergaard","Hougaard, Rikke Frøhlich","Franch, Oskar","Kristoffersen, Emil Laust","Stougaard, Magnus","Leong, Kam W","Ho, Yi-Ping","Sørensen, Esben Skipper","Birkedal, Victoria","Desideri, Alessandro","Knudsen, Birgitta R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-225411"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","University of Rome La Sapienza"],"keyword":["Drug delivery","Fluorescence quenching","MD simulation","Self assembly","Temperature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temperature controlled encapsulation and release of an active enzyme in the cavity of a self assembled dna nanocage","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/nn4030543","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-225411","identifier":[{"id":"84888868249","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24168393","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a87c6dbc-4575-4330-a700-b697bbf4778c"],"keyword":["DNA nanocage","MD simulation","controlled encapsulation and release","drug delivery","fluorescence-quenching","self-assembly","temperature"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E5F111780388BEEB8E29A80BBF51688D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/nn4030543","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of rome la sapienza","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Rome La Sapienza","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sissel","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Sissel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Federico","key":"iacovel