12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Victoria","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","locid":"7055d6e9-f1c4-4ecf-84b7-8d579b2bb667","name":"Birkedal, Victoria","orcid":"0000-0002-1360-8870","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"desideripau","last":"Desideri","locid":"803796a7-159c-4d0f-a4e8-36fba5989d3f","name":"Desideri, Alessandro","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitta R","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"50fca07c-ced4-453a-a26a-0d664c9a1491","name":"Knudsen, Birgitta R.","name_org":"Knudsen, Birgitta R","orcid":"0000-0002-3484-3802","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24168393"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/nn4030543","issn":["19360851","1936086X"],"issn_org":["19360851"],"issue":"11","journal":"ACS Nano","pages":"9724-9734","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS Nano","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84888868249"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a87c6dbc-4575-4330-a700-b697bbf4778c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Temperature-Controlled Encapsulation and Release of an Active Enzyme in the Cavity of a Self-Assembled DNA Nanocage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-225411","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The ability to synthesize, characterize, and manipulate DNA forms the foundation of a range of advanced disciplines including genomics, molecular biology, and biomolecular engineering. In particular for the latter field, DNA has proven useful as a structural or functional component in nanoscale self-assembled structures, antisense therapeutics, microarray diagnostics, and biosensors. Such applications frequently require DNA to be modified and conjugated to other macromolecules, including proteins, polymers, or fatty acids, in order to equip the system with properties required for a particular application. However, conjugation of DNA to large molecular components using classical chemistries often suffers from suboptimal yields. Here, we report the use of terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase (TdT) for direct enzymatic ligation of native DNA to nucleotide triphosphates coupled to proteins and other large macromolecules. We demonstrate facile synthesis routes for a range of NTP-activated macromolecules and subsequent ligation to the 3′ hydroxyl group of oligodeoxynucleotides using TdT. The reaction is highly specific and proceeds rapidly and essentially to completion at micromolar concentrations. As a proof of principle, parallelly labeled oligonucleotides were used to produce nanopatterned DNA origami structures, demonstrating rapid and versatile incorporation of non-DNA components into DNA nanoarchitectures.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sørensen, Rasmus Schøler","Okholm, Anders Hauge","Schaffert, David Henning","Kodal, Anne Louise Bank","Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager","Kjems, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-247547"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DNA Nanoteknologi"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enzymatic ligation of large biomolecules to dna","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/nn403386f","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-247547","identifier":[{"id":"84884923830","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23927463","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-cee1bb6d-3843-41a1-ba71-d376f42a4a16"],"keyword":["Biokonjugering","DNA Nanoteknologi","Enzymatiske reaktioner"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-61B4A5E29076534FB427D9EC365B32D6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/nn403386f","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Kemi, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Schøler","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"dd13ff30-6bd7-4512-bc60-efa5c5b0ebdd","name":"Sørensen, Rasmus Schøler","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Hauge","key":"okholmpau","last":"Okholm","locid":"f264fed0-c43e-4f71-843a-7787595ad043","name":"Okholm, Anders Hauge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David Henning","key":"schaffertpau","last":"Schaffert","locid":"680e746e-7ceb-488c-af97-2385ce6479d3","name":"Schaffert, David Henning","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Louise Bank","key":"kodalpau","last":"Kodal","locid":"765efe10-0aa6-4d31-9803-fb5e322fcf3e","name":"Kodal, Anne Louise Bank","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kurt Vesterager","key":"gothelfpau","last":"Gothelf","locid":"8ca43d09-e887-432e-8775-ab2f38db1e6d","name":"Gothelf, Kurt Vesterager","orcid":"0000-0003-2399-3757","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"kjemspau","last":"Kjems","locid":"f5915d75-aca3-437a-9a9d-f4fdfef7accd","name":"Kjems, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-9317","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23927463"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/nn403386f","issn":["19360851","1936086X"],"issn_org":["19360851"],"issue":"9","journal":"ACS Nano","pages":"8098-8104","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS Nano","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884923830"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cee1bb6d-3843-41a1-ba71-d376f42a4a16"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Enzymatic Ligation of Large Biomolecules to DNA","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-247547","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"After the successful launch of CryoSat‐2 in April 2010, the first direct Arctic validation campaign of the satellite was carried out in the period April 15 ‐ May 8, 2011. This report describes the airborne part of the CryoSat Validation Experiment (CryoVEx) 2011, and includes; 1) Data collected with the ESA airborne Ku‐band interferometric radar (ASIRAS), coincident airborne laser scanner (ALS) and vertical photography to acquire data over sea‐ and land ice along CryoSat‐2 ground tracks. The airborne campaign was coordinated by DTU Space using the Norlandair Twin Otter (TF‐POF). 2) Sea ice thickness data obtained with an airborne electromagnetic (AEM) induction sounder conducted by Alfred Wegener Institute (AWI) with fixed‐wing airplane (Polar‐5, Basler BT‐67). DTU Space airborne team visited five main validation sites: Devon ice cap (Canada), Austfonna ice cap (Svalbard), the EGIG line crossing the Greenland Ice Sheet, as well as the sea ice north of CFS Alert (Ellesmere Island), and sea ice north off Svalbard. Selected tracks were planned to match CryoSat‐2 passes and a few of the sea ice flights out of CFS Alert were coordinated with AWI Polar‐5 carrying the AEM induction sounder and NASA’s Operation IceBridge P‐3 carrying a variety of instruments for sea ice and snow retrieval. At each validation site ground teams measured ice and snow properties, and raised corner reflectors acting as a surface reference point to estimate the penetration depth of the ASIRAS radar. This report describes in details the airborne systems, together with campaign implementation plan, data processing and data quality analysis. The CryoVEx 2011 campaign was a success and the processed data is of high quality. The datasets are very important in order to understand the CryoSat‐2 radar signals over sea‐ and land ice.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Skourup, Henriette","Barletta, Valentina Roberta","Einarsson, Indriði","Forsberg, René","Haas, C.","Helm, V.","Hendricks, S.","Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-363863"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Germany"],"glorg":["Alfred Wegener Institute - Helmholtz Centre for Polar and Marine Research","All Global Affiliations","University of Alberta"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"esa cryovex 000000002011 airborne field campaign with asiras radar em induction sounder and laser scanner","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/73772291/CryoVEx2011_fieldreport_ver4_DTUprint.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-363863","ids":["dtu-c67d1d1f-bc28-49f1-87d2-a325c90b7e87"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DD1EE536CF6B406FC3FB7462BDEF847C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/73772291/CryoVEx2011_fieldreport_ver4_DTUprint.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of alberta","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Alberta","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"alfred wegener institute helmholtz centre for polar and marine research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Alfred Wegener Institute - Helmholtz Centre for Polar and Marine Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette","key":"skouruppau","last":"Skourup","locid":"f5fe613f-20e5-4a69-9eff-f03779801182","name":"Skourup, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-4468-8033","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina Roberta","key":"barlettapau","last":"Barletta","locid":"9662b7b8-5901-45b2-bba3-dd8e3879f864","name":"Barletta, Valentina Roberta","orcid":"0000-0003-4427-0830","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Indriði","key":"einarssonpau","last":"Einarsson","locid":"085a5058-00e6-4e28-80ca-ee888c10c647","name":"Einarsson, Indriði","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"V.","key":"helmpau","last":"Helm","name":"Helm, V.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"hendrickspau","last":"Hendricks","name":"Hendricks, S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sine Munk","key":"hvidegaardpau","last":"Hvidegaard","locid":"92b07d8f-692c-4ebb-bc40-f44224f3f143","name":"Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","orcid":"0000-0001-8159-6499","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"1","pages":"120","place":"Kgs. Lyngby","publisher":"DTU Space","repno":"Technical Report, No. 1","series":"Technical Report","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c67d1d1f-bc28-49f1-87d2-a325c90b7e87"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"ESA CryoVEx 2011 : Airborne field campaign with ASIRAS radar, EM induction sounder and laser scanner","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-363863","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"In order to increase the understanding of the changing climate, the European Space Agency has launched the Climate Change Initiative (ESA CCI), a program which joins scientists and space agencies into 13 projects either affecting or affected by the concurrent changes. This work is part of the Ice Sheets CCI and four parameters are to be determined for the Greenland Ice Sheet (GrIS), each resulting in a dataset made available to the public: Surface Elevation Changes (SEC), surface velocities, grounding line locations, and calving front locations. All CCI projects have completed a so-called Round Robin exercise in which the scientific community was asked to provide their best estimate of the sought parameters as well as a feedback sheet describing their work. By inter-comparing and validating the results, obtained from research institutions world-wide, it is possible to develop the most optimal method for determining each parameter. This work describes the SEC Round Robin and the subsequent conclusions leading to the creation of a method for determining GrIS SEC values. The participants used either Envisat radar or ICESat laser altimetry over Jakobshavn Isbræ drainage basin, and the submissions led to inter-comparisons of radar vs. altimetry as well as cross-over vs. repeat-track analyses. Due to the high accuracy of the former and the high spatial resolution of the latter, a method, which combines the two techniques will provide the most accurate SEC estimates. The data supporting the final GrIS analysis stem from the radar altimeters on-board Envisat, ERS-1 and ERS-2. The accuracy of laser data exceeds that of radar altimetry; the Round Robin analysis has, however, proven the latter equally capable of dealing with surface topography thereby making such data applicable in SEC analyses extending all the way from the interior ice sheet to margin regions. This shows good potential for a~future inclusion of ESA CryoSat-2 and Sentinel-3 radar data in the analysis, and thus for obtaining reliable SEC estimates throughout the entire GrIS.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Fredenslund Levinsen, Joanna","Khvorostovsky, K.","Ticconi, F.","Shepherd, A.","Forsberg, René","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Muir, A.","Pie, N.","Felikson, D.","Flament, T.","Hurkmans, R.","Moholdt, G.","Gunter, B.","Lindenbergh, R. C.","Kleinherenbrink, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-364650"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["France","Netherlands","Norway","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Laboratoire d’Études en Géophysique et Océanographie Spatiales","Nansen Environmental and Remote Sensing Center","Scripps Institution of Oceanography","University College London","University of Bristol","University of Leeds","University of Texas at Dallas"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"esa s ice sheets cci validation and inter comparison of surface elevation changes derived from laser and radar altimetry over jakobshavn isbræ greenland round robin results","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/72754467/tcd_7_5433_2013.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-364650","ids":["dtu-c93642ac-c9c3-4b10-881d-c46da69729a9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C20632027406C97EC1F911BCB19FEA8D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.the-cryosphere-discuss.net/7/5433/2013/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws