LL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-aa0ccbe1-fa74-4430-bb76-6a854350dd8d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Delusion and Disclosure: Human disposal and the aesthetics of vagueness","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-226316","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We study the implications of a recently published mass balance of the Greenland ice sheet (GrIS), derived from repeated surface elevation measurements from NASA’s ice cloud and land elevation satellite (ICESat) for the time period between 2003 and 2008. To characterize the effects of this new, high‐resolution GrIS mass balance, we study the time‐variations of various geophysical quantities in response to the current mass loss. They include vertical uplift and subsidence, geoid height variations, global patterns of sea level change (or fingerprints), and regional sea level variations along the coasts of Greenland. Long‐wavelength uplifts and gravity variations in response to current or past ice thickness variations are obtained solving the sea level equation, which accounts for both the elastic and the viscoelastic components of deformation. To capture the short‐wavelength components of vertical uplift in response to current ice mass loss, which is not resolved by satellite gravity observations, we have specifically developed a high‐resolution regional elastic rebound (ER) model. The elastic component of vertical uplift is combined with estimates of the viscoelastic displacement fields associated with the process of glacial‐isostatic adjustment (GIA), according to a set of published ice chronologies and associated mantle rheological profiles. We compare the sensitivity of global positioning system (GPS) observations along the coasts of Greenland to the ongoing ER and GIA. In notable contrast with past reports, we show that vertical velocities obtained by GPS data from five stations with sufficiently long records and from one tide gauge at the GrIS margins can be reconciled with model predictions based on the ICE‐5G deglaciation model and the ER associated with the new ICESat‐derived mass balance.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Spada, G.","Ruggieri, G.","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Nielsen, Karina","Melini, D.","Colleoni, F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-312566"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Euro-Mediterranean Center on Climate Change","Istituto Nazionale Di Geofisica E Vulcanologia","University of Urbino"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greenland uplift and regional sea level changes from icesat observations and gia modelling","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-246X.2012.05443.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-312566","identifier":[{"id":"84860834371","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1aa1c291-318b-4704-a044-08a5053c45c2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0CBFDEECBCD33C8E2B98B6D8AA4C0404"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-246X.2012.05443.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of urbino","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Urbino","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"istituto nazionale di geofisica e vulcanologia","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Istituto Nazionale Di Geofisica E Vulcanologia","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"euro mediterranean center on climate change","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Euro-Mediterranean Center on Climate Change","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"spadapau","last":"Spada","name":"Spada, G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"ruggieripau","last":"Ruggieri","name":"Ruggieri, G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karina","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"35a43dde-d05b-4527-b0e7-1094f9e66c04","name":"Nielsen, Karina","orcid":"0000-0002-0035-1869","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"melinipau","last":"Melini","name":"Melini, D.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"colleonipau","last":"Colleoni","name":"Colleoni, F.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1365-246x.2012.05443.x","issn":["0956540X","1365246X"],"issn_org":["0956540X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Geophysical Journal International","pages":"1457-1474","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Geophysical Journal International","volume":"189"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860834371"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1aa1c291-318b-4704-a044-08a5053c45c2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Greenland uplift and regional sea level changes from ICESat observations and GIA modelling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-312566","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Complex carbohydrates play important functions for circulation of proteins and cells. They provide protective shields and refraction from non-specific interactions with negative charges from sialic acids to enhance circulatory half-life. For recombinant protein therapeutics carbohydrates are especially important to enhance size and reduce glomerular filtration loss. Carbohydrates are, however, also ligands for a large number of carbohydrate-binding lectins exposed to the circulatory system that serve as scavenger receptors for the innate immune system, or have more specific roles in targeting of glycoproteins and cells.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sørensen, Anne Louise Tølbøll","Clausen, Henrik","Wandall, Hans H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-499718"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"carbohydrate clearance receptors in transfusion medicine","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbagen.2012.07.008","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-499718","identifier":[{"id":"22846227","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84865057755","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b1f6eb88-b6d6-4c4b-913d-4f9fa381fc9b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E7AA4BC5D443A9F2AC93672EB531F232"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbagen.2012.07.008","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Louise Tølbøll","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f415d4a2-da27-4b48-94dd-ed0df74eb1e1","name":"Sørensen, Anne Louise Tølbøll","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"a7882c09-1275-4857-8b5b-7e3efc1d088d","name":"Clausen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0915-5055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans H","key":"wandallpau","last":"Wandall","locid":"05df527d-13fd-4de9-9bb6-1a7b604bc6fa","name":"Wandall, Hans H","orcid":"0000-0003-0240-9232","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22846227"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbagen.2012.07.008","issn":["03044165","18728006"],"issn_org":["03044165"],"issue":"11","journal":"BBA General Subjects","pages":"1797-808","status":"p","title":"BBA General Subjects","volume":"1820"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865057755"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b1f6eb88-b6d6-4c4b-913d-4f9fa381fc9b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Carbohydrate clearance receptors in transfusion medicine","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-499718","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Background To enhance accuracy in evaluating prognosis and target therapy, there is a need for biomarkers in COPD. Yet, there are no reliable biomarkers that can differentiate between phenotypes of COPD. MFAP4 is a glycoprotein, co-localized with elastin and microfibrils in elastic fibres. We hypothesized that circulating MFAP4 reflects elastin degradation and thereby emphysema in COPD patients. Methods Plasma levels of MFAP4 (pMFAP4) were determined by ELISA in 74 Danish COPD patients from the multicentre ECLIPSE (Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate End-points) study. Associations between log-transformed pMFAP4 levels and clinical outcomes were assessed by multiple regression analysis. Age, gender and current smoking were included as covariates. Results Levels of pMFAP4 associated significantly with GOLD stages and were significantly higher in GOLD IV than in II. LogpMFAP4 was positively correlated to percentage of low attenuation area on HRCT (LAA%) (β: 0.007, p<0.005). There was moreover a significant negative association between plasma logpMFAP4 and FEV1/FVC index (β:-0.007, p<0.05), reversibility (β:-0.6p<0.05). There was a significant interaction between gender and BMI and Fat Free Mass Index respective (FFMI), showing a significant negative association between MFAP4 and BMI (β:-0.03, p<0.01) and FFMI (β:-0.08, p<0.005) among women. Conclusion MFAP4 levels in plasma were associated with severity of COPD and were correlated to clinical characteristics of the emphysema phenotype.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Johansson, Sofie Lock","Roberts, Nassim Bazeghi","Schlosser, Anders","Johansson, Helle Wulf","Titlestad, Ingrid Louise","Tornoe, Ida","Holmskov, Uffe","Vestbo, Jørgen","Sorensen, Grith Lykke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-608975"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-22","place":"Birmingham, gb","start":"2012-06-22","title":"COPD8","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microfibril associated protein 000000000004 mfap000000000004 as a biomarker of emphysema","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-608975","ids":["sdu-7ceb667f-f62f-4e4c-a8b1-ed962f9e32cf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-54FEE88982150E31A409A6174C9FF9B9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Cardiovascular and Renal Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sofie Lock","key":"johanssonsofielockpau","last":"Johansson","locid":"71fb7f1b-e46c-4333-8a12-3fb7ad0772c9","name":"Johansson, Sofie Lock","orcid":"0000-0003-0597-9468","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nassim Bazeghi","key":"robertsnassimbazeghipau","last":"Roberts","name":"Roberts, Nassim Bazeghi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"schlosseranderspau","last":"Schlosser","locid":"9658ed75-0e49-4680-a1e9-909c39b74fa2","name":"Schlosser, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-8693-2148","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Wulf","key":"johanssonhellewulfpau","last":"Johansson","locid":"3e85a00a-2456-44f4-8671-e8e9fe81296d","name":"Johansson, Helle Wulf","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid Louise","key":"titlestadingridlou