ch-Lynge, Sofie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Sørensen","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"78918005-837a-4b5c-b5f9-3f71d33f8047","name":"Dalgaard, Tina Sørensen","orcid":"0000-0002-3424-6047","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liselotte Rothmann","key":"noruppau","last":"Norup","locid":"0bb0f5f6-3402-45f9-83f7-488dbdcbdf1f","name":"Norup, Liselotte Rothmann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"John Elmerdahl","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, John Elmerdahl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Risdahl","key":"juulmadsenpau","last":"Juul-Madsen","locid":"3829e4a9-b29d-474f-9d37-c83a72fc564c","name":"Juul-Madsen, Helle Risdahl","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"62-62","place":"Edinburgh","status":"p","title":"AIRG 2012: Scientific Programme and Abstracs"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ea7a7b3a-74c0-486e-9eaf-8fd0273fb460"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The binding ability of purified chicken Mannose-Binding Lectin (cMBL) to <em>Salmonella enterica </em>serotype B, C1 and D","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263169","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This study investigated the kinetics of multi-enzymatic degradation of soluble wheat arabinoxylan by monitoring the release of xylose and arabinose during designed treatments with mono-component enzymes at different substrate concentrations. The results of different combinations of α-l-arabinofuranosidases (EC 3.2.1.55), one derived from Aspergillus niger (AFAn) and one from Bifidobacterium adolescentis (AFBa), respectively, a β-xylosidase (EC 3.2.1.37) from Trichoderma reesei, and an engineered D11F/R122D variant of Bacillus subtilis XynA endo-1,4-β-xylanase (EC 3.2.1.8) were examined. The two selected α-l-arabinofuranosidases catalyze liberation of arabinose residues linked 1→3 to singly (AFAn) or doubly (AFBa) substituted xyloses in arabinoxylan, respectively. When added to arabinoxylan at equimolar levels, the AFBa enzyme catalyzed the release of more arabinose, i.e. had a higher rate constant than AFAn, but with respect to the xylose release, AFAn – as expected – exhibited a better synergistic effect than AFBa with β-xylosidase. This synergistic effect with AFAn was estimated to increase the number of β-xylosidase catalyzed cuts from ∼3 (with β-xylosidase alone) to ∼7 in each arabinoxylan substrate molecule. However, the synergistic effects between β-xylosidase and the α-l-arabinofuranosidases on the xylose release were low as compared to the effect of xylanase addition with β-xylosidase, which increased the xylose release by ∼25 times in 30min, to a yield equivalent to ∼104 β-xylosidase catalyzed cuts in each arabinoxylan substrate molecule. At equimolar addition levels of the four enzymes, the xylanase activity was thus rate-limiting for the β-xylosidase catalyzed depolymerization to release xylose from arabinoxylan. The work provides clues to design efficient enzymatic degradation of arabinoxylan into fermentable monosaccharides.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Louise Enggaard","Xu, Cheng","Sørensen, Jens","Nielsen, Michael Krogsgaard","Meyer, Anne S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-339581"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Enzyme kinetics","Synergy","β Xylosidase","β l Arabinofuranosidase"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enzyme kinetics and identification of the rate limiting step of enzymatic arabinoxylan degradation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bej.2012.08.004","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-339581","identifier":[{"id":"84865604955","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-75327c62-47b9-451f-bd0a-397fa387d1da"],"keyword":["Arabinoxylan hydrolysis","Endo-xylanase","Enzyme kinetics","Synergy","β-Xylosidase","β-l-Arabinofuranosidase"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F1B2C3F8A5D151E371E956F9CA4A9764"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bej.2012.08.004","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Danisco AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"