"Bo","key":"baslundpedh","last":"Baslund","name":"Baslund, Bo","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulla","key":"feldtrasmussenpedh","last":"Feldt-Rasmussen","name":"Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"kastruppedh","last":"Kastrup","name":"Kastrup, Jens","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per Soelberg","key":"sørensenpedh","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Per Soelberg","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1. udgave","isbn":["9788777496387"],"pages":"291-300","place":"København","publisher":"FADL's Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"Lærebog i Medicin","title":"Medicin","volume":"1"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3d2d5b84-7b08-4d03-ac83-920db4991c80"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Pleuras og mediastinums sygdomme samt bronkiektasier","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-590772","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Inhibition of the ternary protein complex of the synaptic scaffolding protein postsynaptic density protein-95 (PSD-95), neuronal nitric oxide synthase (nNOS), and the N-methyl-d-aspartate (NMDA) receptor is a potential strategy for treating ischemic brain damage, but high-affinity inhibitors are lacking. Here we report the design and synthesis of a novel dimeric inhibitor, Tat-NPEG4(IETDV)(2) (Tat-N-dimer), which binds the tandem PDZ1-2 domain of PSD-95 with an unprecedented high affinity of 4.6 nM, and displays extensive protease-resistance as evaluated in vitro by stability-measurements in human blood plasma. X-ray crystallography, NMR, and small-angle X-ray scattering (SAXS) deduced a true bivalent interaction between dimeric inhibitor and PDZ1-2, and also provided a dynamic model of the conformational changes of PDZ1-2 induced by the dimeric inhibitor. A single intravenous injection of Tat-N-dimer (3 nmol/g) to mice subjected to focal cerebral ischemia reduces infarct volume with 40% and restores motor functions. Thus, Tat-N-dimer is a highly efficacious neuroprotective agent with therapeutic potential in stroke.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Bach, Anders","Clausen, Bettina H","Møller, Magda","Vestergaard, Bente","Chi, Celestine N","Round, Adam","Sørensen, Pernille Louise","Nissen, Klaus Bertram","Kastrup, Jette Sandholm","Gajhede, Michael","Jemth, Per","Kristensen, Anders S","Lundström, Patrik","Lambertsen, Kate Lykke","Strømgaard, Kristian"],"cuid":["S02-090.14-047006"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Linköping University","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["European Molecular Biology Laboratory, Grenoble Outstation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a high affinity dimeric inhibitor of psd 000000000095 bivalently interacts with pdz000000000001 000000000002 and protects against ischemic brain damage","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1113761109","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.14-047006","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3295328","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84857753632","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22343531","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e7bef392-7d2b-49de-a760-46154795bb3c","sdu-2529e227-fdef-404b-b241-13eb72d2639d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C9F0F3FB25F5494F9ADE71575A1E89A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1113761109","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Medicinal Chemistry Research","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Neurobiology Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD