},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark (DTU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karsten","key":"dahlkarstenpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"1dda7881-6c80-4eeb-8403-a286b82efda5","name":"Dahl, Karsten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte Louise Jansen","key":"petersendittelouisejansenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"30ab3ac8-ccdc-41c0-a475-fad2c5c9bce3","name":"Petersen, Ditte Louise Jansen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ib Krag","key":"petersenibkragpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"16540647-0159-4732-a397-fe141979724b","name":"Petersen, Ib Krag","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"dolmerperpau","last":"Dolmer","name":"Dolmer, Per","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Kirk","key":"sørensenthomaskirkpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Thomas Kirk","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte","key":"worsøeclausenlottepau","last":"Worsøe Clausen","name":"Worsøe Clausen, Lotte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-60700cc4-7ab1-4977-97a0-092688064a33"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Karakterisering af fremherskende og særlige habitattyper i havbund og vandsøjle i de danske farvande","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-184400","year":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Mating between closely related individuals often causes reduced fitness, which is termed ‘inbreeding depression’. Inbreeding is, therefore, a threat towards the persistence of animal and plant populations. Here we present methods and results from a practical for high-school and first-year university students and discuss learning outcomes of the exercise as an example of inquiry-based science teaching. We use the model organism Drosophila melanogaster to test the ability of inbred and control (non-inbred) females to survive heat stress exposure. Flies were anaesthetised and collected into vials before exposure to 38°C heat stress in a water bath for 1 h. Half an hour later the number of comatose inbred and control flies were scored and chi-square statistic procedures were used to test for different degrees of heat stress tolerance between the two lines of flies. The practical introduces the students to central topics in population genetics and demonstrates potential consequences of inbreeding and environmental stress on fitness. Furthermore, the practical gives insight into how to design, analyse, and interpret the results of a scientific study.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pedersen, Kamilla Sofie","Pedersen, Louise Dybdahl","Sørensen, Anders Christian","Nielsen, Anna Busch","Kristensen, Torsten Nygård"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-257689"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Environmental stress","Heat tolerance","Inbreeding depression","Statistics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating inbreeding depression for heat stress tolerance in the model organism em drosophila melanogaster em","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00219266.2011.561361","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-257689","identifier":[{"id":"84863191162","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e0d17770-d45b-11de-be3f-000ea68e967b"],"keyword":["Inquiry-based science teaching","environmental stress","heat tolerance","inbreeding depression","statistics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C94CE2014B6F70777352AAA78F8AEEF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00219266.2011.561361","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Agricultural Sciences, Populationsgenetik og Embryologi"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kamilla Sofie","key":"pedersenkamillasofiepau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"33881572-23fe-4aad-99f9-343cf67dfe44","name":"Pedersen, Kamilla Sofie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Dybdahl","key":"pedersenlouisedybdahlpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7db30fdf-b447-49bb-85b5-f47736335e01","name":"Pedersen, Louise Dybdahl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Christian","key":"sørensenanderschristianpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"8afa1bfd-aee7-4e28-bcfd-25ddabffb8db","name":"Sørensen, Anders Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Busch","key":"nielsenannabuschpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"64a538fa-e3f9-4e90-8e41-0dbb2f1cc5e9","name":"Nielsen, Anna Busch","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torsten Nygård","key":"kristensentorstennygårdpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"405950ef-7c21-4b42-89d3-4ff45f227de2","name":"Kristensen, Torsten Nygård","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00219266.2011.561361","issn":["00219266","21576009"],"issn_org":["00219266"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Biological Education","pages":"52-57","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Education","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84863191162"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e0d17770-d45b-11de-be3f-000ea68e967b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Investigating inbreeding depression for heat stress tolerance in the model organism <em>Drosophila melanogaster</em>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-257689","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Bannayan-Riley-Ruvalcaba syndrome is a rare disease, which is characterized by macrocephaly, benign hamartomas, lipomas, haemangiomas, pigmented maculae, developmental delay and mental retardation. This case report describes how the combination of macrocephaly, hypertelorism, high palate and intestinal polyposis led to the diagnosis of this syndrome in a two year and seven month-old girl. The diagnosis was confirmed by molecular genetic analysis showing deletion of the entire PTEN gene and the majority of the neighbouring gene BMPR1A, which predisposes to juvenile polyposis.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vibede, Louise Dyrberg","Jensen, Uffe Birk","Sørensen, Tine Høg","Pedersen, Lia Mendes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-267131"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bannayan riley ruvalcabas syndrom og juvenil polypose hos en toårig pige","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84864755170","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-267131","identifier":[{"id":"22673385","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84864755170","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f181073c-fda1-4f23-9901-02fd65a6ebf0"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-386CF2D3F7B260513D40D7978F83CF49"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Børneafdelingen, Aalborg Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Dyrberg","key":"vibedepau","last":"Vibede","locid":"621e2387-07b3-43f1-8c10-06e112b19c8f","name":"Vibede, Louise Dyrberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uffe Birk","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"54eb5276-38e5-433b-b654-7f770ddba0ed","name":"Jensen, Uffe Birk","orcid":"0000-0002-6205-6355","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine Høg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"30f53f76-e9f5-4dc3-a746-c25623042e0f","name":"Sørensen, Tine Høg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lia Mendes","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bc0cf932-cebb-4d48-8d36-3d729228c35b","name":"Pedersen, Lia Mendes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22673385"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"23","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"1614-1615","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"174"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84864755170"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f181073c-fda1-4f23-9901-02fd65a6ebf0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Bannayan-Riley-Ruvalcabas syndrom og juvenil polypose hos en toårig pige","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-267131","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"There are still discrepancies in published ice sheet mass balance results, even between ones based on the same data sets. It can be difficult to conclude from where the discrepancies arise, and it is therefore important to cross calibrate methods, data and models in order to determine the uncertainty associated with these. We present mass change time series at basin scale for both Greenland and Antarctica, derived from GRACE data. We use two independent methods, several different data sets to derive mass changes associated with appropriate error bars. Then for each basin we show the GIA correction on trends with its uncertainties. The first method applied is based on a mass inversion, while the second one uses integration over a representation given in water equivalent. We find good agreement between the resulting mass changes based on the two independent methods, especially in the behaviour of time series. We compare our GRACE derived regional estimates with independent mass change results based on altimetry data from NASA’s Ice Cloud and land Elevation Satellite.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Barletta, Valentina Roberta","Forsberg, René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-374655"],"event":{"end":"2012-04-27","place":"Vienna, at","start":"2012-04-22","title":"European Geosciences Union General Assembly 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monthly solutions of ice sheet mass balance at basin scale and their associated uncertainties","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/9770875/b.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-374655","ids":["dtu-ea3cfdc1-479b-4314-88ba-7d2d48d7be8f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4D5C47963232E2BE0203EEA0D8EC54A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/9770875/b.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Valentina Roberta","key":"barlettapau","last":"Barletta","locid":"9662b7b8-5901-45b2-bba3-dd8e3879f864","name":"Barletta, Valentina Roberta","orcid":"0000-0003-4427-0830","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["10297006","16077962"],"issn_org":["16077962"],"journal":"Geophysical Research Abstracts","publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","status":"p","title":"Geophysical Research Abstracts","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ea3cfdc1-479b-4314-88ba-7d2d48d7be8f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Monthly solutions of ice sheet mass balance at basin scale – and their associated uncertainties","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-374655","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Ryssel, Mia","Sørensen, Louise Marie","Arneborg, Nils","Jespersen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-443612"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-22","place":"Vevey, ch","start":"2012-06-20","title":"3rd European Yeast Flavour Workshop","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flavour compound production by em debaryomyces hansenii em em yarrowia lipolytica em and em saccharomyces cerevisiae em","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-443612","ids":["ku-540762e4-7314-4662-b3bc-3ab575634d12"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-25E22A8882265BA5D807D0BB4BEFB27F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mia","key":"rysselpau","last":"Ryssel","locid":"bb2e324a-c61a-43c3-812c-d6d35ba59f7f","name":"Ryssel, Mia","orcid":"0000-0003-0876-4470","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Marie","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"05dbfd8e-9510-4c28-8368-dba4340d8447","name":"Sørensen, Louise Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils","key":"arneborgpau","last":"Arneborg","locid":"362a10c9-2cc4-4666-9788-883e0fd6ac3e","name":"Arneborg, Nils","orcid":"0000-0002-4323-5446","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"a156c6e3-9562-4d35-9305-53a39c62e076","name":"Jespersen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2555-5948","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"30","publisher":"COST","status":"p","subtitle":"programme &amp; abstract book","title":"Biotechnology for natural flavours &amp; fragrances production"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-540762e4-7314-4662-b3bc-3ab575634d12"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Flavour compound production by <em>Debaryomyces hansenii</em>, <em>Yarrowia lipolytica </em>and <em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</em>","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-443612","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This study aims to identify key miRNAs in circulation, which predict ongoing beta-cell destruction and regeneration in children with newly diagnosed Type 1 Diabetes (T1D). We compared expression level of sera miRNAs from new onset T1D children and age-matched healthy controls and related the miRNAs expression levels to beta-cell function and glycaemic control. Global miRNA sequencing analyses were performed on sera pools from two T1D cohorts (n = 275 and 129, resp.) and one control group (n = 151). We identified twelve upregulated human miRNAs in T1D patients (miR-152, miR-30a-5p, miR-181a, miR-24, miR-148a, miR-210, miR-27a, miR-29a, miR-26a, miR-27b, miR-25, miR-200a); several of these miRNAs were linked to apoptosis and beta-cell networks. Furthermore, we identified miR-25 as negatively associated with residual beta-cell function (est.: -0.12, P = 0.0037), and positively associated with glycaemic control (HbA1c) (est.: 0.11, P = 0.0035) 3 months after onset [corrected]. In conclusion this study demonstrates that miR-25 might be a \"tissue-specific\" miRNA for glycaemic control 3 months after diagnosis in new onset T1D children and therefore supports the role of circulating miRNAs as predictive biomarkers for tissue physiopathology and potential intervention targets.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lotte B","Wang, Cheng","Sørensen, Kaspar","Bang-Berthelsen, Claus H","Hansen, Lars","Andersen, Marie Louise Max","Hougaard, Philip","Juul, Anders","Zhang, Chen-Yu","Pociot, Flemming","Mortensen, Henrik B"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-493027"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating levels of microrna from children with newly diagnosed type 000000000001 diabetes and healthy controls evidence that mir 000000000025 associates to residual beta cell function and glycaemic control during disease progression","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2012/896362","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-493027","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3398606","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"22829805","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84864981566","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a6c7f4f0-1344-4edf-b15f-75e352e9aabd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-6-F79F5429195473913B38F190B92F2B0B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2012/896362","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lotte B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lotte B","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cheng","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Cheng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kaspar","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Kaspar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Claus H","key":"bangberthelsenpau","last":"Bang-Berthelsen","name":"Bang-Berthelsen, Claus H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lars","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marie Louise Max","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Marie Louise Max","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Philip","key":"hougaardpau","last":"Hougaard","name":"Hougaard, Philip","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chen-Yu","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Chen-Yu","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Flemming","key":"pociotpau","last":"Pociot","name":"Pociot, Flemming","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik B","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"f1a10f64-1be6-42df-b4ee-7df370fcc9d0","name":"Mortensen, Henrik B","orcid":"0000-0001-9231-8363","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22829805"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2012/896362","issn":["16875214","16875303"],"issn_org":["16875214"],"journal":"Experimental Diabetes Research","pages":"896362","status":"p","title":"Experimental Diabetes Research","volume":"2012"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84864981566"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a6c7f4f0-1344-4edf-b15f-75e352e9aabd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Circulating levels of microRNA from children with newly diagnosed type 1 diabetes and healthy controls : evidence that miR-25 associates to residual beta-cell function and glycaemic control during disease progression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-493027","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["von Sperling, Marie Louise","Jakobsen, John","Johansen, Jørgen","Sørensen, Jens Ahm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-645043"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-01","place":"København, dk","start":"2012-06-01","title":"Dansk Selskab for Plastik- og Rekonstruktionskirurgi's foråsmøde","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"squamous cell cancer of the nasal vestibule follow up on a 000000000010 year period in southern denmark 000000002000 000000002009","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-645043","ids":["sdu-fb2356b5-a82e-42be-99f0-bd8d46361cd6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2B2496ACC8CEE5141B8F778EC5D25256"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise","key":"vonsperlingpau","last":"von Sperling","name":"von Sperling, Marie Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, John","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"7b9ef019-61d4-4b88-8109-5745bf524ada","name":"Johansen, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-3911-3929","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ahm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fb2356b5-a82e-42be-99f0-bd8d46361cd6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Squamous cell cancer of the nasal vestibule: Follow-up on a 10 year period in Southern Denmark (2000-2009)","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-645043","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Within the last decade, the Greenland ice sheet (GrIS) and its surroundings have experienced record high surface temperatures (Mote, 2007; Box et al., 2010), ice sheet melt extent (Fettweis et al., 2011) and record-low summer sea-ice extent (Nghiem et al., 2007). Using three independent data sets, we derive, for the first time, consistent ice-mass trends and temporal variations within seven major drainage basins from gravity fields from the Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment (GRACE; Tapley et al., 2004), surface-ice velocities from Inteferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar (InSAR; Rignot and Kanagaratnam, 2006) together with output of the regional atmospheric climate modelling (RACMO2/GR; Ettema et al., 2009), and surface-elevation changes from the Ice, cloud and land elevation satellite (ICESat; Sørensen et al., 2011). We show that changing ice discharge (D), surface melting and subsequent run-off (M/R) and precipitation (P) all contribute, in a complex and regionally variable interplay, to the increasingly negative mass balance of the GrIS observed within the last decade. Interannual variability in P along the northwest and west coasts of the GrIS largely explains the apparent regional mass loss increase during 2002–2010, and obscures increasing M/R and D since the 1990s. In winter 2002/2003 and 2008/2009, accumulation anomalies in the east and southeast temporarily outweighed the losses by M/R and D that prevailed during 2003–2008, and after summer 2010. Overall, for all basins of the GrIS, the decadal variability of anomalies in P, M/R and D between 1958 and 2010 (w.r.t. 1961–1990) was significantly exceeded by the regional trends observed during the GRACE period (2002–2011).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Sasgen, Ingo","van den Broeke, Michiel","Bamber, J.L.Jonathan L.","Rignot, Eric","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Wouters, Bert","Martinec, Zdeněk","Velicogna, Isabella","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-035040"],"filters":