{"abstract":"It has been questioned whether bone marrow-derived mesenchymal stromal cells (MSCs) from patients with ischemic heart disease are suitable for use in regenerative stem cell therapy. We compared MSCs from patients with chronic coronary artery disease (CAD) and MSCs from young healthy donors with respect to phenotype, proliferation and endothelial differentiation capacity.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Friis, Tina","Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","Hansen, Susanne Kofoed","Hansen, Louise","Bindslev, Lene","Kastrup, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-461401"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of mesenchymal stromal cells from young healthy donors and patients with severe chronic coronary artery disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/00365513.2010.550310","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-461401","identifier":[{"id":"79954552616","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-71b78133-93b8-4bb6-8331-94af0813b56c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B19F410E31EE754878F6A87CA55068A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/00365513.2010.550310","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Tina","key":"friistinapau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Tina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mandana","key":"haacksørensenmandanapau","last":"Haack-Sørensen","name":"Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne Kofoed","key":"hansensusannekofoedpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Susanne Kofoed","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"hansenlouisepau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Louise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"bindslevlenepau","last":"Bindslev","name":"Bindslev, Lene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"kastrupjenspau","last":"Kastrup","locid":"12c1241f-23da-492c-84b0-36691cb95255","name":"Kastrup, Jens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/00365513.2010.550310","issn":["00365513","0085591X"],"issn_org":["00365513"],"issue":"3","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","pages":"193-202","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79954552616"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-71b78133-93b8-4bb6-8331-94af0813b56c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comparison of mesenchymal stromal cells from young healthy donors and patients with severe chronic coronary artery disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-461401","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The Streptococcus pyogenes cysteine protease SpeB (streptococcal pyrogenic exotoxin B) is important for the invasive potential of the bacteria, but its production is down-regulated following systemic infection. This prompted us to investigate if SpeB potentiated the host immune response after systemic spreading. Addition of SpeB to human plasma increased plasma-mediated bacterial killing and prolonged coagulation time through the intrinsic pathway of coagulation. This effect was independent of the enzymatic activity of SpeB and was mediated by a non-covalent medium-affinity binding and modification of the serpin A1AT (a-1 antitrypsin). Consequently, addition of A1AT to plasma increased bacterial survival. Sequestration of A1AT by SpeB led to enhanced contact system activation, supported by increased bacterial growth in prekallikrein deficient plasma. In a mouse model of systemic infection, administration of SpeB reduced significantly bacterial dissemination. The findings reveal an additional layer of complexity to host-microbe interactions that may be of benefit in the treatment of severe bacterial infections.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Meinert Niclasen, Louise","Olsen, Johan Gotthardt","Dagil, Robert","Qing, Zhang","Sørensen, Ole E","Kragelund, Birthe B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-463576"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Bacterial Proteins","Chemotaxis","Exotoxins","Humans","Leukocytes Mononuclear","Male","Mice","Mice Inbred BALB C","Protein Binding","Streptococcal Infections","Streptococcus pyogenes","alpha 1 Antitrypsin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"streptococcal pyogenic exotoxin b speb boosts the contact system via binding of a 000000000001 antitrypsin","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1042/BJ20100984","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-463576","identifier":[{"id":"79251543226","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21080914","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-754f1323-baa6-4335-8c5a-2492b9be8018"],"keyword":["Animals","Bacterial Proteins","Chemotaxis","Exotoxins","Humans","Leukocytes, Mononuclear","Male","Mice","Mice, Inbred BALB C","Protein Binding","Streptococcal Infections","Streptococcus pyogenes","alpha 1-Antitrypsin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3784F7FBC5D6B0EE8E1617569DD3456E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1042/BJ20100984","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Biomolecular Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"meinertniclasenpau","last":"Meinert Niclasen","locid":"1fc657d3-3e42-4873-ba08-85ffab8a077d","name":"Meinert Niclasen, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Johan G","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"9635604a-372b-4034-b54d-904698148ec8","name":"Olsen, Johan Gotthardt","name_org":"Olsen, Johan G","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Robert","key":"dagilpau","last":"Dagil","locid":"e44c46e9-cbd4-4bdb-91ed-f5e48954b99c","name":"Dagil, Robert","orcid":"0000-0002-5594-0716","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhang","key":"qingpau","last":"Qing","name":"Qing, Zhang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole E","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"bf489eb7-92ee-472f-ad2b-1c20fa