{"abstract":"Elevation data from airborne Light Detection and Ranging (LiDAR) campaigns are used in an attempt to evaluate the accuracy of the Advanced Spaceborne Thermal Emission and Reflection Radiometer (ASTER) global digital elevation model (GDEM) in Greenland. The LiDAR elevation data set is characterized by a high spatial resolution of about 1 m and elevation accuracy of 20–30 cm root mean square error (RMSE). The LiDAR data sets used were acquired during ice-monitoring campaigns carried out from 2003 to 2008. The study areas include ice-free regions, local ice caps and the ice sheet margin. A linear error of 15–65 m was derived, which is far greater than the 20-m product specification. This estimation is biased by both the seasonal and the climatic changes in local ice caps because the ASTER GDEM was computed from imagery acquired in the period 2000–2009. High sloping areas along the coastal regions of Greenland and the effect of the number of scenes used to generate the ASTER GDEM as well as relief are associated with the GDEM accuracy.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Forsberg, René"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365731"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aster gdem validation using lidar data over coastal regions of greenland","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01431161.2010.527389","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365731","identifier":[{"id":"80054723837","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ccdc93b8-eb98-40ae-94f7-1d08fcc25d1f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-499C7D5F9D0C5D9DEEC3BEEEAB901503"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01431161.2010.527389","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Space Institute, Geodynamics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sine Munk","key":"hvidegaardpau","last":"Hvidegaard","locid":"92b07d8f-692c-4ebb-bc40-f44224f3f143","name":"Hvidegaard, Sine Munk","orcid":"0000-0001-8159-6499","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Sandberg","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c6cb90f-da30-48a2-872f-a94b8100749b","name":"Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-3771-4061","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"forsbergpau","last":"Forsberg","locid":"be93c88f-cc39-43d8-bf6f-ff4787c55c23","name":"Forsberg, René","orcid":"0000-0002-7288-9545","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01431161.2010.527389","issn":["2150704X","21507058"],"issn_org":["2150704X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Remote Sensing Letters","pages":"85-91","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Remote Sensing Letters","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80054723837"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ccdc93b8-eb98-40ae-94f7-1d08fcc25d1f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"ASTER GDEM validation using LiDAR data over coastal regions of Greenland","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-365731","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Aims. We evaluated the feasibility, safety and efficacy of intra-myocardial injection of autologous mesenchymal stromal cells derived endothelial progenitor cell (MSC) in patients with stable coronary artery disease (CAD) and refractory angina in this first in man trial. Methods and results. A total of 31 patients with stable CAD, moderate to severe angina and no further revascularization options, were included. Bone marrow MSC were isolated and culture expanded for 6-8 weeks. It was feasible and safe to establish in-hospital culture expansion of autologous MSC and perform intra-myocardial injection of MSC. After six months follow-up myocardial perfusion was unaltered, but the patients increased exercise capacity (p <0.001), reduction in CCS Class (p <0.001), angina attacks (p <0.001) and nitroglycerin consumption (p <0.001), and improved Seattle Angina Questionnaire (SAQ) evaluations (p <0.001). For all parameters there was a tendency towards improved outcome with increasing numbers of cells injected. In the MRI substudy: ejection fraction (p <0.001), systolic wall thickness (p = 0.03) and wall thickening (p = 0.03) all improved. Conclusions. The study demonstrated that it was safe to treat patients with stable CAD with autologous culture expanded MSC. Moreover, MSC treated patients had significant improvement in left ventricular function and exercise capacity, in addition to an improvement in clinical symptoms and SAQ evaluations.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Friis, Tina","Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","Mathiasen, Anders Bruun","Ripa, Rasmus S","Kristoffersen, Ulrik Sloth","Jørgensen, Erik","Hansen, Louise","Bindslev, Lene","Kjaer, Andreas","Hesse, Birger","Dickmeiss, Ebbe","Kastrup, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446008"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mesenchymal stromal cell derived endothelial progenitor treatment in patients with refractory angina","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/14017431.2011.569571","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-446008","identifier":[{"id":"79957523072","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-57eb6fb9-60b9-4cd0-9569-5227e11df690"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24ACB894851B062C7B9C6D5C46C0B5E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/14017431.2011.569571","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Tina","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Tina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mandana","key":"haacksørensenpau","last":"Haack-Sørensen","name":"Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders B","key":"mathiasenpau","last":"Mathiasen","locid":"9dda0e1c-af26-43e0-8ba6-3de29980b77e","name":"Mathiasen, Anders Bruun","name_org":"Mathiasen, Anders B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus S","key":"ripapau","last":"Ripa","name":"Ripa, Rasmus S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrik S","key":"kristoffersenpau","last":"Kristoffersen","locid":"0feeab5a-3bd6-4dac-8ea4-fdc4de0cbd85","name":"Kristoffersen, Ulrik Sloth","name_org":"Kristoffersen, Ulrik S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","fir