{"abstract":"A simple cheese model mimicking a cheese surface was developed for the detection of cheese flavour formation of yeasts. A total of 56 flavour compounds were detected by dynamic headspace sampling followed by gas chromatography - mass spectrometry analysis. Yarrowia lipolytica CBS2075 primarily produced sulphides, furanes and short-chain ketones; Saccharomyces cerevisiae D7 primarily produced esters and Debaryomyces hansenii D18335 primarily produced branched-chain aldehydes and alcohols. For several of the detected flavour compounds, an increase in production was observed upon exposure to dairy-relevant environmental stress conditions including high NaCl concentration and low temperature. The predominant yeasts on the cheese surface may be important for development of flavour, and thus the use of yeasts as ripening cultures have the potential to affect the flavour of cheese.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sørensen, Louise Marie","Gori, Klaus","Petersen, Mikael Agerlin","Jespersen, Lene","Arneborg, Nils"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-521448"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flavour compound production by em yarrowia lipolytica em em saccharomyces cerevisiae em and em debaryomyces hansenii em in a cheese surface model","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.idairyj.2011.06.005","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-521448","identifier":[{"id":"80052894013","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d63e8174-9dcb-4670-a49c-ed9c19370ffc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-730283E76175726225E6AEA2ABE2B1F4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science?_ob=MiamiImageURL&_cid=271246&_user=6447644&_pii=S0958694611001816&_check=y&_origin=&_coverDate=31-Dec-2011&view=c&wchp=dGLzVBA-zSkzk&md5=3d9be869134d29c18cfaa571d2801c87/1-s2.0-S0958694611001816-main.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.idairyj.2011.06.005","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Marie","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"05dbfd8e-9510-4c28-8368-dba4340d8447","name":"Sørensen, Louise Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus","key":"goripau","last":"Gori","locid":"6ae6cff6-0e79-4678-a867-6e85d7ea2ee4","name":"Gori, Klaus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikael Agerlin","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9f4065a7-ea41-4357-b2ca-73903fd418c0","name":"Petersen, Mikael Agerlin","orcid":"0000-0002-4106-7696","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"a156c6e3-9562-4d35-9305-53a39c62e076","name":"Jespersen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2555-5948","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils","key":"arneborgpau","last":"Arneborg","locid":"362a10c9-2cc4-4666-9788-883e0fd6ac3e","name":"Arneborg, Nils","orcid":"0000-0002-4323-5446","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.idairyj.2011.06.005","issn":["09586946","18790143"],"issn_org":["09586946"],"issue":"12","journal":"International Dairy Journal","pages":"970-978","status":"p","title":"International Dairy Journal","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80052894013"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d63e8174-9dcb-4670-a49c-ed9c19370ffc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Flavour compound production by <em>Yarrowia lipolytica</em>,<em> Saccharomyces cerevisiae </em>and <em>Debaryomyces hansenii </em>in a cheese-surface model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-521448","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Jo mere synlig, handlekraftig og engageret sygeplejersker oplever deres nærmeste leder, jo mere tilfredse er sygeplejerskerne med deres arbejde. En åben kommunikation og det at blive set af sin leder har også en positiv effekt på sygeplejerskernes arbejdsglæde.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sørensen, Louise Kryspin","Holm-Petersen, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-663355"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hvad giver sygeplejersker arbejdsglæde resultater fra en spørgeskemaundersøgelse september 000000002011","src":["vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/2051678/dsi-3323.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-663355","ids":["vive-5757d6b5-c9f5-4421-989c-772fa4bcf5c6"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C5FDB2280C2B395AA8E21C60879E6235"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/2051678/dsi-3323.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["VIVE - The Danish Center for Social Science Research, VIVE Governance and Management"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Kryspin","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Louise Kryspin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christina","key":"holmpetersenpau","last":"Holm-Petersen","locid":"46bd96cc-a8b5-4d71-bc3e-da488711cc13","name":"Holm-Petersen, Christina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788772663630"],"place":"København","publisher":"DSI Forlag","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["vive-5757d6b5-c9f5-4421-989c-772fa4bcf5c6"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Hvad giver sygeplejersker arbejdsglæde? : Resultater fra en spørgeskemaundersøgelse september 2011","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-663355","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"DNA exchange in bacteria via conjugative plasmids is believed to be among the most important contributing factors to the rapid evolution- and diversification rates observed in bacterial species. The IncX1 plasmids are particularly interesting in relation to enteric bacteria, and typically carry genetic loads like antibiotic resistance genes and virulence factors. So far, however, a \"pure\" version of these molecular parasites, without genetic loads, has yet to be isolated from the environment. Here we report the construction of pX1.0, a fully synthesized IncX1 plasmid capable of horizontal transfer between different enteric bacteria. The designed pX1.0 sequence was derived from the consensus gene content of five IncX1 plasmids and three other, more divergent, members of the same phylogenetic group. The pX1.0 plasmid was shown to replicate stably in E. coli with a plasmid DNA per total DNA ratio corresponding to approximately 3-9 plasmids per chromosome depending on the growth phase of the host. Through conjugation, pX1.0 was able to self-transfer horizontally into an isogenic strain of E. coli as well as into two additional species belonging to the family Enterobacteriaceae. Our results demonstrate the immediate applicability of recent advances made within the field of synthetic biology for designing and constructing DNA systems, previously existing only in silica.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Lars Hestbjerg","Bentzon-Tilia, Mikkel","Bentzon-Tilia, Sara","Norman, Anders","Rafty, Louise","Sørensen, Søren J."],"cuid":["S02-086.96-027650"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DNA2.0, Menlo Park, California"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design and synthesis of a quintessential self transmissible incx000000000001 plasmid px000000000001 000000000000","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/41005125/journal.pone.0019912.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.96-027650","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3097218","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"79956227193","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21625636","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ce67a233-16e2-4535-9c86-1b5f90481a56","ku-d68615d3-fae3-47d3-abb2-613d23c0e2bf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-33C0369CF3C0FA07AB1ECBA2B4B400B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/41005125/journal.pone.0019912.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0019912","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Resea