{"abstract":"Darier disease is an autosomal dominant genodermatosis caused by germline mutations in the ATP2A2 gene. Clinical expression is variable, including rare segmental phenotypes thought to be caused by postzygotic mosaicism. Genetic counseling of segmental Darier patients is complex, as risk of transmitting a nonsegmental phenotype to offspring is of unknown magnitude. We present the first in-depth molecular analysis of a mosaic patient with segmental disease, quantifying proportions of mutated and normal alleles in various tissues. Pyrosequence analysis of DNA from semen, affected and normal skin, peripheral leukocytes and hair revealed an uneven distribution of the mutated allele, from 14% in semen to 37% in affected skin. We suggest a model for segmental manifestation expression where a threshold number of mutated cells is needed for manifestation development. We further recommend molecular analysis of the ATP2A2 gene in semen of male patients with segmental Darier disease to improve genetic counseling.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Harboe, Theresa Larriba","Willems, Patrick","Jespersgaard, Cathrine","Poulsen, Marie Louise Mølgaard","Sørensen, Flemming Brandt","Bisgaard, Søs Marie Luise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-599471"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mosaicism in segmental darier disease an in depth molecular analysis quantifying proportions of mutated alleles in various tissues","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000328404","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-599471","identifier":[{"id":"21720150","type":"pmid"},{"id":"80052475791","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-5bbbc1d7-970c-439f-a1cb-02f105b11a32"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-4C2FE735DF090AC33DFA8240B8FB3746"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000328404","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Clinical Pathology (Vejle)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Vejle Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Theresa Larriba","key":"harboepau","last":"Harboe","name":"Harboe, Theresa Larriba","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"willemspau","last":"Willems","name":"Willems, Patrick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine","key":"jespersgaardpau","last":"Jespersgaard","name":"Jespersgaard, Cathrine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise Mølgaard","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Marie Louise Mølgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming Brandt","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ac3af930-9550-4d18-9269-4dc0a6d649e5","name":"Sørensen, Flemming Brandt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søs Marie Luise","key":"bisgaardpau","last":"Bisgaard","locid":"d4ef4618-338a-4715-8587-ff8726b9da39","name":"Bisgaard, Søs Marie Luise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21720150"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000328404","issn":["10188665","14219832"],"issn_org":["10188665"],"issue":"4","journal":"Dermatology","pages":"292-6","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Dermatology","volume":"222"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80052475791"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5bbbc1d7-970c-439f-a1cb-02f105b11a32"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Mosaicism in segmental darier disease: an in-depth molecular analysis quantifying proportions of mutated alleles in various tissues","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-599471","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"ICESat has provided surface elevation measurements of the ice sheets since the launch in January 2003, resulting in a unique dataset for monitoring the changes of the cryosphere. Here, we present a novel method for determining the mass balance of the Greenland ice sheet, derived from ICESat altimetry data. Three different methods for deriving elevation changes from the ICESat altimetry dataset are used. This multi-method approach provides a method to assess the complexity of deriving elevation changes from this dataset. The altimetry alone can not provide an estimate of the mass balance of the Greenland ice sheet. Firn dynamics and surface densities are important factors that contribute to the mass change derived from remote-sensing altimetry. The volume change derived from ICESat data is corrected for changes in firn compaction over the observation period, vertical bedrock movement and an intercampaign elevation bias in the ICESat data. Subsequently, the corrected volume change is converted into mass change by the application of a simple surface density model, in which some of the ice dynamics are accounted for. The firn compaction and density models are driven by the HIRHAM5 regional climate model, forced by the ERA-Interim re-analysis product, at the lateral boundaries. We find annual mass loss estimates of the Greenland ice sheet in the range of 191 +/- 23Gt yr(-1) to 240 +/- 28 Gt yr(-1) for the period October 2003 to March 2008. These results are in good agreement with several other studies of the Greenland ice sheet mass balance, based on different remote-sensing techniques.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sørensen, Louise Sandberg","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Nielsen, Karina","Lucas-Picher, P.","Spada, G.","Adalgeirsdottir, G.","Forsberg, René","Hvidberg, C. S."],"cuid":["S02-099.75-033014"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Urbino"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-DMI"],"OT":["Dipartimento di Scienze di Base e Fondamenti, Urbino University \"Carlo Bo\", Via Santa Chiara, 27, 61029 Urbino (PU), Italy"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-DMI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mass balance of the greenland ice sheet 000000002003 000000002008 from icesat data the impact of interpolation sampling and firn density","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6387891/A39ADDE2d01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.75-033014","identifier":[{"id":"79952479280","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-13d6018b-b1e5-4139-8cb5-2f68a4e2393a","ku-5b9ee441-d99f-4957-956b-b3d7dcfbaaf4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EA169D7B33BDA3D50980579A7D9CC093"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.the-cryosphere.net/5/173/2011/tc-5-173-2011.html","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/tc-5-173-2011","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6387891/A39ADDE2d01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2011TCry....5..173S","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Natio