n","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-140620","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Septin9 (Sept9) is a member of the filament-forming septin family of structural proteins and is associated with a variety of cancers and with hereditary neuralgic amyotrophy. We have generated mice with constitutive and conditional Sept9 knockout alleles. Homozygous deletion of Sept9 results in embryonic lethality around day 10 of gestation whereas mice homozygous for the conditional allele develop normally. Here we report the consequences of homozygous loss of Sept9 in immortalized murine embryonic fibroblasts. Proliferation rate was not changed but cells without Sept9 had an altered morphology compared to normal cells, particularly under low serum stress. Abnormal, fragmented, and multiple nuclei were more frequent in cells without Sept9. Cell migration, as measured by gap-filling and filter-invasion assays, was impaired, but individual cells did not move less than wild-type cells. Sept9 knockout cells showed a reduced resistance to hypo-osmotic stress. Stress fiber and vinculin staining at focal adhesion points was less prominent. Long septin filaments stained for Sept7 disappeared. Instead, staining was found in short, often curved filaments and rings. Furthermore, Sept7 was no longer localized to the mitotic spindle. Together, these data reveal the importance of Sept9 for septin filament formation and general cell stability.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Füchtbauer, Annette","Lassen, Louise Berkhoudt","Jensen, Astrid Bøgh","Howard, Jennifer","Quiroga, Adan De Salas","Warming, Søren","Sørensen, Annette Balle","Pedersen, Finn Skou","Füchtbauer, Ernst-Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-163028"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Institutes of Health (NIH)"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"septin000000000009 is involved in septin filament formation and cellular stability","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/80052703007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-163028","identifier":[{"id":"80052703007","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3b1adcba-2e2a-4e68-a374-fe3f606506cd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-31B1BBE6DD40C339906143DD5262EB0F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"national institutes of health","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Institutes of Health (NIH)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"kum ministry of culture archives museums and royal library denmark","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-KUM","l3nn":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","namevar":["Royal Danish Library"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-KUM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette C.","key":"füchtbauerannettepau","last":"Füchtbauer","locid":"66388f14-f717-452e-b5fb-4b643c706fd9","name":"Füchtbauer, Annette","name_org":"Füchtbauer, Annette C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Berkhoudt","key":"lassenlouiseberkhoudtpau","last":"Lass