ons","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-78b858b3-577d-4f80-9d47-0b9f6549e5bf"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"De lokale aktionsgrupper som arnested for samarbejdsdrevet innovation i landdistrikterne?","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-564057","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Background aims. Adoptive transfer of tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes (TIL) has proven effective in metastatic melanoma and should therefore be explored in other types of cancer. The aim of this study was to examine the feasibility of potentially expanding clinically relevant quantities of tumor-specific T-cell cultures from TIL from patients with head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC) using a more rapid expansion procedure compared with previous HNSCC studies. Methods. In a two-step expansion process, initially TIL bulk cultures were established from primary and recurrent HNSCC tumors in high-dose interleukin (IL)-2. Secondly, selected bulk cultures were rapidly expanded using anti-CD3 antibody, feeder cells and high-dose IL-2. T-cell subsets were phenotypically characterized using flow cytometry. T-cell receptor (TCR) clonotype mapping was applied to examine clonotype dynamics during culture. Interferon (INF)-¿ detection by Elispot and Cr(51) release assay determined the specificity and functional capacity of selected TIL pre- and post-rapid expansion. Results. TIL bulk cultures were expanded in 80% of the patients included, showing tumor specificity in 60% of the patients. Rapid expansions generated up to 3500-fold expansion of selected TIL cultures within 17 days. The cultures mainly consisted of T-effector memory cells, with varying distributions of CD8(+) and CD4(+) subtypes both among cultures and patients. TCR clonotype mapping demonstrated oligoclonal expanded cultures, ranging from approximately 10 to 30 T-cell clonotypes. TIL from large-scale rapid expansions maintained functional capacity, and contained tumor-specific T cells. Conclusion. The procedure is feasible for expansion of TIL from HNSCC, ensuring clinically relevant expansion folds within 7 weeks. The cell culture kinetics and phenotypes of the TIL resemble previously published results on TIL from melanoma, setting the stage for clinical testing of this promising treatment strategy for patients with HNSCC.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Junker, Niels","Andersen, Mads Hald","Wenandy, Lynn","Dombernowsky, Sarah Louise","Kiss, Katalin","Sørensen, Christian Hjort","Therkildsen, Marianne Hamilton","Buchwald, Christian von","Andersen, Elo","thor Straten, Per","Svane, Inge Marie","Andersen, Mads Hald"],"cuid":["S02-089.97-041794"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adoptive Transfer","Adult","Aged","Antigens CD3","CD4 Positive T Lymphocytes","CD8 Positive T Lymphocytes","Carcinoma Squamous Cell","Cells Cultured","Feeder Cells","Female","Head and Neck Neoplasms","Humans","Immunotherapy Adoptive","Interferon gamma","Interleukin 2","Lymphocytes Tumor Infiltrating","Male","Middle Aged","Receptors Antigen T Cell","T Lymphocyte Subsets"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bimodal ex vivo expansion of t cells from patients with head and neck squamous cell carcinoma a prerequisite for adoptive cell transfer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/14653249.2011.563291","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.97-041794","identifier":[{"id":"21428850","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84860389787","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3ff19c0f-e70b-4493-beeb-dacf683b6acb","ku-b0f73fc2-c37d-48c3-8cc3-5a69ad2b964a"],"keyword":["Adoptive Transfer","Adult","Aged","Antigens, CD3","CD4-Positive T-Lymphocytes","CD8-Positive T-Lymphocytes","Carcinoma, Squamous Cell","Cells, Cultured","Feeder Cells","Female","Head and Neck Neoplasms","Humans","Immunotherapy, Adoptive","Interferon-gamma","Interleukin-2","Lymphocytes, Tumor-Infiltrating","Male","Middle Aged","Receptors, Antigen, T-Cell","T-Lymphocyte Subsets"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-067FCC635F9DE59AA37E24FF3481CA0B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/14653249.2011.563291","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Graduate School of Health and Medical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Niels","key":"junkernielspau","last":"Junker","locid":"767f54e0-53dc-4455-b8cb-ab9fba99027f","name":"Junker, Niels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mads Hald","key":"andersenmadshaldpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f6dda437-480e-4d5e-b0a3-3287c9d2372a","name":"Andersen, Mads Hald","orcid":"0000-0002-2914-9605","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lynn","key":"wenandylynnpau","last":"Wenandy","name":"Wenandy, Lynn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah Louise","key":"dombernowskysarahlouisepau","last":"Dombernowsky","locid":"f70104b4-17a4-4719-8b74-80f1b7d5a707","name":"Dombernowsky, Sarah Louise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Katalin","key":"kisskatalinpau","last":"Kiss","locid":"523e33c6-7773-4c5b-b99c-320c89965c62","name":"Kiss, Katalin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Hjort","key":"sørensenchristianhjortpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c6f2ec98-9856-4e9d-8757-e5b0d6978778","name":"Sørensen, Christian Hjort","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne Hamilton","key":"therkildsenmariannehamiltonpau","last":"Therkildsen","locid":"2450e96f-b92a-415f-a003-b457b37b7908","name":"Therkildsen, Marianne Hamilton","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vo